window.AKK_DIRECTED_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_DIRECTED_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":301,"title":"Chapter 301: Backstabbing from My Own Father","paragraphs":["\"The Yue Army?\" Yue Fuguang was genuinely surprised by this title.","Although in ancient times, an army, unless directly under the emperor, would always more or less bear the surname or mark of its commander.","But she hadn't expected that less than an hour after selecting her five thousand men, the title of the Yue Army would already be established.","Seeing that they had arrived at the dining hall, Wei Shouyi invited everyone to sit in a private room, then took a wooden box from a guard.","He opened the wooden box and took out a piece of date-red silk.","As he unfolded it, he said, \"Junior Preceptor, you heard correctly, it is the Yue Army. What I hold in my hand is the flag of the Yue Army.","It was made a long time ago, just waiting to be shown to you when you came to select your men today.\"","He unfurled the flag of the purported Yue Army. \"Please take a look, is there anything that needs to be modified?\"","The pattern on it was designed by a grandmaster in the field of calligraphy and painting, whom they had put a lot of effort into finding.","Originally, it would have cost a large sum of money, but when Master Mo heard that he was designing a military flag for the Junior Preceptor, he refused to take a single penny and instructed him to make sure the Junior Preceptor saw it first.","He could modify it at any time according to the Junior Preceptor's requests.","It was the first time Wei Shouyi had seen Master Mo Pingsheng, known for being arrogant, supercilious, and difficult to get along with, be so accommodating!","Yue Fuguang didn't know about these underlying details; she only focused on the military flag.","The flag that appeared before her eyes was made of top-grade silk, three or four meters long when unfolded. It had a red background, with a bright moon embroidered in silver thread positioned in the upper center.","Surrounding the bright moon were faint auspicious clouds embroidered with gold and silver threads, supporting it. A vigorous and powerful golden character for 'Yue' was deeply embedded within the silvery-white bright moon.","The sunlight shining through the window lattice outside happened to spill onto the flag spread out on the table. The golden and silver lights sparkled, and the red silk combined with the gold and silver colors to form a perfect picture.","Yue Fuguang gently stroked the 'Yue' character embroidered with gold thread, which felt like a relief sculpture. She fell silent for a few breaths before shaking her head and saying, \"I think this flag is very good as it is. There's no need to change it.\"","She then said to Wei Shouyi and the other generals, \"You all are very thoughtful!\"","Everyone hastily replied that they wouldn't dare claim the credit.","She turned around and looked at the group of young masters who were looking at her with eager anticipation, \"Are you guys really going to the Sancha region?","There are no brothels or teahouses and taverns there.","Can you really endure that kind of hardship?\"","She smiled and looked at Yu Boming, \"My second brother was also exiled there by our family to endure hardship and gain experience. Don't just follow the crowd!\"","Yu Boming smiled and replied, \"Listen to what you're saying, little sister. Second brother went there voluntarily, it wasn't an exile. Besides, I know about your arrangements there.","It's true that there are no brothels or taverns, but as for enduring hardship, that might not necessarily be the case.\"","He nudged Lin Huaijing, who was standing beside him the whole time, seemingly intentionally undermining Yue Fuguang, but actually meaning to reveal some information to everyone.","He said, \"Huaijing, I haven't told you this, but the Chef Yu in our Junior Preceptor's small kitchen actually has five disciples in total.","She herself and her eldest disciple are in my sister's small kitchen.","The second and third disciples are in the imperial kitchen in the palace, and the fourth disciple is in the main kitchen of our manor.","The fifth disciple took a group of his own disciples and grand-disciples to the Sancha region.\"","He smiled proudly, \"So when it comes to enduring hardship, it's only the training that's tough. As for food, our Junior Preceptor definitely won't mistreat her brothers!\"","Cai Bing, a hidden foodie, immediately punched Yu Boming on the shoulder, \"Second Son Yu, why didn't you say so earlier!\"","If he had said it earlier, he would have already hugged the Junior Preceptor's leg and cried, begging to go!","Every time Yu Boming returned to the military camp from his manor, he would bring a lot of food. Of course, they would also bring some, only more, never less, but none of it was as delicious as the food made by the chef of the Yu Manor.","The fifth disciple in the Sancha region shouldn't be much worse than the fourth disciple in the Yu Manor.","Yue Fuguang also didn't expect that her one sentence would attract her second brother's product placement. Before she could say anything else, the young masters had already bowed again and said, \"We are willing to join the Yue Army and go to garrison the Sancha region. We beg the Junior Preceptor to grant our request!\"","They said they wanted to join the Yue Army, which was equivalent to boarding her ship. Yue Fuguang saw that the parents were just stroking their beards, smiling, and nodding, without any intention of stopping them.","She paused and said, \"Since your minds are made up, then go if you want to. It's just...\"","Her gaze turned to Bao Zihui, who was lagging at the back and trying to muddle through. \"Baozi, you've been married for less than half a year. Don't join in the fun!\"","As someone with a family, you shouldn't play around with a group of single dogs. These people are all guys who only have to feed themselves to feed their whole family.","Being called out by Yue Fuguang, Bao Zihui knew that begging the Junior Preceptor at this time was useless, so he could only cast a hopeful gaze at his father and grandfather.","Little did he know that Bao Qianjun, who had already quietly persuaded Old Master Bao Yuanjun, did indeed step forward under his son's eager gaze.","However, the words he spoke caused Bao Zihui's brain to crash. The smile froze on his face, and his heart shattered into pieces.","Wei Yan patted the dumbfounded Bao Zihui's shoulder somewhat insincerely, sighing that a backstab from one's old father was the most fatal!","But since he had already achieved his wish, he really couldn't empathize with his brother's plight. Hahahahaha!","At this time, Bao Qianjun said, \"The Junior Preceptor is right. Bao Zihui is a newlywed, and it is indeed not suitable for him to leave the capital for a long time at this moment.","However, this subordinate is currently idle at home with nothing to do. I wonder if I could follow the army to the Sancha region.","Even if it is just as a lowly foot soldier, this subordinate is willing!\"","Afraid that Yue Fuguang wouldn't agree, he continued, \"These are my heartfelt words and sincere request. I earnestly beg the Junior Preceptor to grant it!","This subordinate will definitely dedicate myself entirely to the Yue Army! I will not disappoint you, my Lady!\"","Yue Fuguang absolutely never expected things to take this turn. The young master couldn't go, so the parent was taking the field instead?","Looking at Bao Zihui, who had been backstabbed by his own father and wore a bitter expression, Yue Fuguang's mouth twitched. Not only did she lack any sympathy in her wicked heart, but she actually began to seriously consider Bao Qianjun's request.","Although these young masters had undergone a massive transformation after a few months of training, it was hard to guarantee they wouldn't cause trouble thousands of miles away without their parents watching over them.","So having a parent go along to keep them in check wasn't a bad idea.","Moreover, Emperor Mingxi hadn't yet closed the net on the Sima family, and Bao Qianjun certainly wouldn't be reinstated to his original post anytime soon. Going to the Sancha region, far away from the Sima family's gaze, was indeed a good choice.","She pondered for a moment, thinking of Bao Qianjun's upright character, and said, \"Since Lord Bao values the Yue Army so highly, then this Junior Preceptor will allow it!","It just so happens that the Yue Army is newly established, and we still need your help to keep an eye on things.\"","Seeing that Yue Fuguang had agreed, Bao Qianjun looked thrilled, while Bao Zihui's expression grew even fouler. Sure enough, the joys and sorrows of father and son were not connected.","Before he could express his gratitude, Yue Fuguang continued, \"Lord Bao will temporarily hold the position of Army Sergeant, and I will also have to trouble you to temporarily serve concurrently as the Recording Adjutant and Logistics Officer.","These are all temporary. Later on, when I find suitable people to replace you, Lord Bao will have a lighter load.","What does Lord Bao think?\""]},{"number":302,"title":"Chapter 302: Thank you, Lord Assistant Minister, for bestowing the medicine","paragraphs":["Bao Qianjun immediately took a step forward, bowed solemnly, and said, \"Bao Qianjun, Sergeant of the Yue Army, thanks Your Excellency for your trust!\"","Seeing Bao Qianjun's successful on-the-spot job application, others who had idle family members at home couldn't help but feel a bit restless.","But then they thought about how the Yue Army was a place many people couldn't even dream of joining. If they tried to send the 'trash' from their families to the Yue Army, leaving aside whether the Junior Preceptor would accept them or not...","...they probably wouldn't even be able to get past His Majesty.","The officials temporarily suppressed their restless little thoughts. After all, having successfully sent their sons into the Yue Army, they had managed to cling to the Junior Preceptor's coattails.","Yue Fuguang, however, remembered another matter. She turned to ask Wei Shouyi, \"General Wei, how is the Imperial Academy of Medicine's research on the cowpox method going?\"","She had tossed the method to them and hadn't asked about it since. Only now, when it was time to use it, did she remember to ask about the progress.","It could be said that she was truly a hands-off boss, not worrying about a single extra thing!","Mentioning this, Wei Shouyi's face filled with joy. He said, \"I heard from Imperial Physician Sun the day before yesterday that they have already tested it on a hundred or so death row inmates in the Heavenly Prison.","The cowpox method is highly feasible. The Imperial Academy of Medicine is currently producing the vaccine. Starting tomorrow, they will take the lead in inoculating Your Excellency's five thousand soldiers in batches, ensuring it won't delay their departure at the end of the month.\"","[Master, is the vaccine made by mortals reliable? Won't there be any problems?]","[It shouldn't be. The cowpox method isn't some highly advanced technique; it shouldn't be difficult for them to master. Besides, they've already tested it on death row inmates, so it should be safe.","However, what you said isn't entirely unreasonable. To prevent any accidents, I'll just give them an extra layer of insurance.]","[What does Master want to do?]","[Little Zhu, put a bottle of Minor Restoration Pills into my Qiankun sleeve. Remember to make the dosage suitable for mortals.","Just put in ten pills for now.]","Hearing about an elixir, especially one they had never heard of before called the Minor Restoration Pill, everyone's hearts were filled with curiosity.","However, a few sharp-minded individuals quickly caught the words \"Qiankun sleeve\" in the Junior Preceptor's words.","In the most widely circulated tales of immortals in Great Yan, immortals had a universe within their sleeves that could hold all things. Wasn't the Junior Preceptor's Qiankun sleeve exactly that universe within a sleeve?!","Thinking of this, it was as if needles had grown on the stools beneath some people's bottoms, making them feel restless and on edge.","\"General Wei, here is a bottle of elixirs given to me by a friend. Keep it safe for now.\"","As Yue Fuguang spoke, she took out a pink jade bottle, about the thickness of two adult men's thumbs, from her wide and light sleeve.","Wei Shouyi received it with both hands and asked Yue Fuguang with a look of confusion, \"Your Excellency bestows this medicine, but I wonder what kind of medicine is in this bottle and what ailments it treats?\"","Yue Fuguang pointed at the pink jade bottle and said, \"The elixir in the bottle is called the Minor Restoration Pill. It can clear the yin energy from the internal organs and transform yin into yang.","It can also replenish vitality, strengthen one's essence, and has miraculous effects in treating the five overstrains and seven impairments.\"","Hearing that it could replenish vitality, strengthen essence, and had miraculous effects on the five overstrains and seven impairments, the eyes of everyone present instantly widened. They sparkled with starlight, their faces clearly spelling out the word 'desire'.","\"General Wei, this is a life-saving medicine prepared for those five thousand soldiers. If any soldier suffers from a persistent high fever during the inoculation process, take out one pill, dissolve it in water, and have them drink it. One pill is enough for two people to consume. You must keep it safe.\"","[Master, look at the eyes of these people. Will someone use their seniority to bully the weak and embezzle the elixirs you prepared for your own soldiers?]","[Little Zhu, these officials are probably just curious. They are all people in high positions; how could they be so shallow as to embezzle this little bit of medicine?","Besides, who would dare to embezzle my things?]","As Yue Fuguang's words fell, an invisible pressure swept through the entire private room.","Everyone felt as if their entire bodies were locked down by an invisible aura, trapping them within a square inch.","A layer of sweat had unknowingly formed on their backs, and their hands hidden in their sleeves began to tremble involuntarily.","Yue Fuguang merely swept a faint glance over them, and any thieving intentions the crowd hadn't even had time to fully form were completely nipped in the bud.","They continuously made excuses for themselves in their hearts: the Junior Preceptor understood them too well. They were truly just purely curious; how could they actually dare to embezzle the Junior Preceptor's belongings?","Was it that living this life wasn't good enough, or did they not want to live a good life in their next life either?","They hadn't forgotten that these two ancestors had the ability to hunt them down for several lifetimes!","Playing tricks right under her nose was worse than just directly asking for the medicine. Who knows, if the Junior Preceptor was happy and remembered their past friendship, she might actually give them some!","Wei Shouyi tightly gripped the jade bottle in his hand. With the Junior Preceptor's words, he was finally certain that this medicine belonged to his Right Martial Guard New Army Camp. Even His Majesty wouldn't dare reach out for this bottle of medicine.","He cupped his fists and bowed solemnly, saying, \"I thank Your Excellency for bestowing this medicine on behalf of the soldiers!\"","His heart was surging with emotion at this moment, unable to describe the exact feeling. He only felt that the Junior Preceptor was merciful, even taking the lives of common soldiers to heart. They had not worshipped the wrong immortal.","Thinking of himself, Wei Shouyi, although he had the backing of his elders, he had also struggled and fought his way up from a lowly soldier step by step through his own fists and hard work. After all, those who only relied on their ancestors' shelter and weren't tough themselves either died or never reached high positions in their entire lives.","The battlefield was cruel and bloody. As the saying goes, a general's success is built on ten thousand rotting bones. For them to meet a superior who valued the lives of ordinary soldiers at their age was a blessing for the young pups, and it was also his luck, because only he knew how rare this was.","Wei Shouyi thought to himself that if that person was the Junior Preceptor, it would be like connecting to the Heavenly Dao above and the underworld below. With such a huge backer, no one would dare to truly make things difficult for them, except for the enemy!","Wei Shouyi couldn't help but feel proud. His decision to stuff his son, Wei Huaping, into the Yue Army was simply too wise, wasn't it!~","Meanwhile, the young dandies couldn't help but look at each other, puffing out their chests in front of their old men, wearing expressions of \"That's our boss, I'm proud.\"","The fathers just cast a sidelong glance at the young pups who were acting all arrogant just because they had a backer. They didn't even dare to snort, only silently drinking their tea while waiting for the food to be served.","...","Yue Fuguang lay under the crabapple tree. The afternoon sun filtered through the flowers and leaves, spilling over her. The recliner swayed back and forth, much like a cradle.","The dapples of light under the flowering tree flickered on her body with the swaying of the recliner.","If Shen Chunying hadn't still been reporting on the progress of the Yue Army soldiers' inoculation, she probably would have fallen comfortably asleep long ago.","Holding the slip of paper in her hand, Shen Chunying said, \"My Lord, we just received news from the Second Miss's side. Second Young Master sent word that all five thousand soldiers have completed their inoculations, with zero casualties.\"","What she held in her hand was the latest message Yu Boming had sent to the manor using the radio.","Shen Chunying sighed in admiration countless times; having a radio was truly convenient.","Over the past five days, Second Young Master sent a telegram every day. Her Lord didn't have to leave the house, and the army didn't need to send anyone, yet the two sides could communicate.","When the Second Miss and Fourth Miss received and sent telegrams every day, the several lords of the family were also watching closely every day, the smiles on their lips never fading.","Little did they know that when Yu Boming sent telegrams to the Yu Manor every day, there were even more people gathered around him. Led by Wei Shouyi and the young dandies, with military officers of all ranks bringing up the rear, they packed his small room so tightly that not even a drop of water could trickle through."]},{"number":303,"title":"Chapter 303: What a brazen hussy, how dare she compete with her for the master","paragraphs":["The young masters' eyes were red with envy. They had long heard of the radio's reputation, but they hadn't known exactly how miraculous it was.","But what they had seen and heard over the past few days had greatly shattered their worldview. This was truly transmitting messages across a thousand miles!","To call it the power of an immortal would not be an exaggeration. Everyone watched with burning desire, but no one dared to say they wanted to learn it.","After all, this was a skill that could be passed down as a family heirloom. They didn't have the audacity to ask to learn it.","But watching Yu Boming operate it every time, the rhythmic clicking sounds were not only pleasant to the ear, but in their eyes, they were mysterious and incredibly sophisticated.","With just a few random taps, people far away would know exactly what you meant. What could they do if they couldn't suppress the urge to learn it?","The young masters right now were just like the older generation in Yue Fuguang's hometown, whose ultimate dream was to drive a tractor.","The young masters' dream was to become telegraph operators.","At this moment, Yue Fuguang naturally had no idea that the radio had become the biggest news in the Right Martial Guard's new military camp, and that Yu Boming, the only one who knew how to send telegrams, had become the brightest star there.","It could be said that after he thoroughly showed off, the name of the Junior Preceptor, who had brought out such a divine artifact, resonated even more loudly throughout the entire military camp.","The soldiers who had been somewhat afraid and resistant to the vaccination on the first day were scrambling to get vaccinated by the second day.","The Junior Preceptor pitied them and was giving them a divine medicine that would forever protect them from smallpox. They could only pledge their utmost loyalty to repay even a ten-thousandth of her kindness!","No one knew who started it, but every person who received the vaccination would solemnly give a military salute toward the capital in the east.","As for the remaining half of the men, besides being so jealous they wished they could take the others' places, they threw themselves desperately into training. In the second half of the year, they absolutely had to join the Yue Army.","Even when General Wei comforted them, saying that it would be their turn once the Yue Army finished their vaccinations, few were happy.","Hmph! Were they envious, jealous, and hateful just because of the priority vaccinations?","They suddenly thought of the new phrases Second Young Master Yu had taught them: Summer insects cannot discuss ice, and How can a sparrow know the ambition of a swan!","Wei Shouyi, who was rushing back to the capital, still didn't know that he had been secretly mocked by the brats as a summer insect and a sparrow.","Completely unaware of all this, Yue Fuguang lay on her rocking chair. Hearing Shen Chunying report that all five thousand men had been vaccinated without a single casualty, she was also very pleased.","She said, \"It has only been five days since I last went to the military camp to select people. I didn't expect the Imperial Hospital to act so quickly.\"","Shen Chunying smiled and replied, \"According to the Second Young Master, the doctors who vaccinated the soldiers this time included not only the imperial physicians from the Imperial Hospital but also all the reputable doctors in the capital. The idea actually came from Master Xuanmingzi.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Xuanmingzi had a good idea. Explaining it to them ten times is not as effective as letting the doctors practice it hands-on once. With this group of people getting practical experience, the promotion of the cowpox vaccine will surely speed up significantly.\"","Shen Chunying smilingly shared some amusing incidents that happened in the military camp during the vaccination process. Yue Fuguang was listening happily when she saw Taxue and Wuhen, the couple who had run off to play wild for two days without coming home, finally return.","Flap, flap! Flap, flap!","The two large birds landed one after the other at Yue Fuguang's feet, instantly causing the pink crabapple petals on the branches to fall over her like rain.","\"You went out running wild for days, and you still know how to come back?\" Yue Fuguang lightly kicked the two massive birds, instantly causing Taxue and Wuhen to stumble.","Taxue instantly turned into a drama queen. With a small flap of her wings, her increasingly round body flew backward a good two meters.","This scene reminded Yue Fuguang of their first meeting; this fellow had feigned injury to extort her exactly like this back then.","Wuhen, whose reaction was slightly slower, immediately mimicked his wife and flew backward too. Unfortunately, he still had something in his beak, so he only clumsily flew back about a meter.","Taxue, who had already sidled back up to Yue Fuguang's feet, cast a disdainful glance at him. Then, chirping softly, she rubbed her large, fluffy head against Yue Fuguang's leg.","Yue Fuguang ignored her coquettish behavior and looked toward Wuhen, who was trying to imitate his wife by rubbing against her other leg.","\"Wuhen, is that a pigeon in your beak?\"","The snow-white pigeon had been tormented so much that it had lost quite a few feathers, revealing its pink flesh.","Wuhen, who had grown much smarter recently from her feeding, heard Yue Fuguang's words and gently placed the prey in his beak at her feet.","\"Did you bring this back for me?\"","The little creatures had gotten smart. They knew to bring back gifts after going out to play. However, these two were smart enough not to catch a mouse for her.","Chirp, chirp!","Hearing her master's question, Taxue began to chirp as if claiming credit.","Yue Fuguang leaned down and stroked her large head, whose feathers had been nurtured to a smooth and glossy finish, feeling exceptionally nice to the touch. \"I know, I know, our Taxue is the most capable!\"","She also patted Wuhen's head before using her fingers to pick up the half-dead pigeon.","\"My Lady!\" Shen Chunying called out, looking at the pigeon in her hands. Seeing Yue Fuguang look at her in confusion, she continued, \"This subordinate thinks... this pigeon looks like a carrier pigeon, quite similar to the ones kept by the guard squad!\"","She hesitantly took the pigeon Yue Fuguang handed her. Brushing aside a wing covering one of the pigeon's legs, she indeed saw a bamboo tube, the same color as the pigeon's feathers, tied there.","There was a serial number on the bamboo tube: Yue Shiba!","It was the very last of the eighteen pigeons raised by Yue Fuguang's guard squad, and also the one taken by Dongxue to facilitate timely communication when she left the capital!","\"My Lady, this pigeon is Little Eighteen, one of the two that Dongxue took with her.\"","Saying this, she quickly untied the bamboo tube, pulled out a small scroll of paper from inside, and presented it to Yue Fuguang with both hands.","\"Is it a letter from Dongxue?\" Yue Fuguang took the slip of paper but didn't rush to read it. Instead, she took out a small spirit beast pill and stuffed it into the pigeon's beak.","With one pill in its belly, the pigeon that was playing dead instantly perked up and cooed at Yue Fuguang.","Taxue, who was still acting cute by Yue Fuguang's leg, was having none of it. This food not only stole her delicious treats but was now actually trying to steal her meal ticket!","An eagle might tolerate this, but a peregrine falcon absolutely could not!","Taxue squawked at Wuhen. What kind of tramp was this, daring to compete with her for their master!","Seeing the two big birds about to bully the little one, Yue Fuguang quickly took out two more small spirit beast pills and said, \"You two behave.\"","She held up the pigeon in her hand and said, \"Look closely, this one belongs to our family too. Don't bully them in the future, understand?\"","Yue Fuguang didn't know if these two could understand with their current brain capacity, but they chirped at her in response.","She just assumed these two blockheads understood.","She tossed the spirit beast pills into the air. Taxue and Wuhen instantly leaped up to catch them, and soon satisfied purring sounds came from the two birds.","Yue Fuguang stopped paying attention to them and gently unrolled the slip of paper sent by Shen Dongxue.","After reading it, she said to Shen Chunying standing nearby, \"Dongxue says she will arrive in three days. Returning with her are He Qisha, the Master of Seven Swords Villa, and his daughter He Jin.\"","\"Master He and Eldest Miss He from the Seven Swords Villa? Are they coming to visit you, My Lady?\""]},{"number":304,"title":"Chapter 304: It was our presumption to act without your permission, we beg for your forgiveness, my lord","paragraphs":["\"It should be.\"","\"Then, does My Lady wish to see them?\"","Shen Chunying was, after all, an official figure now. The lady they served held great power and a high position, yet she did not cling to authority, nor did she care much for managing mundane affairs in her daily life.","Therefore, as her close attendants, they naturally needed to be well-informed. There were plenty of perceptive people in the court who would pass them information, both openly and in secret.","A few days ago, she heard that the brother-in-law of Master He, Lord Xue Zhipan, had died in his own home. As for the cause of death, everyone remained tight-lipped.","It seemed to involve the Heavenly Star Pavilion and the Panshan Organization, a name they had only recently heard. Furthermore, his youngest son, He Huan, was said to have died in the Xue residence on the same day, in the exact same manner as Xue Zhipan.","To make matters worse, a few days later, He Qisha's younger brother, He Jiuyang, went missing...","Thus, the world knew that the Seven Swords Villa was currently teetering on the edge of a storm. With Villa Master He Qisha requesting an audience at such a time, Shen Chunying worried he might bring trouble to Yue Fuguang.","However, at this moment, Yue Fuguang was both the most afraid of trouble and the least afraid of it.","She was afraid of trouble because she was lazy and didn't want to worry about things; she was unafraid because her increasingly stable status and rapidly growing personal strength left her with nothing to fear.","So, facing Shen Chunying's question, she only thought for a moment before saying, \"There's no harm in seeing them.\"","If it turned out to be too exhausting, she could simply push the matter onto her family or the imperial court to handle.","Meanwhile, the father and daughter of the He family, whom they were just discussing, were traveling day and night with Shen Dongxue toward the capital.","\"Niece of the Luo family, shouldn't the Junior Preceptor have received your letter by now?\"","He Qisha, feeling somewhat anxious, asked for the third time today as they hurried along their journey.","Shen Dongxue... no, Shen Dongxue had already officially returned to her ancestors and reclaimed her lineage. At this point, she should be called Luo Shendong.","Luo Shendong smiled good-naturedly and said, \"Uncle He, My Lady must have surely received my carrier pigeon message by now.\"","Seeing that He Qisha grew more nervous the closer they got to the capital, she couldn't help but comfort him again, \"Uncle He, Sister Jin, you don't need to be nervous.","Our lady is truly a very easygoing person. As long as you do as my mother said, serve her with respect and treat her with sincerity, the Junior Preceptor will definitely not punish you.","However, whether she will accept you into her fold depends on the will of Heaven and your own luck!\"","How many people in the entire capital wanted to cling to the Junior Preceptor's golden thigh?","And how many had actually succeeded?","Therefore, every one of them who managed to stay by the lady's side was extremely lucky. In the words of her older sister Chunying, they had spent a lifetime's worth of luck just to meet her.","He Jin, dressed in a crisp purple martial outfit, looking as beautiful and valiant as a blooming hibiscus flower in July, broke into a smile upon hearing her words.","She said, \"Father, Sister Dong'er is right. As long as we show our utmost sincerity, I believe the Junior Preceptor will surely see it.\"","Though she said this, she was comforting herself just as much as she was comforting her father. After all, knowing they would arrive in the capital by tomorrow, her hands gripping the reins had been sweating much more over the past two days!","The next day, after Yue Fuguang returned from the morning court assembly and had just finished her lunch, Cuizhu came to report that Shen Dongxue had returned and was already at the second gate.","Yue Fuguang smiled and said, \"Cuizhu, Dongxue has returned to her ancestral lineage. From now on, when you see her, you must call her Luo Shendong.\"","Yue Fuguang took Cuiyu with her and had just sat down in the flower hall when she looked up and saw Luo Shendong walking in together with the two sisters, including Shen Chunying.","\"My Lady, your subordinate has returned!\" Luo Shendong greeted Yue Fuguang with a bright smile, cupping her fists in a respectful salute.","Yue Fuguang also smiled and nodded, saying, \"It is good that you have returned safely.\"","She pointed to the chairs below and said, \"You two, sit down and speak.\"","After the two thanked her and sat down, Luo Shendong recounted some of what she had seen and heard on the journey. Finally, she asked, \"My Lady, do you wish to see the father and daughter of the He family that your subordinate mentioned in the pigeon message?\"","\"Shendong, you said in your letter that the father and daughter came to express their gratitude. It seems I have never helped them, so where does this gratitude come from?\"","She did indeed have the idea of taking the Five Mountains and Six Villas under her wing, but it was rather abrupt for the Seven Swords Villa, with which she had no prior interaction, to suddenly approach her.","Hearing Yue Fuguang ask for the reason, Luo Shendong stood up, looking a bit embarrassed, and said, \"My Lady, this was all an independent decision made by my mother and me.","He Qisha is a good friend of my mother. He was plotted against by villains and suffered severe injuries. After My Lady bestowed the Antidote Pill and the Rejuvenation Pill...","On our way back to the Sunset Glow Villa, my mother and I made a detour to the Seven Swords Villa.","Mother spared one of the Rejuvenation Pills My Lady gave us and gave it to the heavily injured He Qisha.\"","At this point, Luo Shendong bowed deeply and said, \"My mother and I took the liberty of giving away what My Lady bestowed upon us to another person. Please forgive us, My Lady.\"","\"Sit down. You do not need to be so cautious. Since I gave the items to Luo Xue, they belong to her. She naturally has the freedom to dispose of them as she wishes.","It seems the medicinal effect of the Rejuvenation Pill is quite good. Is He Qisha fully healed?\"","Yue Fuguang had only heard the system boast about how wonderful the Rejuvenation Pill, originally priced at thirty points each, was. However, she had never seen with her own eyes how effective it would be on a mortal martial artist's severe injuries when a single pill was divided into over a dozen portions.","Speaking of the Rejuvenation Pill's efficacy, a wide smile appeared on Luo Shendong's face, and she even looked a bit excited. She said, \"My Lady, you might not know this, but when my mother and I arrived at the Seven Swords Villa, He Qisha was already so severely injured that he could not get out of bed.","The doctor diagnosed that he wouldn't survive for three months. Who knew that after taking your pill, He Qisha not only fully recovered from his injuries in less than half an hour, but his martial arts cultivation even improved.\"","Her eyes were full of stars as she looked at Yue Fuguang. \"It's no exaggeration to call your pill a fairy pill.\"","[It was originally a pill for immortal cultivators, so it naturally deserves the name of a fairy pill when given to mortals.","However, if I really gave them the pills used by us people of the immortal realm, your mortal bodies wouldn't be able to withstand a true fairy pill.]","Hearing the complaints of Lord Artifact, Cuizhu, Shen Chunying, and Luo Shendong all smiled in their hearts. They still needed Lord Artifact to clear up their confusion before they knew there were so many differences between 'fairy pills.'","After praising the pill, Luo Shendong continued, \"After He Qisha's injuries healed, my mother thought that the Seven Swords Villa was similar to the Sunset Villa, and perhaps it could be of some slight use to the Junior Preceptor.","So, without your permission, she informed He Qisha of the pill's origin, which led to him accompanying me to the capital to express his gratitude.","We acted presumptuously, and we ask for your forgiveness!\"","Saying this, Luo Shendong stood up again. She was actually very apprehensive in her heart. They had acted rashly in this matter, and she didn't know if the adult would blame them.","Yue Fuguang pondered for a moment. She still had some understanding of the guards around her. From Dai Yuxing, Zhang Fang, to the Shen sisters, Liu Wei, and Xu Xiaoman, they were all very tight-lipped about her affairs.","They never revealed the slightest bit of her affairs in front of outsiders.","Therefore, she could somewhat guess the thoughts of the Luo mother and daughter.","It was nothing more than Luo Xue wanting to draw the Seven Swords Villa to her camp after helping an old friend.","In this way, she would have an extra force in her hands, and the Seven Swords Villa would also have her, the most popular and extraordinary Junior Preceptor of the current dynasty, as a backer."]},{"number":305,"title":"Chapter 305: Enlistment","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang said, \"Sit down. I will not hold you accountable for this matter for now, but you must be more cautious in the future. You know I do not like complications, nor do I enjoy being disturbed by trivial matters.\"","Although she was not afraid of the news of her possessing precious medicine getting out—in fact, He Qisha's incident might even attract some martial artists to seek her patronage—the principle remained: she disliked trouble and did not want people to think she was easy-going or easily manipulated.","Given her current status and position, there was no need for her to adopt a populist approach. Maintaining a distance from everyone was the best choice.","The three immediately replied, \"We have taken your words to heart, my lord.\"","Luo Shendong said, \"My lord, regarding an incident like today's, this subordinate will absolutely not repeat it!\"","If there were a next time, she would have no face left to remain by the lord's side. They all knew their duty was to protect the lord's safety.","They had no right to make decisions for her, even under the pretext of acting for her own good.","\"Invite the He father and daughter in.\"","Since the Seven Swords Manor was being delivered into her hands, she had no reason not to take it.","Soon, Luo Shendong led a man and a woman inside.","The middle-aged man was He Qisha. He stood over six feet tall, with a broad, powerful build, a square face, a full beard, and a ruddy complexion that showed no trace of someone who had just recovered from a severe injury.","His eyes were sharp and spirited, but upon seeing Yue Fuguang seated in the host's position, he quickly lowered his gaze slightly, appearing extremely respectful.","The young woman following a step behind wore a purple martial attire. She was tall and slender with delicate features, and her movements carried a natural, unrestrained air.","Like her father, she briefly glanced at Yue Fuguang in the host's seat before promptly lowering her head. Her slightly clenched fists revealed her nervousness.","The father and daughter stopped about five meters from Yue Fuguang and performed a formal cupped-fist salute. \"He Qisha of the Seven Swords Manor, with my daughter He Jin, pay our respects to the Junior Mentor!\"","\"He Jin pays her respects to the Junior Mentor!\"","Yue Fuguang gave a slight nod and said mildly, \"You have come a long way. Please, both of you, be seated.\"","After expressing their thanks, they took their seats in the lowest positions.","[Master, this He Qisha is quite fortunate. Thanks to your elixir, he actually escaped a certain death!]","He Qisha had barely settled half of himself onto his chair when these words abruptly sounded in his ear.","The speaker seemed to be right next to his ear. If He Qisha weren't a seasoned veteran of the martial world, accustomed to great storms and possessing solid composure, he might have jumped up from his chair in shock.","His reaction was not unwarranted, as he was certain the voice had sounded right by his ear, not at the normal conversational distance one would expect in the room.","Given his age and status, his thoughts mirrored Luo Xue's at the time: this voice did not belong to anyone present in the room. Recalling Luo Xue's extremely subtle hints before their arrival...","He Jin instantly went on full alert. The muscles beneath her martial attire tensed, and her recently relaxed hands swiftly clenched into fists again, ready for action.","Father and daughter exchanged an almost imperceptible glance. After the initial tension, they carefully recalled the content mentioned in that voice.","A certain death?","Indeed, it had been certain. The physicians who examined him had all shaken their heads, practically declaring him beyond cure.","As a man waiting to die, he never imagined that a single small pill from an old friend would completely cure him within half an hour.","Thinking of this, He Qisha, disregarding the origin and strangeness of the voice, cupped his fists towards Yue Fuguang and said, \"We are deeply grateful for your grace in granting us an audience despite your busy schedule, my lord. We hope you will forgive our intrusion.\"","Yue Fuguang remained impassive. \"You flatter me, Manor Lord He.\"","He Qisha shook his head, his face full of gratitude. \"My lord may not know this, but just over a month ago, I was harmed by a villain, suffering severe injuries that left me hanging by a thread. Thanks to your divine medicine, I was restored to health in one dose. This kindness is like being reborn.\"","He stood up and bowed deeply. \"Your grace and virtue, my lord, are as weighty as a mountain. Even if I were to tie grass knots or hold a ring in my mouth in gratitude, I could never repay one ten-thousandth of this debt.\"","He raised his head, his gaze firm as he looked at Yue Fuguang. \"From this day forward, whatever command you may have, I, He Qisha, and the Seven Swords Manor behind me, will brave any danger without hesitation.\"","He Jin also said, \"Saving my father's life is akin to saving the lives of my brother and myself.\" She performed a solemn bow. \"Though lacking in talent, I am somewhat skilled in martial arts. I, He Jin, am willing to serve you, holding your horse's reins or whip, ready to follow your orders at any time.\"","[Master, this He Jin is quite clever. She understands that your one pill saved the lives of all three of them.","According to the original fate, after He Qisha was killed by He Jiuyang and Panshan, she and her brother He Heng were pursued by He Huan.","Although they narrowly escaped death, a few years later, the two siblings still met their end while trying to avenge their father.]","\"Now that He Qisha is safe, such a fate will naturally not occur again.\"","[That's true. Who would have thought Master's unintentional act would end up saving the entire Seven Swords Manor? They are indeed lucky.","However, Master is not short of people to command.]","This time, the father and daughter heard clearly. One of the voices belonged to the lord before them, but they had not seen her lips move!","As for the guess of ventriloquism, He Qisha was the first to dismiss it. Coincidentally, he happened to be skilled in that very art himself.","Both father and daughter were accomplished martial artists. Upon meeting, they had sensed that the lord before them, while exerting a subtle, intangible pressure, definitely possessed no martial arts skills.","Could it be that this lord was truly an immortal incarnate, capable of things ordinary people could not?","On their journey here, the father and daughter had heard no shortage of folk rumors among the common people about this lord, each more fantastical than tales of gods and spirits.","The He father and daughter couldn't help but let their thoughts drift towards the supernatural as well.","Yue Fuguang nodded and said, \"Manor Lord He's misfortune has been relayed to me by Shendong. Manor Lord Luo's willingness to use the elixir to save you was also due to the old friendship between you. I do not deserve your gratitude.\"","\"No, no, Junior Mentor. The great life-saving grace you have shown us, my father and I, is engraved in our hearts.\"","Seeing that Yue Fuguang was not taking his offer, He Qisha grew anxious. He quickly stood up and declared solemnly once more, \"Junior Mentor, our Seven Swords Manor is willing, just like the Sunset Glow Manor, to serve you with utmost sincerity. Please do not look down on us for our martial world origins or consider us too crude to be of use!\"","He directly went down on one knee. \"I, He Qisha, swear upon heaven and earth my willingness to lead the Seven Swords Manor in pledging our lives to serve you. If I ever break this oath, may I be forsaken by both gods and men!\"","[Master, this He Qisha is making reckless vows. He doesn't know you are a true immortal. If he betrays you, he truly will be forsaken by gods and men!","Little Zhu can chase him all the way to the underworld and have King Yama give him a proper reception!]","After a moment of shock, He Qisha felt boundless ecstasy. Being shrewd, he instantly connected many dots.","Their master's exalted status, the strange attitude of the court, and the mysterious voices they heard today... all found a reasonable explanation!","This golden thigh—even if he had to kneel here until death today, he, He Qisha, must cling to it.","Having already been as good as dead once, he understood all too well the difference between having a powerful backer and not having one—a gap wider than that between a man and a dog."]},{"number":306,"title":"Chapter 306: The Land of Three Crossroads, the Gateway of the Nation","paragraphs":["And the mysterious disappearance of his good younger brother He Jiuyang... he dared not think too much about it.","\"We beg you not to reject us, please accept us!\" He Qisha was very shrewd, kowtowing and pleading earnestly.","\"My lord, He Jin's feelings are also sincere.\" She imitated her father's gesture and bowed down, speaking earnestly, \"He Jin is well aware that you are surrounded by many talents and do not lack my humble skills.","He Jin wishes to serve by your side as a humble maid, I beg you to grant this request!\"","[Master, the ambitions of Panshan and Tianxing Tower to covet the Seven Swords Manor remain undiminished. If you do not accept them, the Seven Swords Manor will eventually fall into the hands of villains.]","'Little Zhu, why are you also urging this immortal lord to accept them?'","[Master, it's just out of boredom. There are no formidable demons or monsters in this mortal realm for me to catch for amusement. Little Zhu just wants something to do!]","'Alright, as you wish!' The tone sounded quite reluctant and forced.","Her voice was faint as she said, \"Both of you, rise. Sit and speak.\"","After expressing their thanks, the two stood up and took their seats. Yue Fuguang continued, \"This official prefers tranquility and does not involve myself much in daily affairs. In the future, the Seven Swords Manor will be like the Sunset Glow Manor; report any matters first to my guards.\"","He Qisha's face lit up with joy, and he cupped his hands, saying, \"This subordinate will follow all arrangements from our Master!\"","Yue Fuguang's heart skipped a beat. Goodness, this He Qisha was perceptive. He no longer called her 'my lord' but directly switched to addressing her as 'Master'.","The distinction between closeness and distance was immediately clear!","She then looked at He Jin. \"He Jin, do you know Dai Yuxing?\"","The martial world is divided by sects and also by background. Dai Yuxing hailed from Chongming Mountain, one of the Five Mountains and Six Manors, and might be acquainted with the young lady of the Seven Swords Manor, hence the previous question.","He Jin replied, \"In reply to you, my lord, we have known each other since childhood.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded and continued asking, \"Then, between your martial arts and his, whose is superior?\"","He Jin hadn't expected Yue Fuguang to ask this so directly. She paused and said, \"The last time we sparred was a year ago. That time, we each had victories and defeats, so it was a draw.","A year has passed now, I do not know who is superior or inferior at present.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Since that is the case, then you shall take over Zhang Fang's position as Commandant, a fifth-rank junior official position.\"","Fifth-rank junior!","Father and daughter immediately stood up. He Jin stammered, \"M-my lord... isn't that... isn't that a bit too high?","I... this subordinate has not achieved the slightest merit...\"","In the court of the Great Yan dynasty, aside from you, my lord, there was no second female official. There were a few female generals in the army, but those all came from hereditary military families.","Other female officials, like the Shen Chunying sisters, were all by your side, my lord.","Before coming here, she would never have dared to imagine that one moment she was a martial artist with an uncertain future, and with a single word from you, my lord, she would gain an official position, and a fifth-rank junior one at that!","Higher in rank than the county magistrate who oversaw their manor!","He Qisha's face also flushed slightly red. He too looked at Yue Fuguang and said, \"Indeed, Master, A'Jin is still young and has not achieved any merit. Suddenly occupying a high position might not command respect from others.\"","Yue Fuguang waved her hand dismissively. \"You worry too much. Who would dare to question this official's words?\"","[Exactly! Anyone who dares to question the master's decision is not worthy of staying to serve by the master's side.]","At this moment, father and daughter truly felt the domineering authority and unmatched confidence of this person who decided matters with a single word.","Luo Shendong, who had been quietly acting as part of the background without uttering a word, saw that the matter was settled and couldn't help but ask with confusion, \"My lord, if Sister A'Jin assumes the position of Left Commandant...","then what about Lord Zhang Fang...\"","Could it be that during the time she was away, he caused trouble and was expelled?","Yue Fuguang understood her implication and a faint smile curled at the corner of her mouth. \"In two days, the Moon Army will set out to station at the Three Forks Land.","Zhang Fang applied to me two days ago, wishing to go along. I permitted it.\"","Zhang Fang wanted to go to the battlefield but also wished to remain by her side. The Moon Army presented him with this opportunity.","The Moon Army was Yue Fuguang's Moon Army. Even if he left the Yu residence, he would still be a person of the Junior Mentor. Therefore, after weighing the pros and cons, he still approached Yue Fuguang to explain his thoughts.","Yue Fuguang also felt that Zhang Fang was well-suited for the army. He was considered one of her own, so going to the Moon Army to assist Yu Boming and keep an eye on things for her was a good choice, and she agreed to his request.","[Host, this He Qisha is quite savvy. With him as an example, those who wish to pledge allegiance to you in the future will have a model to follow.]","After seeing off the He father and daughter, Yue Fuguang lay back on the recliner under the pear blossom tree. While coaxing herself to sleep, she said, 'It's precisely because he is savvy that I gifted him one Detoxification Pill and one Revival Spring Pill.'","Although these pills were inconsequential to her current wealth exceeding one hundred thousand, they were perfect for winning people's hearts.","One pill was equivalent to a life. Having witnessed the efficacy of the pills, He Qisha would surely sing her praises far and wide and be willing to die for her.","\"Bowing his head and prostrating in worship\" perfectly described He Qisha, who received the pills with trembling hands at that time.","The act she and her system put on was precisely to set an example for those who wish to seek refuge with her in the future.","She needed personnel and influence, but she wouldn't accept just anyone. Without sufficient sincerity and loyalty, those who wished to opportunistically ride on her coattails were truly thinking too much!","The fifth year of Yuankang, the twenty-third day of the fifth month. Auspicious for sacrifices, prayers, moving, and travel.","Mid-morning. Emperor Mingxi, his ministers who had concluded the grand court assembly early, and Yue Fuguang once again arrived at the drill ground of the new Right Martial Guard camp.","The morning sun had just risen. On the drill ground, the banners of the Great Yan's new recruits and the shimmering gold and silver banners of the Moon Army fluttered gently in the morning breeze.","Ten thousand new soldiers stood in neat formation, their faces youthful but their gazes resolute.","The emperor, dressed in informal attire, slowly ascended the command platform, his eyes scanning the entire field like torches.","Drawing a deep breath, his voice boomed like a great bell, resonating in all directions, \"Young men, seeing you standing here, I am suddenly reminded of a morning twenty years ago when I too was once a member on the drill ground.\"","Whether ancient or modern, when people reach a certain age, they like to reminisce. Looking at the young faces below the platform, Emperor Mingxi couldn't help but think of himself twenty years ago.","Unfavored by his imperial father, yet as the Crown Prince, the heir to the state, he too had entered the military camp and guarded the border.","Once one starts reminiscing about the past, emotions easily become abundant. As one of the people closest to Emperor Mingxi, Yue Fuguang clearly saw tears glistening in the corners of the emperor's eyes.","He continued, \"Back then, I was about your age, not understanding parting, only seeing spears and blades gleaming under the sunlight. But today, I am here on this drill ground to bid farewell to you, sending you to the place farthest from the capital.\"","The wind swept across the drill ground, making the military flags snap and flutter. The emperor's robes were also stirred by the morning breeze, making his entire figure appear more majestic.","\"I want to tell you, the place you go to today is not a battlefield, but the eaves of your homes.","The Three Forks Land is the gateway of our dynasty, and you are our court's first line of defense. What you guard is not only the border of Great Yan but also the peaceful days of your parents, brothers, sisters, wives, and children at home.\"","As he spoke, he raised his hand and pointed to the clothes he was wearing, gently brushing over the robe that was overly plain for an emperor. \"I deliberately wore this this morning. It is related to the same crop you will be stationed near.","This item is called cotton, a good thing found for the people of the world by our dynasty's Junior Mentor.\""]},{"number":307,"title":"Chapter 307: Walkie-Talkie","paragraphs":["\"This item is called cotton, a fine thing that our dynasty's Lord Junior Preceptor has found for the people of the world.\"","Saying this, he cast a gentle smile at Yue Fuguang, who was standing below. \"Cotton, like hemp, can be spun into thread and woven into cloth. Just like the clothes I am wearing today, they are made of cloth woven from cotton, called cotton cloth.","Cotton cloth is soft and breathable, sturdy and wear-resistant. Not only can cotton be used to weave cloth, but it can also be made into winter clothes and quilts. Its warmth is not much inferior to that of fur cloaks.","In the future, when cotton is planted all over our Great Yan, even the common people will have cotton clothes to ward off the cold in the freezing winter.","Therefore, although your journey this time has no danger of weapons and war, you bear a heavy responsibility and a long road ahead.\"","He took a gleaming spear from the platform and said loudly, \"This spear has not yet drunk blood.\" He struck the shaft heavily against the ground. \"Yet it is the best weapon of our Great Yan. In the future, it will accompany you to guard the borders of our Great Yan, serving as your most loyal companion.","Finally, I clearly inform you today that the promise the Lord Junior Preceptor made to you, I have approved!","I hope you will not disappoint my entrustment, nor the trust of the Lord Junior Preceptor!\"","\"Long live the Emperor!\"","\"Long live the Emperor!\"","\"May the Lord Junior Preceptor prosper!\"","\"May the Lord Junior Preceptor prosper!\"...","Tens of thousands of people shouted in unison, their voices shaking the heavens and the earth!","[Master, it is a good thing they said 'prosper' for the Lord Junior Preceptor instead of 'long live' (ten thousand years). Otherwise, wouldn't they be cursing you? For an immortal, ten thousand years is truly a short life!]","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers were originally extremely excited by this enthusiastic scene, and the courtiers were just short of shouting along with them.","However, the words of Lord Artifact suddenly echoed in their ears—words that made these mortals envious every time they heard them.","If they knew modern terminology, they would know that this was the System humblebragging.","The army was ready to depart. Yue Fuguang waved her hand and called over her second brother, Yu Boming. Her little follower, Lin Huaijing, followed closely behind him.","The young dandies lagging behind exchanged glances and also followed. Who told their fathers to be there too!","Yue Fuguang took the box carried by Shen Chunying behind her, and the eyes of the surrounding people followed her movements to look at the box.","They had seen the box in the hands of the Lord Junior Preceptor's guard early on. Looking at that dark green box, they couldn't help but think of the one containing the long-distance telegraph radio, which seemed to be this kind of box too.","Therefore, everyone, including Emperor Mingxi, had long been curious about what was inside.","She opened the box; inside were ten black walkie-talkies.","Catching a glimpse from the corners of their eyes of this black object in Yue Fuguang's hand, which, like the radio, was made of an unidentifiable material, the crowd stopped putting on acts of deep father-son affection with the boys about to travel far.","Dropping the act entirely, led by Emperor Mingxi, they all leaned their heads over.","Before Yue Fuguang and Yu Boming could say much, Emperor Mingxi couldn't help but ask first, \"Fuguang, what is this object in your hand?","Why does it look to me like its material is very similar to some accessories of the radio?\"","Yue Fuguang saw that everyone's eyes were practically glued to the walkie-talkies. Emperor Mingxi even couldn't resist reaching out his paw to pick one up from the box, turning it over and over to examine it.","Her mouth twitched, and she smiled, saying, \"Your Majesty, My Lords, this thing is called a walkie-talkie. Like the previous radio, it is used for communication between two places.\"","Hearing that it was also an item for communication, Emperor Mingxi suddenly felt that the little black lump in his hand was as heavy as a thousand catties. Had he been too rough when he was turning it over and over just now?!","He didn't break the good stuff, did he?!","Emperor Mingxi changed his grip to cradling it and asked with full expectation, \"Fuguang, can this little thing also transmit messages over a thousand miles? Why don't I see a button for sending telegraphs?\"","This black lump also had little square blocks and an 'ear', but because they were different from the telegraph button, Emperor Mingxi didn't dare to touch any of them.","\"Your Majesty, this cannot transmit messages over a thousand miles.\"","It couldn't transmit over a thousand miles? Emperor Mingxi and his ministers were somewhat disappointed to hear this answer. However, on second thought, that radio was so big, and this black lump was so small. Making such a small thing transmit over a thousand miles was indeed a bit too much to ask!","Before they could be disappointed for long, they heard Yue Fuguang continue, \"However, it can transmit voices within a hundred miles, in real-time, just like how I am speaking face-to-face with Your Majesty right now!\"","Transmit voices within a hundred miles?","Emperor Mingxi widened his eyes, staring in astonishment at the thing in his hand. His hands couldn't help but tremble a bit, and for a moment, he couldn't speak a single word.","He had also been to the battlefield, so he naturally knew what this thing meant for the military.","This little thing might be small, but its function was just as heaven-defying as the radio!","The crowd of civil and military officials and soldiers surrounding them all shared the same blank expression of sheer astonishment.","For a moment, the area with over a hundred people was dead silent; you could hear a pin drop.","\"Your Majesty!\" Yu Chongshan, who was relatively calm, couldn't help but snap Emperor Mingxi out of it.","Seeing that their Emperor was imagining who-knows-what, his face growing more and more excited.","His eyes were fixed on the walkie-talkie in his hand, but his hands were trembling non-stop.","Yu Chongshan thought: Your Majesty, tremble if you must, but don't tremble while holding the walkie-talkie my granddaughter gave to my grandson!","If it breaks, whose fault will it be?","Even if you are the noble Supreme Ruler, there is no way you can find an identical one to replace it!","Emperor Mingxi was just imagining himself using this item to slaughter enemies in all directions when he was suddenly interrupted. He was annoyed in his heart, but his face looked a bit sluggish and bewildered, clearly showing a disconnect between his mind and actions.","However, he was only bewildered for a moment before he looked at Yue Fuguang with sparkling eyes. \"Fuguang, you just said that this little thing called a walkie-talkie can transmit voices over a hundred miles? Is it true?!\"","Yue Fuguang said casually, \"Guaranteed!\"","The System also chimed in to complain: [Is a walkie-talkie with a hundred-mile range really worth them acting like this? If they knew that Master also has a communication tool called a mobile phone, which can transmit voices over ten thousand miles and even let you see the other person's face as if you were talking face-to-face, wouldn't they die of excitement?]","\"Little Zhu, if they knew how powerful a mobile phone's functions are, but couldn't use it in this world, they wouldn't die of excitement. They would die of envy from having a treasure but being unable to use it!","You and I, servant and master, are kind immortals, so let's just not tell them this news!\"","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers: It's too late, we already know! We knew it long ago! Groundhog screaming JPG","Not to mention the powerful functions of the mobile phone mentioned by the Little Immortal, just the ability to transmit voices over ten thousand miles like talking face-to-face had already made them salivate and dream about it day and night since the first time they heard Lord Artifact mention it.","It was hateful that they were mere mortals and couldn't use the magical artifacts of immortals!","Seeing the somewhat dumbfounded crowd, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but suggest, \"Your Majesty, how about we give it a try right now?\"","It would also be a good opportunity to teach Yu Boming how to operate it on the spot. Doing it once is more effective than explaining it ten times.","\"Yes, yes, yes, let's try it, try it right now!\"","Yue Fuguang nodded and said to the young dandies standing to the side, \"You guys, come over here.\"","As her words fell, seven or eight young dandies gathered around without hesitation. Led by Wei Yan, they cupped their hands to Yue Fuguang and said, \"Greetings, Lord Junior Preceptor!\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. She picked up a walkie-talkie and said, \"I will only demonstrate this once, so watch carefully.\"","Hearing her say this, everyone looked extremely excited. With flushed faces and wide eyes, they nodded frantically."]},{"number":308,"title":"Chapter 308: Testing","paragraphs":["As for saying some polite remarks, at this moment they could only tremble their lips and say a single word, \"Yes.\"","Everyone knew that by saying this, Yue Fuguang meant to employ these young lads, and they would be the ones using this treasure capable of transmitting voices over a hundred miles in the future.","The group of fathers standing on the periphery looked at their sons, who had been good-for-nothings just half a year ago, and now no longer felt their past disdain.","They only felt that although their own sons were a bit of a scoundrel, nothing could stop their good luck!","They had been interacting with the Junior Preceptor for almost a year and were still merely colleagues, but the young lads were already considered half of the Junior Preceptor's own people.","As long as they didn't act foolishly and court death, under the protection of the Junior Preceptor, even if they fared poorly in the future, they would still surpass their fathers and ancestors, doing better than their old men!","For a moment, everyone's eyes were filled with smiles; aside from the royal family, there was no one who didn't hope their next generation would be stronger than themselves.","And they faintly gathered behind Emperor Mingxi and Yu Chongshan.","Soon, Yue Fuguang explained the steps clearly and said to the crowd, \"Each of you take a walkie-talkie, ride a fast horse, and gallop in different directions.\"","She looked up at the time, \"Limit it to ten miles; once you reach it, come back.\"","The few of them replied in unison, \"We obey the Junior Preceptor's orders!\"","Wei Yan and the others carefully took out a walkie-talkie from the box and hung it on their chests.","\"Remember to report the distance every little while!\" Emperor Mingxi instructed.","\"Yes, Your Majesty!\"","Watching the eight fast horses gallop away, Yue Fuguang handed the last one to Yu Boming, \"Second Brother, take this. Right now, you will act as the main caller to communicate with them.\"","At this moment, besides the one in Emperor Mingxi's hand, only the one in her hand remained.","Yu Boming had just gotten his hands on it and familiarized himself with it when a clear voice came from the walkie-talkie in his hand.","\"Boming, it's me, Cai Bing. Am I the first?\"","The old father Cai Xian's face darkened when he heard his son's lively voice.","The old father, who was just feeling proud of his son, suddenly felt his hands itching again, and his callused hand unconsciously rested on the jade belt at his waist.","\"Cai Bing, you're cheating! Boming, I am Huo Shui, I'm second!\"","Another old father with a dark face was added, while the other fathers silently prayed in their hearts that their little brats wouldn't cause any trouble; otherwise, they would definitely beat their sons behind the Junior Preceptor's back before parting!","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow and gave Yu Boming a look, which he instantly understood.","Although the other party couldn't see it, Yu Boming's face instantly turned serious as he said, \"Cai Bing, Cai Bing, this is Yu Boming. Please observe communication discipline, or your calling privileges will be confiscated. Respond if you copy!\"","The other side hesitated for a moment and loudly said, \"Copy that, over!\"","Yu Boming similarly warned Huo Sui, and the communication channel instantly fell silent.","Soon, formal communication began one after another, and Wei Huaping and the other seven reported their current distances.","When they reached a distance of ten miles, the call was still clear, and Yue Fuguang signaled Yu Boming to call them back.","Taking advantage of the gap while they were returning, Yue Fuguang took a small wooden box from He Jin and handed it to Yu Boming, saying, \"Second Brother, inside are the pills I prepared. The usage and effects have all been written clearly.\"","She patted the box and said, \"Make sure to keep it safe and don't let it fall into the hands of others.\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's words, the crowd silently blocked the figures of Yu Boming and Yue Fuguang to prevent them from being seen by more people.","Yu Boming carefully took the box, his eyes slightly red, and said with a slightly hoarse voice, \"Don't worry, sister. As long as I am alive, the medicine will be here. I will take good care of the Three Forks Land for you!\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head, \"Although the pills are precious, they are far less important than you, Second Brother. I gave you the pills to save your lives.","Not for you to lose your lives protecting them!\"","She patted Yu Boming's... arm like a little adult, \"You must remember this, Second Brother. Don't put the cart before the horse!\"","[Exactly, mere pills, is there a need for him to protect them with his life! Master, why is this Yu Boming still so silly!]","'Little Zhu, one pill equals one life. He is holding a hundred lives in this box, so it's understandable for him to act this way.'","[Master, you are just too lenient towards your own people!]","'If your master wasn't lenient, then when you broke my Seven-Treasure Glazed Lamp that could exorcise demons and ward off evil, shouldn't I have punished you to face the wall for three hundred years?'","[Ahaha, Master is the best! If Little Zhu was made to face the wall for three hundred years without moving, Little Zhu would die of boredom!]","The corners of everyone's mouths twitched upon hearing this. They all pursed their lips, trying hard to hold back their laughter. Without even looking, they could imagine the great divine artifact twisting itself into a pretzel right now, acting cute and coquettish.","Where was the slightest shadow of the domineering divine artifact that would casually cripple this one or strike that one dead to be seen now?","As for the box of pills that made everyone green with envy, several officials led by Cai Xian and Huo Ying silently glanced at their colleagues.","The deep meaning in that glance blatantly told their colleagues that the box contained their sons' chances of survival, and no one was allowed to touch it!","Otherwise...","Everyone silently lowered their heads. They weren't afraid of those officials, but rather taking the Junior Preceptor into consideration.","Even if they were given ten times the courage, they wouldn't dare touch a single bit of her belongings. Otherwise, once they went to sleep, they could forget about ever waking up again!","Looking at Yue Fuguang, who currently had a gentle and harmless expression, the crowd shook their heads; it was all a facade!","This person had never been known for having a good temper! Not to mention that protective divine artifact of hers.","Despite it acting cute with the Junior Preceptor right now, if they dared to make a rash move, even His Majesty wouldn't be able to save them.","In the eyes of the divine artifact, His Majesty was merely an ant slightly more noble than them!","Could Emperor Mingxi not understand this?","He understood it even better than his ministers. Given his friendship with Fuguang, why would he need to snatch anything?","If he really needed something, wouldn't it be faster and safer to just ask nicely?","Xie Zhiyan's eyes flickered as he imperceptibly swept his gaze across the scene, taking in everyone's reactions.","He unconsciously stroked the jade pendant hanging at his waist, which was one of a pair gifted by the Junior Preceptor for his wedding.","The other piece hung at the Crown Princess's waist.","Emperor Mingxi took the lead in praising, \"Fuguang is still the most thoughtful. The Yu family boy is truly blessed to have a sister worrying about him all the time.\"","Yu Boming scratched his head in embarrassment and said with a red face, \"Fuguang is naturally the best sister in the world!\"","Yu Shuchun looked at Yue Fuguang with a face full of pride, then turned to his son with a stern face and said, \"Since you know that, as an older brother, you naturally have to think more for your sister!","I don't expect you to be the best brother in the world, but don't let your sister worry so much about you at such a young age!\"","Seeing his father's stern face, Yu Boming quickly said, \"Father is right, I will definitely keep it in mind!\"","Yue Fuguang teasingly smiled and said, \"Second Brother, you must take care of yourself. Remember to send a message back home promptly if anything happens, and remember to come back next year to get married!\"","She couldn't delay his marriage for her own affairs. Not to mention that her future second sister-in-law was a good girl, so of course he had to marry her and bring her home as soon as possible."]},{"number":309,"title":"Chapter 309: The Choice for the Sister-in-Law","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang's words made the already blushing Yu Boming turn even redder. He carefully glanced at his elders and his sister, who wore a blatant teasing expression.","He nodded awkwardly, \"Don't worry, Fuguang, Second Brother has memorized it all!\"","Yu Chongshan looked at his grandson and granddaughter, the smile never fading from his face.","Wang Shouchen and several other elder officials surrounded him, praising them endlessly out of envy.","Yu Chongshan accepted all the praises from his colleagues without refusing a single one, gladly taking it all in!","Emperor Mingxi watched this with a twinge of jealousy and sourness. This old fellow was getting better and better at showing off, but he had to admit, the man had the capital to do so.","If Fuguang had been born into their imperial family, he probably wouldn't have been able to resist starting to expand his empire's territories by now!","Meanwhile, He Jin, who was officially on her first day of work, watched her master interact with His Majesty and the Crown Prince, chatting and laughing merrily with a group of important court officials.","Moreover, everything faintly centered around her. Even the Emperor—if she wasn't mistaken—yielded somewhat to the Junior Preceptor. His tone was familiar, mostly coaxing her.","The heir apparent of Great Yan, His Royal Highness the Crown Prince, had practically become the Junior Preceptor's background prop, constantly following by her side. Although he didn't speak much, anyone could see that his respect for the Junior Preceptor was no less than his respect for the Emperor.","The Crown Prince: Respect for his biological father was just for show, but his respect for the Junior Preceptor was genuine!","He Jin suddenly thought of her father. He had successfully become a retainer under the Junior Preceptor, and she herself had become the Junior Preceptor's guard, holding a proper official rank of the secondary fifth grade from the imperial court.","Her father, who should have returned to the Seven Swords Villa after the matter was settled, was in no rush to go back.","In his words, he needed to do something for his master before he could return with peace of mind.","He Qisha: Silly daughter, although we've managed to cling to the Junior Preceptor's golden thigh, there are so many people around her, and subordinates are divided into close and distant ones.","He had to do more for the Junior Preceptor and increase his weight in her heart before he dared to go back with peace of mind!","\"Second Sister, look, it's Second Brother's contingent!\"","At this moment, the taverns and teahouses along the Heavenly Street of Shangjing were filled with noble madams and young ladies who were rarely seen on ordinary days.","The female members of the Yu family were currently sitting in the Heavenly Street's largest restaurant, the Fortune Full Pavilion, drinking tea while waiting for the army to pass by.","At this time, the third daughter, Yu Ningzi, called out to Yu Ningxuan. The Yu sisters quickly ran to the window, opened it halfway, and looked out. \"Where? Why haven't I seen Second Brother and the others yet?\"","Seeing the sisters crowding around one window, Old Madam Yu suppressed a smile, shook her head, and instructed, \"Be careful, don't fall out!\"","Yu Ningxin, who was slowly becoming a bit more lively, smiled and turned back to Old Madam Yu, saying, \"Don't worry, Grandmother, your granddaughter will help you see if Little Seventh has come.\"","First Madam Yu, nee Zhang, smiled and said to Old Madam Yu, \"Mother, Xin Yatou is visibly much more clever and lively than before.\"","Old Madam Yu also smiled and whispered to her three daughters-in-law, \"This is very good. With their younger sister around, our family's girls cannot learn that petty behavior and lose our Fuguang's face.\"","Even the concubine-born daughters would marry into good families to enjoy blessings in the future, so they had to stand strong on their own.","Old Madam Yu specifically said to Second Madam, nee Wang, \"Your eldest sister-in-law has to manage the household and constantly look after the affairs in Fuguang's courtyard, so she cannot spare the energy. Second daughter-in-law, you should take more care of the children from the third branch, especially the third and fifth girls. Seeing that they have reached the age of marriage, they need to be taught well.\"","The two grandsons of the third branch had their biological father, grandfather, and uncle to watch over them, but the girls were in the inner courtyard. In the past, Madam Sun had let their own concubine mothers raise them.","The concubines themselves were of servant or humble origins; what knowledge did they have to teach their daughters well?","Therefore, the granddaughters still had to be entrusted to the care of the second daughter-in-law, who came from a prestigious family.","The Yu family had hired several teachers to instruct the girls, but when it came to managing a household and handling social relations, the teachers were not necessarily better than the first and second daughters-in-law, who were born into noble families.","\"Grandmother, Mother, it's Second Brother! I see Second Brother!\"","From afar, the female members of the Yu family looked at Yu Boming, who was sitting on a date-red steed, looking incredibly spirited in his full armor. Their eyes couldn't help but reveal excitement and reluctance to part.","Madam Zhang said, \"Second Sister-in-law, Xiao Er looks truly energetic wearing this armor!\"","Madam Wang said modestly, \"This is all thanks to Fuguang. Xiao Er is just benefiting from having a good younger sister!\"","Yu Ningxuan added, \"Eldest Aunt, Mother, Seventh Sister said Second Brother's armor is called Mountain Pattern Armor. The one he is wearing is the second of its kind in Great Yan. Seventh Sister also said that in the future, all the soldiers of Great Yan will gradually be equipped with this kind of armor.\"","Hearing her say Seventh Sister said in every sentence, everyone couldn't help but laugh.","Just then, Yu Boming's horse arrived beneath the restaurant where the Yu family women were. As soon as he entered the main street, he kept looking in this direction because his seventh sister had told him that the women of the family would all come here to see him off.","Who knew that as soon as he got close, he would hear his mother's distinct laughter, as well as that of his aunts...","He was going on a long journey, and they were this happy?","Yu Boming felt very wronged. He wanted to find someone to talk to, but when he turned around, he saw Lin Huaijing, who was dressed in the same attire and following closely behind his horse.","He had to admit that wearing this armor made even the most delicate-looking Lin Huaijing appear somewhat more heroic.","\"A-Jing...\" Lin Huaijing took one look at Yu Boming's overwhelming desire to pour his heart out, then looked up at the Yu family aunts who were smiling brightly at them...","Yue Fuguang only found out later that the Yu family women had smilingly sent off a tearful Yu Boming.","If Zheng Feng, who had already been promoted to Deputy Commander, hadn't suppressed his annoyance and amusement to coax the man away for the sake of Yue Fuguang's face, Yu Boming probably would have become a spectacle during the send-off.","Second Aunt Yu then said, \"Fuguang is right. Next year, we must settle Xiao Er's marriage. If a boy doesn't start a family and take on responsibilities, he will never grow up, no matter how old he gets.\"","Yue Fuguang really wanted to add a sentence: Men remain boys until they die!","Her mother, Madam Zhang, also smiled and said, \"Isn't that so! That's why the eldest's marriage must also be settled quickly. If he keeps delaying his marriage, it will affect the marriages of his younger brothers and sisters.\"","\"Mother, do you already have a candidate in mind for Eldest Sister-in-law?\"","Speaking of this, Madam Zhang's face was full of smiles. She held Yue Fuguang's hand and said, \"Your mother and your aunt came to find you today precisely for this matter.\"","Second Aunt Yu also chimed in, \"Fuguang, what do you think of the Hong family's girl, the one whose boudoir name is Yueling?\"","Hong Yueling? Looking at her mother and Second Aunt's expressions, after all the twists and turns, was Miss Hong really going to become her eldest sister-in-law?","\"Miss Hong? I think she's quite good.\" Yue Fuguang thought for a moment but still couldn't help reminding them, \"Mother, are Eldest Brother and Miss Hong themselves willing?\"","Although this place emphasized the orders of parents and the words of matchmakers, their family now had the conditions to naturally choose a marriage partner that both sides were willing to accept.","Hong Yueling was a girl with her own ideas and thoughts. Although she had many unavoidable circumstances and ultimately had to marry Murong Qian.","But it was still that saying: a forced melon is not sweet. Even if this melon would live a good life later on, if the heart was unhappy, how could the days pass smoothly and satisfactorily?"]},{"number":310,"title":"Chapter 310: They Were All Deceived by the Killer","paragraphs":["Speaking of this, Mrs. Zhang lowered her voice, and Second Aunt Yu also wore a mysterious smile. Yue Fuguang, who was always eager for gossip, instantly smelled drama in the air.","Something was definitely going on!","Mrs. Zhang whispered, \"A few days ago, when your three older brothers were coming home for their end-of-month break, they saved a mother and daughter on the way.\"","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but widen her eyes, looking at Mrs. Zhang with suspicion. It couldn't be such a coincidence!","The Yu family wouldn't have deliberately staged a hero-saving-the-beauty scene just to marry a girl, would they?","But she quickly shook her head. No, they wouldn't go that far!","\"Mother, are the girl and mother that Eldest Brother and the others saved Hong Yueling and Madam Fang?\" Yue Fuguang directly voiced her guess.","Mrs. Zhang nodded. \"Our Fuguang is indeed smart, guessing it right away! We later found out that Lord Hong has been ill recently and hasn't been getting better, so Madam Fang took Miss Hong to the temple to pray for him.","Who knew they would encounter highwaymen on the road? If they hadn't happened to run into your eldest brother and the others passing by on their way home from the academy, and since our family has many guards, that mother and daughter would have probably suffered a terrible fate.\"","[Master, the Hong mother and daughter went to pray because Hong Feng was bewitched by Concubine Mu into sending them. Moreover, other than the carriage driver, they only brought one guard; the rest were all maids and old female servants.","Those highwaymen were also local thugs hired by Concubine Mu.]","'This Hong Feng supposedly angered the Emperor and was despised by him, ordered to reflect on his mistakes behind closed doors. He can't even stay peaceful at home, taking his anger out on his wife and daughter!","And that Concubine Mu, what kind of trouble is she stirring up now?'","[Seeing that the marriage alliance between the Hong and Murong families fell through, Concubine Mu's goal of finding a high-status match for her son was thwarted, so she was naturally angry.","Furthermore, seeing Hong Feng treating that mother and daughter better day by day since he was punished to stay home, she became anxious to get rid of them so they wouldn't be an eyesore to her and her children.","Hong Feng is easily swayed. When Concubine Mu used the excuse of doing it for his own good, saying that the prayers of the legitimate wife and daughter could dispel bad luck and illness, he believed her!","He completely forgot why the Emperor despised him in the first place.]","Yue Fuguang clicked her tongue. Hong Feng had listened to her entire revelation back then; there was no way he didn't know why the Emperor was angry.","To still act as if nothing happened and let his old mother and Concubine Mu manage the household, she had to admit he was really oblivious.","'No wonder Hong Feng is still just a Reader-in-Waiting at the Hanlin Academy. With his lack of tact, he'll probably die of old age in that position.'","[Master, if the Yu family has such in-laws in the future, let alone being a help, they will purely be a burden.]","'Little Zhu, whether they are a burden or not isn't up to them. They can only hold us back if I let them; if I don't, no one can even think about getting close.'","[Master, do you mean to make Hong Yueling lose her father?]","Hearing the words of the divine artifact and looking at their Fuguang's expression...","The two women tightly gripped their silk handkerchiefs. Although they were afraid, they were mostly moved.","Their Fuguang usually looked cold and indifferent, but she was absolutely devoted to her siblings.","What other family was like theirs, where every single older brother and sister had benefited from their younger sister?","Mrs. Zhang and Second Aunt Yu were actually also worried that the Hong family would hold them back in the future. However, they felt the two children were a good match and couldn't make up their minds, which was why they came to ask their precious darling.","In the words of the old master and old madam, the brothers would all have to rely on their sister in the future and be Fuguang's helpers. Whether this bride could be married in or not also depended on their sister's opinion.","Otherwise, what would they do if they brought home a troublemaker? The Yu family already had one Mrs. Sun, and that was enough!","'As an alternative, Hong Feng can either die or leave the capital with his concubine and son. If Eldest Brother and Hong Yueling get engaged, we'll have the Emperor choose a remote place for Hong Feng and send him off to his new post early, so he doesn't stay here and be an eyesore.'","Mrs. Zhang and the other secretly nodded, both feeling this was a good idea. Deep down, they didn't want an irrelevant person to dirty their daughter's hands.","\"Do Mother and Second Aunt mean that because of this incident, Eldest Brother and Miss Hong have taken a liking to each other?\"","If Hong Yueling no longer thought about marrying the Crown Prince, having her as a sister-in-law wouldn't be bad.","\"The day the Hong family sent their thank-you gifts, you were at school and not home. Miss Hong and Madam Fang came over personally.","Looking at the expressions of your eldest brother and Miss Hong at the time, this marriage should work out.\"","As long as the two children were willing, their family only needed to propose; even a royal marriage could be secured.","Having such a precious darling at home gave them that much confidence.","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Since that's the case, I also think Miss Hong is quite nice.\"","Seeing Yue Fuguang agree, Mrs. Zhang smiled and said, \"Then Mother will invite Madam Cai to help propose the marriage tomorrow.\"","Among high-ranking officials in the Great Yan Dynasty, if they truly had their eyes on a family's daughter, to show their respect for her, the proposal wouldn't just involve a matchmaker. They would also find a noble female guest to help propose.","The higher the status of this female guest, the more it demonstrated the groom's family's status and showed their high regard for the bride's side.","\"Is the Madam Cai you mentioned Cai Bing's mother? With Madam Cai helping to propose, nothing should go wrong.\"","The wife of the Minister of Justice certainly had high enough status. Moreover, not only was Madam Cai noble, but she was also straightforward and decisive. She would definitely be able to suppress Hong Feng's mother, who might want to cause trouble in the Hong family, forcing her to bow her head and accept this marriage.","Once the marriage between the two families was settled, Yue Fuguang would send them out of the capital. If they didn't leave, she would send them on their way to the afterlife.","However, as the saying goes, plans cannot keep up with changes. Originally, Mrs. Zhang only invited Madam Cai, but unexpectedly, the news spread very quickly among the ladies.","Before Madam Cai even went to the Hong family, Madam Wei showed up, volunteering to go together with Madam Cai.","How could Mrs. Zhang refuse? She naturally thanked her profusely.","Just as the marriage between the children of the Yu and Hong families reached the stage of exchanging names, two major events occurred in the capital city.","One was the appearance of a low-priced white paper called Snowflake Paper in the Great Yan Bookstore, which was snapped up by scholars as soon as it hit the market.","The other was that the Ninth Prince was assassinated on his way to Baoye Temple to pray. As for whether he died, there were constant rumors among the people, but since the royal family never held a funeral, everyone assumed the Ninth Prince was fine.","After all, he was the Emperor's son; how could he die so easily?","Yue Fuguang looked at Wei Ping, who was reporting this matter. However, throughout the court and the public, aside from a few ministers, most people didn't take this matter too seriously.","[Master, Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and the others were all deceived by the assassins.]","'Little Zhu, do you mean the assassins aren't from the aristocratic families that Wei Ping and the others investigated?'","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers also pricked up their ears. The Fourth Prince and Ninth Prince had encountered 'accidents' multiple times, all starting when news of the papermaking and printing techniques spread.","Originally, the methods used by those hiding in the dark against the two were relatively 'mild', mainly focusing on creating accidental deaths for them.","But ever since cheap and high-quality paper was produced using the new papermaking technique, those people suddenly escalated from staging accidents to direct assassinations on the streets."]},{"number":311,"title":"Chapter 311: Panshan Has Armor","paragraphs":["Actually, Yue Fuguang couldn't quite understand. The things had already been brought out, so what was the use of killing those two people? The paper would still be made, and the books would still be printed.","Why they were so obsessed with this was truly baffling!","[Master, there is indeed the involvement of aristocratic family forces in this assassination, but the operation was not led by them. Half of the assassins were their own raised death squads, while the other half were hired killers they paid for.]","\"Are the Tianxing Pavilion people considered Youtan's? It can't be the Fengyu Pavilion. With Feng Yang captured, Fengyu Pavilion shouldn't be able to make any waves in Dayan for a short time.\"","[Master, it's the people of Panshan, they intervened! Actually, the emergence of the new papermaking and movable type printing techniques had the biggest impact not only on the aristocratic families trying to monopolize the spread of knowledge, but also on Panshan, which attempts to control the courts and dynastic changes of various countries.","The person who acted against Old Nine Xie this time is one of the leaders of the Earth Division of the Panshan organization, codenamed Old Man.","His disguise is that of a dying old man living in the blacksmith workshop in the South City, Langtou Alley. His son, daughter-in-law, and eldest grandson are all his subordinates in the Earth Division.]","\"Are you saying that the people of the aristocratic families are also colluding with Panshan?\"","[They have indeed been in contact for a long time, but the people of the aristocratic families do not know they are from the Panshan organization, because these people have always liked to put on another disguise when doing things.","This is also the reason why, up to now, few people in the Dayan court know the name of Panshan.","But if you tell these lords the once-resounding names of the Iron Hand Gang, the Longevity Sect, the Pingliang Way, and the Blood Blade Hall, they have definitely heard of them all.]","\"Little Zhu, do you mean these organizations were all Panshan's shell... disguises.\"","Yue Fuguang changed her words in time, almost blurting out the term shell company from her hometown.","And Emperor Mingxi and his ministers all gasped when they heard the names of these organizations.","The Iron Hand Gang was once very popular in Western Qiang, while the Longevity Sect once made a great name in Southern Yue. It was said that the death of Gan Sheng's father, the old Emperor Gan Chengjiang, was related to this Longevity Sect that operated under the guise of seeking immortality.","The Blood Blade Hall was in Northern Li, and the Pingliang Way just happened to rise in their Dayan, only it was pacified a few years ago because it manipulated the common people to rebel.","They didn't expect the enemy to be a centipede that dies hard; they had only chopped off an insignificant claw!","The main body was unharmed. In fact, if it weren't for the Junior Preceptor, they would still not know the name Panshan!","[Yes, these are all one of Panshan's organizations in various countries. And the one that assassinated Old Nine Xie this time is one of Panshan's new disguises after the annihilation of the Pingliang Way, the Phantom Assassination Hall.]","\"Phantom Assassination Hall? An assassin organization? Why haven't I heard Wei Ping and the others mention it? It seems that no one from this organization participated in the assassinations aimed at me.\"","[Master, that's because some assassins have two or three identities. For example, an assassin from Fengyu Pavilion might be a temporary worker for Fengyu Pavilion, and their social identity could be from all walks of life.","So why couldn't they be Panshan's people sneaking in?","Even in the most strictly organized Youtan, there are quite a few of Panshan's people. So sometimes when Panshan wants to get rid of someone, they don't need to act under their own name at all. As long as they pay, their own people in these assassin organizations can do their bidding under someone else's banner.","Master, look at these civil and military officials in the court, the ones who will die at the hands of the so-called Fengyu Pavilion, Tianxing Pavilion, and Youtan in the future.","In fact, most of the buyers are Panshan. The ways they die are also varied; some are poisoned like the royal father and son, some die from accidental falls, some drink themselves to death, and some are stabbed to death by street thugs in broad daylight...]","\"These ways of dying are not very decent!\" Yue Fuguang seemed to glance over casually, but everyone her eyes swept across felt their bodies tighten and a chill down their backs. The weather, which was originally a bit hot, instantly became bone-chilling.","This sudden alternation of cold and hot made people sweat easily. Some people silently lowered their heads and wiped the cold sweat from their foreheads. These two ancestors were truly too terrifying.","Eating melons and gossiping is one thing, but why do they always bring up their death states?","And being like the royal father and son, is that very glorious?","The royal father and son duo were already numb to the point of speechlessness.","Even Emperor Mingxi, who had been a bit full of himself lately, settled down after being openly and secretly beaten down by the two ancestors.","Dayan hadn't taken off yet, the external enemies were still strong, and after clearing out some internal enemies, even more were discovered. The pressure kept him from getting carried away!","[Master, the Ninth Prince is severely injured and going to die. Will Master save him?]","\"I won't save him. I'm more curious about what Northern Li will do after losing the Ninth Prince as a chess piece. And the forces that Bei Ye and Bei Yue left beside the Ninth Prince.","Because of this assassination, most of them are gone. If Northern Li finds out that it was done by the alliance of Panshan and the Dayan aristocratic families, I wonder how they will retaliate?\"","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers exchanged a subtle glance. Rest assured, Gan Sheng and Bei Ji would soon know the mastermind behind the assassination of the prince in the Dayan dynasty.","[Master, what do you think the emperors would do if they knew that the Blood Blade Hall, Longevity Way, and Iron Hand Gang in their own countries were all tentacles of this mysterious Panshan?]","What would they do? Emperor Mingxi and his ministers could tell you: they would exterminate them at all costs. How can one allow others to snore beside one's bed?","Even an emperor would be wary of such a powerful organization, which is why he ordered two forces, one open and one secret, to investigate this organization.","Emperor Mingxi curled his lips into a smile. Dayan couldn't be the only one doing the work; his peers should also make a move and give this Panshan some trouble.","Before Emperor Mingxi's smile could climb from the corners of his mouth to the tips of his eyes, he was interrupted by an urgent voice.","It was the time for the morning court assembly. Who was so unafraid of death to interrupt the emperor and ministers discussing official business at this time?","\"Your Majesty, bad news, Your Majesty... Your Majesty, the Fourth Prince... the Fourth Prince was assassinated, and the Ninth Prince... the Ninth Prince has passed away!\"","An eunuch stumbled and crawled into the main hall, kneeling down to report the mourning as soon as he entered.","Many people frowned, secretly thinking it was bad luck!","\"What did you say! Little Nine is gone?\" Emperor Mingxi suddenly stood up, his face instantly hanging with an expression of absolute grief and disbelief.","Only Yue Fuguang, who was closest to him, saw that the heart-wrenching sorrow did not reach his eyes, and even the tears in the corners of his eyes were forced out by him blinking hard.","If Emperor Mingxi had lost all father-son affection for the Ninth Prince because of his status as an illegitimate child born of adultery.","Then recently, the Ninth Prince's frequent contact with people from Northern Li had completely disappointed Emperor Mingxi, and made it clearer to him why he was able to kill his brother and then murder his father in the original timeline. Everything had a trace to follow.","This time, saying he went to Baoye Temple to pray for his biological mother was just an excuse. He was just trying to rendezvous with important figures from Northern Li, which gave the assassins the opportunity to kill him.","Emperor Mingxi's performance continued. He staggered two steps and was quickly supported by Eunuch Qian so he wouldn't fall. \"Also, what did you just say, Old Four was assassinated?\"","Emperor Mingxi pointed at the eunuch who was still kowtowing and begging for forgiveness, and sternly said, \"Speak, who did it? Is Old Four alright?\"","The eunuch's face was covered in tears, and he stammered, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, the Fourth Prince, he... he is severely injured... unconscious.\"","\"What!\"","\"What?\"","Of the two exclamations of \"What?\", one came from Emperor Mingxi, the biological father of the Fourth Prince.","And the other came from the Deputy Censor-in-Chief, Zhang Tingji."]},{"number":312,"title":"Chapter 312: The Strange Poison 'Red Spider Lily'","paragraphs":["\"System, the emperor is acting way too slowly. It is one thing that he has not reeled in the net on the Sima family, but how can he let the Zhang family jump around until now? Zhang Tingji is just a Deputy Censor-in-Chief. Could he not find any excuse to strip him of his position?\"","[Host, it will be soon. The Zhang family has in-laws everywhere. To avoid leaving any future troubles, and to neither kill an innocent nor let a guilty one go, the emperor must distinguish everything clearly before making a move.]","It was estimated that a batch of capital officials would soon be dismissed or demoted out of the capital, perfectly making room for the new imperial scholars next year.","\"Little Zhu, why is this Zhang Tingji so agitated? Does the Fourth Prince have some connection with him?\"","At this time, Emperor Mingxi, supported by the Crown Prince, had already walked to the center of the hall. He said to the civil and military officials standing on both sides, \"The court session is suspended.\"","He then turned to Yue Fuguang and said, \"Fuguang, come with me to see Old Four and Old Nine.\"","He had not finished enjoying this gossip yet. He also wanted to know what connection Zhang Tingji had with Old Four, or rather, the Southern Yue behind him.","\"Your Majesty, the situation is unclear. It would be safer for us to accompany and protect you,\" Lord Feng Tang and a few other officials with martial arts skills stepped forward and requested.","Huo Ying bowed. \"Indeed, Your Majesty. The rebels are rampant, and we are willing to attend by Your Majesty's side.\"","Yue Fuguang: If you guys reined in those expressions of wanting to continue gossiping, I might actually believe your loyalty to the monarch!","Emperor Mingxi pondered briefly and nodded in agreement. \"Let us go see Old Four first!\"","The Ninth Prince was already dead; seeing him a little earlier or later made no difference.","But Fourth Master Xie was injured after all, his life or death uncertain. Furthermore, he was his biological son. Even though he hated Concubine Xin and the Southern Yue behind her.","He did not have much affection for this son, whom the two ancestors called a menace, but he was his own flesh and blood after all. At this moment, even if just to put on a show for Southern Yue, he had to go see Old Four first.","[Host, the eighteen hundred points for the Ninth Prince have been credited to our account. The Fourth Prince is definitely not dead yet; his point contribution is still zero.]","The person and the system did not even need to consume system energy now; just looking at the point income told them who was dead and who was still alive.","\"System, never mind the points for now. Please continue your performance.\"","[Master, the Zhang family favored the Fourth Prince early on and planned to send a daughter to be his secondary consort. After some discussion, the Zhang family chose Zhang Tingji's youngest daughter.","This is the normal reaction of a future father-in-law learning that his future son-in-law has been assassinated.","A son-in-law is half a son. Although the marriage has not been finalized, this Zhang Tingji has already adopted the role of a father-in-law, so of course he is as agitated as a biological father!]","\"If this Fourth Master Xie dies early, would not this young lady of the Zhang family dodge a bullet?\"","[Master, actually in the original timeline, Fourth Master Xie was also assassinated. That time, he was not only severely injured but also poisoned.","This Zhang Tingji gave Emperor Mingxi the idea of arranging a marriage to ward off bad luck, and volunteered, recommending his own daughter with a face full of loyalty to the sovereign.","It was just that because it was a marriage to ward off bad luck and the Fourth Prince's survival was uncertain, he temporarily changed the candidate from his youngest legitimate daughter to his third concubine-born daughter of a similar age.","However, according to the timeline, this should have happened three years later, and the ones who made the move were still the Ninth Prince's people.]","\"Are you saying that this Zhang Tingji is very likely to propose a marriage to ward off bad luck again this time?\"","[Yes, for the sake of power, he is very likely to sacrifice that third concubine-born daughter again. Master, will you save this Fourth Prince later?]","\"Little Zhu, everyone knows he is a menace. The only reason I have not personally eliminated this threat is that I do not want to dirty my own hands. To ask me to actively save him, that is impossible!\"","[What if the emperor, unaware of the truth, asks you for medicine?]","Emperor Mingxi's heart stirred; he also really wanted to know if the Junior Preceptor would give it.","\"Then I will definitely give it!\"","[Why?]","Emperor Mingxi and his officials had the same question in their hearts.","The Junior Preceptor was not someone easy to talk to. If she really did not want to, even their Majesty could not force her the slightest bit.","She had just said she would not save him, but now she said she would give the medicine if His Majesty asked. What was her plan?","Emperor Mingxi also wanted to know what Yue Fuguang was thinking. For some reason, he always felt that what followed would not be anything good!","It could only be said that Emperor Mingxi understood Yue Fuguang's temper too well. Just as he thought this, he heard by his ear, \"Why else? If the emperor asks for medicine, it only means that Fourth Master Xie is not fated to die. If Heaven wants to destroy his Great Yan Dynasty, I will naturally help make it happen!\"","Emperor Mingxi's face darkened. Since when did you give the Heavenly Dao so much face? It wants to destroy Great Yan and you just go along with it?","Why did he find that so hard to believe!","[Master, Fourth Master Xie's destructive power is indeed great, but it is not enough to truly destroy Great Yan; that was the result of efforts from multiple parties!]","The result of efforts from multiple parties? Xie Zhiyan, who was supporting the emperor, twitched the corner of his mouth. The divine artifact, having studied for so long, still used such dramatic wording!","Emperor Mingxi: Then do you two dare to list the names of all those parties who made the effort? He guaranteed he would beat them all to death, leaving not a single one alive!","\"But since Fourth Master Xie did not die after being severely injured by an assassination in the original timeline, maybe he will not die this time even without us saving him.\"","[Master, the swords used to assassinate Fourth Master Xie were all coated with deadly poison, so he is not only injured but also poisoned.]","\"Poisoned? Isn't that the area of expertise of his biological mother Concubine Xin and his grandmaster Yue Ying? How could a grand-disciple of Du Zhongxian die from poisoning?\"","Emperor Mingxi and his officials also felt that in this imperial palace, other than the Crown Prince and his wife who had been bestowed medicine by the Junior Preceptor, Fourth Master Xie was the only one who didn't fear being poisoned.","For someone who manufactured poisons long-term, who wouldn't have some antidotes on them?","[Master, this time is different. The poison Fourth Master Xie was afflicted with is Spider Lily, a rare new poison recently developed by Li Sanming. Just hearing the name, you know that those who are poisoned by it will most likely have to take a trip to the banks of the River of Forgetfulness.]","\"Li Sanming's latest work? Who is so capable as to use the Poison King's medicine on Fourth Master Xie right after it was produced?\"","[It was done by the Tianxing Pavilion. The mastermind behind it is naturally Northern Li.]","\"Why did Northern Li suddenly target Fourth Master Xie? Firstly, he is not favored, and secondly, he has no real power. Moreover, he is still being assassinated by the noble families. The people of Northern Li could completely sit on the mountain and watch the tigers fight, reaping the spoils without lifting a finger.\"","[It is precisely because of these recent assassinations that the people staying by the Ninth Prince's side saw clearly the Fourth Prince's strength. They also figured out the fact that he, just like the Ninth Prince, is a pawn of Southern Yue, except that compared to the Ninth Prince, he is the Emperor's biological son.","The Tianxing Pavilion's poisoning of the Fourth Prince this time was also carried out by blending into the attacks of the noble family alliance.","Even if the Emperor investigates, he won't trace it back to them.]","\"Is Northern Li in such a hurry to get rid of Fourth Master Xie because his role clashes with the Ninth Prince's?","Why is it that the people of Northern Li have figured out Fourth Master Xie's background, yet the Emperor still seems completely oblivious?\"","[Because he's stupid?]","Emperor Mingxi was almost pushed over the edge by the word stupid. He didn't even need to pretend to be sad anymore; his steps genuinely staggered as he walked.","\"Imperial Father, Fourth Brother will be fine. Please don't worry too much!\"","The Crown Prince supported Emperor Mingxi, offering a timely reminder that sounded like a comforting remark."]},{"number":313,"title":"Chapter 313: Then let him die","paragraphs":["[Concubine Xin's attempt to secretly harm the Crown Princess of the Eastern Palace was also witnessed by the people of Northern Li, who naturally learned of Southern Yue's ambitions.","The Empress and the Emperor could not find out who the mastermind was, also because Northern Li followed behind the Southern Yue people to clean up the traces for her.","At that time, although they also wanted to kill Fourth Master Xie, in comparison, it would be even better if they could take the lives of the Crown Prince and his wife first.]","\"Aren't the Southern Yue people overthinking this? Old Nine Xie is obviously not as favored as before. Even without the Crown Prince and Fourth Master Xie, he still has several older brothers above him. It wouldn't be his turn anyway.\"","[Master, as long as the ones in front are all dead, won't it be his turn!]","The ones in front are all dead! Emperor Mingxi's eyes turned red when he heard this. Up until now, even counting the ones still in his concubines' wombs, he only had thirteen sons.","Gan Sheng! How vicious, wanting the lives of all his sons just for a fake!","[Besides, counting Fourth Master Xie and that new emperor, the three of them combined almost achieved the accomplishment of wiping out their entire family!]","Cough, cough! Cough, cough!","Emperor Mingxi could no longer bear it and started coughing violently!","\"Imperial Father, are you alright?\"","Xie Zhiyan asked with concern while rubbing the Emperor's back to soothe his breath, \"Imperial Father, how about taking a palanquin over?\"","Emperor Mingxi waved his hand weakly. \"I will walk there myself!\"","His heart was filled with intense hatred right now. He was afraid that if he went over and saw that Fourth Master Xie was not dead, he would not be able to resist strangling him to death with his own hands.","\"Has an imperial physician been summoned for the fourth prince?\" he asked the eunuch leading the way.","The eunuch was one of Concubine Xin's own people, personally chosen for her son. He was very anxious at the moment, secretly hoping the Emperor would walk faster.","Who knew that the Emperor seemed too heartbroken and was walking slower and slower, and now even stopped to ask him about summoning the imperial physician.","The eunuch immediately replied, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, after the incident occurred, this servant already ordered someone to invite Imperial Physician Sun. By now, the physician has likely arrived.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded and continued to walk, seemingly anxious but actually taking his time.","\"Indeed, the Emperor's children all died quite tragically, and his lineage almost died out completely. We've only seen a situation like his once in thousands of years.\"","The color slowly drained from Emperor Mingxi's face, his teeth grinding audibly. His heart was indescribably bitter, and the sorrowful look on his face became a bit more genuine.","[Host, if we keep talking, won't the Emperor die from anger?]","\"No, it will hurt his body at most, he won't die!\"","[Host, your desire for revenge is too strong. It's been two months, and you still want to get back at him.]","\"System, I told you, I am a petty person who seeks revenge for the smallest grievance. The Emperor has been a bit arrogant lately. If I don't knock some sense into him a few more times to make him see reality, I'm really afraid that one day we will have to replace him with someone else on the throne.","Even if the succession of the throne is peaceful, it will somewhat affect our plans.","Besides, I am only attacking him verbally at most, not striking him with lightning. I'm already giving him a lot of face!\"","The group, no matter how slowly they walked, soon arrived at Xie Zhiwei's Nanping Palace.","\"Fourth, how is my fourth son?\" Emperor Mingxi put on an act like a drama king as soon as he entered the door.","His face was full of worry, and the heart of a loving father was written all over his face, but it did not reach his eyes.","Yue Fuguang even added a line for him in her mind: 'Fourth, how is my fourth son, is he dead yet?'","\"Your Majesty, the Fourth Prince has suffered severe injuries and has been poisoned with a highly toxic substance. We officials are currently trying to find a way to detoxify His Highness.\"","Sun Huajing truthfully reported the Fourth Prince's condition to Emperor Mingxi. He was also not very sure what their Emperor was thinking right now.","As imperial physicians, they naturally tried their best to treat him, but he and several colleagues had examined the poison in the Fourth Prince, and they simply could not determine what kind of poison it was, let alone how to cure it.","In the Fourth Prince's current situation, the injury was a minor matter; the poison was the fatal point. Right now, even Daoist Master Xuanmingzi was helpless for the time being. In the entire Great Yan, the only person who could save the Fourth Prince's life was the Junior Preceptor.","Sun Huajing subtly glanced at Yue Fuguang, who was sitting to the side drinking tea, and then carefully peeked at Emperor Mingxi's expression.","Seeing that neither of these two spoke, he formed a guess in his heart.","Next, Xuanmingzi and the imperial physicians tried together to help the Fourth Prince detoxify, but unfortunately, his breathing inevitably grew weaker and weaker.","Sun Huajing came to report again, \"Your Majesty, the Fourth Prince is in critical condition. We officials are incompetent; we cannot cure this poison!\"","Emperor Mingxi seemingly waved his hand in sorrowful helplessness. \"Just do your best to treat him. No matter what method you use, even if it just delays the inevitable for a moment, it is fine.","If you need precious medicinal herbs, go and open my private treasury.\"","Yue Fuguang, who had seen what was in the Emperor's private treasury, secretly thought: Your private treasury is full of highly potent tonic items. Are you sure you're not trying to send Fourth Master Xie on his way faster!","Sun Huajing received the order, and this time he was certain that His Majesty truly intended to give up on the Fourth Prince!","Yue Fuguang grew bored waiting and started gossiping with the system again.","\"Little Zhu, the Fourth Prince is about to die, why haven't we seen Concubine Xin and Yue Ying?","Her son is dying. No matter how much this Concubine Xin pretends to be aloof from worldly affairs, she should have shown up by now, right?\"","Emperor Mingxi and the others had also noticed something was wrong early on. As his biological mother, even if Concubine Xin usually deliberately acted indifferent and uncaring towards the Fourth Prince,","She should have come to see him at this time; otherwise, she wouldn't be able to pass the Emperor's scrutiny.","[Master, in the battle just now, Yue Ying was injured to his last breath while trying to save the Fourth Prince and his own son.","Concubine Xin is currently dragging the dying Yue Ying around in her own palace to develop an antidote to save the Fourth Prince, so of course the two of them cannot come.]","\"Based on your assessment, can she develop the antidote before Fourth Master Xie breathes his last?\"","Hearing this, Emperor Mingxi somewhat regretted telling Sun Huajing and the others to delay for time.","[In the original timeline, Fourth Master Xie was also poisoned when he was assassinated, but the poison used that time was not the new one developed by Li Sanming, and they actually managed to drag it out until Concubine Xin formulated the antidote.","But this time, apart from you, Master, no one can save him.]","\"Then let him die!\"","Not having to do it herself, just standing by and watching was enough to send away such a menace. How wonderful!","Emperor Mingxi and his subjects also secretly breathed a sigh of relief. After all, it was his biological son. Emperor Mingxi thought about it and still planned to go in and see him one last time.","Just then, a large group of people suddenly arrived outside the hall, led by the Empress, followed by a crowd of concubines, princes, and princesses.","Yue Fuguang had felt that something was missing earlier, and it turned out that it wasn't just Concubine Xin and Yue Ying who were missing.","There were also the concubines, princes, and princesses who were supposed to appear at this time to display the royal family's affection, which was thinner than paper.","Seeing Emperor Mingxi, who had just stood up, the crowd gathered around, asking about the Fourth Prince's condition all at once.","A few concubines had already started wiping their tears with their handkerchiefs.","Yue Fuguang widened her eyes, watching their smooth performances, and secretly marveled in her heart. No wonder the Emperor liked to run to the inner harem.","These beautiful women, like spring flowers and autumn moons, each had their own beauty. Even when they cried, they looked like pear blossoms bathed in rain or spring leaves bearing dew. They truly inspired pity, and look, the Emperor was already comforting them with an aching heart.","[Master, why are these ladies crying as if their own children are dying? And the Emperor, hugging and cuddling right in front of the Empress and you, isn't he afraid of dirtying your eyes?]"]},{"number":314,"title":"Chapter 314: Aren't you afraid of being killed in your sleep at night","paragraphs":["\"Little Zhu, how do you know she's shedding tears of sorrow and not tears of excitement?\"","Emperor Mingxi's hand, which had reached out to gently pat his beloved concubine's back, suddenly froze. The weeping beauty before him had tears brimming in her eyes, threatening to fall.","\"Your Majesty, what happened today terrified me and the Eighth Highness to death.\"","Following the words of the Eighth Prince's biological mother, Concubine Qing, the slightly pale-faced Eighth Prince, Xie Zhilian, nodded in cooperation. His chubby little hands tugged at Emperor Mingxi's sleeve, his face full of attachment and adoration.","\"Father Emperor, I saw the assassins who attacked Fourth Brother. They were so scary!\"","Yue Fuguang cast a complicated look at Xie Zhilian. She didn't want to comment much on this Eighth Prince with his complex personality right now.","However, Seventh Brother Xie and the Eighth Princess standing next to him kept looking into the hall, clearly genuinely concerned about the Fourth Prince's condition.","Emperor Mingxi's mood visibly improved as he looked at the circle of children. He said, \"Rest assured, my children, your Fourth Brother will be fine.\"","Who knew that as soon as Emperor Mingxi's words fell, a slap to the face would arrive.","A young eunuch was seen running out of the inner hall in a panic. Upon seeing the Emperor, he cried out mournfully, \"Your Majesty, Your Majesty! Imperial Physician Sun says the Fourth Prince... the Fourth Prince is not going to make it!\"","Hearing that the Fourth Prince was dying, the expressions of the people in the hall varied. The only constant was Yue Fuguang, who was still nibbling on the pastries Eunuch Qian had specially prepared for her.","It was already mealtime, and seeing that they wouldn't be able to leave anytime soon, she had to quickly fill her stomach.","\"System, when will you stop consuming my energy?\"","[Host, that will have to wait until the system is fully recovered or we unbind.]","The system had no choice either. Its operation inherently consumed a bit of the host's energy. Furthermore, with two systems running, both upgraded to level four, wouldn't it drain the host even more!","Pastries like these could only trick the mouth; they could no longer satisfy Yue Fuguang's energy consumption.","Yue Fuguang secretly popped a Fasting Pill into her mouth. The longan-sized pill did not taste as good as it looked.","She couldn't help but complain inwardly: Do the pill cultivators in the cultivation world not eat these things themselves? They only care about efficacy; has no one ever thought of improving the taste?","Watching Emperor Mingxi and his group taking the lead to walk inside, Yue Fuguang remained seated.","Seeing that Yue Fuguang didn't go in, Feng Tang and the others also stopped in their tracks.","Seeing Feng Tang, Yue Fuguang suddenly remembered her young study companion and asked, \"Lord Feng, is Feng Xiu's health better?\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang ask about his second son, the corners of Feng Tang's mouth had just curled into a smile when he thought of the situation inside right now. He immediately put on a serious face and replied in a low voice, \"Thank you for your concern, Junior Preceptor. That boy ate the pastries you sent, and in his joy, he fully recovered in less than two days. He will be able to attend school tomorrow.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"It wouldn't hurt to let him rest for a couple more days. Wu Yunmiao and the others have taken notes for him, so his studies won't be delayed.\"","Wu Yong also chimed in, \"The Junior Preceptor is right. My Little Four and Miss Bao take an extra set of notes for Brother Xiu every day. Lord Feng doesn't need to worry about his coursework.\"","[Master, in the original timeline, it seems Feng Xiu didn't survive this illness and passed away.]","\"Of my three newly added study companions, two died in childhood, and one didn't even live past twenty. Adding my two older sisters, the five of them combined didn't even live to be a hundred years old!\"","Feng Tang and Wu Yong exchanged a glance. One as a father and the other as an older brother, they felt both sorrow and relief in their hearts.","Regardless of what the original fate was, with the appearance of the Junior Preceptor in this life, whether it was the Great Yan dynasty or their personal destinies, things were bound to be different!","\"Little Zhu, help me find some prescriptions for treating cold ailments that can be made here, like Cinnamon Twig Decoction, Ephedra Decoction, and Schizonepeta and Saposhnikovia Toxin-Defeating Powder.\"","Sun Huajing, who had just walked out from inside, heard these medicine names head-on. Cinnamon Twig Decoction... does it contain cinnamon?","Currently, cinnamon was only used as a spice; no physician had yet used it as a medicinal herb.","Sun Huajing then thought of the latter two medicine names and couldn't help but speculate on the ingredients of the prescriptions. To treat a cold, schizonepeta, saposhnikovia, and angelica root must surely be included...","Seeing him lost in thought, Wei Ping and the others couldn't help but ask, \"Imperial Physician Sun, how are things inside?\"","Wei Ping's words interrupted his train of thought. Catching sight of Yue Fuguang, who was also looking at him, Sun Huajing immediately gathered his wits and bowed to Yue Fuguang and the others. \"Junior Preceptor, My Lords, the Fourth Prince's condition is not optimistic.\"","The implication was that he wouldn't make it past today.","As soon as his words fell, Emperor Mingxi walked out with a group of people, looking grief-stricken.","His eyes were red, and a teardrop still hung at the corner of his eye.","Looking as if he were overly heartbroken but forcing himself to hold on, he said, \"Imperial Physician Sun, you all keep a close watch on the Fourth Prince.\"","He turned to Yue Fuguang and the others and said, \"Fuguang, come with Us to see Little Nine.\"","To see if he was really dead.","After the incident where the Prince of Qi substituted one thing for another, he could never be completely at ease.","The group had not walked far from the main hall when they heard the hall doors behind them suddenly close.","Yue Fuguang, along with the others, couldn't help but turn around to look. Who was so bold? The Emperor had just stepped out, and someone couldn't wait to shut the doors. What was the meaning of this?","These weren't the palace gates that needed to be shut tight. With the current lighting conditions, even if a few windows in the hall used glass, shutting the doors would make it dark inside!","Just as these thoughts arose, Yue Fuguang heard the system's notification sound in her ear: [Master, there are assassins!]","At the same time, the defensive shield around her instantly activated.","Meanwhile, over twenty assassins dressed as eunuchs and court ladies suddenly charged at them from all directions.","Their eyes were fierce and full of hatred, showing a readiness to fight to the death. Rather than assassins, they were more like death squads.","\"Protect His Majesty!\" Xie Zhiyan shouted, drawing the sword from his waist and blocking the front of the Emperor and Empress.","At this moment, he even found the time to glance at Yue Fuguang standing beside him. He took another step forward, positioning himself perfectly to shield her, the Emperor, and the Empress.","By now, the crowd had reacted, and the guards surrounded Emperor Mingxi in the center.","The concubines, princes, and princesses were also tightly encircled by the guards. Because there were too many people to protect, there were too few left to fight the assassins.","Feng Tang, Wei Ping, and the others exchanged glances and faced the armed assassins barehanded.","They had only used protecting the Emperor as an excuse; who knew it would actually come true!","Who was the jinx that brought it up first?","[Is the Emperor competent or not? With so many people harboring disloyal intentions on his own turf, he actually didn't know!","Isn't he afraid of being slaughtered in his sleep in the middle of the night!]","Emperor Mingxi, surrounded in the middle, also felt wronged. To lure out all the hidden fish, he had refrained from taking action against some people.","He even used himself as bait. Unfortunately, despite all his calculations, he didn't anticipate that they would strike in the Pingnan Palace.","At this moment, most of his guards were outside the palace gates.","Looking at the bolted gates, the crowd exchanged glances, and the protective circle slowly pushed outward."]},{"number":315,"title":"Chapter 315: The First Gunshot","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang looked at the blue-gleaming blades and called out a warning, \"Everyone be careful, their swords and sabers are poisoned!\"","Although she could cure the poison, wasn't there a dying Fourth Master Xie lying inside? When the time came, should she save them or not?","Moreover, she felt that this assassination attempt in broad daylight was a bit strange.","'System, could they be doing this on purpose? Just to get these people injured and poisoned, and then force me to hand over the antidote?'","How did these people know she had the antidote anyway?","[Host, your guess is completely correct, let's expose her!]","[Master, be careful, they are coming for your antidote!]","'What? Little Zhu, do you mean these assassins know I have the antidote to save Fourth Master Xie? So these assassins are from Nanyue?'","[Yes, they somehow learned that you have a medicine that cures a hundred poisons. The assassination was also an idea Yue Ying gave to Concubine Xin before his death. To take you hostage, or hurt the people here, to force you to hand over the antidote.]","'These mortals are really courting death!'","The crowd could hear the impatience and murderous intent in the Junior Preceptor's words. Emperor Mingxi and the Crown Prince cast a hasty glance at her.","They saw her face covered in frost. 'No one can force me to do what I don't want to do!'","\"Lord Yu, be careful!\" Just then, an assassin suddenly appeared behind Yu Shuchun, who was charging at the very front closest to the main doors. Three of them completely surrounded Yu Shuchun in the middle.","It could be seen that in the arena, aside from Yue Fuguang, Emperor Mingxi, and the Crown Prince, the one being besieged the most was Yue Fuguang's biological second uncle, Yu Shuchun.","Seeing that a man's blade was about to hack into Yu Shuchun's back, Yue Fuguang instantly took out a handgun from her storage ring.","The moment the cool, highly futuristic interstellar handgun appeared in her hand, she didn't even need to aim before firing instantly.","With a whoosh, a beam of light laced with lightning shot out.","Pfft!","The light beam struck the hand of the assassin raising the scimitar.","Ah! My hand!","Along with the splattering blood came the assassin's shrill scream and the dumbfounded reactions of his two companions.","Hearing the miserable shriek of the person behind him, Yu Shuchun turned around, and seeing Yue Fuguang holding the gun, he instantly felt relieved.","He didn't care what kind of weapon his niece was holding; anyway, it wouldn't hurt him no matter what.","Yue Fuguang only paused for a second. After confirming that the gun in her hand truly had no recoil and the sound was very light, she quickly overcame her fear of firing a gun for the first time, especially at living people.","She quickly turned the muzzle. Whoosh, whoosh, whoosh, whoosh, whoosh, whoosh! Blood splattered everywhere.","She fired over ten shots in a row, taking down one assassin with each shot, all hitting their legs. Between the pain and the fear, these people lost their ability and courage to continue fighting the moment they were shot.","Some assassins refused to believe it and tried to use the steel swords in their hands to block the light beam bullets like they would arrows. As a result, the beam of light easily passed through the blade, ravaging his body without any decrease in power.","The remaining dozen or so assassins who hadn't been shot looked at their bloody, mangled companions who even smelled slightly charred. The last bit of fire in their hearts to fight to the death was extinguished.","With absolute submission, they clattered and clanked as they threw their weapons far away.","Resolutely drawing a clear line between themselves and those weapons!","It was too tragic, truly too tragic. They could accept being stabbed to death with a sword or hacked to death with a saber, but they could not endure being silently hit by this unknown weapon—not dying, but suffering pain worse than death.","Facing Yue Fuguang's dark muzzle, these people didn't even have the courage to bite down on their poison sacs.","The crowd looked at Yue Fuguang, whose face was currently as cold as frost and whose expression was stern, like a god of death. They all widened their eyes and could not help but swallow their saliva unconsciously.","One by one, they stood frozen in place, not daring to move. They simply didn't dare to move!","Even the assassins rolling on the ground clutching their painful legs could not snap the crowd out of being scared silly by this sudden turn of events.","Yu Shuchun, however, ignored the wailing assassins and his dumbfounded colleagues. He quickly ran in front of Yue Fuguang and asked with a face full of worry, \"Fuguang, are you alright? Are you tired?\"","Are you tired? Not to mention the others, even the assassins lying on the ground had a momentary pause in their crying when they heard this!","Is this something a human would say?","Taking down so many of them in just a dozen breaths of time, how tired could she be?","Yue Fuguang put away the gun and replied, \"Second Uncle, I'm fine!\" Originally, when putting the gun away, she had wanted to blow on the muzzle to act cool.","But seeing the circle of people staring at her with burning gazes, she realized these bumpkins wouldn't understand the coolness of her blowing on the gun anyway, so she ultimately decided to forget it!","System: Are you sure it's not because this gun doesn't have the smell of gunpowder, so it's not suitable for acting cool!","\"It's good that you're fine, it's good that you're fine.\" Seeing the tense atmosphere around them, he couldn't help but say, \"If you lost a single hair today, your grandfather and father would definitely give your second uncle a mixed double beating when we get back!\"","Hearing him say this, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but laugh, \"I'll plead for mercy for Second Uncle when the time comes.\"","With this smile of hers, it was like the melting of ice and snow and the return of spring to the earth. The people around them also couldn't help but breathe a sigh of relief.","They were still more familiar with the current Junior Preceptor; the one just now was truly too terrifying!","The crowd silently looked toward their Emperor. The responsibility of maintaining the Junior Preceptor's mood was something their Emperor should shoulder.","\"That's great then. With Fuguang here, Second Uncle will definitely be spared from this beating.\"","Yu Shuchun's words held a hidden meaning, and everyone present naturally heard the implication.","It was Xie Zhiyan who broke the silence first. He said, \"Imperial Father, Imperial Mother, the younger brothers and sisters are all terrified. Let us leave this place first with the Junior Preceptor and the lords.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded and ordered the commander of the guards, who had finally broken through the palace doors and rushed in, \"Escort all these people into the Heavenly Prison. Do not let them die!\"","He then turned around and glanced at the tightly shut doors of the hall, his eyes filled with undisguised, fierce murderous intent. \"Escort the Fourth Prince and all the eunuchs and maids in the Xinrong Hall into the grand prison.","Without my orders, not a single one is allowed to be let go!\"","The commander of the guards received the order and left. After all the serving personnel were arrested, as for what would happen to the Fourth Prince and Concubine Xin, that was not something a commander like him needed to worry about.","The rule for staying alive in this imperial palace was to act according to orders and absolutely not ask too many questions.","The crowd exited the Pingnan Palace. The Empress led the concubines, princes, and princesses away, all looking lost in spirit. It was estimated that Imperial Physician Sun and the others would be extremely busy today.","The Emperor also took a group of ministers to his own Hall of Mental Cultivation.","After taking a sip of tea, Yue Fuguang asked with an indifferent expression, \"Does Your Majesty not have anything you want to ask me?\"","[Master, the Emperor wouldn't want to take your laser handgun for himself after seeing how powerful it is, would he?]","'What is there to fear? He is a mortal; even if he takes it, he won't be able to use it.'","Mortals couldn't use it even if they took it? Emperor Mingxi couldn't describe the taste in his heart.","He was both glad that such a powerful weapon couldn't be used by just anyone, and disappointed that this also included himself!","No matter how great his disappointment was, Emperor Mingxi quickly collected his emotions. He looked at Yue Fuguang with a face full of affection and asked with timely curiosity, \"Fuguang, I do indeed want to ask you, that... thing from just now, is it a hidden weapon?","Why do I feel that its power is several times greater than the repeating crossbow you gave the Crown Prince?\"","Zhou Qi'an, who had already entered the Ministry of Works, had produced the repeating crossbow and the siege ballista based on the blueprints provided by Yue Fuguang, and their power was indeed quite good."]},{"number":316,"title":"Chapter 316: Anomaly of Mars, Venus Visible in Daylight","paragraphs":["But compared to the laser gun in Fu Guang's hand, the repeating crossbow was still far inferior.","The more Emperor Mingxi thought about it, the more he liked it. This thing was incredibly lethal. It could pierce straight through flesh and bone, and it was so fast that even the best martial arts masters of Qinggong would find it hard to dodge at close range.","Not to mention trying to block it with swords or blades—didn't they just see it pierce right through the blade of a sword, striking the body with undiminished power?","With a flip of Yue Fuguang's hand, a beautiful, bright silver handgun appeared in her grasp.","\"Your Majesty, this thing is called a handgun. Whether in terms of power or range, a repeating crossbow cannot compare to it.\"","She generously handed the gun to Emperor Mingxi. She had already locked the magazine anyway, so she wasn't worried about it misfiring in his hands.","Emperor Mingxi subtly wiped his slightly sweaty hands on the hem of his robe before carefully taking this exquisite, compact marvel that exuded an alluring metallic luster yet possessed incredibly formidable destructive power.","In the eyes of the Great Yan's ruler and his ministers, this object was currently both beautiful and dangerous.","Emperor Mingxi simply rested the handgun in his palm, not daring to touch it haphazardly, afraid that a careless move would cause it to spit tongues of fire again.","Seeing his hand remain stiff, Yue Fuguang said, \"Your Majesty, please feel free to examine it. It cannot fire right now, nor can it hurt anyone.\"","Emperor Mingxi thought it made sense and carefully stroked the streamlined body of the gun. The civil and military officials who had rushed over upon hearing of the attack on the Emperor and Empress entered the grand hall, only to see their Emperor gazing obsessively at a strangely shaped object in his hand.","That look in his eyes—even when he looked at his favored concubine Zhou Yunxin back in the day, it was nothing more than this!","The Minister of Works, Lu Qi, was the most curious. After paying his respects, he couldn't help but lean in to take a couple of looks.","\"Your Majesty, why does it look to this humble subject like this thing isn't made of steel?\"","Emperor Mingxi had noticed this long ago. Before he even had the chance to ask, Lu Qi beat him to it.","He looked with eyes full of a thirst for knowledge toward Yue Fuguang, who was softly comforting Yu Chongshan.","\"Fuguang, Minister Lu is right. To me, it doesn't look like steel either. Can our Great Yan forge such a thing?\"","Knowing it was impossible, Emperor Mingxi still wouldn't give up, looking at Yue Fuguang with that one-in-a-ten-thousand sliver of hope.","[Of course, the handgun wasn't forged using inferior materials like steel. This is made of carbon nanotubes and superalloys. How could you mere mortals have ever seen such a thing!]","\"Your Majesty, this is the only one of its kind in the world. The material used is extraterrestrial meteorite iron. With Great Yan's current level of technology, it is absolutely impossible to create another.\"","Seeing the unconcealed disappointment on the faces of those who had witnessed the handgun's power, Yue Fuguang, who had no intention of introducing firearms to Great Yan just yet, changed the subject and asked, \"Your Majesty, aren't you curious about where this thing came from?\"","Emperor Mingxi realized she was right. They had been so focused on looking at the gun, how could they have forgotten to be 'curious' about it?","He coughed lightly and asked in a cover-up manner, \"Wasn't this a gift from your incredibly resourceful maritime merchant friend?\"","Emperor Mingxi sighed in his heart. If overseas merchants truly had so many novelties, he would have vigorously developed the navy long ago; he wouldn't have waited until now.","[Master, this emperor isn't too bright, but his judgment this time isn't bad. At least he knows that I, the Spirit Orb, am incredibly resourceful and omnipotent!]","Emperor Mingxi felt absolutely no joy at being praised by the great divine artifact at this moment.","Yue Fuguang shook her head, putting on an expression as if she were laying her cards on the table. \"Your Majesty, actually, there is something I haven't told you all, and it's regarding my identity.\"","At this point, she paused slightly and swept her gaze across the room. Sure enough, seeing her say this, the expressions on everyone's faces became unpredictable.","They guessed in their hearts: Could it be that the Junior Preceptor was going to lay her cards on the table and reveal her identity as an immortal descended to the mortal realm!","The expectant expressions on some people's faces were already showing.","Emperor Mingxi was clearly having a bit of trouble suppressing his excitement, his eyes shining astonishingly bright. He smiled and said, \"Fuguang, what other identity do you have that I and the lords here do not know about?\"","Yue Fuguang couldn't stand seeing Emperor Mingxi too happy, so she said, \"Your Majesty, actually, during my three years at the Daoist temple, aside from Master Qingxuan...","I also took another master. That lightning-summoning talisman from last time wasn't given by a wandering Daoist priest. Just like this handgun, it was given to me by my master, Chuyunzi.","Because I have encountered several assassinations since coming to the capital, my master was worried about my safety and thus sent me weapons for self-defense.\"","Emperor Mingxi's heart, upon hearing Yue Fuguang's nonsense, went 'smack,' dropped right back to where it was, and shattered into eight pieces!","The smiles on the others' faces froze completely. The entire grand hall fell into a momentary silence. The sun was setting in the west, making the room seem even darker. Eunuch Qian silently lit the lamps.","The wind from outside the window poured in, sweeping past the wicks, causing the candlelight to flicker and dance.","The ruler and ministers of Great Yan were only downcast for a short while. To Yue Fuguang, it just looked like they were so shocked by the news that they needed time to digest it.","\"My master is a person like an idle cloud or a wild crane; Your Majesty need not worry that he would be detrimental to Great Yan.\" She then smiled at Yu Chongshan and said, \"Grandfather, were you also startled?\"","Yu Chongshan shook his head. \"My Yu family should thank him for taking care of you!\"","Hearing their conversation, Emperor Mingxi had completely recovered from his disappointment by now. Knowing full well that she was fooling them, he still had to put on a smiling face and play along. He forced out a smile and asked half-heartedly, \"Chuyunzi? How come I have never heard of such a great master in our Great Yan?\"","He turned his head to look at Xuanmingzi, \"Master Xuanmingzi, have you ever heard the name Chuyunzi?\"","Seeing the Emperor kick the ball to him, Xuanmingzi picked up the conversation and said, \"To reply to Your Majesty, this poor Daoist has never heard of such a Daoist brother in our sect either.\"","\"Your Majesty, Daoist Master, my master is a reclusive expert who does not often walk among mortals, so it is not surprising that you haven't heard of him.","It is also because of this that I did not clarify this matter to Your Majesty in the beginning.","My master loves tranquility and does not like his quiet cultivation to be disturbed.\" So you all better not ask anymore, I really don't want to rack my brains to make up stories.","Saying this, she frowned, looking somewhat conflicted. Xie Zhiyan immediately saw her hesitation and asked, \"Does the Junior Preceptor still have some difficulties? You might as well speak them out.\"","Yue Fuguang subtly gave him an appreciative look: You catch on fast, kid!","Her brows did not relax. After a pause, she said, \"My master said he observed the stars at night and saw abnormalities in Mars, and Venus appeared during the day.","Furthermore, the five planets are moving erratically, gathering and dispersing unpredictably. There are occasional flashes of phantom stars, and signs of abnormal cloud vapors.\"","Hiss!","The others didn't quite understand, but they knew it wasn't anything good. Only Xuanmingzi understood clearly. Hearing so many stacking disasters, he couldn't help but suck in a breath of cold air.","Everyone also understood in their hearts that this was the Junior Preceptor using her master's mouth to give them a warning!","It seemed the Junior Preceptor was soft-hearted after all. She couldn't bear to see the people suffer and was giving His Majesty and them an early heads-up.","Although everyone already knew a little, they were still grateful in their hearts. The expert Xuanmingzi took the lead in asking, \"Does the Junior Preceptor mean that a large-scale drought will occur in Great Yan in the future?\"","He glanced at Emperor Mingxi and the Crown Prince, continuing, \"And signs of great turmoil?\"","Regardless of how the expressions of Emperor Mingxi and his ministers changed, whether genuine or feigned, Yue Fuguang nodded affirmatively. \"That is what my master said. He even said that if things are allowed to develop unchecked, with Mars lingering in the heart constellation, both Your Majesty and the Crown Prince will be in grave danger!\""]},{"number":317,"title":"Chapter 317: Your Majesty, You're Overacting","paragraphs":["Hiss!","Emperor Mingxi's hand trembled, and he accidentally plucked out two of his own beard hairs.","Emperor Mingxi: My hand slipped!","The officials: Your Majesty, you are overacting!","The Crown Prince stroked his smooth chin: Hearing the news of my impending doom, is my reaction a bit too calm?","The sovereign and his ministers had known about this for a long time, so he was not very worried.","The only thing they could not figure out now was why the Junior Preceptor suddenly told them so much. Had she changed her mind and wanted to give the Great Yan Dynasty a helping hand?","Or was it because today's assassination attempt had thoroughly disappointed her, making this a final warning before she left, to honor the bond they had formed over the past days!","[Master, why did you suddenly tell the Emperor all this? Aren't you afraid he will convict you of the crime of spreading rumors to deceive the masses?","Didn't we agree to just watch him build his tall building and watch it collapse, without interfering?","Why did you change your mind and give them an early warning? Look at these people, they don't look like they would listen to advice anyway!]","Emperor Mingxi: What do you mean convict her of spreading rumors? The Junior Preceptor is willing to speak plainly, which means we no longer have to do everything sneakily. We couldn't be happier!","Who would dare to convict her!","The civil and military officials tried hard to straighten their expressions, silently rebutting the divine artifact's claim that they wouldn't listen to advice.","They were obviously super easy to persuade, okay!","As for the building collapsing... the wind was loud outside, they... didn't hear a thing!","\"Isn't it because I have received too much incense offerings? Taking this opportunity to give them a little warning can be considered settling the karma.","Today's events have made me a bit annoyed. It would be best if the Emperor could convict me of spreading rumors.","Then we would have the perfect excuse to leave this place. From then on, the sky is high and the ocean is wide; where couldn't we go!\"","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers: Want to abandon us and run away? Don't even think about it!","The Minister of Revenue was the first to jump out and ask, \"When and where will this drought mentioned by the Junior Preceptor occur? My Ministry of Revenue should prepare accordingly.\"","\"Is Minister He not going to verify it first?\"","He Hongguang firmly shook his head. \"No need to verify. I trust the Junior Preceptor's words.\"","Saying so, he bowed to Yue Fuguang, thanking her for her bluntness.","Wang Shouchen also chimed in, \"I also believe the Junior Preceptor's words are not alarmist. If there is anything else, please feel free to speak, Junior Preceptor. My Court of the Imperial Stud must also prepare in advance for all the common people in the world.\"","Seeing that his ministers had all expressed their stances, Emperor Mingxi hurriedly said, \"Fuguang, I also believe you! I also want to thank you for your frankness on behalf of the people of the world.\"","Xie Zhiyan also added, \"Yes, Junior Preceptor. If there is similar news in the future, please be sure to speak frankly.\"","Saying this, he also stood up and bowed to Yue Fuguang. \"I also thank the Junior Preceptor for the warning on behalf of the people of the world.\"","Yue Fuguang raised her hand and said, \"Your Highness the Crown Prince does not need to be so polite. Since everyone trusts me, I will speak plainly.\"","She scanned the crowd, her gaze finally landing on Emperor Mingxi. \"Your Majesty, the great drought will occur in the spring of the eighth year of Yuankang. In fact, signs of the drought will appear as early as the early winter of the seventh year of Yuankang.","By the spring of the eighth year, not a single drop of rain will fall, and the people of the world will suddenly realize that a great drought has arrived. As for the scope...\"","She looked at everyone with a solemn face and said, \"North to Beili, east to Qingzhou, and west to Xiqiang. Even in the south, where rain is most abundant, Nanzhao and Nanyue will initially experience drought in some areas. But later, heavy rains will pour down in these two countries for months on end.","Three of the six countries will suffer from drought. Only Dongyi will face typhoons and floods, while Nanzhao and Nanyue will first experience drought and then floods.\"","Although they had known this for a long time, hearing Yue Fuguang say it personally today still made everyone's faces look exceedingly grim.","The bad news was confirmed, leaving no room for any lucky flukes in their hearts. Although they were prepared early on, for a moment, everyone still did not know what to say.","With the entire country suffering from a disaster, how should they provide relief? Their neighbors would also be suffering, making the danger even greater.","Even they couldn't help but want to go next door and rob a bit, so the others would only want even more.","Before they could think more, they heard Yue Fuguang continue, \"As for the duration of the drought, not a drop of rain will fall for two to three years. I hope Your Majesty and all the lords will prepare early.","At that time, the five planets will move out of alignment. Not only will there be internal instability, but the borders will also have no peace.\"","Seeing everyone silent, Yu Chongshan said, \"Fuguang, the Great Yan Dynasty has the corn, sweet potatoes, and potatoes you provided. If we plant more of these high-yield crops over the next two years, is it possible to tide over the crisis?\"","\"Yes, yes, yes, we still have the precious grain!\" Emperor Mingxi echoed repeatedly. Looking at Yue Fuguang full of hope, he said, \"Fuguang, Beloved Subject Yu is right. With these, our Great Yan people should be free from worry, right?\"","\"That will depend on how Your Majesty and the lords promote and manage them from now on. Good things also require good policies and a super strong execution capability with everyone united from top to bottom. Your Majesty, the common people are the foundation.","Even if there is a drought for three consecutive years, wealthy families will not go hungry.\"","They naturally understood the implied meaning.","Having dropped this massive bombshell, Yue Fuguang waved her sleeves and left, leaving Emperor Mingxi and his ministers to discuss countermeasures late into the night.","Now that Yue Fuguang had brought the matter of the drought out into the open and laid her cards on the table, the sovereign and ministers of Great Yan placed even higher importance on those three types of grain on the royal estates and her own estate.","During this period, Yue Fuguang went to her own estate and the royal estate respectively to rain down a spiritual shower that promoted growth.","Because of the irrigation from Yue Fuguang's spiritual rain, the sweet potatoes, corn, and potatoes were not only growing well but were expected to be harvested half a month to a month early.","Emperor Mingxi finally managed to freeload a bit of the spiritual rain under the guise of inspecting the newly recruited army. He was so happy that he was in a good mood during the morning court sessions for several days in a row.","However, whether he was in a good mood or not had nothing to do with Yue Fuguang. Using that assassination attempt as an excuse, she gave them the cold shoulder for a few days.","To please her, Emperor Mingxi finally agreed that Yue Fuguang only needed to attend court four days a month before September.","As for her studies, they would talk about it when autumn arrived.","Therefore, at this moment, Yue Fuguang was comfortably lying on her estate. Built according to the regulations of a prince's mansion, the environment was beautiful, and everything was to her liking. She sighed countless times, thinking that enjoying the cool breeze in a large house was indeed the most comfortable.","In front of her was an ice basin, and beside her was the ultimate summer treat: chilled watermelon.","In several vases on the table behind her were arranged various fresh flowers that Cuizhu and the others had picked from the mountain this morning.","Not having to attend court or school, whenever she was hungry or thirsty, she just had to reach out and call, and all kinds of green, pollution-free delicacies would be served on the table. The front and back of the house were filled with flowers and orchards.","With beautiful scenery outside the room and a beauty inside, Yue Fuguang sighed countless times in her heart that this was the life an immortal should live!","\"Fuguang, Second Brother sent a message saying that many suspicious people have been spotted near the camp recently.\"","Covered in sweat, the two sisters Yu Ningxin and Yu Ningxuan arrived hand in hand. As soon as they entered the door, the impatient Yu Ningxuan picked up a piece of watermelon from the table and started munching on it.","While munching, she didn't forget to tell her the latest news received from Sancha Land.","\"Sweet!\" Outside, Yu Ningxuan could still pretend a bit, but once she reached Yue Fuguang's place, she showed her true colors.","She ate the watermelon very boldly. \"Second Brother also said how sweet the watermelons are at his place. I think no matter how sweet they are, they can't compare to the ones on Fuguang's estate.\"","\"Didn't I have Qingzhu and the others send some to the courtyards of you, Grandmother, and Mother?\" Looking at her ravenous appearance, it seemed like she hadn't eaten any yet?"]},{"number":318,"title":"Chapter 318: The Imperial Manor Under Attack","paragraphs":["Her princely estate, covering over a hundred acres, not only had numerous courtyards but even the lotus pond where golden lotuses were originally planted had become one of the gardens in her estate.","So for this summer retreat, she didn't just come to stay by herself; several of her sisters and Old Madam Yu also came along.","Since they were all girls, the elders of the Yu family wouldn't feel at ease without a senior family member keeping an eye on them.","\"Didn't Fourth Sister and I just get back from outside?\"","\"Second Sister and I went to the workshop this morning. Some essential oils and soaps have already been produced. Fuguang, take a look and see if there are any issues.\"","Saying this, Yu Ningxin took out a few small porcelain bottles and several exquisitely crafted carved wooden boxes from a box close at hand.","Yue Fuguang sat up, inspected them one by one, and then took a sniff.","The essential oils were made from summer flowers like Chinese roses, lilies, and lotuses.","\"They smell quite nice. You made these just in time. I just ran out of my plum blossom and orchid floral waters, and I only have a few bottles left of the pear blossom and peach blossom ones.\"","Putting down the essential oils and floral waters, she picked up the soap from the carved wooden box. A pleasant floral scent immediately filled her nose.","The bars of soap, smooth as congealed fat in shades of pale pink, light yellow, and translucent white, were all carved with different beautiful floral patterns.","Their level of exquisiteness even surpassed those she had bought from the system mall.","\"The appearance is beautiful, but have you sisters tested their effectiveness?\"","\"All of us have tried them. After using them, the skin feels fine and smooth, and their cleansing effect is excellent.\"","Yu Ningxin stretched out her own lustrous little hand, sniffed it lightly, and said, \"The fragrance also lasts a long time.\"","\"Fuguang, Third Sister and the others are still keeping an eye on things at the two workshops. If you don't have any issues on your end, shall we ramp up production?\"","Yu Ningxuan was impatient. \"The ones made in the spring sold out ages ago. I receive several letters sent from the city every single day.","They are all sent by the servants of various madams and young ladies, urging us to stock new goods!\"","Speaking of this, Yu Ningxin covered her mouth and chuckled, \"Even Mother and Grandmother have quite a few madams beating around the bush to rush them.\"","Mentioning this matter, Yu Ningxuan also laughed. \"Our brothers, grandfather, and uncles haven't escaped it either.\"","She looked at Yue Fuguang, who was lying leisurely on a rocking chair, and said, \"I reckon Fuguang is the only one in the family who enjoys peace and quiet. No one dares to come and rush her.\"","According to her grandfather, the Emperor had repeatedly given explicit and implicit hints, resulting in all the family's inventory ending up in the palace. Her grandfather was now terrified of being summoned by the Emperor alone.","Yue Fuguang smiled and said, \"Rushing is useless. Even if we don't intentionally use hunger marketing, our current production capacity couldn't possibly keep up with their demands.\"","\"Aren't we going to expand the business?\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"We'll talk about it in a few years.\"","Right now, the nerves of the entire court and country had been pulled taut by her. The steel blade of a three-year drought hung over their heads, and all the land was being used to grow edible crops. For the time being, it was enough for her to just play around in her own territory.","Having finished with that topic, she turned the conversation back to the telegram. \"Second Sister, did Second Brother say whether he has found out the other party's background and intentions?\"","\"Second Brother said in the telegram that Zheng Feng and Zhang Fang led some men and caught a few of them. They are all spies from Western Qiang and Northern Li. As for their purpose, naturally, it was because they saw the novel things planted there and went over to gather intelligence.\"","Yu Ningxuan thought for a moment and added, \"Everyone in Great Yan knows you found high-yield, premium potato seeds. I guess they probably want to see if potatoes are planted on your Sancha land!\"","Yue Fuguang smiled. Hearing Yu Ningxuan's guess, she felt that her Second Sister had really used her brain.","\"Then they are really going to be disappointed!\"","Yue Fuguang's smile was full of malice. \"You can never catch all of these kinds of people. Once they discover that my rice has a high yield, they definitely won't be able to resist making a move.\"","Yu Ningxin was a little worried. \"The next batch of two thousand guards won't set off until the end of August. Can those five thousand men withstand the espionage from Western Qiang and Northern Li?\"","It would be one thing if they only dispatched spies, but if they send an army over, those five thousand men are all raw recruits who haven't seen blood yet. They might not be able to handle it.","Once they realize there is profit to be made, those two factions will very likely join forces, just like the previous few assassinations they attempted against Fuguang.","Ever since Yu Ningxin and Yu Ningxuan became Yue Fuguang's study companions, with Yue Fuguang's intentional or unintentional guidance, the two of them learned more and more information, and their horizons broadened increasingly.","Their way of thinking was already different from most of the noble young ladies in Great Yan.","Yue Fuguang revealed a sly smile. \"Don't worry. Before they even get the chance to rob us, someone will be 'secretly reselling' the rice seeds.\"","If you want them, then I'll give them to you. Robbing is so much effort and people have to die. It's better to just spend a little more money to buy them!","As soon as the two of them saw her smile, which looked like a cat that had stolen a fish, they knew that her schemes were mostly very wicked.","\"You, what bad idea are you cooking up again? I think...\"","Before Yu Ningxuan could finish her sentence, He Jin walked in quickly with an anxious look on her face. Seeing Yue Fuguang, she cupped her fists and said, \"My Lady, Qi Xiang, a marquis from the Crown Prince's estate, just came to report that the imperial estate has been attacked. His Majesty has gone over there with the Crown Prince and all the lords.","His Majesty requests that you also go over.\"","\"The imperial estate was attacked?\" Yue Fuguang suddenly sat up from the lounge chair. \"Where is Qi Xiang?\"","\"In the outer courtyard.\"","\"Prepare the carriage!\"","As she spoke, she stood up and walked out. The sisters Shen Chunying and Luo Shendong also quickly followed.","After taking only a few steps, Shen Chunying quickly ran back, picked up the icebox that had only melted a little, and left.","It was so hot outside. Without ice to cool down the carriage, how could My Lady endure it?","Seeing this, Luo Shendong also turned back to grab some pastries, tea, and iced watermelon.","Walking behind Yue Fuguang, He Jin saw Shen Chunying's actions and then watched Luo Shendong run back, silently giving her a thumbs-up.","Signaling that she had learned something!","No wonder out of all of them, My Lady liked these two sisters the most. There was a reason for it; who told them to be so genuinely considerate!","[Master, Shen Chunying is quite considerate. Aside from Cuizhu, she takes care of My Lady the best!]","\"Yes, Chunying is good. Shendong and He Jin are also not bad; they do their guard duties very dedicatedly.\"","The three of them were very happy to hear Yue Fuguang's praise. The fact that My Lady could see and acknowledge their efforts was better than anything else.","[Master, is Shen Chunying about to break through?]","\"Are you sure she is about to break through to the next realm?\"","[In my perception, she will be able to reach Zhang Fang's level in another two or three months.]","\"Still two or three months? That's too long. Little Zhu, when we get back, inject a small Peiyuan Pill into Chunying's body. With your pill, I believe she will be able to break through her cultivation level tomorrow.\"","By this time, the group had already reached the outer courtyard, where they saw Qi Xiang waiting in front of her carriage with dozens of guards.","Not to mention the envy of Yue Fuguang's guards, even Qi Xiang couldn't help but take a few extra glances at Shen Chunying when he heard that the Little Immortal Lord was bestowing medicine, and a pill to boost cultivation at that.","Why was she able to gain the favor of these two ancestors? Qi Xiang expressed that he wanted to learn!","\"Marquis Qi Xiang greets Lord Junior Preceptor!\"","Qi Xiang bowed respectfully. When he came, the Crown Prince had repeatedly instructed him to ensure the safety of the Junior Preceptor on the road.","All of them could perish, but the Junior Preceptor could not lose a single hair.","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Tell me on the way!\"","She took the lead in boarding the carriage, and Qi Xiang rode alongside on horseback, briefly explaining the attack on the imperial estate.","Yue Fuguang frowned. \"Are you saying that the people who attacked the imperial estate this time used fire, and in broad daylight no less?\""]},{"number":319,"title":"Chapter 319: The Crops in the Thirty-Six Mu of Land Have Been Stricken","paragraphs":["They really had a lot of nerve!","\"Are the losses severe?\" For the attack to succeed, was it because the attackers were highly skilled and daring, or because the guards were simply useless?","If she remembered correctly, the head of the guards at the imperial estate seemed to be Emperor Mingxi's own nephew, Shen Kang's eldest brother, Shen Jian.","She heard that this man was highly capable, so how could someone have found a loophole this time? Usually, a great reputation is not built on nothing. Could it be that he was an exception?","\"Your subordinate has not yet been to the imperial estate, but according to the people reporting to His Royal Highness the Crown Prince, twenty to thirty acres of land caught fire.\"","As a military officer of the Crown Prince's Six Armies and a trusted confidant of the Crown Prince, Qi Xiang more or less knew what was planted in the imperial estate.","Hearing the report, his heart ached terribly.","Qi Xiang lowered his head slightly, carefully stealing a glance at Yue Fuguang inside the carriage from the corner of his eye.","Through the carriage window, he saw that the Junior Preceptor's face was completely calm. Even after hearing that twenty or thirty acres of land had been destroyed, she showed no extra emotion.","The crops in the imperial estate were also the Junior Preceptor's lifeblood. She might look calm right now, but her heart must be aching too.","Yue Fuguang didn't know what Qi Xiang was thinking. Right now, she was busy looking for the System for an emergency rescue.","Twenty to thirty acres might not seem like much, but if converted into seeds, it would be enough to plant over a hundred acres, and by the year after next, it would be thousands of acres. Thousands of acres of food could save so many people during a famine year!","'System, is the shop still unavailable?'","[Does the host want to buy some seeds to replant?]","'I do have that intention. When exactly will the shop open?'","It had been half a year. No matter how heavily injured the Main System was, it should have recovered by now. If she hadn't had enough points at the time and hoarded enough goods, such a long delay would have affected her plans, even if her secret identity hadn't been exposed!","[Host, there's something I forgot to tell you. Over a month ago, the Main System began to gradually open the system shops across various planes.]","'Then why can't we use ours yet? Hasn't our turn come? No way, don't you have connections with the higher-up systems? We shouldn't have been left behind!'","[Hehehe, the Main System said that the later a system's shop is opened, the greater the discount on goods will be as compensation.]","Hearing that there was an advantage to be taken, Yue Fuguang instantly perked up. Her eyes sparkled, practically taking the shape of points.","But she immediately put on a straight face and pretended to be calm, asking, 'How big? Could it possibly be lower than ninety percent off?'","[All items start at a ninety percent discount, and some items are buy two get one free. Does that count?]","Yue Fuguang's hands, which were holding a slice of watermelon, trembled slightly. At the thought of all the good things in the shop that she wanted but couldn't bear to buy before, her heart grew fiery with excitement.","She coughed lightly and said, 'That's not bad. The key is when it will open.'","[Host, if you need it urgently, I can apply for it right now.]","'Then apply for it quickly. Also, let it slide this time, but if something like this happens again in the future, you must notify me so we can discuss it.'","The System also knew that it had acted on its own and forgotten to explain it to the host afterward, which was its fault.","So it said in a very fawning manner, [Don't worry, Host. There will absolutely not be a next time. I only dared to choose to delay the shop's opening because I knew that even if you needed it urgently, I could quickly get the application approved for you.]","With the Main System around, it wasn't difficult for it to pull some strings for its own host.","Moreover, ever since being locked in the system space once, the System didn't really dare to bother Yue Fuguang with trivial matters right after she fell asleep.","Yue Fuguang felt reassured in her heart, and her face grew even calmer. As long as the system shop was there, she had nothing to worry about in this small ancient world.","Yue Fuguang's carriage passed through three checkpoints along the way. From a mile away, they could see squads of patrolling soldiers moving through the fields.","\"Junior Preceptor, you've arrived?\"","Yue Fuguang's carriage had just stopped. Before her carriage curtain was even opened, she saw Qian Gui, Eunuch Qian, waiting by the side of the road through the thin gauze curtain.","\"Eunuch Qian, why are you here?\"","Yue Fuguang got out of the carriage and looked ahead. She saw the vermilion gates of the royal villa, which she had passed by twice before with only a fleeting glance, now wide open, hidden amidst the lush forest and tall bamboo.","Inside, shadows were moving about, and guards stood in large numbers. Even from a distance, one could feel an atmosphere of chilling solemnity.","\"This old servant was ordered by His Majesty to come here specifically to receive the Junior Preceptor.\" Qian Gui carefully held up an umbrella for her to block the still fiercely hot afternoon sun.","Yue Fuguang followed Qian Gui inside, passing through corridors and alleys. The further they went, the more guards there were. Everyone was on high alert, and whenever someone approached, their eyes would turn sharp for a moment.","Even such a tense atmosphere did not affect Yue Fuguang's appreciation of the royal villa's scenery.","It was midsummer now, and the flowers in the villa were a bit wilted from the sun. Only the Chinese roses of varying shades were blooming fiercely.","Eunuch Qian, seeing her calm face and that she was still in the mood to enjoy the scenery, inexplicably felt much more at ease in his heart as well.","He even smiled and said, \"When we are done with our work, if the Junior Preceptor has free time, this old servant will take you on a proper tour of this garden.\"","Yue Fuguang smiled and said, \"That would be wonderful.\"","Thinking of Eunuch Qian's daily care for her, and seeing his face covered in sweat while still holding an umbrella for her, she said, \"Old Qian, my estate is quite nice too. When you have time, come over to escape the summer heat! There will be plenty of big watermelons!\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's invitation, Eunuch Qian's old face immediately wrinkled into a smile like a chrysanthemum, thinking of the big watermelons the Junior Preceptor had ordered to be sent to the palace.","He had the honor of being rewarded with them twice by His Majesty. That taste was indeed much better than what was produced on the royal estates.","\"Then this old servant is in for a treat. When I have some free time, I will definitely go and bother the Junior Preceptor.\"","Qi Xiang, who was following behind, couldn't help but glance again at Eunuch Qian, who was respectfully leading Yue Fuguang inside.","How did he also manage to win the Junior Preceptor's favor?","Qi Xiang was a studious person who wanted to make progress. He couldn't help but recall the similarities between Shen Chunying and Eunuch Qian.","If he could figure it out, it would probably be his opportunity...","Yue Fuguang arrived at the main courtyard without any hindrance. Before she could even enter the courtyard gate, she saw Xie Zhiyan coming out to welcome her.","\"Junior Preceptor, you've had a hard journey.\" Xie Zhiyan naturally took the umbrella from Qian Gui's hands.","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"How are things at the estate now? I heard from Qi Xiang that twenty to thirty acres of land were lost?\"","Xie Zhiyan's face didn't look too good. As he led her toward the main hall, he said, \"We just tallied up two ignition points. A total of thirty-six acres of crops have suffered!\"","When he mentioned the thirty-six acres, Xie Zhiyan's hand holding the umbrella handle subconsciously tightened. Yue Fuguang worried that if he used a little more force, he might crush the handle to pieces.","\"Which seedlings were destroyed?\" There was only a little over a month left until harvest. If it was high-yield crops like sweet potatoes and potatoes, calculating it meant suddenly losing enough seeds for over a hundred acres. By the year after next, that would mean a harvest of hundreds of thousands of pounds of food. It truly made one's heart ache.","\"It was mainly the cornfields, and about seven or eight acres of the adjacent sweet potato fields were also affected. Fortunately, the stalks were still green, so the fire burned slower. If it had been a month later, the consequences would have been unimaginable.\"","Just thinking about that possibility caused the color to drain from Xie Zhiyan's face.","Yue Fuguang still maintained a calm expression, but the words she spoke deeply thrilled the three people present, including Xie Zhiyan.","She said, seemingly casually, \"It's not a big problem. There's still time to replant a season of autumn sweet potatoes.\""]},{"number":320,"title":"Chapter 320: Spending Money, Spending Glory","paragraphs":["Xie Zhiyan suddenly turned his head to look at her, his voice unconsciously rising, \"Lord Junior Preceptor, are you saying that you have autumn sweet potato seeds there?\"","The few people who had already walked to the bottom of the hall's steps were only a few meters away from the main hall. Xie Zhiyan's words were naturally heard loud and clear by the Great Yan monarch and officials inside, led by Emperor Mingxi, all of whom wore exceptionally ugly expressions.","Emperor Mingxi stood up abruptly. Before he even arrived, his voice carried over, \"Fuguang is here? Old Qian, why didn't you announce her arrival so I could welcome her in advance?\"","Yue Fuguang looked at his hypocritical politeness and walked inside while saying, \"Your Majesty, didn't you already have Old Qian go to the door to receive me?\"","\"Fuguang, it must be hot on the road. Come sit here quickly, it's close to the ice box and cool.\"","There were seven or eight ice boxes placed in the hundred-square-meter hall. As soon as Yue Fuguang walked in, she felt enveloped by a comfortable coolness.","Looking again at the twenty or so officials standing in the hall, all of their faces were covered in sweat. This was due to their internal anxiety and had nothing to do with the scorching sun outside.","As Emperor Mingxi spoke, he personally poured warm water for Yue Fuguang and handed it to her. This attentiveness left Qian Gui with nothing to do for a moment.","The officials also cupped their hands and smiled at her. Yue Fuguang nodded in greeting.","After sitting down and drinking some tea, she finally noticed a person kneeling straight on the right side of the hall.","He was in his twenties, still wearing a suit of soft armor on such a hot day. With sword-like eyebrows and starry eyes, he embodied both heroism and nobility. His slightly dark face currently held an abnormal flush. Seeing Yue Fuguang come in, he swept a glance at her from the corner of his eye and didn't dare to look again.","Yue Fuguang also acted as if she had just seen him, asking despite knowing the answer, \"Your Majesty, what is going on here?\"","Emperor Mingxi followed her gaze and saw the person kneeling on the ground. He said with exasperation at his failure to meet expectations, \"This is Shen Jian, the commander of the guards here. The seedlings in the imperial estate were destroyed, and he and his subordinates bear an undeniable responsibility.\"","\"Then has Your Majesty found out the whole story?\"","Emperor Mingxi seemed very angry, but if he really had to heavily punish his quite capable biological nephew, he would probably be reluctant to do so.","\"Wei Ping, Cai Xian, you two come and explain to the Lord Junior Preceptor.\"","The miserable duo looked at each other, acknowledged the order, and stepped forward.","Seeing that it was these two in charge again, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but feel sorry for these two brothers in distress.","Ever since she started exposing secrets, these two hadn't had a single day of rest. They were either catching domestic spies or foreign spies.","They were either catching domestic imperial relatives and high-ranking officials or on their way to catching foreign princes and princesses.","For a brief moment, Yue Fuguang's conscience pricked her, wondering if she should treat them a little better in the future.","After all, even with her occasional feeding, while everyone else was glowing with health, these two were visibly aging day by day.","Cai Xian spoke first, \"Reporting to Your Majesty and the Lord Junior Preceptor, the guards have caught three people in total. These three were originally instructed by someone to come here and gather information. For some reason, when one of them saw unfamiliar crops like corn and sweet potatoes, and realized they weren't the potatoes they were looking for, he feared he wouldn't get paid if he returned empty-handed. Thus, he acted maliciously and set fire to the fields.\"","\"Minister Cai, are the identities of these three confirmed?\"","Looking for potatoes but not going to Xuanwei Prefecture, and instead finding the royal estate, these people were not simple!","\"Upon investigation, all three are scoundrels from nearby villages. They were bribed by someone with ulterior motives and sneaked into the imperial estate while the management was lax during the construction of the Autumn Sacrifice Lutai next door, attempting to find out where the potatoes are planted.\"","These people were idlers from nearby villages. Although the imperial estate's guards had been stationed here for a long time, they really didn't recognize them.","Moreover, because it was only the third day since the construction of the Lutai began, the guards hadn't fully familiarized themselves with all the craftsmen yet. Thus, the security was slightly relaxed, allowing these few to exploit the loophole. It was all a matter of fate and timing!","[Master, Cai Xian and the others were fooled!]","Cai Xian still kept his head slightly lowered, but his peripheral vision unexpectedly met Wei Ping's. Sure enough, from Lord Divine Artifact, they could truly learn some different information.","They had verified it; the identities of the three people were not an issue. But commoners, even reckless scoundrels, wouldn't be completely without fear.","These three, who usually had to bow and scrape when seeing the village head and whose highest official encounter was the county magistrate, how could they have the guts to burn the Emperor's estate?","Just because they drank a couple of extra cups of cheap wine at noon and drank themselves silly?","[Fooled by whom? Those three scoundrels?]","[Master, these three are indeed commoners from Shanqianba ahead, but among them, that Song Xiaoer, strictly speaking, is no ordinary scoundrel. Behind him is a boss named Hua Qian. Hua Qian and that Brother Wicked are good friends; they are both involved in the underworld.]","[Little Zhu, are you saying this matter is related to the underworld of Shangjing City? Is Hua Qian his real name? And was Song Xiaoer instructed by this Hua Qian?]","[Hehehe, the name is a bit weird, but it is indeed his real name. Hua Qian instructed Song Xiaoer, but the mastermind wasn't him, but his older brother Hua Rong. Master might not have heard the name Hua Rong, but you must have heard his other nickname, Black Widow!]","[Black Widow? Are you saying Black Widow is a man? And a local of Shangjing City?]","Emperor Mingxi and his officials also furrowed their brows tightly. The Drunken Rakshasa, Poison Young Master, and Black Widow had long made a name for themselves in the martial arts world.","They had only recently learned from the Junior Preceptor and her companions that these three notorious menaces were actually all members of Panshan.","The Drunken Rakshasa, whom they had captured not long ago, was indeed a person possessing both male and female traits.","Therefore, the Divine Artifact's claim that the famous, beautiful, and charming Black Widow was actually a man was not that hard to accept.","[That is right, the Black Widow was also a handsome young man in his early years. Later, he became romantically involved with a young and beautiful widow.","Who knew that the widow would later dump him and marry someone else.","Young and hot-blooded, Hua Rong slaughtered all five members of that family on a dark and windy night, and from then on, he became a fugitive in the martial arts world.","Later, through a series of twists and turns, he joined Panshan. When he re-emerged into the world, due to his early experiences, he had developed a twisted hobby. He loved preying on young widows the most, and he also enjoyed disguising himself as a young widow to seduce his mission targets. Hence, he earned the title of Black Widow.]","\"So, you mean the mastermind behind today's incident is Panshan? How did they know potatoes were planted here?\"","[They got the news from the Dongyi people. There are Panshan spies among the Dongyi as well.]","Yue Fuguang was a bit speechless. Just how many tentacles did Panshan have? Their people were everywhere. She wanted to uproot this organization completely, but today's incident further proved that it truly would not be that easy.","But looking at the whopping 58,000 mission points on the quest panel, it was truly tempting!","\"Have you two lords thoroughly investigated the schemers behind this?\"","The information has already been revealed to you, so hurry up and speak the truth!","As expected, Wei Ping did not disappoint her. He stepped forward on his own initiative and said, \"To answer the Junior Preceptor, according to Song Xiao'er's confession, he was instructed by his boss, Hua Qian, who ordered him to secretly investigate the exact location where the potatoes were planted in the imperial estate.","And we found out that Hua Qian has an older brother named Hua Rong, nicknamed the Black Widow, who was once good friends with the Drunken Rakshasa currently held in the heavenly prison.\""]},{"number":321,"title":"Chapter 321: Insider Information","paragraphs":["The people around watched Wei Ping, without blushing or skipping a beat, take the information he had eavesdropped on and, without changing a bit, present it to the Junior Preceptor as his own findings. They all felt that when it came to being thick-skinned, they were far inferior to Vice Minister Wei.","It had only been a little over two hours since the incident occurred. Weren't you afraid of being exposed in front of the two ancestors when claiming to have found out so much?","[Master, since when did Wei Ping and the others become so efficient?]","\"It might be because the situation is serious this time, and the people they caught aren't professional spies. That Song Xiao'er is just a local ruffian. Once his reckless courage fades, he will still be terrified when facing the authorities.\"","\"Then have you found Hua Rong's whereabouts?\" Thinking of Matsuyama, whom she had once half-roasted with a lightning strike, she continued, \"Did Matsuyama say how they learned that potatoes were planted in the royal estate?\"","Wei Ping cupped his hands and said, \"There is something you do not know, Junior Preceptor. Because Matsuyama is heavily injured, we didn't dare to use severe torture on him, so we got relatively little information out of him.\"","\"What about the others? His subordinates, and that royal princess named Yōko?\"","\"We learned of three Eastern Yi spy strongholds from them, which have all been eradicated. However, the twelve people captured are all low-level spies who know very little...\" Wei Ping's voice grew quieter as he spoke.","Those people were incredibly stubborn. After being subjected to severe torture, the information they spat out was half true and half false. If they hadn't been vigilant, the deadly traps set by the Eastern Yi people would have become their burial grounds.","It was also because of this that they truly acknowledged the Eastern Yi, the weakest of the six nations, for the first time.","The short-statured Yi people were cunning and treacherous. Especially that royal princess—because they had shown her mercy, she didn't speak a single word of truth. Every piece of information she gave was intended to get them killed.","The moment Wei Ping thought about how his son had a child with her in the original timeline, he felt sick to his stomach!","Yue Fuguang looked at the increasingly aging Wei Ping, who had grown white hair prematurely, and felt helpless. Wasn't it a bit too demanding, and a mismatch of skills, to make a Vice Minister deal with professional spies?","It seemed that Great Yan urgently needed to establish a dedicated anti-espionage agency, the Secret Spy Bureau.","[Master, I know the answer to this!]","For Wei Ping, who was so embarrassed he could have dug a two-courtyard mansion with his toes, hearing these words was like listening to heavenly music. The sweat constantly breaking out on his back suddenly felt cool.","'Little Zhu, do you know who leaked the information?'","As Yue Fuguang asked this, Emperor Mingxi waved his hand at Wei Ping, dismissing him, and then said to the kneeling Shen Jian, \"Your punishment will be discussed later. The most urgent matter right now is to conduct an internal investigation of all the soldiers stationed at the royal estate.","In my view, the information obtained by the Eastern Yi people was most likely leaked by someone stationed at the royal estate.","Furthermore, the fact that those three scoundrels managed to sneak in right under your noses and successfully set two fires shows that there are serious problems with your security.","As the commander, Shen Jian, you bear an undeniable responsibility!\"","[Master, the Emperor is finally smart for once. The information really was leaked by a lowly soldier stationed here.]","'Little Zhu, is this soldier an Eastern Yi spy? How much information did he actually leak?'","Shen Jian, who had already stood up, turned pale upon hearing this. His knees gave way, and if he didn't have martial arts training, his legs probably would have been so weak that he'd be kneeling again.","His throat tightened, and his heart pounded wildly. If it was truly as Junior Preceptor Yue said, then he, Shen Jian, really couldn't escape the blame and had failed the trust of his uncle and cousin.","He carefully and quickly shot a glance from the corner of his eye at the Junior Preceptor sitting next to his royal uncle.","Whether it was his parents or his younger siblings, they were all full of praise whenever they mentioned this Junior Preceptor.","The two spiritual rains at the royal estate were also caused by her. They had followed along and truly gained many benefits, but strictly speaking, this was his first time meeting this Junior Preceptor.","Thinking back to what she said when she entered earlier, it seemed that the life, death, glory, and disgrace of himself and all the soldiers at the royal estate were entirely tied to her alone.","\"Your Majesty, I know my crime! Today's incident was entirely caused by my improper protection. Please punish me, Your Majesty!\" Shen Jian bowed. He was willing to accept the punishment for his poor management, and he wanted even more to root out the menace within his ranks.","Otherwise, keeping such a person around meant that his subordinates would sooner or later be dragged down to their deaths by this one individual.","[Master, this Shen Jian does indeed have problems in his management, but it's also because of certain rules he set that only the potatoes have been leaked so far.","The names of sweet potatoes and corn are still unknown to the outside world.]","'Little Zhu, hurry up and tell me about it.'","[Master, after Shen Jian led his men to garrison the royal estate, he assigned management zones to each officer.","The soldier who leaked the information about the potatoes belonged to a squad responsible for guarding a hundred acres of potatoes.","Because there were rules against wandering around, and because the areas guarded in all directions around their squad were also potato fields.","This led him to believe that the royal estate only planted one type of crop. So later, when he sold the information to the Eastern Yi people, he only mentioned potatoes.]","'Sold information to the Eastern Yi? He isn't an Eastern Yi spy? Is he a spy from another organization?'","[No, the guards Shen Jian selected come from relatively clean backgrounds. Aside from a few having minor flaws, there aren't any major issues.","This lowly soldier who sold information to the Eastern Yi people is named Cheng Erniu. Coincidentally, he is from the same hometown as those three ruffians who set fire to the royal estate.","Cheng Erniu's family lives in Shanhouba, and he has six family members at home, including his parents and siblings.","He has an older brother, a younger brother, and a younger sister. Being the middle child, he wasn't valued at home. After joining the army, he still had to use his military pay to support his younger brother's civil service exams.","This time, his selling of information to the Eastern Yi people was also facilitated by his younger brother, Cheng Shanbao, who is a Tongsheng scholar.]","'Cheng Shanbao? Why did he do this, and how did he meet the Eastern Yi people?'","[Master, Cheng Shanbao was originally a scholar, but he got addicted to gambling and incurred a massive debt of silver.","In order to keep his hands, when he was raising money to pay off the debt, he lied to his parents, claiming he needed the money to buy gifts to become the disciple of a famous master.","However, although Mother and Father Cheng favored him greatly in daily life, the family's living expenses relied on the fields' output, and his school tuition was entirely supported by Cheng Erniu's military pay.","So the two Cheng elders simply couldn't produce the hundred-odd taels of silver needed to buy gifts for the master. Later, the Cheng parents borrowed from all their relatives, but they were still short by over seventy taels.","At this time, Cheng Shanbao's schoolmaster, Scholar Xu, seeing his difficulties, introduced him to Liu Goro.]","'Is this Liu Goro the same Kogoro who is currently locked up in the celestial prison?'","[Yes, that's him. The Eastern Yi people grew suspicious when they saw the royal estate was heavily guarded. Later, Cheng Shanbao bragged to his classmates that his second brother was an officer in the Royal Guards and was stationed inside the royal estate.","This news spread like wildfire and reached the ears of Liu Goro and his group. That's what led to them deliberately luring Cheng Shanbao into gambling and incurring debt, so that to raise money to pay it off, the whole family pitched in to persuade the foolishly filial Cheng Erniu to sell information about the royal estate.]"]},{"number":322,"title":"Chapter 322: I Want No Silver or Gold","paragraphs":["\"Then what is going on with this Scholar Xu? How could he know the Dongyi people?\"","[Master, Scholar Xu's name is Xu Tongchen. His ancestor was Xu Yannian, who once served as the prime minister of the Great Zhou Dynasty, and his son married the daughter of the Last Emperor.","This Xu Tongchen is the descendant of the Last Emperor's daughter. Moreover, tracing back through the Tong family, they are maternal cousins with Tong Jiye. Because of this relationship, the two families have long been in contact.","In the south, apart from the Sima family, the other major families are all involved in maritime trade and have some sort of connection with the Dongyi people.]","Emperor Mingxi lowered his head slightly, slowly sipping his tea. Looking closely at his hand holding the cup, the veins were bulging. He was clearly furious about the collusion between the remnants of the previous dynasty and the Dongyi people.","The Tong family members in Xingzhou and Yizhou had all been captured. Based on their confessions, Wei Ping and the others traced the clues to Xinzhou. Various signs indicated that Xinzhou was hiding the descendants of the Tong family and the legitimate son of the Last Emperor.","However, they had not yet found this big fish. To avoid alerting the enemy, they only kept Tong Jiye and his associates under surveillance, waiting for the right moment to close the net.","He hadn't expected there to be someone so closely connected to them here, willing to sell out the Great Yan to foreigners just to restore their fallen nation!","Standing in the corner, Dong Qianli glanced at Lu Qi. As the Minister of Revenue, he had naturally seen the secret investigations ordered by Emperor Mingxi regarding the maritime trade profits of the various families.","It could be said that the prominent families in the south were filthy rich because of maritime trade. Yet, not only did they evade taxes, but they also colluded with pirates, and now with the Dongyi people. They truly deserved to die!","He only hoped that the Ministry of Works could build the warships as soon as possible. By then, the new naval forces trained by the Great Yan could sail out on the new warships to pacify the pirates, and that would be the time to bring down the Sima family.","Lu Qi certainly understood the meaning behind Dong Qianli's glance, but building a new type of large sea vessel was a process of trial and error for the Ministry of Works; they couldn't speed it up even if they wanted to.","[Liu Goro's public identity is a grocery store owner, and his shop is located in the area where Hua Qian and his gang collect protection fees.","Once, while the two were drinking, Liu Goro originally wanted to ask this local snake about the imperial estate. Unexpectedly, he was filled with liquor by Hua Qian. In his drunken state, he let it slip, allowing Hua Qian to learn about the potatoes at the imperial estate, who then passed the information to Hua Rong.","That is what led to the arson incident today.]","\"Since a few people had already sneaked in, why didn't they just secretly dig up a few potato plants instead of setting a fire?\"","[Because the matter of the potatoes has increasingly boosted the prestige of the emperor and the imperial court among the common people. This is something that Panshan, an organization dedicated to overthrowing the current ruling family, does not want to see.","As long as there are no potatoes, the prestige the emperor built in the name of the potatoes will plummet from the high mountains to the bottom of the valley.]","Emperor Mingxi stood up abruptly and said to Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and Shen Jian, \"My three lords, I will give you two days.","Within two days, I want to see all those involved captured. Three scoundrels wouldn't have the guts to go against the royal family.","There must be someone behind them. Go and dig all these people out, leave no one behind!\"","He looked at Wei Ping and Cai Xian and added, \"Especially that Black Widow. Even if you have to dig three feet into the ground, you must dig her out!\"","[Master, digging three feet into the ground won't dig out Black Widow at all.]","\"Why do you say that, Little Zhu? Do you know where Black Widow is hiding?\"","[Hehe, Master, Little Zhu actually does know. He is currently hiding in a secret room of a ruined temple on Qingliang Mountain outside the southern city.","The depth of that secret room is three meters, not three feet.]","\"This Black Widow is quite good at hiding. If it's really as you say, then Wei Ping and Cai Xian will have a hard time finding him.\"","[Master, do you not plan to tell them?]","Yue Fuguang paused and said, \"For the sake of Wei Yan and Cai Bing, I do need to intervene a bit. If they can't find him by tomorrow, it won't be too late to leak the information then.","I can just use this opportunity to let them sort through the suspicious individuals. They might just inadvertently catch a few little mice.","Don't forget, in just over a month, the crops outside will reach the harvest season. It's good to clean up inside and outside the capital in advance.\"","\"We obey His Majesty's decree!\" The two solemnly accepted the order.","It goes without saying that they had mixed feelings in their hearts. The two never expected that one day, they would prematurely enjoy the protection and benefits brought by their most disappointing sons.","Clinging to the Junior Preceptor's golden thigh was truly worth it!","In the crowd, the Yu father and son wore bright smiles, showing immense support for Yue Fuguang's decision.","They had thought the matter would end here, and Yu Chongshan had already lifted his foot to walk toward Yue Fuguang.","Having not seen her for many days, he naturally missed her very much. Although he received news from the estate every day, nothing compared to seeing her in person and asking clearly if the child was doing well.","However, right at that moment, Emperor Mingxi leaned forward, inching slightly closer to Yue Fuguang. With a smile he thought was amiable and approachable on his face, he said, \"Fuguang, when you came in just now, I heard the Crown Prince say you have autumn sweet potato seeds over there?\"","[Master, why is the emperor smiling like the Big Bad Wolf disguised as the grandmother?]","\"Don't worry, your master isn't Little Red Riding Hood. He can't eat me.\"","Emperor Mingxi was quite speechless at the back-and-forth between these two little ancestors. Holding back his twitching mouth, he continued, \"Look, could the imperial court buy some from you at a high price?\"","Yue Fuguang raised her eyes to meet Emperor Mingxi's eager, aged face and subtly took a step back.","Xie Zhiyan perceptively handed her a small bowl of iced watermelon puree, smiling as he said, \"Junior Preceptor, please taste how the watermelons produced from the estate are.\"","Emperor Mingxi also knew he was being a bit too eager, so he smiled and chimed in, \"I think they are still slightly inferior to the Golden Scales and Jade Qilin from Fuguang's estate.\"","Yue Fuguang took two bites before replying, \"Your Majesty, I do have some autumn sweet potato seeds left over there. I was originally saving them to make dried sweet potatoes.","Since Your Majesty wants them, I will give them to you.\"","Emperor Mingxi was so excited he nearly stood up. He laughed heartily and said good several times in a row.","The officials in the hall also wore faces full of smiles, one after another showering Yue Fuguang with loud praises and flattery.","\"However.\" With Yue Fuguang's however, the originally lively hall instantly went quiet. Emperor Mingxi's smile also froze on his face, his facial muscles twitching uncontrollably.","Yue Fuguang caught a glimpse of the chrysanthemum-like wrinkles frozen at the corners of his eyes and secretly shook her head. The emperor's skincare routine was really lacking!","In his forties, right at the prime flower-like age, and look at what he had done to himself!","Power doesn't necessarily nourish a person! Anyone who worries too much will look old!","\"Fuguang, just say it. As long as the imperial court can do it, there is nothing we won't grant.\" Even without the matter of the autumn sweet potato seeds.","Given Yue Fuguang's importance, as long as it was a request she made, even if they had to mobilize the entire nation's strength, they would have to find a way to fulfill her wishes.","\"Your Majesty, I do not want money.\"","She shifted her gaze to Huo Ying. \"I heard that Minister Huo has recruited over twenty thousand new soldiers from various places in the past couple of months.\"","Huo Ying cupped his fists and replied, \"It is indeed as the Junior Preceptor says. Following the recruitment standards of the Right Martial Guard's new army, I have recruited a total of twenty-eight thousand five hundred new soldiers from the prefectures and counties around the capital.","Friends, please move your prosperous little hands to click on the request for updates, thank you very much! Cupped fists!"]},{"number":323,"title":"Chapter 323: Is today the fifth seventh day of Xie Laosi's death","paragraphs":["All training was conducted according to the complete methods of the new military camp. Currently, the results are a bit worse than the batch from the new military camp, but given a little more time, there shouldn't be much difference...","Huo Ying revealed the exact situation of this new army of 28,500 men to Yue Fuguang, hiding absolutely nothing.","Because he roughly guessed Yue Fuguang's purpose for asking, he naturally had to explain clearly so she could make judgments and choices.","Yue Fuguang nodded and said to Emperor Mingxi, Your Majesty, how about exchanging five hundred men for fifty acres of sweet potato seeds?","Hearing that she indeed wanted to add people, Emperor Mingxi smiled without any hesitation, How could five hundred be enough? I will make it a full thousand for you.","Next month, you can pick three thousand men yourself to go to the Three-Pronged Land.","With a wave of his hand, he smiled and said, Rest assured, it won't delay your cotton harvest.","Seeing Emperor Mingxi being so generous, Yue Fuguang was also very happy. Your Majesty, send someone to my estate tomorrow to transport the seeds.","Emperor Mingxi originally wanted to say, why not bring them back today and have people plant them overnight? Wouldn't the seeds sprout a day earlier if planted a day earlier?","But knowing that Yue Fuguang had an even more uncompromising temper than himself, the Emperor, he immediately shut his mouth.","However, he soon realized that keeping his mouth shut was a good thing.","[Master, the autumn sweet potatoes are already in the warehouse. Why didn't you let the Emperor bring them back right now?]","Little Zhu, since the Emperor was so generous as to give me an extra five hundred men, we won't be stingy either.","Soak those seeds in the spiritual spring water overnight. I believe that even without the spiritual rain, it will guarantee they grow vigorously and can be harvested early.","Hearing about these unexpected pleasant surprises, Emperor Mingxi's eyes suddenly lit up, and he felt extremely fortunate for his previous restraint.","On the second day after all the sweet potatoes were planted, Yue Fuguang received news that the notorious Black Widow had been captured.","With the capture of the Cheng Erniu brothers and the imprisonment of Xu Tongchen's entire family, the fire incident at the imperial estate further exposed the long-dormant remnants of the previous dynasty.","Within a few days, even the commoners in the capital knew that the remnants of the previous dynasty still harbored ambitions to restore their nation, actually attempting to burn the long-awaited high-yield potatoes.","This was an attempt to cut off their food supply and take their lives.","Fueled by those with ulterior motives, the rallying cries to report and capture the previous dynasty's remnants, protect the Great Yan's prosperous peace, and ensure the common people had food to eat reached an unprecedented high.","Even in the villages near Yue Fuguang's estate, the commoners hired to help pull weeds on the farm shared a bitter hatred of the enemy and were filled with righteous indignation when discussing the matter.","However, these people did not know that the very ground they stood on, the fields they were helping to weed and fertilize, were planted with the potatoes they had been longing for.","And the sweet potatoes, an unheard-of and unseen crop that was equally high-yielding.","On the fifth day of the seventh month in the fifth year of Yuankang, it was once again the day for Yue Fuguang to attend the morning court session.","Early in the morning, she followed Yu Chongshan and his son into the palace. Head-on, they ran into the Second and Third Princes, who had gradually established their own residences outside after the Crown Prince's wedding.","Yue Fuguang remembered that she seemed to have sent them housewarming gifts, but it was all handled by Madam Zhang in her name. She wasn't clear on what exactly was sent, only remembering that she seemed to have added a set of kitchenware for each household!","Little Zhu, is today Fourth Master Xie's fifth seven-day memorial?","[Master remembers correctly. Today is indeed the day Fourth Master Xie's soul goes to the Home-Viewing Pavilion.]","When the Second and Third Princes saw Yue Fuguang, they quickly came over to respectfully greet her, only to hear the two ancestors mention their fourth brother's soul.","Suddenly, they felt that even on a July morning, it was a bit cold.","The two brothers unconsciously leaned closer to each other. They had dressed too thinly before leaving the house, completely unable to block the gusts of ghostly wind blowing from nowhere.","On the way to the Court Hall, they didn't dare stray too far from Yue Fuguang, this immortal lord.","After all, even if there really were ghosts and monsters, they wouldn't dare get close to her, right!","Not to mention anything else, the Divine Artifact had connections in the underworld; even the Lord of Hell could be ordered around by it.","He died early in this life before he had time to commit evil. When the judge evaluates him, won't he be able to enter reincarnation again?","[Does Master not want to give him a chance to reincarnate? How about I greet the Lord of Hell? In a couple of years, with natural disasters and man-made calamities, more will die and fewer will be born. The chance to reincarnate will be rare indeed.]","Emperor Mingxi, who had waited for the civil and military officials to take their places before stepping into the main hall, had barely set foot inside when he heard such a morbid topic. He immediately felt unwell, and his slightly drowsy and unclear mind instantly became sharp.","It was also on the way to the court session that Qian Gui reminded him, making him remember that today was his fourth son's fifth seven-day memorial, something he hadn't taken much to heart.","Who knew that on this sensitive day, hearing the Divine Artifact's remarks would make Emperor Mingxi's hairs stand on end.","Along with his hairs, his ears also perked up.","The ruler and ministers of Great Yan were currently in a mood where they were both terrified and eager to listen, perfectly demonstrating the attitude of being weak yet addicted to the thrill.","Regarding the underworld where they must go after death, they had always held an attitude of reverence and keeping a respectful distance. Now that they had a chance to learn a bit more in advance about their future resting place, they naturally couldn't bear to miss a single word.","Yue Fuguang deliberately paused for a moment before saying, Forget it, look at Second Brother Xie and Xie San now; they aren't missing any arms or legs.","Second Brother Xie and Xie San? The Second Prince and Third Prince glanced at each other. She was talking about the two of them, right?","They really wanted to tell Yue Fuguang: Junior Preceptor, we have names! We are called Xie Zhimin and Xie Zhixin!","How come when you mention the Crown Prince, you use his full name, but when you mention us, it's just Two and Three? Isn't the favoritism a bit too obvious?","As for the mention of missing arms and legs, the two brothers, who had long guessed they would die a bad death, were completely thick-skinned about it. It was just losing an arm or a leg; compared to losing their lives, it was nothing!","The two tacitly looked towards their eldest brother in unison. With their eldest brother, who was certified by the two ancestors, protecting them, their arms and legs were safe.","As for their biological father, the two silently shook their heads. Their old man had too many sons; he was not as reliable as the eldest brother they had recently gone out of their way to curry favor with.","Regarding the fact that two of their younger brothers had died in succession and their imperial father didn't seem to feel much about it, the young brothers Second Brother Xie and Xie San felt very deeply about this.","Only Xie Wu, upon hearing these things, silently began to edge closer to Yu Zhongchun in the crowd of ministers.","Yu Zhongchun silently cupped his hands in greeting to Xie Zhiquan, who had moved next to him, but in his heart, he was thinking: Has this Fifth Prince been scared silly, thinking that as the father of the Immortal Lord, he could protect him?","This kid must be overthinking it!","Xie Liu wasn't bitten to death by a venomous snake, and Xie Qi wasn't trampled into mud by horses. Fourth Master Xie's evil karma wasn't completed; that is his serendipity.","Emperor Mingxi gritted his teeth, staring fixedly below, cursing the deceased Fourth Master Xie a thousand times in his heart.","Even if he had many sons, hearing them meet with accidents one after another like this, even a dozen sons wouldn't be enough to withstand such destruction!","At this moment, the main hall was dead silent. Eunuch Qian forced himself to swallow his saliva, and his call of If there are matters, present your memorials echoed in the main hall, yet sounded particularly jarring.","After Qian Gui's words fell, no one stepped forward. Yu Chongshan quickly glanced at his granddaughter on the high seat, took two steps forward, and said, Reporting to Your Majesty, this subject has a memorial to present."]},{"number":324,"title":"Chapter 324: Would you like to take a look","paragraphs":["Seeing that it was Yu Chongshan, Emperor Mingxi's face softened, and his voice sounded slightly exhausted as he asked, \"What does Beloved Subject Yu have to report?\"","\"Reporting to Your Majesty, regarding the matter of water conservancy construction...\" Yu Chongshan began to report one by one the water conservancy projects and river channel cleanups that the Ministry of Works planned to construct before the drought arrived.","This was also to ensure that on the basis of having food to survive the disaster, the common people also had the most basic drinking water guarantee projects.","Yue Fuguang was drowsy as she listened. Seeing that she was about to slack off, the system quickly continued the previous topic.","Hearing that Yu Chongshan had already mentioned organizing well-drilling teams to explore underground waterways in villages and counties across various prefectures, digging more wells, and finding more springs in the mountains, the system said, [Master, the day before yesterday was the fifth seven of Xie Jiu. I heard from World Peace that under the Yellow Springs, he, Zhou Yunxin, and Chonghua, a family of three, actually reunited.]","Hearing this news, Yue Fuguang's sleepiness completely disappeared. Having pulled the banner of the underworld for so long, she only recently learned from the system that there really was an underworld in this world.","Lord Yama was not a distant myth or legend either!","When she got this news at the time, she was not much better off than those Great Yan monarchs and ministers below, and she wished she could sleep with one eye open to stand guard at night.","Why was she afraid?","Because she felt guilty. No matter what the cause and effect were, she had indeed sent many people down. What if one slipped through the net and didn't return to the underworld after death...","If the system hadn't guaranteed that the main god system was equivalent to the boss of the heavenly law of each small world, invulnerable to gods and ghosts, and that the two of them did have some privileges with Lord Yama.","And the system's sentence, [Host, Lord Yama also doesn't want the world to be in chaos and so many people to die, otherwise the underworld will be full, not to mention the quota for reincarnation will be reduced, which will also have a great impact on him, so our existence is a good thing for Lord Yama.]","Made her feel a little at ease. Yue Fuguang felt that based on the wild words they had let out before, she could pick up her bucket and run away now!","After struggling for two days, between dragging the system to immediately head to the next world and continuing to complete the task, Yue Fuguang finally chose to continue the task.","Once the scar was healed, the pain was forgotten. After these few days of self-hypnosis, Yue Fuguang, who had completely recovered, felt that she could do it again.","She immediately replied, \"Little Zhu, how long have Zhou Yunxin and Chonghua been dead, and they haven't been thrown into hell yet?\"","[Master, in the past half a year, for some unknown reason, the number of poultry and livestock raised in Great Yan territory has increased, and the quota for reincarnation in the animal path is in short supply.","So, Zhou Yunxin, Chonghua, Zhuo Fei, Zhou Fushan, Xu Changyue, and others... no, and other ghosts, who had originally harmed several lives and should have been thrown into the Hell of Tongue Ripping and the Hell of Ice Mountains to be punished in turn, were pulled up to be reincarnated together with other ghosts with deep sins.]","Hearing this string of dozens of familiar names, going from humans to ghosts, and now going to reincarnate into the animal path, everyone just felt that the hall today was blowing cold air from everywhere.","They always felt like someone was breathing down their necks, otherwise why would it feel colder and colder?","Eunuch Qian saw a layer of goosebumps on Emperor Mingxi's neck and very sensibly moved the ice basin closest to him a little further away.","To be honest, he also felt a little cold. Who told Eunuch Qian, as the chief eunuch beside Emperor Mingxi, to be exceptionally familiar with that mother and son!","These ghosts coming up to reincarnate wouldn't conveniently come to see if they were doing well, would they!","Thinking of this, everyone felt unwell and moved closer to each other, wanting to draw some warmth and courage from the other party.","Yue Fuguang also only suddenly realized when she heard the system reporting people's names like reporting dish names that they had sent a bit too many people down, hadn't they?","But looking at the points that were about to reach level five, she instantly felt that she could send a few more down.","\"Little Zhu, do you mean they are going to reincarnate into cats and dogs?\"","[Master, it's not that good!]","Not that good, everyone was startled. Combined with what Lord Divine Artifact mentioned earlier, a trace of understanding arose in the hearts of everyone present.","Only Dong Qianli and Wang Shouchen's eyes flickered. This idea of promoting rural breeding was still inspired by the pasture of the Right Martial Guard New Army Camp.","As of now, the promotion effect was good. Except for large livestock such as pigs, cattle, and sheep, the common people could still afford to raise chickens, ducks, geese, and rabbits, these small domestic animals.","During the New Year, every household could also add a plate of meat dishes to improve their lives. The two never expected that this dish might be their former colleagues or enemies.","The two leaned closer together. This topic... is really getting more and more underworld, isn't it!","But they wouldn't regret it! The drought that began in the eighth year of Yuankang, although Lord Junior Preceptor didn't go into detail, they always felt it wasn't that simple. A word 'locust' always lingered in their minds.","If the common people raised more chickens and ducks, perhaps when the time really came, they could resist a little.","So this matter still had to be vigorously promoted.","[They are all reincarnating as poultry and livestock. Going to reincarnate now, by the end of the year, they will go back again.]","Going back again by the end of the year is because they were served on the table!","It's really underworld enough!","Countless thoughts surged in everyone's hearts. Could every bite of meat they eat in the future possibly be the next life of their old acquaintances?","The entire court, as the topic of the two ancestors became more and more underworld, once again fell into a bizarre silence.","Yu Chongshan was also very helpless. He really tried his best!","\"Beloved subjects, are there any good solutions?\"","Following Emperor Mingxi's question, the ministers fell into deep thought, frowning one by one as if thinking hard for a solution.","[Master, Fourth Master Xie has already arrived at the Home-Viewing Pavilion, do you want to see?]","\"System, can you really broadcast the affairs of the underworld live? Are they not images obtained from other places?\" She had just accepted that this ancient world had an underworld, and the system was playing so big. She was really a little afraid that she wouldn't scare the Great Yan monarchs and ministers in a while, but instead would scare herself.","Just like watching a horror movie, although a group of people watching together does embolden one, it doesn't mean one is truly unafraid.","There is always one who screams the loudest in the crowd, could it possibly be herself!","[Host, I can indeed broadcast it live, but considering that it consumes too much energy, I used AI to regenerate what I saw once.","I guarantee a reproduction rate of over 90%, do you dare to look?]","\"Look, what's there to be afraid of!\" Saying so, her actions were very honest as she shrank back into the chair. It could be said that her actions highly reproduced herself watching a horror movie with friends.","\"Little Zhu, let's take a look then!\"","As Yue Fuguang's words fell, apart from herself, others could not tell that it was an AI-produced image. Like water waves, after rippling out layers of ripples, a scene that the Great Yan monarchs and ministers had never seen before slowly emerged above this court.","Quack!","Minister of Personnel Ji Hongming, who was about to step out of the ranks to report, looked up and just saw Xie Zhiwei, who had been dead for many days, standing on a prominent towering stone platform looking back at 'them'!","He didn't utter a single word, directly letting out a duck's cry out of fright."]},{"number":325,"title":"Chapter 325: Your lifespan is not yet exhausted; how have you come to this place","paragraphs":["He quickly covered his mouth and looked around in a panic. He saw that although his colleagues had not let out such an undignified sound as he had, they were all keeping their heads slightly lowered while rolling their eyes upward to sneak peeks at the air. Their lips were pressed tightly together, their faces were drained of color, and their legs were trembling.","He felt slightly relieved. Everyone was terrified, so surely no one had noticed his rather quiet yelp just now!","Seeing his fourth son again, Emperor Mingxi was also quite frightened, looking down at the ministers who were all rolling their eyes upward to stare at the air.","Had he not known the reason, Emperor Mingxi would have absolutely thought these people had collectively taken some sort of eye-rolling, leg-twitching poison.","As for the fact that some of the colleagues next to them could not see the images in the grand hall and only saw their neighbors rolling their eyes as if they were about to drop dead at any moment...","Emperor Mingxi closed his eyes. He did not know how much longer this matter could be kept a secret. However, it had been almost a year since they started hearing these inner thoughts, and they had discussed it many times. Aside from the rule that they must not harbor any malice toward the Junior Preceptor, they had tested various other patterns multiple times, and none of them worked.","Emperor Mingxi sighed. They just did not have the luck to hear the Immortal Lord's inner thoughts. Who could be blamed for that?","Yue Fuguang thought to herself: The system is restricted by its level and does not allow for a full broadcast of inner thoughts. How could I let you all know that?","She would never do something that exposed her own shortcomings!","Yue Fuguang was also watching the incredibly realistic images in the air. She was in no mood to pick a fight and turned a blind eye to the bizarre behavior of the people below.","The Home-Viewing Terrace stood tall in the middle of a desolate and gloomy wilderness. In front of him was a curved water mirror, and at this moment, the scene displayed within it was precisely the court of the Great Yan dynasty.","The flying eaves of the grand hall, the vermilion pillars coiled with dragons, the smoke curling upward from the bronze censers, Emperor Mingxi sitting steadily on the dragon throne upon the vermilion steps, and the Great Yan ministers below, each with their heads bowed.","\"Little Zhu, why am I not in this picture?\"","[He is but a ghost, naturally unworthy of seeing you, an Immortal Lord. The water mirror of the Home-Viewing Terrace also lacks the power to manifest your image, Master.]","Xie Zhiyan looked up, and his reflection in the water mirror in front of Xie Zhiwei also looked up. His eyes met Xie Zhiwei's on the Home-Viewing Terrace.","Separated by space, life, and death, the two brothers exchanged a glance before looking away.","Concubine Xin was the indirect murderer responsible for Xie Zhiyan's death. He was not completely without resentment toward this younger brother who, despite not yet having the chance to commit evil, was undisputedly a pawn of Nanyue.","Just as the ministers saw themselves in the water mirror and were so terrified they did not know what to do, ripples appeared across the image.","Xie Zhiwei seemed to be pulled by an invisible force, drawing him gently yet irresistibly down from the high terrace and plunging him into the deeper, darker heart of the underworld, the Field of Oblivion.","The sorrowful wails of the Home-Viewing Terrace quickly blurred behind him, replaced by a boundless, hazy gray wilderness.","No grass or trees grew on the ground. There were only pale shadows resembling withered reeds, swaying slightly even without any wind, emitting a rustling sound like the murmurs of countless people whispering and then forgetting.","The intense grief on the faces of the wandering souls walking here gradually turned into sluggishness and bewilderment. Xie Zhiwei was no exception.","Watching the increasingly eerie scenes in the projection, the crowd silently huddled together.","Yue Fuguang cast an envious glance and could not help but talk to the system to ease her fear.","\"Little Zhu, I remember that at the end of the wilderness, it should be the River of Forgetfulness, right?\"","[Master, it is indeed time for the Sanzu River. Look, is there not a river right there?]","Everyone looked over in unison. A large river appeared at the end of the wilderness. The river water was neither clear nor murky, but rather a tranquil, dark gold color, as if molten bronze and evening mist had been blended together.","The water flowed slowly, yet it seemed bottomless.","The riverbanks were lined with bright red spider lilies that had no visible beginning or end. These blooming, fiery flowers were the only vibrant scenery in this world.","Further ahead, they saw the only bridge over the river. On the bridge stood a stone tablet inscribed with the name Naihe.","\"Little Zhu, does Meng Po's soup still taste the same?\"","[Master, it will not change for eight hundred years. However, once her daughter Sanqi takes over the position of Meng Po, perhaps the taste will change.]","Soon, the crowd followed Xie Zhiwei past the Ridge of Vicious Dogs, the Mountain of Golden Roosters, and the Silent Forest, arriving at a magnificent, formidable complex of massive palaces that could not be measured by the standards of the living world.","He appeared abruptly beneath a dark red sky.","The palaces were neither wood nor stone; the material resembled black jade and dark iron, gleaming with a cold, hard luster.","The flying eaves and brackets were like the sharp claws of monsters, reaching into the stagnant, gloomy clouds.","In front of the hall was the boundlessly wide Mirror of Retribution Terrace. The high-hanging mirror was not for looking back at one's homeland, but to illuminate a soul's lifelong sins, revealing every tiny detail so that nothing could hide.","Below the mirror terrace were long, seemingly endless steps.","Each step seemed heavier than the last.","Countless souls were climbing upward silently and with great difficulty. On both sides stood tall, faceless ghost wardens holding various oddly shaped weapons and chains.","Their expressions were solemn, their gazes like lightning, looking down to scan every passing soul. Suddenly, as if sensing something, they raised their eyes and looked over.","This glance met the widened, terrified eyes of the Great Yan sovereign and his ministers.","Yue Fuguang was also startled by the sudden stare. She swallowed hard, trying to steady her voice as she said, \"We have finally reached the Palace of Yama. Little Zhu, where is Lord Yama?\"","As her words fell, the colossal palace doors, like the mouth of an abyss, slowly opened.","Inside was deep and dark. One could only faintly make out the outlines of ten massive desks, as well as an unknown, flickering area deeper within.","As a judge whose face was indistinct but who was vaguely dressed as a scholar slowly opened the Book of Life and Death, an invisible, chilling aura of death swept over them.","[Master, based on Xie Zhiwei's actions in this life, a minor character like him does not require Lord Yama to appear.]","\"Xie Zhiwei, according to the records in the Book of Life and Death, your mortal lifespan has not yet ended. Why have you come here?\"","The judge's voice was cold as he held the Book of Life and Death and flipped through a few more pages.","\"Why is your evil karma reduced by so much? Killing brothers and harming sisters, indiscriminately slaughtering ministers and commoners, carrying the lives of tens of thousands on your back, nearly causing a precarious dynasty to overturn...\"","Sentence by sentence, the judge listed the crimes Xie Zhiwei was supposed to commit but had not had the chance to because of his premature death.","\"A heaven-ordained, unforgivable villain actually died before he even had the chance to cause chaos. How truly interesting!\"","Even while saying it was interesting, the judge's hands did not stop as he wrote and drew in the Book of Life and Death.","\"Go line up for reincarnation!\" With a grand wave of the judge's sleeve, a powerful gust of wind struck, sweeping Xie Zhiwei out of the hall in the blink of an eye.","The projection of the grand hall disappeared along with him. Emperor Mingxi and his ministers, having seen the legendary Palace of Yama, the judge, and the Book of Life and Death they cared about most, were unable to snap out of their daze for quite some time.","They all looked dumbfounded, seemingly lost in disappointment, filled with fear yet harboring a hidden sense of anticipation... especially since everyone's heart was itching to know whether they were among the ministers that the judge mentioned Xie Zhiwei would indiscriminately slaughter.","Furthermore, what were their merits recorded in the Book of Life and Death... and how much mortal lifespan did they have left?","If someone destined to die early had their fate changed and defied the heavens due to the Junior Preceptor's appearance, did that mean their own lifespans had changed as well?!"]},{"number":326,"title":"Chapter 326: Do They Still Have Ambitions for the Throne","paragraphs":["Everyone's minds were racing with countless thoughts, yet on the surface, they pretended to listen intently to their colleagues reporting recent political affairs in the royal court.","\"Little Zhu, Xie Zhiwei was taken out before he even had the chance to do evil. Do you think Second Brother Xie and Xie San will still scheme against each other to fight for the position of Crown Prince?","In the original timeline, when their rivalry was at its peak, Fourth Master Xie seized the opportunity to cripple them both, and the two fools even thought it was the other's doing.","Now that Fourth Master Xie is gone, what will their fate be?\"","Hearing this, Xie Zhimin and Xie Zhixin unconsciously leaned closer to the Crown Prince. They were now the Crown Prince's good younger brothers; fighting for the throne had absolutely nothing to do with them!","Seeing his two younger brothers' subtle movements, Xie Zhiyan couldn't help but curl his lips into a smile.","As long as he didn't die, none of his younger brothers, no matter who they were, would ever have a chance.","He was no longer the figurehead Crown Prince of the past, who would tremble in fear and worry about losing his position the moment his imperial father gave him the cold shoulder!","Not to mention the support of the courtiers and his growing reputation among the common people due to the establishment of factories, just having the Junior Preceptor as his greatest backer in the Great Yan dynasty was enough. What did he have to fear?","[Master, these two little pieces of trash have absolutely no chance of ascending to power, nor do they possess the wisdom to rule the realm. They can only live to a ripe old age by peacefully being their princes and lords.","However, it seems they themselves don't want to live peacefully to an old age?]","\"What do you mean? Do they still have ambitions for the throne?\"","Following Yue Fuguang's question, Emperor Mingxi and his officials discreetly glanced at Xie Zhimin and Xie Zhixin, who were already trembling like leaves in the wind, silently and slightly shaking their heads at the Emperor and the Crown Prince.","Seeing their eyes turning red with anxiety, Emperor Mingxi cursed inwardly. Two useless things! They were almost scared to death by just a few words from the Divine Artifact. They truly didn't act like his offspring!","Thinking back to those years, how his imperial father treated him...","[There is something you don't know, Master. Recently, quite a few low-ranking officials have sought refuge under them. Even among the lords in this court, there are a few who want to gamble on the much more difficult merit of supporting a new emperor!","After all, the rougher the seas, the more expensive the fish!]","Yue Fuguang said nonchalantly, \"Low-ranking officials can't make any big waves. Tell me first, who among this court of civil and military officials has such great ambitions?","Seeing that Xie Zhiyan's position as Crown Prince is secure, they still want to pull him down.\"","Xie Zhiyan faked a cough, subtly leaning his body and turning his head halfway to quickly scan the civil and military officials behind him.","Emperor Mingxi's expression cleared up a bit, and he raised an eyebrow. He also really wanted to know who could be so brave in the Great Yan court today, with the Junior Preceptor keeping watch.","Having seen the sights of the Underworld today, although they hadn't had time to think too deeply about it, Emperor Mingxi and his officials had to admit that while the scenes had truly shocked them,","from this moment on, it constantly warned them: only by doing good deeds would they have a future!","Otherwise, when they died one day, the Book of Life and Death wouldn't cover up a single thing for them!","[Master, didn't Little Zhu tell you before that Zhang Tingji wanted Fourth Master Xie as his son-in-law? It's a pity that Fourth Master Xie died early. Now the Zhang family has set their sights on the two brothers, Xie Zhixin and Xie Zhimin.]","\"I remember that Second Brother Xie's primary princess consort was chosen to be the daughter of his uncle, Fu Hong. Although Fu Hong was executed for corruption and perverting the law, and the Fu family is visibly declining,","their marriage arrangement doesn't seem to have changed. They are just waiting for the Fu family's young lady to finish her mourning period before getting married.","Xie San seems to be engaged to Consort De's niece from her maiden family. This young lady from the Bai family is said to be well-educated and reasonable, with an excellent reputation in her inner chambers.","Moreover, coming from a prestigious family, it's impossible for her to step aside to make room for the Zhang family's daughter, right?\"","Thinking of his cousin from his uncle's family, Xie Zhimin couldn't help but frown.","His uncle's betrayal was a thorn in his heart that could never be pulled out. If it weren't for his mother suppressing him, how could a daughter of the Fu family—which now only had two or three minor officials of the sixth or seventh rank left in its clan—still be a good match for him, a dignified Second Prince?","It was only because he had gradually extinguished his desire for the throne. Otherwise, even if his mother forbade it, he would have had plenty of ways to demote a wife to a concubine.","He only dared to entertain this thought in his heart for a brief moment, absolutely terrified that the Junior Preceptor might notice even a hint of it. Otherwise, he would be the one standing on the Home-Viewing Pavilion in the Underworld at a young age!","It had to be said that what he saw and heard today had a huge deterrent effect on Xie Zhimin.","The Book of Life and Death made him afraid to easily harbor malicious thoughts of taking people's lives again. Perhaps, as the Junior Preceptor said, peacefully being his prince and lord was also a good choice. In that case, whether his primary wife's maiden family could provide support was no longer that important.","As long as his Fu family cousin was obedient, it would be fine! Just as he was thinking of accepting his marriage, the voice of the Divine Artifact echoed in his ears.","[Master, it is precisely because of Fu Hong's death that Zhang Tingji feels his opportunity has come. He wants to poach from the Fu family and push his own daughter into the position of the Second Prince's primary consort.","He and the Zhang family behind him will be the Second Prince's greatest reliance.","As long as Second Brother Xie shows his value, the marriage network carefully woven by the Zhang family will also become his support.]","\"I remember that a few days ago, the Zhang family's in-laws somehow angered the Emperor and were successively dismissed from office or banished far away from the capital.","Can the Zhang family's in-laws still exert any influence?\"","Some officials' eyes flickered, thinking of those women of unknown origins in their inner courtyards whom they had given money to and sent away to be married...","Their Emperor hadn't dismissed or demoted all of the Zhang family's in-laws. Only those who truly participated in the fight for the throne had suffered. The rest of them were completely safe and hadn't been affected in the slightest.","[Drawing empty promises, who doesn't know how to do that? Maybe Second Brother Xie, who wants to be the emperor, was moved by it!]","Xie Zhimin hurriedly shook his head in terror at Emperor Mingxi. He wasn't, he didn't, the Divine Artifact was talking nonsense!","Wuwuwu, Xie Zhimin wept silently in his heart. He was so deeply wronged!","Although he had indeed wanted to break off the engagement with his cousin and even used the excuse that close-relative marriage was bad for future generations, he really hadn't fallen for the empty promises Zhang Tingji painted for him.","He knew that with the inner voice of the Junior Preceptor as evidence, the Zhang family's good days wouldn't last long. How could he possibly jump into their pit, which was even bigger than the Fu family's!","Wanting to be the emperor was merely a delusion from before the Junior Preceptor appeared. After the Junior Preceptor arrived, day by day he heard about spies here, rebels there, and remnants of the previous dynasty plotting to restore their nation...","Case after case, which of these could be solved with his level of intelligence?","Although he still occasionally thought about the supreme throne during his midnight dreams, it was just a passing thought. After today's free tour of the Underworld, he felt that he would walk more carefully in the future, terrified of even stepping on an ant!","[And there's Xie San. Although Zhang Tingji quickly ruled him out, Qu Yuan of the Capital Camp Commandery has set his sights on Xie San.","Master doesn't know this Qu Yuan, but if I mention Qu Tong, does Master have an impression?","He is the uncle of Qu Wenxin, the man Yu Ningrong was originally supposed to marry.","Qu Tong was dismissed from office and stripped of his duties last year because he angered His Majesty.","As the direct lineage of the Qu family, they were also somewhat affected. So Qu Yuan thought of clinging to a powerful backer through marriage, and after looking around, he set his eyes on the position of Xie San's secondary consort."]},{"number":327,"title":"Chapter 327: The Crown Prince isn't even dead yet, and you can't wait to jump the gun","paragraphs":["[And that Supervising Secretary of the Six Ministries, do not look down on him just because he is only a seventh-rank official; ambition does not distinguish between high and low ranks.","He also wanted to betroth his sister to Xie San, who told Xie San to enjoy composing poems and associating with literati and scholars on normal days.","This attracted a group of people from humble backgrounds who clearly had no talent but felt they were geniuses.","Their hearts were higher than the sky, unwilling to be ordinary, always having an overarching ambition to climb up. What could yield greater returns than the merit of supporting a new emperor from the very beginning?]","The sovereign and ministers of the Great Yan dynasty nodded silently. Regardless of whether those people could succeed, just speaking of the merits, one could bring honors to their wives and sons, and be appointed as marquises and chancellors.","Apart from the merit of following the Great Ancestor to conquer the world from scratch and establish a dynasty, the next greatest was the merit of supporting a new emperor!","And at this moment, Xie Zhixin, who was called out, finally personally felt the helplessness and terror that his second brother had just endured from their imperial father's coercion and the inexplicable glances swept over by the ministers, intentionally or unintentionally.","He was actually guiltier than Xie Zhimin. After all, unlike his second brother, his wife's family and mother's family were deeply tied together as maternal relatives.","Behind him stood his maternal grandfather's Cui family, an aristocratic family with a heritage of three to four hundred years, and his fiancée's Bai family also had a heritage of two to three hundred years. Both families had many civil officials and scholars over the generations, and their ancestors had even sat in the position of chancellor in the previous dynasty.","The first top scholar in the imperial examination at the founding of Great Yan came from the Bai family. When his imperial father was still the crown prince, in order to gain the support of the Cui and Bai families as well as the scholarly circles, he took his mother and Consort De into the palace.","If it were not for the Junior Preceptor pressing down from above, Xie Zhixin had to put away his ambitions. He was very certain that he would definitely fight his second brother for the throne, just like in the original historical timeline.","But now there were three great mountains pressing on his head: first, the Crown Prince; second, his imperial father; and the biggest one was Junior Preceptor Yue Fuguang.","He could ignore the first and curry favor with the second, but as for The Immortal Lord, she seemed to have no flaws or weaknesses at all, and her temperament was even more unpredictable. He had no way of pleasing or manipulating her.","Thinking of this, Xie Zhixin swallowed hard. Looking up, he met the Junior Preceptor's half-smiling eyes.","Yue Fuguang: Little brat, if it were not for the newly refreshed mission prompt, she would have almost forgotten about the two brothers who had been playing dumb.","It was also because her missions had gone too smoothly that she underestimated the people of the world.","Daring to play tricks in front of her, then today she would use a real ghost to scare them!","\"Xie Zhixin and Xie Zhimin, are they impatiently jumping out before the Crown Prince is even dead?\"","[They are now equivalent to the hope of the whole village. Whether they truly want it in their hearts or not, they have already been propped up by the people below.","People want the merit of supporting a new emperor, so they will push the two to fight.","Especially Xie Zhixin, his maternal grandfather and wife's family are both of aristocratic origin. The assassination of the Fourth Prince and the Ninth Prince had the shadows and silver of these two families behind it.","After all, the Cui and Bai families are very happy to eliminate two competitors for Xie the Third.]","Hearing that the Cui and Bai families had actually participated in the assassination of Xie Si and Xie Jiu behind his back, Xie Zhixin, who originally had a bit of a fluke mentality to muddle through, completely panicked!","He suddenly looked up, meeting his imperial father's sharp eyes and the bloodthirsty smile curling at the corners of his mouth. At this moment, Xie Zhixin felt as if he were standing on the vast and dead Homeland-Viewing Platform in place of Xie Zhiwei.","Before this, he was clearly the victim. Who could tell him how, in just a short while, he had become the perpetrator!","Xie Zhixin thought with a pale face, the disadvantage of the Cui and Bai families was exactly that few high-ranking officials attending the court sessions could hear the Junior Preceptor's inner thoughts.","Of the three people from the two families who could stand in the court, every single one of them had never heard a tiny bit.","Even when facing the often bizarre atmosphere in the court, they never thought deeply about it, still holding onto the plaque of their century-old aristocratic families with complacency.","Looking down on those ministers who rose from humble backgrounds and the civil and military officials who started with the Great Ancestor.","Calling them mud-legs and upstarts!","Now it was great, boasting of wide connections and being well-informed, yet they were excluded from the biggest secret and opportunity of this court.","At this time, Xie Zhixin did not dare to look back at his two uncles and prospective father-in-law.","Although the three of them were not yet the heads of their families, they were all younger generations entrusted with heavy responsibilities by their respective family heads. It was impossible for them to be completely ignorant of the hired killings.","Meanwhile, Cui Quan, Cui Shu, and Bai Jingyuan were also slowly realizing that something was wrong.","What did it mean that their colleagues standing next to them were silently moving away from them?","Just now, they had acted like they had seen a ghost, but the three of them had not made it that obvious. Why were these people acting like this now?","Along with their small movements, a sudden panic inexplicably arose in the three of them.","Their necks felt cold, and why did they have the illusion that their heads were about to fall off?","Feeling guilty but unable to find the source, the three carefully peeked upward, only to meet Emperor Mingxi's sharp gaze and the faint murderous intent hidden within.","In an instant, a cold sweat broke out on their backs, and the great hall felt three degrees colder than before.","Cui Quan thought things were going to turn bad and silently prepared to enter the palace after the morning court to seek an audience with his niece, Consort Rong, to sound her out.","Recently, it seemed the Cui family had not done anything excessive other than making a move against the Fourth and Ninth Princes.","But their Emperor had always been muddle-headed and surely would not find out those things were related to them!","\"Little Zhu, are you saying that the deaths of Xie Si and Xie Jiu are related to the Cui and Bai families?\"","Although these two both had reasons to die, and they did indeed take the blame for her, they died before they had time to commit any sins.","As a bystander and beneficiary, she could casually mention that their early death was better than dying later, but Yue Fuguang would not disregard this favor because of it.","So, while completing the task of cleaning up the aristocratic families, avenging the two of them was just a convenient side task.","[It is indeed inextricably linked. Master, the Great Yan Dynasty has eight major aristocratic families and twelve minor ones.","The word minor here is in comparison to the eight major families, which have a heritage of three to four hundred years, possessing massive wealth and cultural lineage.","In fact, the minor families are also behemoths to many people.]","Yue Fuguang nodded. As the saying goes, a starved camel is still bigger than a horse; the minor families were not something declining humble families could compare to.","[To protect their own interests, these aristocratic families formed an alliance to resist imperial power and anyone who damages their interests.]","\"Because the papermaking and printing techniques dug up the roots of their control over the cultural lineage, they assassinated Xie Si and Xie Jiu, who took the blame for me?\"","[It indeed started because of the printing and papermaking techniques, but the Cui and Bai families exerted the most effort, also because it involved the battle for the succession.","Without these two families fueling the flames, they would not still be holding onto it after the printing and papermaking techniques became an established fact.","The interior of the aristocratic families is not a monolith either. On the surface, led by the Cui and Bai families, they support Xie San, who has aristocratic bloodlines."]},{"number":328,"title":"Chapter 328: Which brother do you get along with best in your daily life","paragraphs":["But the other families were also secretly placing their bets behind the scenes. The Emperor's sons, except for those still nursing, had all been invested in by them.","No matter who ascended the throne in the future, the interests of the noble families would not be affected. ]","The Emperor's face turned ashen. His sons were fighting to the death, but the ultimate beneficiaries were outsiders!","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers couldn't help but think of roosters fighting to the death in a cockfight, while the noble families were the spectators who had placed their bets, standing outside the ring waving flags and cheering...","In the royal court, the four brothers, including the Crown Prince, Second Brother Xie, Xie San, and Fifth Brother Xie, kept a wooden expression as they bore the increasing number of gazes cast upon them. They appeared calm, but in reality, they had already cursed the ancestors of those noble families a thousand times over in their hearts.","The second and third brothers both wanted to go back after court and stick pins into voodoo dolls!","The brothers had indeed received quite a few tributes from the noble families over the years, but they never expected them to have such a plan, placing bets on multiple sides.","Xie Zhiyan's lips curled up slightly. Among the brothers, perhaps he was the only one who always knew that while the noble families sent gifts to the Eastern Palace, the other brothers would also receive gifts of corresponding value based on their level of favor with their imperial father.","Before this year, other than him, the one who received the most gifts was their Ninth Brother, whom they had jointly assassinated.","\"Did Xie San know about this?\"","[ Does Master mean the assassination? Then Xie San really didn't know.","Actually, as for the Cui and Bai families, although one is Xie San's maternal grandfather's family and the other is his future princess consort's maiden family, both vigorously support him solely because of mutual interests.","But truth be told, the only ones who might have genuine feelings for him are his maternal grandmother and his fiancée, Bai Nianzhu. ]","Xie Zhixin clenched his fists, thinking of his daily interactions with his cousins, and the earnest teachings of his maternal grandfather and uncles with faces full of affection.","Could it be that all of this was fake?","Their kindness to him was all because he was the Emperor's son, not because he was his mother's son, the only child born to their only daughter/sister!","Then the love his grandfather and uncles showed for his mother, was that also fake...","A cold smile touched the corners of Xie Zhixin's mouth. He had thought wrong. What family that truly loved their daughter would send her into the palace when they had a choice?","In vain, he had previously been complacent that he had two great noble families standing behind him. This confidence was something even his Crown Prince brother couldn't match, whose maternal family was the military Xu family and whose Crown Princess came from the ordinary scholarly Shen family.","\"Then Xie San definitely doesn't know this fact either, otherwise he wouldn't consider himself a cut above the rest of his brothers. In this battle for the throne, he also has the power to fight.\"","Standing on his left and right, Xie Zhimin and Xie Zhiquan both turned their heads to look at him, a glint of sharpness unconsciously revealing itself in their eyes.","Well played, you thick-eyebrowed, big-eyed Xie the Third! It turns out your usual brotherly affection was all an act!","You don't even look at the facts. We are all cubs of the same father. Except for the Crown Prince brother, who is both the legitimate and eldest son, among the rest of the brothers, who is nobler than whom?","How dare you look down on us. Kid, if you have the guts, don't leave after court!","Hmph, still wanting to fight for the throne. With them around, other than the Crown Prince brother, no one else should even dream of ascending!","In the eyes of Second Brother Xie and Fifth Brother Xie, Xie Zhiyan's succession was perfectly justifiable. If any other brother went up, they would not submit.","Xie Zhixin shrank his neck under the fierce glares of his two brothers. When they were young, who hadn't had fantasies about the chair under their imperial father's bottom?","Hasn't he been slowly changing since the Junior Preceptor appeared?","Facing the instigations of the elders of the Cui and Bai families, who could not hear the Junior Preceptor's inner voice, he no longer had his previous arrogance and the urge to trample everyone else down.","[ His so-called power to fight, this 'power' is not in his own hands at all. Otherwise, the two families wouldn't have non-stop switched their allegiance to the brother who had the best relationship with Xie San and secretly supported his bid for the throne after he was crippled and lost hope for the great position.","However, the Cui and Bai families had good luck. They actually managed to push him onto the throne, and from then on, the new Emperor became a puppet of the noble families.","The carnival of the noble families had begun!","If it weren't for the fact that within two years, the Great Yan was destroyed by an alliance of several families, the Xie dynasty of Great Yan wouldn't have had another generation of monarchs anyway.","In the end, if the Sima family hadn't stolen the country, the throne would have been usurped by another noble family, and it wouldn't be surprising if another Wang Mang appeared. ]","Who Wang Mang was, they had no way of knowing, but from the context, they knew he was someone from a powerful noble family who stole the country and took the throne.","At this moment, Emperor Mingxi and his ministers once again cast a chilling gaze at Xie Zhixin, immediately wanting to know which of his sons he had the best relationship with in private.","Was the identity of the 'new Emperor' they had been thinking about day and night finally going to be revealed?","Looking at the chilling look his old father cast at him, Xie Zhixin really wanted to sing a mournful song for himself.","But he knew it was inconvenient to defend himself at this time, so he could only silently shake his head at Emperor Mingxi. The persona he had previously established was that of a gentle, kind, respectful, frugal, and yielding gentleman.","He showed brotherly affection to every brother, so he really couldn't say who he had the best relationship with.","If we're talking about now, he silently tugged at the hem of the Crown Prince's sleeve. Right now, he and his Crown Prince brother were the best of friends in the world!","As long as he clung tightly to his imperial brother's thigh, it was equivalent to indirectly clinging to the Junior Preceptor's golden thigh.","Xie Zhixin secretly swore that he would still marry Bai Nianzhu, who was devoted to him, but if the Bai family wanted to use him to seize the throne again, he would absolutely not fall for it.","Seeing that Great Yan was about to become powerful, for the rest of his life, it wouldn't be bad to peacefully lose himself in the beauty of nature with his wife and be a wealthy, idle prince.","The grand court assembly ended. After dropping her bombshells, Yue Fuguang patted her bottom and returned to her mountain villa.","Everyone looked at her retreating figure, desperately wanting to reach out an Erkang (reaching out desperately) hand, begging her to say a little more. The Junior Preceptor's update this time was a bit abrupt; it was the first time she had started something without finishing it.","Who knew that Yue Fuguang's heart was as hard as iron, and she was as eager to return home as a flying arrow. Her footsteps unconsciously quickened, and everyone couldn't help but feel that the Junior Preceptor was walking a bit too hastily today.","Whether Yue Fuguang was in a hurry or not, they didn't know, but the royal trio of brothers who were left behind were secretly complaining in their hearts.","Emperor Mingxi didn't have time to care about his sons who still had ambitions for the throne; he only stared intently at Xie the Third.","\"Number Three, tell your imperial father, which brother do you have the best relationship with usually?\"","He looked at Xie Zhixin, who was surrounded in the middle and had been scared almost into the Crown Prince's arms, softened his tone, and continued, \"Number Three, as long as you tell your imperial father honestly today, your imperial father promises to let bygones be bygones regarding your past actions.\"","This promise to let bygones be bygones was indeed tempting to Xie Zhixin. After all, over the years, for the sake of that position, he had not done any less in framing his brothers.","But... he put on a bitter face and said very honestly, \"May Imperial Father see clearly. Your son, your son used to listen to my grandfather and the others, and outwardly always maintained the persona of a respectful and affectionate brother, treating all my brothers equally.","I didn't have a particularly good or particularly bad relationship with anyone.\"","Even with Xie Zhiwei, who had the worst temper among the brothers, he got along quite well on the surface. As for the dirty tricks played in the dark, those didn't count!","He carefully glanced at his imperial father, whose face was growing darker and darker, silently took a small step forward, and carefully added, \"Your son knows that Imperial Father has always hoped for harmony among us brothers.","Therefore, to gain Imperial Father's favor and attention, your son, your son truly acted this way on a daily basis.\""]},{"number":329,"title":"Chapter 329: Is the task panel broken or infected with a virus","paragraphs":["Emperor Mingxi didn't believe it. Since the Divine Artifact said that the son who had a good relationship with the third son took the throne, it absolutely could not be wrong.","Up to now, the Divine Artifact had not been wrong about a single thing, so the one who was wrong could only be Xie the Third!","Emperor Mingxi tried his best to squeeze out a smile, making himself look amiable and approachable, like a loving father.","He stood up and walked over to Xie Zhixin, reaching out a large hand to gently pat his shoulder. Third Son, come, sit down and let's talk. He pointed to a small stool brought over by Qian Gui.","He then sat back down in the chair behind the imperial desk. Seeing Xie Zhixin sitting with trepidation, carefully resting only half of his buttocks on the stool, he sighed softly and continued, Third Son, think carefully again. Which of your younger brothers do you like to play with the most in your daily life?","You also know that your imperial father and the officials rack their brains day and night to govern Great Yan, just out of fear that he might repeat the mistakes of the past and ruin the vast foundation that our Xie ancestors fought so hard to build.","Just in case, we must find out who this new emperor is. Rest assured, even if we find him, your imperial father won't do anything to him before he has actually done anything.","Hearing Emperor Mingxi play the emotional card with him, Xie Zhixin was overwhelmed by the unexpected favor. He actually frowned and thought hard. Ordinarily, he considered himself to be one of the more scheming ones among his brothers.","Therefore, he usually didn't play much with his second, fourth, and fifth brothers. In fact, aside from these few, he had an age gap with his younger brothers and rarely played with them either.","They were all competitors; who could completely trust anyone else!","Imperial Father, is it possible that this brother is someone your son only became close to in later years?","Seeing Emperor Mingxi's face about to darken again, Xie Zhixin quickly added, Imperial Father, judging from the words of the Junior Preceptor and the Divine Artifact, the incident involving your son and Second Brother should happen a few years from now. At that time, your son will have no hope for the throne, and the Cui and Bai families will turn their support elsewhere, so...","Emperor Mingxi and his officials felt that Xie Zhixin's words made some sense, but they were all extremely disappointed with this conclusion.","They thought they were about to find the prince who was pushed onto the stage by the noble families to be a puppet without realizing it, and who ultimately ruined the country despite a burst of diligence, but unexpectedly it was another empty joy.","Although everyone, including Emperor Mingxi as his father, hadn't figured out how to deal with this son once he was found, not knowing who he was inevitably left everyone feeling a bit uneasy.","Anyone who could sit on the throne must have some destiny and luck upon them, so this person had to be guarded against!","Seeing that their imperial father was about to lose his temper again, Xie Zhiyan quickly interjected, Third Son, think about it. If you had to pick one of your brothers to befriend, who would you choose?","Xie Zhixin didn't even think before replying, Then I would definitely choose the Crown Prince!","Faced with his suddenly enthusiastic younger brother who was clearly trying to cling to him, Xie Zhiyan felt helpless. Besides me, who would you choose?","Xie Zhimin and Xie Zhiquan glared at him, their expressions clearly saying: If you dare choose us, see if we don't beat you to death later!","Xie Zhixin silently turned his head and snorted softly, Imperial Father, Imperial Brother, if I really have to choose one, I would choose the seventh brother.","The seventh brother was the most innocent and least scheming of all the brothers. He still preferred hanging out with people who didn't require him to use his brain.","Not the seventh. Before Xie Zhiyan could speak, Xie Zhimin couldn't help but retort.","It is already known that the seventh brother will be tragically killed under a horse by the fourth brother. He won't even live to see Imperial Father pass away, so that new emperor definitely isn't him!","Xie Zhimin spoke faster than his brain could process, blurting out everything he wanted to say all at once.","It was only after seeing Emperor Mingxi's livid face that he belatedly realized what he had just said.","Carelessly talking about his own father's passing while the man was still alive was indeed a bit unfilial!","Xie Zhimin mimicked Xie Zhixin, silently leaning toward the Crown Prince's embrace—Imperial Brother, save my miserable life!","Then it must be the sixth brother. Sixth Brother's birth mother has a lowly background, and he is usually the most honest among us brothers.","Every time he gave him a gift, it was practical gold or silver, and the sixth brother was most in need of such wealth to manage his daily life.","Sixth Brother Zhifei? Emperor Mingxi lowered his eyes in thought. Although this son also frequently attended the morning assembly, his presence was indeed quite low.","Recently, due to the successive wrongful deaths of the fourth and ninth brothers, the sixth brother had been frightened into a severe illness and still hadn't fully recovered.","He hadn't seen that child for some days either.","Emperor Mingxi always felt that the new emperor shouldn't be this timid son.","Why not the fifth, eighth, tenth, or eleventh? He stared intently at Xie Zhixin. Are they not your younger brothers? Why didn't you choose them?","Emperor Mingxi's question was a bit unreasonable, but as a subject and a son, no matter how shameless or unreasonable it was, Xie Zhixin had to treat it seriously.","He replied, Imperial Father, the fifth brother is too smart. He gave Xie Zhiquan an awkward smile and continued, The eighth brother hides his brilliance behind a dull exterior, and he has the best relationship with the seventh brother. He always felt that this younger brother, who had a low presence just like the sixth, was somewhat playing the pig to eat the tiger.","As for the tenth and eleventh, they are only seven years old right now. Your son... your son doesn't like playing with little kids!","The officials were dumbfounded. His Majesty currently had twelve sons, and even with the candidates narrowed down to one out of five, they still couldn't figure out who that person was.","If the Divine Artifact knew this, would it scold them for being useless?","Meanwhile, the System that everyone was thinking about had no time to scold anyone. It was currently staring blankly at the quest panel alongside Yue Fuguang.","System, is the quest panel broken, or is it possible that you've been infected by some unknown virus?","Rolling its eyes, the System retorted, Host, you and I are one entity. Can't you think something good about me? If I were poisoned by a virus, you wouldn't be this clear-headed right now!","I want to think something good too! But look at the quests on this panel, jumping all over the place. It made our revelations today start strong but end weakly.","We didn't say what needed to be said, and we said a bunch of things that didn't matter.","The quest content on the system panel in front of Yue Fuguang was currently flickering, appearing and disappearing, making her dizzy just looking at it.","If it weren't for the fact that the quest progress bar, which looked like a tree full of branches, remained steady without any changes, Yue Fuguang would have been much more worried. This gave her slight reassurance.","Otherwise, she wouldn't be able to stay this calm while watching the words dance on the panel with the System.","After watching for a while, Yue Fuguang's eyes were nearly blinded by the flickering. She couldn't help but tap the system panel. If it doesn't stop, are we still going to do our quests or not?","Seeing that the current situation was excellent, it would be a joke if they didn't have any problems but the system quests dropped the ball first!","Host, don't be anxious! Maybe the system program is just adjusting?","You're the System. Don't you know if the program is adjusting or not?","I... I'm not responsible for issuing quests, so the quest section is uniformly managed by the sub-main program.","In the past, it seemed the systems were the ones issuing quests. However, after a few cases where systems and hosts exploited quest loopholes to cheat for points and rewards, this authority was revoked from the systems.","It still remembered when the host had just transmigrated and couldn't even get close to the quest targets. To save the host's life, tasks like helping an old lady up the stairs in a Daoist temple or finding a lost hairpin for a noblewoman were counted for points—these were specially approved by the Main System upon its request."]},{"number":330,"title":"Chapter 330: Did Wei Ping do it","paragraphs":["[Host, after Tongtong bound with you, we are on the same side. Therefore, some of the system's permissions are also restricted.]","\"Yesterday, a task popped up to eradicate the aristocratic families and noble clans within a year. I remember previously it was fine to take three to five years. And it wasn't eradicate, it was weaken!\"","Yue Fuguang scratched her head. The difference between weakening and eradicating was huge. One meant a few heads rolling, while the other meant heads rolling everywhere.","She knew how to count; the system shouldn't even think about tricking her.","\"There are twenty large and small aristocratic families. How many people are in them and associated with them? If I really have to eradicate them all, wouldn't a river of blood have to be shed?\"","She was afraid that when the time came, the voices of opposition in the royal court would not be few. They were all of the same class, how could she not understand the principle of the fox mourning the death of the hare?","Thinking of so many human lives, Yue Fuguang looked at her hands. Although she often shouted about fighting and killing on normal days, if she really had to do it, she could handle thirty to fifty people.","But starting with a baseline of thirty to fifty thousand, she felt she could not accept it right now.","I did not kill Boren, but Boren died because of me. She... she felt she still needed some time.","[Host, don't worry, I will ask the main system. Don't carry such a heavy psychological burden either. You have seen the harm of the aristocratic families; in the later stages, it will be a dance of demons.","These people betrayed the country for their own glory and aided the wicked. If they hadn't been partially wiped out by the peasant army later, and then partially killed by the subsequent royal court out of wariness, with these pests around, the world would have been in chaos for far more than three hundred years!]","Seeing Yue Fuguang still puffing her cheeks, it continued, [I am just afraid that while we are expanding the territory on the front lines, these people will cause destruction in the rear.","With them around, many of your ideas will face heavy obstacles when implemented.","Of course, even if this task is not completed, it doesn't matter. All in all, this task is only worth over a hundred thousand points!]","Speaking of points, Yue Fuguang suddenly felt that the system had grabbed her by the lifeline. \"How can there be so many?\"","This was enough points for her to buy one-tenth of the top-tier aptitude!","This time the system mall opened, and for the first time in the special items section, she refreshed various materials for reshaping the body, including aptitude.","The mall had abundant resources. It could be said that as long as there were enough points, there were very few things in this world that could not be bought!","\"So the aristocratic families must die?\"","[The main branches must be eradicated, and the side branches must at least be scattered. Host, for humanity to develop, wealth and knowledge cannot always remain in the hands of a few.","It is one thing if they do not conform to the tide of the era's development, but they even become an obstacle...]","What the system didn't say was that illegitimate children in her hometown could normally inherit family property now; had she never thought about the reason?","Its host probably didn't know yet, but her father had raised three younger siblings outside to fight for her property!","Then again, it was a merit system after all. The tasks issued by the headquarters system to send these people to their deaths were also carefully calculated; it was definitely a matter where the benefits outweighed the disadvantages.","Only when the people of the aristocratic families died would there be a way out for thousands of ordinary commoners. If the tumor was not removed, it would eventually become a disaster.","In the past, the host always talked about how ruthless she was, shouting about fighting and killing all day long.","Now that it was truly a critical moment, she actually wanted to drop the ball.","Yue Fuguang: Are the lives of a few hundred or a few thousand people the same as tens or hundreds of thousands?","However, Yue Fuguang thought about the path she had to take in the future. It seemed that tens of thousands of people were just an appetizer. Expanding territory and unifying the land, how could there be no deaths? This wasn't playing house!","After figuring it out, she slapped the table hard with her small hand and said, \"Alright, let's do it! Just treat it as practice, treat it as building courage for future conquests!\"","Holding her red and throbbing hand, Yue Fuguang once again silently accepted the fact that she was indeed not a good person!","...","Half a month later, Yue Fuguang, who was preparing to open fire on the aristocratic families, finally welcomed the right opportunity in the royal court.","The former Junior Minister of the Court of Judicature and Revision, Acting Minister Wei Ping, finally had the word \"Acting\" removed from his title five days before his thirty-eighth birthday, officially being promoted to Minister of the Court of Judicature and Revision.","It could be considered like a daughter-in-law enduring for years to finally become the mother-in-law.","Listening to Eunuch Qian read out Wei Ping's achievements over the past year, Yue Fuguang rubbed her hands together. Every single item and sentence didn't mention her, but everything was related to her.","Although it looked like she was handing him merits, look at the Wei Ping from a year ago and the Wei Ping now.","A year ago, at thirty-seven, he looked a few years younger than his actual age, full of vigor and spirit.","But after this year, counting the fine lines that had newly crept onto Wei Ping's face, saying he was forty would be a compliment.","\"Little Zhu, so Wei Ping has always been the Junior Minister? I thought he was the Minister!\"","After all, he had always been the one handling the political affairs of the Court of Judicature and Revision. The position of Minister had always been vacant, and his colleagues rarely called him Junior Minister Wei.","[Master, after his predecessor passed away two years ago, Wei Ping has always held the position of Acting Minister.]","\"Who was his predecessor? Why has such an important position as the Minister of the Court of Judicature and Revision been vacant for so long?\"","[Master, the former Minister was named Xu Anzhi. On the surface, he died of illness, but that's actually not the case!]","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers all felt their eyelids twitch. They instinctively sensed that Minister Xu's death was definitely not simple. Based on their understanding of the Divine Artifact, such an opening remark meant there must be something fishy inside.","\"Little Zhu, then tell me, how did he actually die?\"","[Master, this Xu Anzhi naturally died of poisoning, and it was a chronic poison.","The symptoms looked like physical weakness caused by illness. Even a highly skilled imperial physician like Sun Huajing might not necessarily be able to find out that he was poisoned rather than sick.","After all, a characteristic of that poison is that it magnifies the defects in the poisoned person's body, draws out their hidden root causes of illness, slowly worsens their symptoms, and finally leads to death beyond medical cure.","If he could have met a Taoist doctor who understood medicine and poison like Xuanmingzi, he could have lived for a few more years. What a pity!]","Wei Ping silently clenched his fists, a thin layer of sweat forming on his palms. He could not help but think of the few months before Minister Xu passed away...","\"Who wanted to harm him? This has nothing to do with Wei Ping, right? After all, looking at it now, after Xu Anzhi died, he is the biggest beneficiary.\"","His immediate superior was gone, and he was favored by the Emperor. As long as he worked a little harder, he could take the position. No matter how you looked at it, he was suspicious.","Especially given their positions, wanting to quietly kill a few people was right up their professional alley, so it shouldn't be difficult.","Hearing Yue Fuguang's baseless speculation and a huge scapegoat pot dropping right on his head, Wei Ping nearly choked to death on his own saliva.","No, Junior Preceptor, don't you know what kind of person I, Wei Ping, am? Am I the kind of person who would use any means necessary to climb up?","Xu Anzhi was not only his superior but also his friend. Both of them were obsessed with solving mysteries and cracking cases, and could be said to have a relationship of mentor and helpful friend. How could he kill someone for a mere Minister position!","[This time Master guessed wrong. Xu Anzhi's death was not Wei Ping's doing.]","Wei Ping: Kneeling to thank the Divine Artifact for clearing my name! Lighting incense JPG.","[However...] Wei Ping's heart, which hadn't completely settled down, was suspended again. Everyone knew that nothing good ever followed a \"However\"!","[However, it was more or less caused because of him.]"]},{"number":331,"title":"Chapter 331: Silence the Witness","paragraphs":["Wei Ping: No, how did this start because of me? Can you finish it all at once? Lord Artifact, your way of pausing mid-sentence is really going to kill someone from anxiety.","Didn't you see that his colleagues' looks at him had already changed?","If Lord Artifact keeps doing this, he won't have any friends left!","Yue Fuguang saw the deep resentment radiating from him, chuckled inwardly, and acted as his mouthpiece, asking, \"Little Zhu, where did this come from? What exactly did Wei Ping do?\"","Wei Ping: I also want to know what I did!","[Master, do you remember Ling Langshan, whom I mentioned before? He was the elder in Ling Yuanhang's clan, the one with the highest official rank in the Ling family. Xu Anzhi was murdered using the exact same methods because the people behind the scenes noticed him investigating that case from many years ago.]","Hearing the name Ling Langshan, Wei Ping was no longer the only one getting anxious; Ling Yinghua was now added to the mix.","He had not forgotten for a single day what Lord Artifact had said: his own father's death was also foul play, caused by his close association with Ling Langshan.","\"What does that case from years ago have to do with Wei Ping? Was Ling Langshan's death Wei Ping's doing?\"","Clang!","Yue Fuguang had just dropped another massive scapegoat pot right onto Wei Ping's head. The bitterness in his heart felt like it was rising up to his throat!","There was not a trace of joy from his recent promotion and newfound wealth on Wei Ping's face.","He looked like a wrinkled bitter gourd, tears welling up in his eyes. He had proof that the Junior Preceptor was deliberately targeting him!","[Not exactly. But Wei Ping, as the former Left Case Reviewer of the Dali Court, had participated multiple times in investigating the deaths of the Ling family members.","After he was promoted all the way to Deputy Minister of the Dali Court by Xu Anzhi, the two often discussed difficult cases, inevitably bringing up the Ling family death cases from seven or eight years ago.","Wei Ping shared his suspicion that Ling Langshan's death was not from illness, but murder.","He even suspected that the deaths of his entire family were abnormal; Ling Langshan was likely the first Ling family member to be murdered, marking the beginning rather than the end.","It wasn't as outsiders speculated, that the Ling descendants lost their protection upon Ling Langshan's death and were thus targeted. He guessed it was the work of the same group of people.]","Reminded by Lord Artifact, Wei Ping suddenly recalled that more than two years ago, he had indeed discussed this matter with Chief Minister Xu, but it was merely a guess at the time.","Because there was no way to verify it, he had put it out of his mind. If Lord Artifact hadn't brought it up today, he would have forgotten all about it.","Could it be that Brother Xu took his guess to heart and secretly investigated it himself?","No wonder for the few months after that, he seemed to become suddenly very busy, and the time they spent drinking tea and discussing cases lessened.","Especially in the month before his death, he refused to see him much. Could it be that he sensed danger then, and so...","\"Did Xu Anzhi find out something that threatened the people behind the scenes, leading to his murder?\"","[Master, didn't Little Zhu tell you at the beginning of the month that the Cui and Bai families hired assassins to kill Xie Si and Xie Jiu?","To be honest, the Cui and Bai families, being the lowest-ranked among the Eight Great Noble Families.","In terms of murder and taking lives, they are indeed a bit sloppy. Compared to the professional precision of the top few families, they are far behind!]","As soon as these words were spoken, Xie San, also known as Xie Zhixin, became another person whose eyelids began to twitch.","He had thought it strange this morning when he learned the Junior Preceptor would attend the court assembly, feeling an inexplicable sense of dread. So this was what was waiting for him!","After these two ancestors dropped their bombshells last time, his imperial father had secretly sent people to investigate the two families. Half a month had passed, and seeing how his father glared at him with utter displeasure every time they met, he knew those two families had committed no shortage of evil deeds.","They weren't far from death anyway. Were these two ancestors just kicking them a couple more times before they died?","Xie Zhixin rubbed his still-healing buttocks. He had wanted to marry Bai Nianzhu ahead of time before the Bai family's downfall, but ended up getting his backside kicked by his furious father!","It didn't feel like a father beating his own son at all. With that kind of force, even though a day had passed, it still hurt to the touch.","Xie Zhixin fell silent. His imperial father was definitely taking out his anger towards the Cui and Bai families on him!","\"So, the deaths of Ling Langshan and Xu Anzhi were both the doing of the noble families? And the masterminds might be the Zheng, Wang, Kong, Yang, Yuan, and Li families?\"","[Yes, headed by the Zheng and Wang families, with the other families cooperating. Not only did they poison Ling Langshan and Ling Huayan, who was Chancellor Ling's father.","But they also used accidents to kill off the elite younger generation of the Ling family.","When they realized Xu Anzhi was meticulously unraveling the truth and closing in on them, they silenced him using the same method.","If Xu Anzhi hadn't acted cautiously and kept his mouth shut, preventing those people from finding out that Wei Ping was the first to suspect this matter, the grass on his grave would probably be very tall by now!]","Knowing who had murdered his father, Ling Yinghua was already weeping like rain.","Meanwhile, Wei Ping was filled with guilt and gratitude. He felt he had let down Brother Xu. The two had agreed to investigate the case together and even become in-laws.","Yet, his superior and good friend had died a tragic death because of him, while he was able to survive until now only due to his protection!","His heart felt suffocated, and tears silently rolled down from the corners of his eyes...","\"Little Zhu, although the Ling family is also a century-old family of officials, there is still a gap between them and those top families. They wouldn't have been in their way.","Why did the noble families target the Ling family? Poisoning Ling Langshan wasn't enough; they had to exterminate the younger generation of the Ling family too? It looks very much like they wanted to tear up the roots.\"","In these ancient times, destroying a family's foundation was a massive blood feud, the kind of hatred that would be avenged even after ten generations!","[Master, when Ling Langshan was alive, he reached the position of Left Vice Minister of the Ministry of Works, which is your grandfather's current position.","For a time, he was ordered to inspect the local regions. Among his many responsibilities were the harvesting of mountains and marshes, and the manufacturing of pottery and metalware.]","\"Did his death have anything to do with the harvesting of mountains and marshes, and the manufacturing of metalware?\"","This time, the one whose eyelids twitched was Emperor Mingxi. He also recalled that ten years ago, Ling Langshan had indeed been ordered by him to inspect the local regions.","On the surface, it was to inspect the mining of mountain and marsh minerals in various prefectures across the country. In reality, he had only been on the throne for a few years and had received a report that someone in Yizhou was illegally mining copper.","Because his footing was not yet secure, he had no choice but to order Ling Langshan to use the pretext of inspecting mineral development to secretly investigate the illegal copper mining in Yizhou.","Could it be that Ling Langshan was silenced because he discovered the copper mine?","After more than ten years, was that copper mine still there? He remembered that when Ling Langshan reported back to him, he hadn't said that.","[It was related to the emperor's secret mission. The emperor sent him to the local regions to secretly investigate the illegal copper mining in Yizhou.","To avoid drawing attention, Ling Langshan planned to inspect three states: Lianzhou, Hezhou, and finally Yizhou.","There weren't any major issues in Lianzhou, but upon arriving in Hezhou, Ling Langshan discovered that rich deposits of rock salt might be buried beneath the mudstone and shale.","However, because Emperor Mingxi was rushing him, he had no time for further exploration and had to temporarily drop it.","During his trip to Yizhou, he did indeed find someone illegally mining copper, but it was an old mine that had been abandoned for years. The illegal mining was merely the individual actions of nearby commoners who accidentally discovered a few leftover scraps while quarrying stone to build houses.]"]},{"number":332,"title":"Chapter 332: Salt Mine","paragraphs":["Emperor Mingxi nodded. That was indeed how Ling Langshan had reported it to him at the time.","\"So his death was because he discovered a potential salt mine?\"","Coming from a convenient life in her hometown where salt and sugar were never scarce, Yue Fuguang still could not deeply understand the importance of salt to ancient people's lives, even after being in Great Yan for four years.","To go so far as to wipe out an entire clan and kill all those in the know over a single salt mine was something she, someone used to peaceful days, had never imagined.","\"Is it really worth it for a salt mine? It's not a gold or silver mine, even copper or iron would make more sense!\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's words, the ruler and ministers of Great Yan silently added in their hearts: it is absolutely worth it.","It could be said that among the six nations, there was not a single one that did not lack salt.","Before the Junior Preceptor arrived, the common people were reluctant to use salt in their daily meals, and the salt they did use was bitter and astringent.","The army was still using vinegar cloths, and even the refined green salt consumed by the imperial family could not compare to the Junior Preceptor's snowflake salt.","[Master, Great Yan lacks salt, and Northern Li and Western Qiang lack it even more severely. If they could trade, they would willingly exchange a copper mine for a salt mine.","Eastern Yi is surrounded by the sea and seemingly doesn't lack salt, but due to technological limitations, their production is low. They also trade their surplus salt for money, so even in the coastal Eastern Yi, ordinary people cannot afford to eat salt.","As for Nanzhao and Nanyue, they indeed have salt lakes within their borders, but turning the salt lakes into edible salt still falls short due to technology.","Therefore, even though both nations have treasure mountains, their salt is only enough to supply their own people.","So Great Yan's salt includes sea salt, well salt, and rock salt. It seems like there are many choices, but the domestic edible salt is still insufficient.","Naturally, the value of a rock salt mine is no less than copper or iron.]","\"Speaking of salt refining technology, I heard the Crown Prince say that Great Yan's snowflake salt has already entered the market. I suppose it won't be long before the people of Great Yan can also eat salt without a bitter taste.\"","[Master, aside from the Sima family, in the Central Plains, aristocratic families like Zheng and Wang are the masters behind those big salt merchants. And the salt mine discovered by Ling Langshan had long been scouted by the aristocratic families.","Because of his inspection, they delayed the mining. Unexpectedly, Ling Langshan was intentionally or unintentionally led there by local officials who still had some conscience left, and he discovered the salt mine.","The aristocratic families then joined forces with the salt merchants to secretly silence him before Ling Langshan could confirm the salt mine and report the discovery to the emperor.]","\"Then what does this have to do with the other members of the Ling family? Why did they have to slaughter them all, forcing the new clan leader to retreat and defend their ancestral lands?\"","[Because when Ling Langshan was inspecting at the time, he was accompanied by younger members of his clan. First, to take care of his daily life and safety, and second, to conveniently teach the youths about matters of the people's livelihood.","Master knows that travel is not easy for people nowadays. They cannot be compared to immortals like us, and they fall far short of even the modern era we once visited.","Because traveling alone is unsafe, Ling Langshan brought several clan youths along on that inspection tour, teaching them about the local customs and people's livelihoods along the way to build their experience for entering officialdom in the future.]","Yue Fuguang nodded, very much agreeing with the educational methods for the Ling family youths. \"As the saying goes, reading ten thousand books is not as good as traveling ten thousand miles. This is exactly the principle.\"","Little did she know that Yue Fuguang's heartfelt remark, casually quoting the words of the ancients, would deeply shock Emperor Mingxi and his ministers.","Ling Yinghua, who had been crying endlessly over his father's tragic death, still had tears on his face, but his eyes were wide open. If he hadn't been afraid of being seen by Yue Fuguang, he would have definitely discussed it with his colleagues.","The Junior Preceptor's short sentence revealed that if knowledge cannot be grounded, tested, and grown in practice, and is merely empty talk confined to a small corner of the world, then it has no meaning whatsoever.","For scholars pursuing an official career, theory and practice, knowledge and experience are equally important.","\"To see the world, to see all living beings, is ultimately to see oneself. What the Ling family youths did actually shares a similar purpose with you and me descending to the mortal realm to experience trials.\"","[Indeed! It is a pity for those ignorant Ling family youths who died unjustly just because of a suspicion from the aristocratic families.]","\"Little Zhu, you said the aristocratic families are the masters behind the big salt merchants. With such financial power, they must control more than just wealth and literary heritage, right?\"","[Master guessed correctly. Over the years, the aristocratic families have raised tens of thousands of private soldiers. Otherwise, how could they have pushed Emperor Yongjia onto the throne?","It was not only because they had money and bought off some civil and military officials, but also because they held money in one hand and a blade in the other, able to suppress dissenting voices.","If they hadn't been slaughtered by the armies of several nations and their leaders unexpectedly wiped out in one fell swoop by the peasant army, the aristocratic families might have truly grown big and strong relying on these people in that cannibalistic, chaotic world.","It's a pity that the surviving private soldiers later followed the salt merchants and defected to the Sima family. However, slaves with multiple surnames never meet a good end anyway.]","Hearing that the aristocratic families raised private soldiers, the faces of several princes looked terrible, especially Xie Zhixin, who felt like dying.","He carefully raised his head and stole a glance at his royal father.","His royal father's face was dark!","The reason Emperor Mingxi's face was dark was not only because of the aristocratic families raising private soldiers, but also because he heard about the Sima family again!","However, soon after, a bloodthirsty smile appeared at the corners of his mouth. The large net targeting Sima Jing and his family's in-laws had already been cast.","The poisonous yet fragrant bait of the snowflake salt had also been dropped. He would just sit here in the Golden Throne Room of the capital, waiting for Sima Jing to take the bait.","Thinking that Sima Jing would soon be crawling at his feet, crying bitterly in repentance, Emperor Mingxi felt incredibly delighted in his heart.","The more he thought about it, the happier he became. He had no idea that his smile looked increasingly twisted and abnormal to the others.","The first to be frightened was his own son, Xie the Third.","He strongly suspected that his royal father had been driven mad by anger! Xie Zhixin silently moved closer to the Crown Prince and hugged himself tightly.","[Master, look quickly, has the emperor been possessed by some dirty entity?]","Yue Fuguang also pretended to care and said, \"Little Zhu, then take a look around to see if there are any little ghosts or monsters. Don't let those things actually harm the emperor!\"","As soon as Yue Fuguang's words fell, everyone instantly felt a chill from head to toe, their hairs standing on end. This was because the crowd couldn't help but recall the demons and ghosts they had seen in the underworld through Xie Zhiwei's perspective earlier this month!","Half a month had passed, and some of them still occasionally had nightmares in the dead of night about being chased by ghosts.","Even more so, since then, whenever they saw Yue Fuguang, they felt somewhat afraid in their hearts. When speaking on normal days, they were extra careful, fearing they might anger her.","Emperor Mingxi was even more afraid in his heart. He wasn't sure if his royal father and brothers had all gone to reincarnate yet, or if they were still lingering in the underworld.","If someone managed to escape the underworld and run to the human realm like a prison break, he would be their first target for revenge.","As Emperor Mingxi's confidant, Eunuch Qian naturally saw the emperor's fear.","So he deliberately acted as if he were very frightened and took two steps toward the dragon throne. Seeing this, Emperor Mingxi's brows relaxed a bit.","As for the Divine Artifact claiming he was possessed by dirty entities, that was impossible. He knew clearly in his heart that he was perfectly awake and lucid!"]},{"number":333,"title":"Chapter 333: Golden Lotus","paragraphs":["[Master, in a place where dragon aura gathers, even minor ghosts will stay far away. The Emperor's surroundings are clean, and he is in good health! However, real ghosts are easy to avoid, but evil spirits wearing human skin are hard to guard against.]","After Yue Fuguang gave Emperor Mingxi and his ministers a little scare, she patted her bottom and left, leaving the unsettled crowd standing there at a loss.","The imperial city was a place where dragon aura gathered, but their own mansions were not!","They were now terrified that those deceased former colleagues might come to visit them before going to reincarnate. What would they do then?","...","\"What, the golden lotuses have bloomed?\"","Yue Fuguang had just returned to her courtyard from the royal court when she heard Cuizhu tell her this good news.","Thinking about how the weather had indeed been hot these past few days, the metal energy was vigorous.","The golden lotuses that had been in bud and refusing to open had finally reached their blooming season.","She led Shen Chunying, He Jin, and a group of guards towards the garden. Just as they turned onto the tree-lined path from a distance, everyone smelled a faint, distant fragrance of lotus flowers.","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow. This fragrance was spreading a bit too far, wasn't it? Their group was still four or five hundred meters away from the lotus pond in the garden, yet the scent had drifted over through the flowers and trees. Did plants from the cultivation world not know how to hide themselves?","Hiss! Everyone, including Yue Fuguang, was blinded by the golden lotuses shining with golden light under the sun amid the emerald lotus leaves.","Yue Fuguang silently took out the sunglasses she had prepared long ago and put them on. When she looked up again, she saw the afternoon sun generously pouring down on the golden lotuses.","Thus, those golden lotuses were no longer just quietly blooming flowers; they looked more like a whole field of burning, golden flames swaying gently in the breeze.","In Yue Fuguang's eyes, the light seemed alive. It leaped from one flower to another, condensing into a trembling diamond on one petal, and shattering into thousands of tiny starlights on the tip of a leaf.","Sunlight and golden lotuses lost their boundaries at this moment. Was it the sunlight that dyed the petals yellow, or had the petals soaked up the sunlight?","\"My Lord, could these golden lotuses be... not of this mortal realm? Why does this subordinate feel that just smelling their fragrance makes my body feel a bit lighter?\"","A smile hung on Yue Fuguang's lips. He Jin was the only one among her guards who had not been baptized by the spiritual rainwater.","He had hidden ailments in his body, so naturally, his feelings were more obvious than the others.","She smiled and said, \"Since you feel it's good, then smell it more.\"","They were all her own people, so of course, this free benefit could not be wasted.","It was a pity that such a fresh and elegant fragrance could not be collected, but making sachets out of the golden lotus petals would not be much worse.","As for the fact that the golden lotus was a medicinal herb even more precious than century-old ginseng, Yue Fuguang automatically ignored it.","She was not short of good medicine in her storage ring.","Yue Fuguang looked at the sun overhead. The hot golden radiance spilled down, mostly blocked by the tall trees in the garden. Flowers and grass grew abundantly under the mottled shade of the trees, and the breeze blew from the lotus pond, bringing a wave of coolness and fragrance.","She suddenly didn't want to return to her courtyard. It was still early, the scenery was just right, and it was perfect for having afternoon tea.","So she ordered, \"Qingzhu, go get some tea, fruits, and pastries.","Cuizhu, go invite Grandmother and the young ladies over. Also, inform the kitchen that we will have our dinner together at the Lotus Heart Pavilion.\"","Yue Fuguang sat down in the pavilion. By the time she was drinking her third cup of tea, she saw Old Madam Yu walking slowly toward the garden entrance, supported by Yu Ningxuan and her sisters.","Although Cuizhu had warned them earlier, everyone couldn't help but be blinded by the dazzling golden lotuses.","\"As expected of the golden lotuses planted by my granddaughter's own hands, they are very different from those few golden lotuses at the Baoye Temple.\"","Old Madam Yu wiped the physiological tears from the corners of her eyes caused by the stimulation of the lotuses. She took the tea Yue Fuguang handed her, took a sip, and continued, \"Grandmother went to Baoye Temple to offer incense a few days ago and specifically went to the lotus pond in the back mountain to take a look. The golden lotuses there bloomed a few more flowers this year, but they are all small, and their color is a pale gold.\"","Yu Ningxin took over the conversation and said, \"I heard that because of these few golden lotuses, the temple will also hold a sutra-chanting assembly in seven days.\"","Yu Ningxuan's mouth curved into a wicked smile. \"If those Zen masters knew that one golden lotus in Seventh Sister's garden is worth two of theirs, I wonder if anyone would regret holding that assembly of theirs?\"","Yue Fuguang also smiled and said, \"Then we just won't let them know!\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's words, the other Yu family sisters also laughed out loud and chimed in, \"We promise not to say a word outside.\"","Seeing her granddaughters acting like this, Old Madam Yu shook her head helplessly and amusingly, scolding them affectionately, \"Naughty!\"","Yu Ningxuan thought for a moment and said, \"Wouldn't that be like walking in fine clothes at night? I still wanted to properly show off to the Eighth Princess and the others.\"","Yue Fuguang thought of the Eighth Princess, who was locked in the palace all day and just looking forward to growing up quickly so she could go out more. She nodded and said, \"We will send an invitation to Little Eight. Tomorrow happens to be a rest day, so we can bring her over to play for a day.\"","Hearing this, Yu Ningxuan immediately became happy and took the initiative to take on the task, \"Seventh Sister, sit peacefully. How can I let you do rough work like sending invitations yourself?\"","She rolled up her thin sleeves, and a pair of gold-inlaid jade bracelets with lotus patterns on her wrists sparkled in the sunlight. She smilingly poured Yue Fuguang a full cup of tea, \"Sister, drink tea. We sisters will go and return shortly, I guarantee to handle it perfectly for you.\"","Yu Ningxuan left with Yu Ningxin and the other sisters. Seeing her walking as if the wind were under her feet, she guessed that she had probably already bragged to the Eighth Princess long ago.","Based on Yue Fuguang's understanding of the Eighth Princess, once she received the invitation this afternoon, she probably wouldn't even wait overnight; she would rush over even in the dark.","Therefore, she instructed Cuiyu, \"Go and lead some people to tidy up a guest courtyard for the Eighth Princess and her entourage to stay.\"","After thinking about it, she added, \"Notify the kitchen to add a few more dishes.\"","\"Fuguang is adding dishes, did you know Grandfather was coming? My granddaughter really is filial.\"","Before even seeing anyone, the few people in the pavilion heard Yu Chongshan's voice.","Yue Fuguang supported Old Madam Yu and looked toward the bamboo grove on the other side of the garden. They saw Yu Chongshan and a few people walking in through the east corner gate of the garden. Because the pavilion was blocking the view, the first thing Yu Chongshan and his group saw when they entered was Yue Fuguang and her grandmother. Conversely, the golden lotuses were completely obscured by them, the pavilion, and the surrounding flowers and trees.","\"Grandfather!\"","\"How do you lords have the free time to come over?\"","Following behind Yu Chongshan were not attendants, but Lord Lu Qi and several other lords from the Ministry of Works, as well as the Minister of Revenue Dong Qianli, her second uncle Yu Shuchun, and Lord Zheng Ziling.","\"This subordinate greets the Junior Preceptor.\"","\"Lords, please take a seat.\" After everyone exchanged greetings, they sat down according to the host and guest positions.","Fortunately, this pavilion was built large enough, and there were also tea tables placed in the covered corridor extending into the water. Even with dozens of people, it wouldn't seem crowded.","Among the seated guests, apart from a few Ministers who were relatively familiar with Yue Fuguang, the others appeared more or less a bit restrained.","Yu Chongshan only had eyes for his granddaughter and old wife, which resulted in the group completely failing to notice the golden lotuses hidden among the lotus leaves, continuously emitting a clear fragrance."]},{"number":334,"title":"Chapter 334: Gunpowder","paragraphs":["Yu Shuchun couldn't help but twitch his nose and said, \"Fuguang, what kind of incense did you light? How can it smell so good? The fragrance is faint, elegant, and not overwhelming.\"","He stretched his stiff and tired body, exhausted from overwork and the hot weather, and added, \"Smelling this incense, your Second Uncle feels a lot more relaxed.\"","Dong Qianli also smiled and said, \"Brother Yu feels it too? So I'm not the only one who thinks so!\"","Lu Qi stroked his beard with a smile, \"I feel the same way.\"","Hearing their words, a mysterious smile appeared on Yue Fuguang's face.","With sparkling eyes, she said to Yu Chongshan, \"Grandfather, Second Uncle, and my lords, you've come at a perfect time today. What you are smelling isn't incense, but the scent of lotuses.\"","\"Lotus scent?\" Among the group, Zheng Ziling, who hailed from the prominent Zheng clan, was the most cultured and refined.","He also had a deep understanding of perfumery. He had bought absolutely every single item sold in Yue Fuguang's shop, from soaps and essential oils to perfumes.","He had contributed quite a lot to her sales and was considered a loyal customer of the fragrance shop.","\"How is it that it differs so greatly from the lotus scent we usually smell?\" He looked toward the lotus pond. In the distance, amidst the emerald pond, pink and white lotuses were blooming vibrantly.","Up close, the lotus leaves were dense and lush. Golden light occasionally flashed amidst the green, which everyone had assumed was just the shimmering reflection of the water.","Yu Chongshan naturally saw it too, but knowing the inside story, he didn't think like the others. He stood up abruptly and said in pleasant surprise, \"Yue Fuguang, have the golden lotuses bloomed?\"","\"Grandfather will know once he takes a look.\" Yue Fuguang stood up and led the group toward the corridor that extended over the water.","She turned back and warned the crowd, \"My lords, be careful not to let the golden lotuses blind your eyes.\"","Ignoring the others, she silently took out a pair of men's sunglasses and handed them to Yu Chongshan to put on.","Yu Chongshan had seen his granddaughter wear this strange-looking thing called \"glasses\" before. Without needing Yue Fuguang to teach him, he rested them on the bridge of his own nose.","Hiss! Hearing the familiar gasps, the corners of Yue Fuguang's mouth curled up. She knew that even with her kind reminder, these people would inevitably shed tears upon seeing the blinding golden lotuses.","\"This... this golden lotus is far superior to those found elsewhere!\" Yu Shuchun beamed, his eyes crinkling into a smile. \"When it comes to raising flowers, especially golden lotuses, my niece is a cut above the rest.\"","As for who she was a cut above, everyone listened to the underlying tone and naturally understood immediately.","Dong Qianli nodded. \"Brother Yu is right. Such golden lotuses are indeed the only ones of their kind in the whole world.\"","The group observed for a while longer. After Yue Fuguang received a basketful of compliments, they returned to the pavilion to sit down and chat about everyday matters.","\"How did Grandfather and you lords find the free time to come over today?\" Tomorrow was their official rest day, yet they had run over today. Were they openly skipping work and dragging their superiors along with them?","Yu Chongshan smiled and lowered his voice, \"Grandfather and these lords have just come from the Alchemy Bureau.\"","Because they had eavesdropped on Yue Fuguang's inner thoughts, they had learned that this incredibly powerful substance was called gunpowder, a great lethal weapon for dealing with cavalry.","The ruler and officials of Great Yan, all knowing that a war with Western Qiang and Northern Li was inevitable, were single-mindedly focused on manufacturing it.","Through their roundabout questioning of Yue Fuguang—which was actually Yue Fuguang intentionally giving them subtle hints—","They had learned the basic formula. They then chose a hidden location in the mountains near the capital's suburbs to build a workshop. Emperor Mingxi even personally wrote the name \"The First Alchemy Bureau of Great Yan\" for it.","The reason they didn't use the word \"gunpowder\" was not only to prevent people with ulterior motives from snooping but also to temporarily confuse all parties. The ruler and his ministers had not forgotten the fact that Great Yan had been infiltrated like a sieve.","After half a year of research and development, the first batch of gunpowder had finally been produced a few days ago, pending final testing.","Yu Chongshan and Lu Qi, as figures with real power in the Ministry of Works, naturally had to go to the site to inspect the results.","As for the people from the Ministry of Revenue, those who provided the funds naturally had to go to the site to evaluate it as well. Given the previous corruption, Dong Qianli, for the sake of his own life and fortune,","Now guarded the Ministry of Revenue's silver and account books tighter than his own. For any large expenditure, he had to see it with his own eyes to feel at ease.","\"Looking at Grandfather's expression, that gunpowder has been successfully made?\"","Yu Chongshan stroked his beard and nodded with a smile, \"We have indeed achieved some results, but it is still a far cry from the immensely powerful gunpowder you said was made by people overseas.\"","Lu Qi also nodded in agreement, \"Brother Yu is right. The gunpowder currently produced by the Alchemy Bureau can only blast a small hole in the rocks.","But even so, if our border army encounters the cavalry of Northern Li and Western Qiang again, they won't be as fearful as before, having to fill every victory with the lives of our soldiers.\"","Speaking of this, Lu Qi felt quite sorrowful. He had a fine junior in his clan who, a few years ago, during a border conflict between Great Yan and Northern Li,","Had led several small squads in order to pin down the enemy's cavalry on the battlefield, only to be trampled to death by horses.","\"It's already quite good that the artisans of the Ministry of Works could achieve this in such a short time.\"","Yue Fuguang looked at Lu Qi and said, \"Lord Minister, please don't forget to ask His Majesty to reward the artisans for their merits. Gunpowder is dangerous; they are working with their lives on the line.\"","Earning the wages of a cabbage seller while doing life-threatening work—it would be truly unjustifiable not to give them some sweet rewards.","\"There must be brave men under heavy rewards. Similarly, generous treatment and awards can also stimulate the creativity of the artisans.","Perhaps it won't be long before they can develop highly destructive gunpowder.\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's words, Lu Qi nodded repeatedly. \"Lord Junior Preceptor makes a valid point. Once I return, I will request merits for the artisans from His Majesty.\"","Since these words were proposed by the Junior Preceptor, there was no reason for their Emperor not to agree once he knew.","[Master, isn't the gunpowder formula very simple? How did they study it for half a year only to blast a small pit?]","\"Little Zhu, going from nothing to something is the most difficult part. The fact that they could draw inspiration from alchemists' exploding furnaces is already a kind of progress.\"","Yue Fuguang kept her mouth completely shut about the fact that she had intentionally guided them.","[One part sulfur, two parts saltpeter, three parts charcoal, add a little white sugar and the power increases ten thousandfold. In another minor thousand world, even ten-year-old children know this black gunpowder formula.","If you mix them with crushed stones and iron scraps, put them in a clay pot, and light a fire, it scatters like heavenly maidens dropping blossoms. Within a radius of tens of meters, neither man nor beast can survive.]","\"What you're talking about isn't suitable for close combat. The defense of Great Yan's soldiers is poor; it would easily result in killing a thousand enemies while losing eight hundred of our own.\"","Trying hard to memorize this little jingle, Lu Qi and Yu Chongshan exchanged a glance. So what if it wasn't good for close combat? They had catapults!","In the past, they threw stones. Now, they would throw gunpowder pots and the fierce fire oil that they had already fully mastered.","Only the ruler and his ministers knew that while the army of Great Yan seemed to have changed little over the past year, it had actually undergone earth-shattering transformations from within.","The Junior Preceptor's troop training methods had been edited and adapted for use on the veteran troops.","As for the new army, which had rapidly expanded to nearly eighty thousand men, and the navy of over ten thousand, all the recruits were commoners with clean backgrounds.","They used the complete set of training methods, as well as that ideological education. He had heard Huo Ying and Wei Shouyi say more than once that it was truly effective!","[Couldn't they be made into landmines? They explode when stepped on. Bury a ring of them at the border passes, and whoever comes will die.]","Hey guys, please work your magic and hit the urge-update button! Thank you so much! Clasping hands in gratitude!"]},{"number":335,"title":"Chapter 335: I don't know how to compose poetry, but I can recite it","paragraphs":["Lu Qi's eyes lit up, almost outshining the golden light flashing on the golden lotus petals. As expected of the divine artifact, there were truly so many ways to kill!","Since this little ancestor knew so much, he begged it to tell him more!","Would the system grant his wish? Of course not!","As a merit system, if it wasn't for the cover of the melon-eating system, it wouldn't even be able to reveal this much.","After all, once it said these words, from then on, the layout of the battlefield would undergo a subtle change, and countless people would die under black powder in the future.","Unable to hear the conversation between the two anymore, Yu Chongshan smiled and changed the subject. \"It seems that Grandfather came at the right time today. Catching the first bloom of the golden lotus is a good omen!\"","Zheng Ziling greedily breathed in the lotus fragrance in the air and smiled. \"We must thank Elder Brother Yu for the invitation. Otherwise, where could we see such a rare golden lotus in this world?\"","[Master, these few people are indeed lucky. This lotus fragrance is very beneficial to their bodies. Look at that Ministry of Works Director, Sun Chengmin. He has a hidden illness. If nothing unexpected happens, his body will only last another three or four years. Coming here today, smelling the lotus fragrance, and drinking the tea brewed from the golden lotus leaves, you can see his complexion has improved a lot.]","\"I did see that they were all exceptionally exhausted, so I specially brewed these golden lotus leaves. And I see that this Sun Chengmin you mentioned has a darkened glabella. Not only is his health poor, but he also seems to be plagued by bad luck.\"","Yue Fuguang scanned him and easily saw that his luck had been low recently.","This Sun Chengmin was one of Grandfather's confidants, and he was also one of the main people in charge of building this prince-level villa.","Because of these two points, Yue Fuguang deliberately said this, wanting to remind him and also to preserve talent for their side.","Sun Chengmin kept his head half-lowered, possessing the characteristic introversion and reticence of craftsmen of this era.","Hearing the two ancestors mention his name, he merely nervously gripped the white porcelain teacup that emanated a faint lotus leaf scent.","He couldn't help but secretly wonder, so the reason he had been feeling unwell frequently over the past year was because of a hidden illness?","The forty-year-old Sun Chengmin hadn't expected that in the original timeline, he would only live to be forty-three or forty-four.","However, not suffering the pain of a subjugated nation was also quite good. Sun Chengmin had to comfort himself this way.","But he dared not seriously think about what the future held for his wife, children, and his newly born little grandson!","Looking at the few emerald green shreds of lotus leaf in his cup, Sun Chengmin silently drank all the tea, then put the lotus leaves into his mouth and swallowed them down along with the bitterness.","If one could live well, who would want to die early?","Since the Junior Preceptor had given him a chance at survival, there was no reason for him not to grasp it well.","At most, this life of his would belong to the Yu family and the Junior Preceptor in the future.","Yu Chongshan silently patted Sun Chengmin's shoulder. With his granddaughter around, Xiao Sun wouldn't die.","Everyone thanked Yu Chongshan for the invitation and then thanked Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang said, \"My lords, there's no need to be so polite. Please, have some tea.\"","Taking the opportunity, Yu Chongshan poured another cup for Sun Chengmin. Sun Chengmin quickly stood up, repeatedly saying he didn't dare.","Although he was someone Yu Chongshan had single-handedly promoted, he still didn't dare let a superior several ranks higher pour water for him.","\"Xiao Sun, sit still.\" He pressed Sun Chengmin back into his seat and continued, \"Consider this cup of tea my thanks for your dedication in building this villa.\"","Several mechanisms were completed secretly by Sun Chengmin at his private request. Other than their grandfather-granddaughter pair, only Sun Chengmin knew about this.","Sun Chengmin naturally heard what Elder Lord Yu was referring to, but he still declined, \"My lord, you are too serious. These are all things this lower official should do. Besides, we also received gifts from the Junior Preceptor.\"","They were all exquisite gadgets not available on the market. His wife, children, and daughter-in-law couldn't bear to use them themselves; he used all those precious things as gifts.","Thinking of that exquisite mechanism technique, Yue Fuguang felt that although this world didn't have the Mohist school, the mechanism techniques alone really broadened her horizons.","So she said, \"Lord Sun has indeed worked hard. This tea is not bad; you should drink a few more cups.\"","With Yue Fuguang's words, Sun Chengmin silently downed three cups in a row. It seemed he was indeed full of the desire to survive.","Seeing that it was still early, everyone drank fragrant tea and talked enthusiastically. Looking at the beautiful scenery and delicious food before them, their literary spirit surged, and they couldn't help but feel a burst of poetic inspiration.","Old Madam Yu immediately ordered the servants to bring brush, ink, paper, and inkstone. The sisters of the Yu family also came over at this time. The folk customs of the Great Yan were quite open; there was no such thing as tedious restrictions between men and women. The sisters didn't need to avoid them, listening to their grandfather, second uncle, and the others engage in lofty discussions.","While doing some ink-grinding work, even Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin, who returned latest after delivering an invitation to the Eighth Princess, were drafted into service.","Zheng Ziling, who had the strongest literary spirit, thought of Yue Fuguang's phrase \"read ten thousand books, travel ten thousand miles.\"","He couldn't help but say, \"With such beautiful scenery before us, does the Junior Preceptor have a poem?\"","Yue Fuguang: Do I look like someone who can write poetry?","Reciting poetry, maybe, but writing poetry, no!","[Master, don't you know how to recite many poems by mortal masters? Show them a thing or two, and let them know what a Poetry Immortal and Poetry Sage are!]","Poetry Immortal and Poetry Sage? There are such figures in this world?","Everyone present had passed the formal imperial examinations; none of them shrank from reading or writing poetry.","Scholars tended to look down on each other but also appreciated each other. They were naturally very curious about what kind of verses could be called immortal or sage-like.","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and said, \"I don't know how to write poetry, but reciting some poems that you lords have never heard before isn't difficult.\" Although she really wanted to show off, she knew she didn't have the talent to copy the poems of those great masters of different styles.","Everyone cupped their hands. \"Junior Preceptor, please speak. We are all ears.\"","Yue Fuguang slowly walked to the rose trellis that was blooming like a raging fire. The pink, pale yellow, and deep red roses emitted a faint fragrance. If it weren't for the overbearing scent of the golden lotus, this place would have been the domain of the rose fragrance.","She plucked a flower and said, \"The green shade is thick, the summer days are long, the terrace's reflection falls into the pond. A breeze stirs the crystal curtain, a trellis full of roses scents the courtyard.\"","\"Lotus leaves and silk skirts are cut from the same color, hibiscus faces...\"","\"Red lotus fragrance fades, jade mat feels autumn. Lightly unfasten...\"","\"Often remembering the sunset at the creek pavilion, so drunk we forgot the way back...\"","\"The lotus leaves no longer hold up their rain covers...\"","\"Crossing the river to pick hibiscus, the orchid swamp...\"","Everyone only heard Yue Fuguang's little mouth babbling on, not even taking a breath, tossing out more than a dozen poems describing lotuses and summer scenery in a row.","Although they hadn't had time to savor them carefully, everyone was already astounded upon first hearing them.","Lord Zheng Ziling silently rubbed his wrist, which was a bit sore from taking rapid notes, and then looked at the paper full of the fragrance of ink and poetry...","\"Ah! Minister, this lower official hasn't finished writing yet!\"","Zheng Ziling watched helplessly as his hard-earned notes of the poems were taken away by his superior for appreciation, jumping up and down in anxiety.","\"No matter, this old man will help you fill in the last few words.\" Dong Qianli shamelessly took the stack of papers filled with verses and put his head together with Lu Qi to savor them carefully.","Zheng Ziling: Is that what I meant? Doubting life.JPG"]},{"number":336,"title":"Chapter 336: Person Plagued by Bad Luck","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang watched as everyone, including her grandfather and second uncle, gathered around the poem she had tossed out, clicking their tongues in praise.","She suddenly felt she should have had some wine just now, and memorized more in the future, just like that Fan Xian, to thoroughly give the literati of this world a bit of shock from poetry.","At this moment, Yue Fuguang, who was secretly proud of awing the crowd, never expected that because of a small interlude today, the story would change once it spread out.","It was rumored that the Young Preceptor was extremely good at writing poetry, and the reputation that every piece was a masterpiece spread wider and wider, so much so that it later spread throughout the lands of the Six Nations, and even brought about a lot of trouble later on. But all of that is a story for another time.","Knowing nothing of this at the moment, she sat back down beside her grandmother and sisters, smiling as she watched everyone fiercely debating which poem should be the champion and which author should be considered a master.","[Master, I checked. This Sun Chengmin is indeed plagued by bad luck, just as you said.]","\"Oh? Little Zhu, since we have nothing else to do, tell me about it.\"","Hearing their words, the people both near and far unconsciously lowered their voices in conversation.","[At the beginning of the year, Sun Chengmin's youngest daughter unfortunately fell into the water and was almost not saved. Her twin brother was so frightened by seeing his sister fall in that he fell seriously ill.","Less than two months later, his father broke his leg slipping on the icy, snow-covered road.","In May, his eldest daughter-in-law, who was over nine months pregnant, was startled into premature labor. If your grandfather hadn't given Sun Chengmin a century-old ginseng to save her life, it would likely have resulted in the deaths of both mother and child.]","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"In less than half a year, the Sun family has suffered a series of disasters. Is it man-made, or just due to bad luck?\"","[Master, you only know that Sun Chengmin is highly skilled in mechanics, but you don't know that he is also someone who loves to study bizarre and unusual weapons.","The weapons he makes privately are all unconventional, so he is embarrassed to show them to others.","Inspired by your firearms, especially that gun of yours, he actually privately developed a very primitive type of musket.]","\"Oh? He actually created the predecessor of the gun, a musket, in such a short time? He is a talent!","But what does this have to do with his family's bad luck?\"","[Master, although those weapons he makes are not suitable for the military, they are still very useful when fighting an enemy one-on-one.","Therefore, the things he makes are often secretly taken out and sold for money by his nephew, Wei Ming.","After Sun Chengmin found out, he reprimanded him a few times and told him that if he did it again, he would be sent back home.","Because of this, the man harbored a grudge and made a move against the younger generation of the Sun family.]","At this moment, Sun Chengmin only felt his brain buzzing and his teeth chattering incessantly. In the July weather, he felt a bone-piercing cold all over his body.","He never expected that his nephew, whom he usually loved dearly, would harbor a grudge just because he was reprimanded a few times by his uncle for doing something wrong.","Not only did he resent him, but he also committed such a frantic and cruel act against his family. Setting everything else aside, his father was Wei Ming's own maternal grandfather. How could he bring himself to do it?","\"Is this Wei Ming Sun Chengmin's biological nephew?\"","[Wei Ming is the son of Sun Chengmin's younger sister. When Wei Ming was seven years old, his younger sister passed away early. Father Wei married a new wife less than a year later, and the following year she gave birth to a younger brother for him, and later gave birth to two more younger siblings in succession.","Wei Ming's life became increasingly difficult. The Sun family, afraid that their grandson would be tormented and fail to grow up properly, brought him to the Sun household to be raised.","As a result, they never expected this Wei Ming to be an ungrateful wretch, constantly comparing his treatment with that of the Sun family siblings.","He often used the early death of his biological mother and his father's lack of affection to win the sympathy of the Sun family. Not only did he always eat and take more than his share, but he also didn't study well at school, made some fair-weather friends, and picked up the bad habit of gambling.","When he gambled all his money away, he targeted his uncle Sun Chengmin's weapons. After Sun Chengmin caught him stealing, he started having wicked thoughts.]","\"Didn't Sun Chengmin realize that the incidents happening to his family members were man-made?\"","Sun Chengmin nodded. His youngest daughter had indeed told him that she was pushed from behind while playing with ice by the pool at home.","His eldest daughter-in-law also said she was startled by a suddenly appearing black cat during the day, slipped, and fell.","As for his father, the ice at his door was indeed smoother and thicker than elsewhere...","He suspected that someone was targeting the Sun family, but he never thought it was the doing of the biological nephew he had raised!","[He probably did realize it, he just didn't expect it to be his own nephew.","Also, Master, this Wei Ming has stolen from the Sun family again. He is afraid of being discovered, so he is looking for an opportunity these past two days to set a fire and destroy the evidence.]","Sun Chengmin's heart tightened, and he was so shocked he almost stood up from his chair. He wished he could sprout wings and fly home right now.","Just as he was anxiously thinking about how to quietly take his leave early, a group of people slowly walked in through the moon gate of the garden.","The person leading them was none other than Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan. Behind him followed not only the invited Eighth Princess, but also the Seventh Prince, who was inseparable from the Eighth Princess, and... Fifth Brother Xie?","If she remembered correctly, every time this person saw her, it was like a mouse seeing a cat—he couldn't hide fast enough. Why would he take the initiative to come over?","Before Yue Fuguang could figure it out, the Crown Prince and his group had already approached.","After everyone exchanged greetings, they took their seats as host and guests.","Xie Zhiyan took the lead and smiled at Yue Fuguang, saying, \"I heard from Eighth Sister that the golden lotuses planted by the Young Preceptor have bloomed, and you invited her to admire the flowers.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"They just bloomed today. This courtyard full of fragrance is emitted by the golden lotuses.\"","\"I snatched a guard's errand to come here, and it seems I made the right choice. Even before seeing the golden lotuses, just smelling this lotus fragrance relaxes the body and mind significantly.\"","Yue Fuguang pointed toward the lotus pond. \"Look, Your Highness, the golden lotuses are right there!\"","It was already dusk. The intense heat had subsided, and only a glimmer of light remained on the horizon. At this time, the golden lotuses also restrained most of their radiance, leaving only a gentle, glowing luster, like a lamp in the dark night, warm and not dazzling.","Everyone thought to themselves that this hour was actually the best time to view the golden lotuses.","Just as they were thinking this, the afterglow on the horizon completely faded, and the surroundings grew entirely dark. Cuizhu received orders to hold up lamps for the princes and princesses. Under the illumination of the candlelight, the golden lotuses emitted a different, faint golden light, their texture resembling golden jade, appearing even more warm and smooth.","Xie Zhiyan and his group were all full of praise. The Eighth Princess even made an appointment with Yu Ningxuan and the others to come back tomorrow at noon. She wanted to see how dazzling the golden lotuses would be when they shone the brightest.","And the news that Young Preceptor Yue's estate grew the best golden lotuses in all of Great Yan spread like wildfire.","Except for the big three in the imperial palace who didn't make a move, all the other high-ranking officials who could speak with her came to pay their respects to the true appearance of the golden lotuses.","As a result, Yue Fuguang, who was just sitting at home, unexpectedly received a large batch of gifts. However, the storehouse of her separate estate was large, so she didn't have to worry about running out of space to put them.","Her return gift was simply a small jar of lotus leaf tea. Of course, all of this was handled by the men of the Yu family on her behalf. Yue Fuguang just enjoyed her leisure time hiding in her own courtyard, and no one dared to disturb her peace.","However, today was an exception. Why say so? Because the status of the people who came today was exceptionally different."]},{"number":337,"title":"Chapter 337: Master's Visit","paragraphs":["Sitting below her was a figure who acted as the leading voice for the Buddhist and Daoist factions not just in the capital, but across the entire Great Yan dynasty: Master Liaoyuan, the abbot of Baoye Temple.","It had been agreed not to tell the monks of Baoye Temple, but the news spread so widely that Master Liaoyuan still found out. He was among the very first to know.","Liaoyuan was a plump monk with a round, fair-skinned face and a shiny bald head bearing nine precept scars. When he smiled, he looked incredibly benevolent, revealing a mouthful of white teeth.","Yue Fuguang glanced at the string of red sandalwood prayer beads draped over his chubby hand, wondering if this man truly adhered to a strict vegetarian diet year-round without touching a morsel of meat.","However, seeing that he was plump but not greasy, she figured he might just have a large appetite or be the type of person who gained weight just from drinking water.","Sitting next to Liaoyuan was Daoist Qingcheng from the True Immortal Temple. This Daoist Qingcheng was also Xuanmingzi's junior martial brother.","Although Daoist Qingcheng was Xuanmingzi's junior, he looked much older than Xuanmingzi did now.","He appeared to be around the same age as Liaoyuan, roughly in his fifties. Dressed in a cyan Daoist robe, he possessed a transcendent, immortal-like aura.","The fly whisk tucked at his waist was identical to the one Xuanmingzi carried. It was said to have been personally bestowed by their master, with each disciple receiving one.","Daoist Qingcheng, whom Yue Fuguang was secretly judging for looking old, had long noticed that for the past half year or so, every time he saw his senior martial brother, the man seemed younger than the last time.","His transcendent, otherworldly temperament had also deepened compared to the past.","Daoist Qingcheng glanced at Yue Fuguang, who exuded a natural divine aura, and could not help but wonder: was staying by her side truly that nourishing?","If it had just been these two men, they would not have been able to get her to move.","The only reason Yue Fuguang was willing to leave her beloved reclining chair was that her master had also arrived.","Yue Fuguang personally poured a cup of tea for Qingxuan and handed it over. Master, when did you arrive in the capital? Why didn't you let me know in advance so I could send someone to pick you up?","Your master came to the capital a few times in my younger years. I know the way. Why would I need you to send someone? Qingxuan carefully examined her little disciple.","It had been over a year since Fuguang left the Daoist temple. The disciple standing before her had blossomed so much that even her own master could barely recognize her.","Qingxuan sighed inwardly. Children really did change drastically as they grew. It seemed the child had not suffered any hardships over the past year, which gave her some peace of mind.","As for the lotus mark on her disciple's forehead, others might not know, but how could she not? During her three years at the temple, the girl had always covered her forehead with thick bangs. But when Qingxuan had first saved her and cared for her through her illness for so long, she knew very well that the lotus mark had not been there.","Although her disciple had changed a lot over the past year, her lazy streak was exactly like Qingxuan's own. Qingxuan was absolutely certain that this was her disciple and she had not been swapped with an imposter.","She just did not know what method the little girl had used to get such an incredibly spiritual mark. Looking at it for too long even gave Qingxuan the illusion of wanting to bow in worship.","Now she had even grown a golden lotus, something neither the Buddhist nor Daoist factions possessed. Her title as a divine maiden was becoming increasingly solidified. Thinking of this, Qingxuan could not help but worry about her disciple's future.","Being elevated so high meant that if she ever failed to answer their prayers in the future, the very people who praised her would trample her just as hard.","Having lived for over thirty years, Qingxuan knew better than anyone that the human heart was the most fickle thing of all!","Since you are here, Master, you must stay with me for a few more days. Your quarters are in the courtyard right next to the garden. If you want to see the golden lotus, you can do so anytime.","For this person who had pulled her up during her most difficult times, rescued her from a fiery pit, and given her a place to stay, keeping her from sleeping on the streets when she first arrived in this strange world, Yue Fuguang was deeply grateful and genuinely wanted to repay her.","Furthermore, Qingxuan was a free-spirited and easygoing person. Because they shared the same lazy traits, the master and disciple had a deep mutual appreciation for each other.","Given her laziness, traveling thousands of miles to come here was truly a difficult feat for her.","Qingxuan smiled and nodded. Even if you hadn't said anything, your master didn't plan on going back so soon. The journey here nearly exhausted me to death!","Since Qingxuan had considered the potential troubles her disciple might face in the future, how could she leave with peace of mind?","Still having a few connections, she naturally had to stay behind so she could lend a hand when it mattered most.","Hearing Junior Sister Qingxuan say this, Daoist Qingcheng's mouth twitched. If he hadn't specifically sent someone to fetch her, how could this junior sister have ever come to the capital?","He had heard from the people who went to pick her up that she was only willing to travel thirty or forty miles a day. Any more than that, and she would complain of exhaustion.","Sitting in a carriage, she didn't even have to walk herself. He had no idea what she was so tired from. A journey of less than a thousand miles had been dragged out for over a month before she finally arrived in the capital.","Yue Fuguang then looked at Liaoyuan, Daoist Qingcheng, and Xuanmingzi. Since you are all here, why don't you join my master and me in the garden to see the golden lotus?","The system had said that the golden lotus's blooming period was about a month and a half. It had already been blooming for nearly a month, so every viewing was truly one less chance to see it.","By mid-August, when the sweet potatoes, corn, and potatoes were harvested, the golden lotus would also wither. As for the lotus petals, Yue Fuguang had not yet figured out how to use them.","The time when the flower withered was when its fragrance would be the strongest and its medicinal properties the most potent.","Amitabha!","May the Heavenly Lord of Limitless Blessings preserve us!","The morning sunlight shone upon the golden lotus, making its entire body radiate a holy, golden light.","These people were all leading figures of the Buddhist and Daoist factions in Great Yan, so their spiritual sensitivity was naturally much higher than that of ordinary people. Ever since stepping into this garden, every breath they took made them feel as though their bodies were being purified from the inside out.","If it weren't for the inappropriate time and place, Liaoyuan and the others would have loved to sit on the ground and not get up until the flower withered.","That was what they thought, but Liaoyuan and Daoist Qingcheng dared not act presumptuously in front of this True Immortal.","Normally, it was the nobles of the capital who flattered them, but here, they were the ones who had to carefully flatter her.","Daoist Qingcheng glanced back at his Junior Sister Qingxuan, who was smiling so brightly at the golden lotus that her eyes were mere slits. He was truly envious!","This junior sister of his, who had always loved slacking off on her cultivation since childhood, had incredibly good luck!","Yue Fuguang ordered her servants to set out fruits, tea, and pastries in the Lotus Heart Pavilion, and added two extra ice basins since her Master Qingxuan was most afraid of the heat.","Because Liaoyuan and Daoist Qingcheng could not bear to stray too far from the golden lotus, Yue Fuguang simply placed cushions for them in the corridor and left them to their own devices.","She then pulled her master and Xuanmingzi into the pavilion to enjoy the cool breeze.","After drinking a cup of lotus leaf tea, Qingxuan leaned close to Yue Fuguang and whispered, Fuguang, is it just your master's imagination, or does it feel like a lot of my travel fatigue has faded in just this short amount of time?","Yue Fuguang gave her a mysterious smile. Master, why do you think so many high-ranking officials and nobles want to flock to my garden?","Even among thieves big and small, the two commanders, He Jin and Dai Yuxing, had led their guards to capture over a dozen people.","Aside from three or five nameless petty thieves, the rest were all notorious master thieves in the martial world.","Even Poison Young Master, the only remaining active member of the Three Eccentrics, had appeared near the villa.","Yue Fuguang thought that if this person was really targeting her golden lotus, it wouldn't be long before he went to the heavenly prison to reunite with Drunken Rakshasa and Poison Widow.","With so many people scheming for her golden lotus, surprisingly not a single one had noticed that the crops grown on her estate were different from those elsewhere."]},{"number":338,"title":"Chapter 338: Sleep That Never Wakes","paragraphs":["From this, it was evident that these martial artists were not the sort to engage in productive labor.","Perhaps in their eyes, all crops growing in the fields were the same, only differing when finally eaten.","Xuanmingzi smiled at Qingxuan and said, \"Junior Martial Sister Qingxuan, you might not know this, but many people covet this half-pond of golden lotuses belonging to the Junior Preceptor.\"","Qingxuan gazed at the nine golden lotuses radiating golden light in the pond and gently stroked the lotus head of the whisk at her waist. \"Nine is the ultimate number, representing the utmost firmness and yang. When it is full, it overflows; when it is in excess, it wanes. Fuguang, remember to avoid extremes and extravagance, and to maintain balance and harmony.\"","It was rare for Yue Fuguang to see Qingxuan lecturing her so seriously. She couldn't help but smile and reassure her, \"Master, you don't need to worry too much. My estate is very secure. You can just stay here with peace of mind. I promise you'll have an endless supply of chicken, duck, fish, and meat every day.\"","Daoists in the Great Yan Dynasty didn't seem to have dietary restrictions. At least her master didn't, and she was particularly obsessed with food.","It was said that the reason she chose to become a Daoist when she was young was because the food in the Daoist temple was good and filling, which perfectly matched Yue Fuguang's reason for choosing to lie low in the Daoist temple back then.","When she first arrived, Yue Fuguang spent half a month in the Zhou family without seeing a single drop of meat. As a result, when she later heard that the Daoist temple had good food, she came up with the idea of being a Daoist for a few years to fatten herself up before considering anything else.","Qingxuan took a bite of the lotus seed cake. \"And we can't forget these pastries. They taste much better than the ones from Li's Pastry Shop at the foot of the mountain.\"","Yue Fuguang smiled knowingly. Master Qingxuan said it was better than Li's Pastry Shop because the money she had on her was only enough to buy pastries from an affordable shop like Li's.","During their three years in the Daoist temple, whenever Qingxuan had a little money on her, she couldn't resist taking her down the mountain for a good meal.","In the past, when she was alone, she could occasionally eat something nice. Later, with Yue Fuguang's extra mouth to feed, they could only afford street stalls.","After all, although Yue Fuguang was small, her appetite was not small at all due to the system's issues.","\"This is lotus seed cake. In a few days, when the osmanthus flowers in the garden bloom, I'll make osmanthus cake for you, Master. There's also chestnut cake, hibiscus cake, water chestnut cake...\"","Yue Fuguang counted them off on her fingers one by one. By the time she mentioned plum blossom cake and peach blossom wine, Qingxuan had already started swallowing her saliva silently, thinking to herself that she had indeed made the right choice coming here. Her disciple hadn't lied in the letter; there really was so much delicious food here.","Xuanmingzi watched with a smile as the master and disciple chatted about food, completely ignoring the golden lotuses not far away that millions of people dreamed of.","Seeing how well the two got along, he couldn't help but wonder what kind of immortal the Junior Preceptor's divine master was.","After seeing off Liaoyuan and the others, Yue Fuguang returned to her leisurely days. No matter how much of a storm her golden lotuses and her poems caused outside, her villa remained peaceful and quiet.","As the golden lotuses were about to wither, Yue Fuguang visited the recruit camp again on a cloudy afternoon. This time, she selected another three thousand men and sent them to garrison the Three Forks region.","When Yu Boming sent a telegram informing her that the cotton in the Three Forks region was about to be picked, the potatoes, sweet potatoes, and corn on her estate and the imperial estate had also reached the harvest season.","After multiple divinations by Yun Tianxing, the Director of the Imperial Observatory, the auspicious day was finally set for the twenty-third of the eighth lunar month.","And the news of the upcoming harvest of the fine crops spread like wildfire through the streets and alleys of the capital city.","It also spread at a terrifying speed to the surrounding prefectures and counties. During those days, carrier pigeons filled the sky, which delighted the two gluttons, Taxue and Wuhen.","These two would take a few spins in the sky every day, not only feeding themselves until their bellies were round but also bringing back a dozen small bamboo tubes for her each time.","All were unexpected gains from the two birds' hunting.","After reading them, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but exclaim. The owners behind these carrier pigeons were all different, including spies from various countries and people from major domestic factions.","Even the major noble families, who had been gradually pushed into a corner by Emperor Mingxi over the past month or so, were making their final desperate struggles.","Their target was pointing straight at the fine crops.","Not to mention Tianxing Pavilion and Youtan, even Panshan, who had always been hiding behind the scenes, couldn't sit still this time.","Why couldn't they sit still? Because this time, various rumors were flying around among the people. One of them, leaked by an anonymous source, claimed that during this autumn festival, not only would the well-known divine crop, the potato, be harvested.","But there were also previously unheard-of crops with yields as high as the potato: one was the sweet potato, and the other was corn.","And their discoverer was none other than the Junior Preceptor, Yue Fuguang.","The common people didn't know whether the news was true or false, but given the Junior Preceptor's reputation, they were more willing and hopeful that it was true.","As a result, something unexpected happened. As the autumn harvest approached and with a few days left until the autumn festival, the first things to sell out across the Great Yan Dynasty were not various farming tools.","But rather statues of Yue Fuguang and incense candles.","Clearly, between working hard and going to work, the people of Great Yan chose to burn incense.","Consequently, Yue Fuguang and the system were both suffering and happy. Because the incense offerings were too abundant, she was often so stuffed that she couldn't wake up.","Yes, she couldn't wake up, falling into a deep slumber from which she couldn't be roused!","The system's data was also flashing rapidly. Both the person and the system temporarily crashed under the impact of the incense offerings.","\"Daoist Master, Fuguang will be alright, won't she?\"","Old Madam Yu and Yu Chongshan stood before Yue Fuguang's bed. Looking at their granddaughter who had been unconscious for three days, they were so worried that a few more wrinkles appeared on their faces.","Seeing Xuanmingzi taking her pulse but remaining silent for a long time, Old Madam Yu finally couldn't help but ask.","Xuanmingzi shook his head. \"Old Madam, please rest assured. The Junior Preceptor is in good health. Her prolonged slumber should be due to her body repairing itself.\"","He spoke vaguely, but everyone present, including Qingxuan, understood.","She still remembered how surprised she was when she first heard her disciple's inner voice, and how reassured she felt later on.","From this, Qingxuan also seemed to gain some enlightenment. When she first met her disciple, she felt she was different from other children. First, a lotus mark inexplicably appeared on her forehead.","Then, her inner voice leaked out. These two things seemed to have some secret connection.","And everything pointed to one answer: the awakening of Fuguang's divinity!","Regarding this slumber, she and Xuanmingzi shared the same opinion. Fuguang must have received too much mortal incense. Her physical body couldn't bear it, so her divine soul had no choice but to slowly absorb and digest the power of the incense. During this process, her mind was unguarded, leading to her current condition.","Qingxuan also smiled and comforted her, \"Yes, Old Madam, please relax. Senior Martial Brother Xuanming is right. Fuguang descended upon a divine decree; she is blessed with great fortune and a strong life force. How could anything happen to her?\"","Although Yue Fuguang's three-day slumber didn't alarm too many people, everyone in the upper echelons of the Great Yan court who needed to know already knew.","Therefore, the villa was bustling with activity every day, with carriages from various families coming and going to visit.","Ever since Yue Fuguang fell into her slumber, Yu Chongshan had taken a leave of absence. Although he didn't have to attend court, worrying about his granddaughter every day and receiving guests made him more exhausted than attending court.","When Yue Fuguang woke up on the morning of the fifth day, the moment she opened her eyes, she saw Yu Chongshan and Old Madam Yu, who had already been there for nearly half an hour.","\"Grandfather, Grandmother, why are you here? Did something happen at home?\"","Waking up this time, Yue Fuguang only felt completely relaxed, and her energy was exceptionally vigorous. Some of her abilities also seemed to have grown a bit stronger."]},{"number":339,"title":"Chapter 339: Awakening, Return to the City","paragraphs":["With things developing like this, the drought that started in the eighth year of Yuankang would be easy to handle!","Seeing that Yue Fuguang had woken up, the two elders happily hurried over to her bed and said, \"Fuguang, you're awake?\"","Old Madam Yu touched her hand, which felt nice and warm, and continued, \"Everything is fine at home! You slept for four or five days straight, and us two old folks were worried sick, so we came to check on you first thing in the morning.\"","Hearing that she had slept for four or five days, Yue Fuguang's mind raced, and she immediately figured out the reason.","She looked at their noticeably thinner cheeks and the dark circles under their eyes. \"Grandfather, Grandmother, I'm fine. You must be exhausted from these past few days. Go get some rest.\"","She turned sideways, opened the drawer by the bed, took out a small jade bottle, and handed it to Yu Chongshan. \"Grandfather, take one pill each with Grandmother before you go to sleep.\"","Old Madam Yu shook her head. \"Your grandfather and I are in good health. We don't need to take your precious medicine pills.","Grandmother knows your master didn't leave you many, so keep them for yourself just in case.\"","Yue Fuguang knew Old Madam Yu would be reluctant to use them, which was why she handed the pills directly to her grandfather. She took Old Madam Yu's hand and showed her her medicine cabinet. \"Just accept them, Grandmother. Although they are rare, look, your granddaughter still has more here.\"","After seeing the two of them off, Yue Fuguang knocked on the system. \"07, I slept for so long, why didn't you wake me up? If I hadn't been alert and taken a fasting pill before falling asleep, wouldn't I have starved to death?\"","The system's lazy voice replied, \"Host, you were unconscious, and I was crashed. How could I wake you up!\"","\"You crashed from the impact of the incense offerings too?\" Good heavens, it turned out they were both offline.","\"So has your data been repaired? Are there any new features?\"","\"Not that good. To unlock new features, we just have to wait for the system upgrade. However, after the autumn festival in two days, we should be able to upgrade to level five.\"","\"Then what data did you repair this time?\"","\"The merit system and the melon-eating system have both been partially repaired.\" The system didn't give any further details, as it needed some time to digest everything itself.","\"Oh right, Host, after this data repair, the merit system now has a spatial storage slot.\"","\"One? What's the capacity?\"","Others usually started with six or nine, so why did she only get one? At this rate, who knew if she would be able to gather nine by the time she left this world.","\"Ninety-nine items, with no limit on weight or size.\"","Fair enough. She had a storage ring anyway, so the storage space was just the icing on the cake.","The day after waking up, Yue Fuguang took a carriage back to the city with the Yu family. The autumn festival was the day after next, and as the discoverer of the high-yield seeds, she had to attend and even occupy one of the main seats.","On the carriage ride back, Yue Fuguang looked out the window at the sweet potato vines in the fields that were starting to turn yellow. While rubbing a translucent, quail egg-sized bead in her hand like a pair of Baoding balls, she asked the system, \"07, do you think this energy storage bead will work?\"","\"Don't worry, Host. Anything produced by the system is guaranteed to be of the highest quality.\" The system spoke quickly, blurting out the store's advertising slogan.","Worried that the overwhelming incense offerings might shock her soul and cause her to fall into a coma again, Yue Fuguang finally took the system's advice.","She spent a high price in the system store to buy an energy storage bead, which was said to be used by immortal cultivators to store spiritual energy, sword aura, or demonic energy.","She wanted to use it to store the power of the incense offerings that she couldn't digest.","The commoners were too enthusiastic. The autumn festival hadn't even started, and they hadn't even seen the sweet potatoes and corn yet, but they had already given her so much incense.","When the autumn festival arrived and the truth was verified, the incense offerings would definitely be much more than now, if not an astronomical amount.","Just as Yue Fuguang was thinking that the autumn festival would definitely attract more spectators than the one at the beginning of the year because of the new crops, the carriage slowed down.","She lifted a corner of the gauze curtain to look outside and saw that the shade under the trees on both sides of the road was full of people.","Yue Fuguang looked into the distance and saw Lotus Mountain. She calculated in her mind that they were still over ten miles away from the capital, so why were there suddenly so many people here?","Even if they were going to attend the autumn festival, it was too early.","Shen Chunying, who was riding a horse next to the carriage, saw Yue Fuguang lifting the curtain and leaned down to say, \"My Lady, there are too many commoners along the way. To avoid hurting anyone, the carriage will have to travel slowly for this stretch of the journey.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Why are there suddenly so many commoners here?\" She then said to Yue Huaixian, who was observing the situation next to the carriage, \"Cousin, go find out what's going on.\"","Yue Huaixian nodded. After asking someone by the roadside for the reason, he immediately ran back with a smile on his face.","Seeing Yue Fuguang waiting for his news, the corners of Yue Huaixian's mouth unconsciously turned up, revealing a proud smile. \"My Lady, these commoners have all rushed over from nearby prefectures and counties after hearing about the new crops that yield a thousand catties per mu.","They came just to attend the autumn festival the day after next, wanting to see the sweet potatoes, corn, potatoes, and Your Ladyship with their own eyes.\"","His cousin had truly saved countless lives this time, accumulating boundless merit!","The commoners along the way looked at the several carriages and the twenty or thirty guards at the front and back, knowing that the people in the carriages had extraordinary identities.","Afraid of offending the nobles, they unconsciously dodged to the side of the road.","However, there were some people with flickering eyes among them. Looking at the approaching carriages, not only did they not hide, but they also couldn't help but want to get closer.","After the carriage convoy had traveled for a few miles, someone in the crowd suddenly shouted, \"Look, that's Junior Preceptor Yue's carriage!\"","Following this shout, the commoners who were hiding along the way froze in place for a moment. They quietly looked at the most exquisite and beautiful carriage in the front.","\"Greetings to Junior Preceptor Yue!\"","Someone in the crowd shouted, and after the first person knelt down, the others followed suit like harvested wheat, falling to the ground and bowing to the carriage.","\"Greetings to Junior Preceptor Yue!\"","\"I beg Junior Preceptor Yue to bless my family!\"","\"I beg Junior Preceptor Yue to bless my family with a great harvest this year!\"","These were the relatively normal wishes directed at her, but there were also some mixed in, such as, \"I beg Junior Preceptor Yue to bless me with a wife this year!\"","\"I beg Junior Preceptor Yue to bless my wife with a baby boy this time!\"","The corners of Yue Fuguang's mouth twitched. Wasn't her jurisdiction a bit too broad? They were treating her like a turtle in a wishing well!","And having a boy? She wasn't the Goddess of Mercy who brings children. Would begging her be of any use?","Yue Fuguang thought about it carefully. Uh... it seemed like it might actually be useful!","However, the fertility pill was a minor trick after all, and she wasn't prepared to show it to others easily. Otherwise, if everyone wanted to have a boy, how would they find wives in the future? If the gender ratio was unbalanced and everyone ended up a bachelor, wouldn't society be in chaos?","Hmm? Yue Fuguang narrowed her eyes. Although a few people in the crowd were acting covertly, could she not tell the difference between kneeling and squatting, even with long robes covering them?","It wasn't that Yue Fuguang liked being knelt to, but these people were obviously suspicious.","The carriage moved forward slowly. Yue Fuguang sat in the carriage, but her voice carried far away. \"Everyone, there's no need for formalities. Please rise!\"","Following her command to rise, the people who were still kneeling felt as if their bodies were being lifted by an invisible force. Without needing to exert any effort themselves, they involuntarily stood up along with her words."]},{"number":340,"title":"Chapter 340: Intercept, Take Action","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang ignored only those who were squatting.","\"Do it!\" A man with an honest-looking face in the crowd gritted his teeth. Watching the carriage that was about to go far away, he finally couldn't hold back his greed and took the lead, charging out with his men.","The man had just rushed halfway when a group of people walked out of the crowd one after another. These people were dressed simply and looked even more like commoners than they did.","The man lowered his voice and shouted threateningly at the leader, \"Brother, don't get in the way!\"","It would have been fine if he hadn't shouted. The moment he did, he and a few of his fast-running lackeys were surrounded by these 'commoners'.","Then, from all directions, another thirty or forty people dressed as commoners, both men and women, rushed out in a swarm.","These people looked at each other, setting up offensive and defensive stances, but somehow they couldn't distinguish friend from foe. How were they supposed to fight?","Clang!","Clang!","\"Stop!\" Hearing the sound of Shen Chunying, He Jin, and the others drawing their swords, Yue Fuguang ordered her men to stop the carriage.","Rubbing her hands together, she wanted to watch a good show! And maybe find some live targets to test her 'skills' along the way.","\"Shen Chunying, you don't need to worry about me. Take good care of my grandparents and sisters, and tell them not to get off the carriage.\" Yue Fuguang's head was almost sticking out of the carriage window. She looked back while giving orders to the guards.","\"Yes, My Lady!\"","Shen Chunying agreed readily, without any nonsense or tug-of-war about staying behind to protect her under the guise of doing what was best for Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang nodded in satisfaction. The people around her really seemed to be very obedient. No matter what her orders were, no one questioned them; there was only strict execution and striving for the best.","Little did she know that while her only requirements for them were loyalty and obedience, the guard team was incredibly competitive internally.","Ever since Shen Chunying gained Yue Fuguang's favor and her cultivation level improved overnight, the already competitive guard team looked at Shen Chunying, and upon hearing that new members were about to join, they became even more fiercely competitive.","On the other side, seeing Yue Fuguang's carriage stop, some people secretly breathed a sigh of relief.","The various parties about to clash were still trying to distinguish friend from foe.","One of the middle-aged men stepped forward, cupped his hands to the crowd, and said, \"I am Chen Qi. May I ask which paths you brothers are from?\"","The real commoners, who had been stunned by the sudden turn of events, saw that these hundred or so people were holding either daggers or arm-thick clubs. Screaming, they hugged their heads and scattered far away.","Just like that, the relatively spacious concrete road was instantly cleared into a large open space, perfect for a brawl.","Hearing the question from the man calling himself Chen Qi, everyone looked at him, but no one stepped forward to answer.","After a few breaths of silence, a sturdy young man in gray stepped forward. He cupped his hands to Chen Qi and said, \"I am Shen Kang. Greetings, Brother Chen.\"","\"Song Xiang. Greetings, Brother Shen, Brother Chen.\"","Hearing these two familiar names, Yue Fuguang nearly choked on the pastry in her mouth. Good heavens, why were these two here?","And dressed like this, mingling among the commoners.","Yue Fuguang looked over and, upon seeing Shen Kang and Song Xiang's faces, couldn't help but secretly marvel. This disguise technique was absolutely incredible!","Both of them were wearing the gray-black clothes commonly worn by commoners. Their wheat-colored skin bore the marks of wind and frost, and their beards were scruffy, looking as if they hadn't been properly groomed for a long time.","If you didn't hear their voices and only looked at their faces, you could only say that apart from their gender and height, their faces didn't resemble their original selves at all!","No wonder she didn't realize there were acquaintances here at first!","Could they be here to catch bad guys?","She just didn't know how many of these hundred or so people were on her side.","The man who had shouted to strike at the beginning stepped forward and said, \"I am Xiao Yi. I have long heard of the Junior Preceptor's great name. It is fate that I ran into Her Ladyship here today, so I wish to invite her to be a guest at my home. I'd appreciate it if you all could make things convenient for me. I will surely reward you handsomely in the future!\"","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes. You invite me to be a guest, but did you ever ask for my opinion?","Before the man even finished speaking, he waved at the people behind him. Over a dozen people uniformly broke through the crowd or bypassed them, charging straight for Yue Fuguang's carriage.","\"Stop them!\"","At Shen Kang's command, the dozen or so people behind him simultaneously struck out to intercept them.","\"They are from the imperial court! Stop them quickly!\"","Seeing these people draw their weapons, a group of men in black suddenly rushed out from the side to block Shen Kang's subordinates. In an instant, the situation reversed, and Shen Kang's men went from the interceptors to the intercepted.","\"We are also here to lend Brother Xiao a hand!\"","Yue Fuguang's eyes went wide. Good heavens, in just this short amount of time, aside from Shen Kang's group and Xiao Yi, who was clearly looking for trouble with her, another twenty or so people jumped out, splitting into two factions alongside Chen Qi.","Aside from Song Xiang, an officer of the Crown Prince's Six Guards, there were still over forty people in the field who hadn't revealed their identities.","She just didn't know how many of them were brought by Song Xiang.","Yue Fuguang didn't have to wait long. Over a dozen of them leaped up one after another, all targeting her carriage.","\"Stop them! Protect the Junior Preceptor!\"","Song Xiang raised his blade and slashed, taking the lead to intercept one person.","And the man named Chen Qi, just like Song Xiang, intercepted another person.","This massive brawl broke out on a battlefield no more than fifty or sixty meters away from Yue Fuguang.","The various factions clashed furiously with clangs and bangs, but Yue Fuguang felt like she was watching a martial arts movie.","Although she had been assassinated many times, every time she watched this kind of real combat, it felt fresh, with different highlights each time. This was especially true now that she had absolute power to protect herself.","From Yue Fuguang, one could see that the national trait of loving to watch drama hadn't changed a bit, even after changing time and space.","[Host, these people are all coming for you. Can you put away your drama-loving face for a moment?]","'System, put your own face away before you talk about me!'","Don't think she didn't know. With the system's data restoration this time, the previously disadvantaged merit system had definitely recovered more.","However, a system's true nature was just like human nature; once awakened, it was very hard to change.","[I... I'm just afraid that Shen Kang and Song Xiang might suffer a loss, so I'm keeping a closer eye on them! The system can't bear to see our own people get hurt!]","'System, I am not what I used to be. Even without your defensive shield, I can emerge completely unscathed, believe it or not?'","The system glanced at Yue Fuguang's increasingly powerful soul and had to admit that the current host was indeed no longer the weakling she once was. It could only advise, [Host, keep a low profile! Low profile!]","Just as the person and the system were bickering, there was a sudden change in the field. Two of the men rushed out of the battlefield toward the commoners by the side of the road.","\"Don't let them escape!\" Seeing that the people he had been tracking were about to run away because they couldn't win, Shen Kang grew anxious and quickly led his men to pursue.","They had been tailing these people for two days and originally intended to capture them outside the city today, never expecting to accidentally run into the Junior Preceptor returning to the city.","And these people actually dared to make a move against the Junior Preceptor. They were simply audacious.","The two men trying to escape saw the pursuers behind them and exchanged a glance, a ruthless look flashing in their eyes. They kicked over a man who hadn't managed to run far and was hiding behind the bushes, and conveniently snatched a three or four-year-old boy from his arms, holding him by the collar."]},{"number":341,"title":"Chapter 341: Kneel Down","paragraphs":["Another person pulled an old man from the crowd, pressed a bloody dagger against his neck, and shouted loudly at Shen Kang and the others, \"Stop right there! Take one more step, and I'll take this old thing's life!\"","The snatched child, who had been crying loudly in terror, was so startled by this shout that he immediately stopped crying. However, his tears continued to fall silently in torrents as he sobbed and hiccuped, looking incredibly pitiful.","His father endured the pain in his chest and struggled to get up from the ground, but seeing the man's large hand reaching toward the child's neck, he didn't even dare to breathe loudly.","The old man with the knife at his neck was now so terrified that his legs trembled violently, and he kept crying out for mercy, \"Please, my lord, spare my life!\"","\"Please, my lord, let this humble old man go!\"","His family members also knelt on the ground, begging ceaselessly. But as ordinary commoners with no power, influence, or backing, they didn't even dare to beg loudly, terrified of angering the man with the knife.","Seeing the two men using an old man and a young child to threaten him, Shen Kang couldn't help but look back at Yue Fuguang's carriage.","Normally, they would do their best to save people, but they would not give up capturing the criminals just for the lives of one old man and one child.","In their eyes, the lives of ordinary commoners were naturally not as important as an imperial decree!","The ways of the world were just this harsh. In the eyes of the powerful and noble lords, commoners were like weeds; if one crop was lost, it wouldn't be long before another crop grew back.","However, ever since the Junior Preceptor appeared, and they learned that deities and the underworld truly existed in this world, they finally held genuine reverence for heaven and earth in their hearts, rather than just paying lip service like before.","This reverence was not solely for imperial power, but also for the underworld!","He didn't want to end up like his cousin Xie Zhiwei, entering the underworld prematurely, nor did he want to be burdened with a body full of sins after a hundred years.","Therefore, facing this threat, for the first time in his life, Shen Kang hesitated.","Seeing that his threat was effective, the man's wickedness emboldened him, and he grew even more audacious.","He continued shouting at Shen Kang, \"Throw your swords aside and tell your men to stop, now!\"","Shen Kang hesitated slightly. Looking at the criminals right in front of him, he wanted nothing more than to rush forward and capture them immediately. But the reverence in his heart and the Junior Preceptor's unclear stance made him pause his steps.","This lord always had a smiling face, but the consensus among the entire court was that she was actually a difficult immortal lord to deal with, and her temperament was hard to fathom. If he disregarded human lives today and angered her...","Seeing that he didn't comply, the scarred man couldn't help but press the knife closer to the old man's neck, and a line of blood instantly stained the blade red.","\"My lord, spare my life!\" the old man tried hard to shrink his neck back.","Standing beside him, the other man holding the child also pressed the child's neck closer to his own bloodstained dagger.","The child was about to cry when Scarface smiled fiercely and said, \"Even if my brothers and I die today, we'll drag this old man and kid down with us to pad our backs!\"","\"Even if I let you go now, where could you possibly run? You might as well surrender; you can still get lenient treatment!\"","The scarred man was unmoved by Shen Kang's words. His face showed a fierce expression, but his heart was incredibly anxious. He shouted loudly toward the crowd, \"Fourth Brother, Fifth Brother, take Second Brother and retreat quickly!\"","Just as the word retreat left his mouth, and before the people he called could break away from the battle, a muffled bang reached the ears of everyone present.","A mist of blood erupted, dyeing the green grass red.","Scarface, who had just been looking fierce and extremely arrogant, suddenly lost focus in his eyes, and the dagger in his hand fell to the ground with a clang.","Thud!","His entire body fell stiffly backward onto the ground, his eyes filled with unconcealable, deep confusion and bewilderment.","Aside from a large bloody hole in his forehead, there were no other injuries on him.","When Scarface fell, his eyes were still open, staring toward the sky, but he had already stopped breathing.","Scarface didn't know what happened even until his death, so he died with his eyes wide open!","All of this happened in just two or three breaths. Just as the crowd looked in horror at the fallen man, there was another muffled bang.","The other man holding the boy, standing two meters behind and to the side of Scarface, also fell at the sound. As he fell, his facial expression was forever frozen in the moment of terror toward the unknown, lethal hidden weapon.","He had seen the entire process of his older brother's death, but he could not comprehend this manner of dying.","Before he could figure anything out, the grim reaper had already claimed his life. The man's trembling hands, twitching face, and wide-open mouth caused by fear were all frozen in the second before death. His forever unclosable eyes were filled with the terror of death.","Two people died in the blink of an eye!","The entire area fell dead silent!","Shen Kang silently turned his head; he was far too familiar with this sound!","He swallowed hard, trying to tighten his grip on the sword that had almost slipped from his hand, doing his best not to think about what had just flown right past his ear!","He turned around, transforming the fear in his heart into anger, and charged toward the few people in the distance who were roaring, \"Big Brother! Third Brother!\"","The dead silent battlefield came alive again due to the crying and Shen Kang's running. However, when they fought again, they lacked their previous ferocity. Many had already developed the urge to retreat, just waiting for a command from their leader to scatter like birds and beasts.","Inside the carriage, Yue Fuguang, who had fired the sudden shots due to the sudden turn of events, expressed that the first shot grazing Shen Kang's ear was truly just a slip of the hand!","It was absolutely not a warning to him!","Since she had already made a move, Yue Fuguang glanced at the commoners in the distance, then turned her head and stepped out of the carriage.","She stood on the carriage with her hands behind her back, looking forward with a calm expression. From there, she could clearly see the entire battlefield, which made up for the awkwardness of her short stature.","Seeing her come out, He Jin did not urge her to go back inside, but silently stood behind and to the side of her to stand guard.","\"Stop!\" Yue Fuguang's voice was not loud, but it allowed everyone on the battlefield to hear it clearly.","As soon as her words left her mouth, everyone, whether willingly or unwillingly, seemed to be frozen in place. The hands raising swords halted at the moment of striking down, and it seemed the only things on their entire bodies that could still move were their slowly dilating pupils.","\"Kneel!\"","Thud! Thud! Thud!","As her words fell, the sound of knees hitting the ground was surprisingly uniform, without a single person hesitating.","No one could hear any reluctance in the action, and only the people kneeling at this moment knew that they were absolutely not willing!","Unfortunately, no one could speak up for them. Bound by some kind of power, they couldn't utter a single word.","The scene on the battlefield was a bit comical now. Some people were kneeling, and some were standing. The kneeling and standing people were paired up, staring wide-eyed at each other.","Yue Fuguang also instantly distinguished friend from foe.","Yue Fuguang didn't know how others were feeling right now, but she herself was secretly overjoyed. Although she had the assistance of hand seals just now, she believed that as long as she absorbed more incense power, wouldn't she truly be able to achieve the legendary state where words become law?","Then wouldn't it really be possible for her to turn the fake into reality, and truly become a deity walking among mortals?","She hardly dared to imagine it; how majestic that would be!","She secretly rejoiced here, her imaginative thoughts drifting away to the highest heavens.","Meanwhile, both friends and foes on the battlefield were thoroughly shocked and terrified by her move!"]},{"number":342,"title":"Chapter 342: Autumn Sacrifice","paragraphs":["Whether they had stopped and knelt down on their own accord, they knew better than anyone else in their hearts.","To stop fighting just because they were told to depended entirely on whether the enemy's blades agreed. If they didn't, they could only fight while retreating, waiting for an opportunity to obey the command and halt. After all, the words of the Junior Preceptor had to be obeyed.","The people of Great Yan all possessed this awareness. When the Junior Preceptor spoke, even the orders of their direct superiors were rendered useless.","This had been the initial thought of Shen Kang, Song Xiang, and their subordinates.","Unexpectedly, the other side actually \"agreed.\" Their hands moved faster than their brains, and they followed suit, stopping their attacks.","As for the subsequent kneeling, that was obviously not aimed at them!","They firmly believed that the Junior Preceptor could still distinguish between her own people and the enemy.","Yue Fuguang: As long as you are happy!","So now, both friends and foes on the field were eerily quiet. The kneeling villains were trembling all over, cold sweat pouring down their faces, unsure if it was from the heat or from sheer terror.","If stopping just now could be called an accident, then as they knelt, they truly felt a massive pull from an invisible hand on the ground.","When they endured the pain and tried to stand up, they found that their bodies felt as heavy as a thousand pounds!","They couldn't get up at all! Even their pleas for mercy were blocked in their throats, unable to be uttered!","We are doomed!","My life is over!","Yue Fuguang: I was afraid I would grow soft-hearted if they begged for mercy, so is it wrong to silence them?","System: Host, do you even possess such a thing as a soft heart?","The despair of death enveloped these dozens of men who had originally wanted to risk their lives for wealth and glory.","Especially those few who had been near the roadside during the \"battle\" just now, having witnessed the entire process of the kidnapping, the threats, and the inexplicable deaths. They knelt obediently in the direction of Yue Fuguang's carriage.","Paralyzed by fear, they kept themselves prostrated on the ground. When their accomplices resisted and tried to stand up, they didn't dare make a single unnecessary movement.","Yue Fuguang actually had another move she had not yet tested, but since everyone was currently kneeling and there was no suitable target, she couldn't help but feel a little disappointed.","Since the turmoil was resolved, Yue Fuguang directly ordered the two men, \"Song Xiang, capture everyone and take them away! Shen Kang, pacify the commoners!\"","\"Yes, my Lord!\" The two bowed to her and answered loudly in unison.","Yue Fuguang resisted the urge to plug her ears. There was really no need to be so loud; she could hear them perfectly fine!","She was certain that these two idiots had definitely used their internal energy just now.","Just as she turned around to return to the carriage, she accidentally caught sight of Song Xiang and Shen Kang looking at each other. In perfect sync, they both raised their eyebrows at one another in a provocative display.","\"System, what just happened wasn't aimed at me, right?\"","Otherwise, it would be truly frustrating to encounter assassinations every now and then. Although Yue Fuguang had already foreseen that she would encounter more of these incidents after the autumn harvest, it didn't stop her from feeling annoyed by the abundance of flies and mosquitoes buzzing around her right now.","[Host, we just happened to be at the right place at the right time. Because the Autumn Sacrifice is approaching, Wei Ping and Cai Xian have been working with the newly established Secret Spy Division these past few days and discovered many spies from various major factions.","So they sent Shen Kang and Song Xiang to arrest them, and they just happened to bump into us returning to the city.","These people didn't know they had already been exposed and still thought they could capture you to claim a reward.","Host, ever since the rumors of sweet potatoes and corn spread, your value has doubled. The bounty on your head in the black market is incredibly high!]","The more the system spoke, the more excited it became. Although she couldn't see it, Yue Fuguang could perfectly imagine its thrilled expression.","Why were her hands suddenly itching so much!","\"System, is this really something worth being happy about? Although I am safe and sound, there are always these flies coming out to disgust people, and it's quite annoying, okay?\" These people were like weeds; cut one batch down, and another would spring up. They simply couldn't be wiped out completely.","Besides, assassination had always been an unsolvable problem throughout history and across the world. She just thought about it briefly and stopped dwelling on it. She would deal with whatever came her way.","[Host, just treat it as watching a play. Look, if it weren't for your unexpected appearance today, Song Xiang and Shen Kang would at most only have been able to catch the thirty or so people they had investigated.","The extra dozen or so people were all opportunists trying to fish in troubled waters.","Host, apart from those few emperors, you are now the biggest, most fragrant bait in this world. One cast catches a whole string of people!]","Yue Fuguang: Am I the kind of person who sacrifices herself for others? They want to use me as bait? They shouldn't be surprised if they break their teeth on me.","\"System, if you upgrade to level five, will you be able to come out for some fresh air?\"","[Yes! So Host, you must work hard and quickly upgrade to level five so you can let me out for some fresh air!]","It was the most pitiful system in the world. Thinking of its peers, they could roam the real world at level two, but it had to reach level five just to gain that ability, and even then, there were various restrictions.","System 07 spun around speechlessly. Had it destroyed a planet in its previous life to be treated like this?!","Before Yue Fuguang's carriage even entered the capital, the news of her assassination attempt had already spread throughout the upper echelons of Great Yan.","Emperor Mingxi pointed at their noses and severely scolded Cai Xian, Wei Ping, Feng Tang, and Zheng Zicheng—who was Zheng Feng's father and the newly appointed Deputy Envoy of the Secret Spy Division.","Afterward, the Emperor himself was summoned to Shou'an Palace by the Empress Dowager and given a stern lecture. Accompanying him in the scolding was the Chief Envoy of the Secret Spy Division, Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan.","By the time the father and son emerged from Shou'an Palace looking thoroughly crestfallen, Yue Fuguang had already finished receiving her family's warm, anxious greetings and was enjoying her lunch.","As for the Yu family father and son, they were busy receiving visitors from various families who came to check on them. They drank a lot of tea and received countless gifts, not resting until the evening.","Yue Fuguang, who had already struck it rich, looked at the room full of gifts and couldn't help but think that if she ever truly ran out of money one day, she could probably become wealthy again just by relying on these presents.","The sun and moon moved on, and another day passed.","The capital city was bustling with crowds and extraordinary liveliness on the surface, while behind the scenes, Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and the members of the Secret Spy Division were so busy they were run off their feet. Thus arrived the twenty-third day of the eighth month in the fifth year of Yuankang.","At three quarters past the hour of Yin, the waning moon had not yet set. A thin layer of frost condensed on the three-tier white jade railings of the Circular Mound Altar in the southern suburbs, and seventy-two bronze eternal lamps swayed, casting solemn halos in the autumn wind.","The top of the altar held the spirit tablets of deities such as the Lunar and Solar Gods, while the east side featured the altar for worshipping the God of Agriculture. In front of the ochre curtains stood various agricultural tools wrapped in silk, and nine pottery tureens were filled to the brim with potatoes, corn, and sweet potatoes that Shen Jian had personally dug up the previous night under imperial orders.","On both sides of the yellow earth imperial path, extending three hundred paces from the crimson steps, stood the Imperial Feathered Forest Guards in black robes and red skirts, gripping their halberds. Behind them were eight hundred lacquer trees laden with golden-red persimmons.","When the cool morning breeze swept across the bronze and stone chimes on the racks of the Court of Imperial Sacrifices' music troupe, it occasionally brought forth a low, resonant hum. This intertwined with the distant sound of carriages and horses and the approaching voices of the crowd, forming a unique harmony.","When Yue Fuguang arrived, everything was ready. Following the guidance of the Ministry of Rites, she ascended to the second level of the altar and once again stood beside the Crown Prince.","As Yue Fuguang sized up this newly built altar, she couldn't help but mutter internally. Every single time, she was placed in this exact position, making her look as though she were the second heir to the dynasty.","It was only because it was her; if it had been anyone else, they would have been suspected to death by now.","Thinking of the troubles that had arisen from building this altar, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but ask Xie Zhiyan, who was standing perfectly straight, \"Crown Prince, more than a month has passed. How is the growth of that newly planted batch of sweet potatoes?\"","She had just arrived right on time and had only caught a hasty glimpse, unable to clearly see the situation in the sweet potato fields at all."]},{"number":343,"title":"Chapter 343: Gather the Grain","paragraphs":["Xie Zhiyan smiled, his eyes brighter than the fading stars on the horizon. \"Rest assured, Junior Preceptor. The sweet potatoes in those dozens of acres have all survived and are growing exceptionally well.","Elder Lord Wang Shouchen said they will be ready for harvest in less than two months.\"","Calculating the time, they could be stored in the granary by the end of October. The capital usually saw snow around mid-November, so it was a great fortune to be able to harvest them before the heavy snow. This was all thanks to the Junior Preceptor soaking them in spiritual water.","Therefore, upon learning of the assassination attempt on the Junior Preceptor, he, his imperial father, and his cousin Shen Kang, who had gone to handle errands, were severely reprimanded by his imperial grandmother.","It was said that the divine tablet enshrined in his grandmother's rear hall had long been secretly replaced with a jade statue of the Junior Preceptor, just like his mother's.","He had seen it, and could only say that the jade artisan's carving skills were extraordinary. The statue's demeanor perfectly captured the Junior Preceptor's current appearance—a faint smile on her lips, yet inspiring an unavoidable sense of awe.","Yue Fuguang did not know what Xie Zhiyan was thinking. She nodded, toying with the jade pendant hanging at her waist. \"Send someone to harvest the sugar beets on my estate in a few days. The profit share from the sugar production will be divided as we previously agreed.\"","Thinking of the severe drought in the eighth year of Yuankang, Yue Fuguang did not plan to promote the large-scale cultivation of sugar beets right now, so she added, \"Do not expand the planting for the next two years.","We will wait until my master's prophecy regarding the natural disaster has passed.\"","Xie Zhiyan nodded solemnly. \"Everything will be done according to the Junior Preceptor's wishes.\"","To prepare for the natural disaster two years from now, the Ministry of Works, the Ministry of Revenue, and the Court of Imperial Agriculture were arguably the three busiest government offices.","One was responsible for water conservancy projects, with people all over the country feverishly digging canals and wells to store more water for the future.","One was responsible for financial support, and the other for planning grain cultivation for the next two years.","He looked at the tens of thousands of acres of fertile fields in the distance, deeply curious about exactly how much grain a single acre could produce.","Everyone, from the emperor to the civil and military officials, from the rich to the poor, shared Xie Zhiyan's thoughts. Their hearts felt as though they were being scratched by a cat, anxiously counting every drop of the water clock.","As the sun rose, the Grand Prayer Official waved a vermilion command flag, and the burnt-offering furnace suddenly billowed with the fresh fragrance of pine and cypress.","The Emperor, wearing the twelve-symbol dark and crimson sacrificial robes and a green jade disc at his waist, walked slowly up the dragon-patterned steps to the tune of the \"Chapter of Universal Harmony\" from the Central Harmony Shao Music.","With every step he took, the ritual official chanted loudly, \"Tread the hardships of sowing and reaping, remember the heavy burden of the people's heaven.\" When he reached the top, the first light of dawn from the east illuminated the bronze grain-patterned tripod before the altar.","At exactly the hour of Si, the first offering was made.","Wang Shouchen, Chief Minister of the Court of Imperial Agriculture, slowly stepped forward holding a modified military shovel. The Emperor took the tool and mimed the action of hoeing and digging the field.","Planted in the large earthen vessel before him were the potatoes transported from Xuanwei Prefecture and the sweet potatoes that Shen Jian had personally dug up from the imperial estate yesterday.","Emperor Mingxi tossed one dug-up potato and one sweet potato into the tripod.","Yun Tianxing, Director of the Directorate of Astronomy, handed freshly brewed sweet wine to Emperor Mingxi. He took the wine goblet and poured the liquid into the octagonal earthen vessel. As the wine seeped into the soil, the observing village elders began to sing the \"Song of Harvest\" in unison: \"In the eighth month we build the threshing floor, in the ninth month we gather the crops...\"","The steam from the grand sacrifice of the three beasts mixed with the unique sweet aroma of the sweet potatoes, rising into blue smoke.","Yue Fuguang looked up and watched the Emperor take a gilded wine vessel, sprinkling the fine liquor over the fertile soil in the four directions of east, south, west, and north.","The final offering was the sacrificial text co-written by the Ministry of Rites and the great talents of the Hanlin Academy.","Standing amidst the curling incense smoke, the Emperor unrolled the sacrificial text with its green jade rollers, his voice echoing across the fields: \"In the autumn of the fifth year of Yuankang, the year of Bingwu, on the Renzi day of the eighth month, I, the succeeding Son of Heaven and subject, dare to declare to... Possessing the four virtues, joining with heaven and earth, harmonizing with the sun and moon, changing with the four seasons, beautiful in clothing, moderate in food and drink, the dawn is lush, the swan's traces are vast, relying on those above and below, the fields and crops are blessed to be enjoyed, the grand offering of joyful arts, spiritual cattle and spiritual sheep, two households and two males... The high gods are solemn, the four seas are bright and vast, the ghosts and gods are clear, the ghosts and gods are familiar...\"","This rhythmic, undulating voice was incredibly hypnotic; Yue Fuguang felt sleepy just listening to it.","She glanced at Xie Zhiyan, whose gaze was equally somewhat vacant, knowing that while the guy's body was here, his soul had flown off to who knows where.","There were quite a few officials and commoners whose minds were wandering just like the two of them. Everyone was curious about the yield in the fields; who had the patience to listen to the Emperor's lengthy nonsense!","When Emperor Mingxi threw the sacrificial text into the furnace to burn, a flock of wild geese suddenly swept across the horizon. The drowsy crowd slowly woke up in the atmosphere created by the firelight.","\"Your Majesty, look at the sky!\" Yun Tianxing shouted excitedly, pointing upwards. \"The flock of geese looks like the character for Abundance! Your Majesty, this is a sign sent down by heaven and earth!\"","The sovereign and his subjects looked up at the sky. Yue Fuguang had good eyesight and saw clouds with colorful edges floating in the bright blue sky. The multicolored display looked very auspicious.","Beneath the colorful clouds, a flock of geese, visibly numbering around a hundred, flew across the sky. The formation passed right over everyone's heads, and looking up from below, it indeed looked very much like the character for harvest.","As the civil and military officials and the common people shouted \"Long live the King,\" their voices shaking the forests and fields, Yue Fuguang was thinking that if she hadn't seen it with her own eyes, she would have thought they were actors hired by the Emperor for dramatic effect.","She remembered that when she went to school as a child, the textbooks clearly stated that geese would sometimes fly in the shape of a horizontal line, and sometimes in a V-shape.","How could they form the character for Abundance?","She stared at the departing flock of geese, and the more she looked, the more something felt off. Although they were high and far away, Yue Fuguang was not the same as before; her eyesight was excellent.","Soon, she spotted two show-offs, one in front and one in back, within the flock that had now shifted into a V-shape. Her mouth twitched uncontrollably.","Those two clowns, who else could they be but her Taxue and Wuhen!","These two had really become spirits, putting on a show for her here! Even if she lacked confidence in herself, did she lack confidence in the system's products and the spiritual rain?","Even without this auspicious sign, a bountiful harvest was inevitable.","Xie Zhiyan noticed the change in Yue Fuguang's expression and swallowed the words that were on the tip of his tongue.","Do not ask what shouldn't be asked; that was his mother's warning to him.","After everyone's excitement subsided, the main event of the day finally arrived: harvesting the grain!","Yue Fuguang followed Emperor Mingxi to the intersection of the sweet potato and corn fields.","She and the Crown Prince now each held a military shovel in their hands. After the Emperor dug the first spadeful, they followed suit and dug forcefully.","The civil and military officials standing behind the three of them, as well as the common people further away, all watched their movements eagerly.","Wang Shouchen and a few others watched as Yue Fuguang thrust the sharp shovel into the soil without even looking. Their hearts leaped into their throats, as if the shovel was not digging into the ground, but stabbing right into their lungs.","Whether it was the hundreds of officials and guards present, the tens of thousands of commoners further away, or the hundreds of thousands stretching for over a dozen miles.","At this moment, it was as if a pause button had been pressed. They maintained a surprisingly unanimous silence, as if terrified that even the slightest noise would scare away the grain buried in the soil.","The silence of these hundreds of thousands of people was all in anticipation of one result.","The soil quality of the imperial estate was good, and the farmers on the estate had cared for it meticulously. The soil was loose, so without much effort from the three of them, a large sweet potato plant was unearthed.","Gasp!","Gasp!","Everyone's burning gazes focused on the root of that half-yellow seedling. Below it hung eight or nine large and small, long and short, shuttle-shaped red tubers. Judging by their color, anyone who saw them would feel that the name red potato was well-deserved."]},{"number":344,"title":"Chapter 344: Grateful thanks to the Young Master for his gracious compassion","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang looked at the size of the sweet potatoes and estimated their weight.","As the surrounding people were already getting excited, she shook her head in dissatisfaction, silently picked up the shovel, and dug a few more times into the soil.","Her actions were naturally seen by the excited crowd who had been constantly paying attention to the situation here. After calculating the weight of the eight or nine sweet potatoes from this single vine, those with experience had already begun estimating the yield per acre.","If every vine yielded eight or nine of them, regardless of size, a rough calculation meant that an acre of sweet potatoes could yield at least five or six thousand jin, maybe even seven thousand jin. The yield of these sweet potatoes was even higher than that of potatoes!","Whether it was due to excitement or something else, Yue Fuguang realized that aside from the sound of sharp intakes of breath, not a single person made a sound.","Even as Wang Shouchen, Ling Yinghua, and the others shed tears of excitement, they did so silently. This ocean of excitement was a silent pantomime.","Yue Fuguang swept her peripheral vision over the crowd. Some officials were trembling with excitement like Parkinson's patients, while others looked as though their eyes were about to roll back in their heads.","At this moment, they simultaneously watched the Junior Preceptor digging into the earth again. Aside from the different clothing... how familiar was this scene?","Dead memories were awakened. Those who were trembling trembled even more, and those shedding tears wept more fiercely. Only those on the verge of passing out relied on their sheer willpower, pinching their thighs hard to keep themselves from fainting on the spot.","They kept coaxing themselves inwardly: they could not faint. Missing this moment of witnessing history would surely be a lifelong regret.","What is more... the crowd tightly gripped the military shovels in their hands, using them to support their tottering bodies. What is more, they would have to take the field themselves later—they absolutely could not miss it!","Facing hundreds, even thousands of eyes, Yue Fuguang did not panic at all. This was mainly because she had an enigmatic confidence in the products of the System and the efficacy of the spiritual rainwater.","Just now, when she started digging the sweet potatoes, she was slacking off and just going through the motions, but now she was using her true strength.","After a few shovelfuls, a small pit was dug in the ridge of the field. Just like the last time she dug potatoes, this time the harvest was also abundant.","After a bout of professional digging by Yue Fuguang, five sweet potatoes of varying sizes lay in the black soil.","Ho, ho!","Someone unconsciously let out a hoarse gasping sound. The crowd stared at the newly dug sweet potatoes with different postures and expressions, their faces flushed red, not uttering a single word.","\"Weigh them!\" It was Emperor Mingxi who recovered his senses first. A single command to weigh them broke the silence and awakened the crowd that had fallen into a stupor.","Wang Shouchen, who was originally responsible for weighing, stared at the small pile of sweet potatoes on the ground. He had slumped to the earth and was completely unable to stand up.","Seeing this, the young and strong Wei Ping, Feng Tang, and a few others quickly stepped forward, picked up the scale, and began weighing.","Yue Fuguang thought to herself: I thought you guys would help the old lord up, but I didn't expect you to just grab the work for yourselves!","Although both of their hands were shaking, and the sweat on their palms got mixed with a bit of mud when grabbing the sweet potatoes, the two of them worked together and finally managed to place the dozen or so sweet potatoes onto the scale pan.","Old Lord Wang Shouchen reached out a desperate hand, desperately wanting to shout: Put down those sweet potatoes and let this old man do it!","This was originally my job! Will no one speak up for this old man? Screaming groundhog image.","Unfortunately, his strength failed him. The more anxious he got, the more he just let out hoarse gasps, the only difference being that they were slightly louder.","However, among everyone present, other than Yue Fuguang, no one paid attention to his burning anxiety.","The crowd's eyes followed the sliding weight back and forth to find the exact mark, moving up and down to determine the weight.","Yue Fuguang glanced at the crowd, who were staring with bloodshot eyes and looking utterly obsessed. She wondered if they would be able to hold up later—what if a few of them actually fainted?","What a sin, what a sin!","Although she cried \"sin\" in her heart, Yue Fuguang was actually quite looking forward to seeing exactly how many would faint at once. She was truly very curious!","The crowd was also very curious, only their curiosity was not on the same wavelength as Yue Fuguang's.","\"Sixteen jin and eight taels!\"","\"Sixteen jin and eight taels...\"","Wei Ping shouted with a trembling voice, and Feng Tang loudly echoed him with a hoarse throat.","The echo of Feng Tang's voice still lingered, yet the field once again fell into a terrifying silence.","Wang Shouchen only felt a buzz in his brain. The entire world turned a dark, ashen gray; only the sweet potatoes on the scale pan remained a vibrant red, perhaps even redder than before.","He was not the only one who fell backward to the ground. If Emperor Mingxi had not been caught by the Crown Prince's quick reflexes, he too would have followed the crowd and slumped onto the dirt.","Yue Fuguang's eyes darted around as she silently began to count heads!","Beside her, Emperor Mingxi had tightly gripped the hand the Crown Prince was using to support him. With tears in his eyes, he looked at the sweet potato field and said, \"Eldest son, did I hear that wrong? Was it sixteen jin and eight taels?\"","Xie Zhiyan, also terrified that his old man might pass out, hurriedly nodded and repeatedly agreed, \"Yes, yes, yes, Imperial Father, you did not hear wrong. Lord Wei and the others weighed it at exactly sixteen jin and eight taels!\"","The father and son were now supporting each other, both feeling the rapid thumping of each other's hearts and their trembling hands.","Emperor Mingxi's eyes went blank for a moment before he suddenly shouted, as if experiencing a sudden burst of terminal lucidity, \"Crown Prince, Crown Prince... Great Yan... is saved! It is saved!\"","Hearing these words, tears instantly streamed down Xie Zhiyan's face. He nodded desperately, \"Imperial Father is right, Great Yan... is saved!\"","Although Yue Fuguang had brought out various technologies and seeds prior to this, and because of her inner voice, the entire Great Yan dynasty had already avoided many people and events that would have led to its gradual downfall.","But because of natural disasters, and because of the endless spies and traitors that could never be fully rooted out, in truth, from the sovereign down to the ministers, Great Yan had always kept its heart in its throat.","Although they occasionally got a little carried away in the face of various achievements, not once had they felt as certain as they did upon seeing these sweet potatoes: Great Yan was saved!","As long as the vast majority of the common people had full bellies and did not revolt, even if Great Yan faced the schemes of several nations and domestic crises, they would always find a way to stabilize the situation.","\"We kowtow and thank the Heavens for its mercy!\"","\"We bow and thank the Junior Preceptor for her mercy!\"","\"We kowtow and thank the Heavens for its mercy!\"","\"We bow and thank the Junior Preceptor for her mercy!\"","...","The continuous shouts and commotion from the civil and military officials naturally attracted the attention of the observing commoners in the distance. From afar, they could see the Emperor and the lords digging the earth.","They were so nervous and excited that they did not dare to breathe too loudly. Even the young children in the women's arms and the mischievous boys riding on their fathers' shoulders were uncharacteristically quiet and well-behaved at this moment.","The commoners had been waiting quietly for quite a while. Why were the Emperor and those high officials either standing still or lying down, just not moving at all!","If they had known that digging the earth was so strenuous for the Emperor and the lords, they should have just let them do it!","They dealt with the land all year round and had plenty of strength.","In the crowd, a few people looked at the commoners craning their necks to see forward. Among them, a tall, skinny young man spoke in a moderate voice, \"Big brother, do you think maybe the crops in the field did not grow well, so the Emperor and the lords...\"","He did not finish his sentence, but his unspoken words provoked endless speculation.","Some people were swayed upon hearing his words, but the vast majority did not quite believe it. An elderly farmer looked at this beardless young man who spoke so carelessly and uttered inauspicious words right off the bat. He could not help but scold him, \"What do you young people know! I have been dealing with the land for decades.","Just by looking at the seedlings, I know the harvest in the field cannot go wrong.\""]},{"number":345,"title":"Chapter 345: Forever in the Annals of History","paragraphs":["He might be old and dim-sighted, but he wasn't blind in his heart. Those tall, tree-like plants and the continuous vines across the field were clearly meticulously tended.","Even if the yield per acre wasn't as high as the potatoes they had seen earlier, it wouldn't be far off.","\"Old Man Liu is right, we also believe in the Lord Junior Preceptor!\"","\"Yes, we believe in the Lord Junior Preceptor!\"","The tall, thin young man who had spoken first looked displeased. Being reprimanded by that mud-legged old man was one thing, but how did these people bring the topic back to that Junior Preceptor Yue after just two sentences?","He really wanted to say, what does the grain yield per acre have to do with your Lord Junior Preceptor? What is the use of believing in her!","Just as he was about to retort, he was held back by the man beside him, whom he called 'Big Brother'.","That man was also dressed as a farmer. With his bronze skin, he was entirely inconspicuous in the crowd. Had the person next to him not spoken, no one would have noticed these two 'brothers'.","The man shook his head at the youth, signaling him to say no more. He who talks much errs much. Couldn't he see that people around them were already secretly sizing them up?","Since their provocative words had no effect, it was not suitable to say more. Although these ignorant mud-legs couldn't hear the hidden provocation in their words, their natural desire to protect that Junior Preceptor Yue was exceptionally firm, unexpectedly ruining their little scheme.","The man thought of how his master's household had recently been constrained at every turn because of the one sitting in the imperial court, making life in the estate increasingly difficult.","Even close servants like them were forced to restrain their actions. They could no longer be as reckless as before. If they fancied someone's wife or daughter, they could no longer just bring her home regardless of whether her parents and brothers agreed, as they used to.","In the past, even if they bullied men, seized women, and beat to death the family members who came to their door to cause trouble, they were never afraid of facing a lawsuit.","Although they were domestic slaves, being favored by their master made them used to being above others. To make them recognize their status now, return to the bottom, and have lives as cheap as grass like these commoners—how could they endure it!","The man looked up, vaguely discerning the movements of His Majesty the Emperor and the officials through the surging crowd.","He secretly prayed in his heart that the crops in the field had better all rot and ruin!","It was a pity that the fire didn't burn this imperial estate clean... Song Xiao'er was truly a piece of trash!","Just as the malice in the man's heart was about to turn him into a demon, waves of exclamations and cries grew louder and louder in his ears.","His eyes suddenly lit up. Could his wish be coming true? The grain in the fields was indeed...","\"Sixteen catties and eight taels!\"","\"The official said sixteen catties and eight taels!\"","\"What sixteen catties and eight taels?\"","Someone asked urgently, not quite understanding what this weight, which they understood upon hearing, actually represented.","While the crowd was urgently inquiring, the tall, thin youth couldn't help but run his mouth again, \"Could it be that one acre only yields sixteen catties and eight taels?\"","He spoke with a laugh. On a normal day, people would just think it was a frivolous joke by a young man who didn't know the gravity of the situation.","But at this moment, to say such a thing, the malice was practically plastered on everyone's faces. Even the most honest and naive man could sense that this person clearly did not want the land to have a good harvest!","This kind of person didn't seem like someone who relied on the land to eat.","\"Young man, you can skip a meal, but you can't speak nonsense. All of us are hoping for a high yield of the divine grain, so that us poor commoners can have a full meal!\"","\"Yes, we all hope for a high yield of the divine grain so we can eat our fill!\"","\"High yield of divine grain, we eat our fill!\" The young men in the crowd joined in the shouting, their righteous indignation directed at the young man who had just spoken.","His 'Big Brother' glared at the young man, frustrated by his incompetence, and had to step forward to apologize. \"Old sir, brothers, please forgive us. My younger brother doesn't know how to speak. In fact, we brothers are also full of hope that the divine grain can yield thousands or tens of thousands of catties per acre.\"","When he said 'tens of thousands of catties,' he emphasized it heavily. It seemed sincere, but few would believe his words.","Just as the crowd's gaze toward the two brothers grew increasingly suspicious, waves of exclamations came from the front again.","\"The official said it's sweet potatoes, one sweet potato plant yields sixteen catties and eight taels!\"","\"Sixteen catties and eight taels for one sweet potato plant!\"","\"Datou, did the official say how many sweet potatoes can be planted in one acre?\" an elegantly dressed old man asked the burly man passing the message in front of him.","\"Sir Scholar, I don't know either.\" The man called Datou blushed and shook his head in embarrassment.","Seeing the crowd's disappointment, he added, \"Word from the front says that the Emperor has ordered the farmers to start digging. Maybe we'll know in a while.\"","He scratched his head honestly, \"A few hundred catties per acre should be possible.\" They were all experienced farmers, they had at least this much judgment.","Emperor Mingxi indeed ordered to dig up one acre of the sweet potato field first to weigh the yield, but the ones doing the digging were not farmers.","Instead, they were the high officials from the imperial court, wearing purple and crimson robes, or at the very least blue robes.","Those minor officials in green robes could only stand at the edge of the field and stare blankly, alongside their precious Emperor.","However, having an even more precious Lord Junior Preceptor standing nearby made them feel somewhat balanced in their hearts.","Yue Fuguang sat under the Emperor's imperial yellow silk umbrella, drinking fragrant tea personally poured by Qian Gui, and said to Xie Zhiyan, who was eager to try and join the sweet potato digging army, \"Crown Prince, go to the next field and break off a few ears of corn to weigh.\"","Xie Zhiyan's eyes lit up. Right, because the sweet potatoes were such a gem in front of them, how did everyone forget about the corn!","\"Lord Junior Preceptor, wait a moment, I'll be right back!\"","After speaking, he hurriedly left with Song Xiang and a few others.","Emperor Mingxi looked at his eldest son, who was rarely so lively. Lacking his usual steady composure, he led people to rush to the very front, not even letting Song Xiang and the others clear the way before plunging into the slightly yellowing green gauze tent of crops. He lifted the hem of his bright yellow Crown Prince attire and casually tucked it into his jade belt.","Emperor Mingxi couldn't help but frown. Just as he was about to say something, he saw Yue Fuguang's appreciative gaze and held his tongue.","Out of the corner of his eye, he could already see his trusted ministers, sweating profusely, their official hats askew from the effort of digging the ground.","Senior officials like Wang Shouchen, Ling Yinghua, and Bao Yuanjun had already begun using the hems of their brand-new official robes to hold large, bright sweet potatoes, walking towards him.","The reprimands he wanted to utter completely dissipated the moment he saw the sweet potatoes.","To be honest, if it weren't for his status, he would have wanted to join in and personally harvest Great Yan's first acre of sweet potatoes.","This moment would surely be recorded in the annals of history and remembered by future generations.","Emperor Mingxi's thought was correct; this scene was indeed recorded forever in the annals of history. The General History of Great Yan - Basic Annals of Agricultural Administration recorded: In the autumn of the fifth year of Yuankang, on the Rengzi day of the eighth month, the Emperor personally led the hundred officials to the Shanglin Park in the suburbs of the capital to harvest the divine grain called sweet potato... The Three Dukes and Nine Ministers... The purple and crimson robes shone brightly among the field paths. The Minister of Agriculture measured the soil with a jade tablet, the Grand Astrologer stood by with bamboo slips, and the Libationer held the potatoes in his official robe. Their shape was like a shuttle, their color like red jade, heavy as black jade, with numerous fruits hanging from a single vine.","The Emperor rejoiced and held them up to show the masses. The ministers bowed in congratulation, their voices shaking the forests and fields.","(Appendix: Excerpt from the Diaries of Activity and Repose: The Emperor wiped his sweat and smiled at the Junior Preceptor: \"You said the sweet potato was refreshingly sweet, you indeed did not deceive Us.\")","The young preceptor remained seated and replied, \"Though simple and unadorned, this is far superior to the fine nectar served in the imperial courts.\"","The Emperor unfastened his blade to help sever the vines. The jade inlaid upon his scabbard fell and was lost in the fields, yet he made no effort to search for it. The peasants later passed this tale down as the \"Admonition of the Buried Jade,\" saying it meant one should value the harvest over precious jewels."]},{"number":346,"title":"Chapter 346: The Name of the Goddess","paragraphs":["At this moment, His Majesty the Emperor, who had completely forgotten about the existence of the Imperial Diarist beside him, heard Yue Fuguang mention that sweet potatoes could be eaten raw and tasted quite good. Emperor Mingxi followed her advice. He held a small knife to peel the sweet potato, and once the pinkish-white flesh was revealed, he couldn't help but take a bite.","It was surprisingly sweet and crisp, very delicious.","The ministers craned their necks to look, their eyes full of desire. Some even unconsciously swallowed along with Emperor Mingxi.","Everyone's performance today was completely seen by the inconspicuous minor official in a green robe behind them—the Imperial Diarist. He watched without blinking and recorded every move and every word of the monarch and his subjects without missing a single detail.","Even someone like Yue Fuguang, who cared about her public image, tried her best to avoid this person.","One acre of land was quickly harvested with everyone's concerted efforts. The sweet potatoes were specially cleaned of dirt and piled together. From a distance, it looked like a small red hill.","Bring the scales! Emperor Mingxi ordered. A dozen people from the Ministry of Revenue took out the large scales and record books they had prepared in advance, and began to weigh and record methodically.","Everyone's attention was on the yield per acre of the sweet potatoes. They had no mind to pay attention to the corn that Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan and his subordinates carried back trip after trip using the hems of their robes.","Only Yue Fuguang, who didn't care much about the sweet potato yield, quietly gave an order to the Crown Prince, asking him to harvest an acre of corn as well, husk it, and wait to weigh it.","Your Majesty! Eight... eight thousand... two hundred and sixty-six jin!","Eight thousand two hundred and sixty-six jin!","Beloved Subject Dong, what did you say?","Emperor Mingxi's face went blank for a moment. His lips trembled slightly, his hands shook non-stop like a Parkinson's patient, and his voice couldn't help but rise a few pitches.","Although he had anticipated that sweet potatoes would definitely have a high yield, his highest estimate in his heart was only five or six thousand jin at most.","So at this moment, caught off guard by the weight of eight thousand two hundred and sixty-six jin, he felt a bit dizzy, as if all the bones in his body had become lighter.","Your Majesty, this humble subject said, the sweet potato yield per acre is eight thousand two hundred and sixty-six jin!","After getting confirmation again, the monarch and subjects of Great Yan completely fell into ecstasy. Everyone celebrated with each other, and all bowed deeply to Yue Fuguang, who was sitting leisurely under an umbrella drinking tea.","Facing everyone's thanks and bows, Yue Fuguang remained calm on the surface, but she was somewhat disappointed in her heart. The sweet potatoes of Great Yan were strictly selected by the system and blessed by two spiritual rains, yet the yield per acre still didn't break ten thousand jin.","Little Zhu, the soil fertility of Great Yan is still too weak. Even with the irrigation of spiritual rain, the yield actually hasn't surpassed ten thousand jin!","When the commoners plant it, without the blessing of the spiritual rain, and with soil even more barren than the imperial estate, wouldn't the yield be even lower?","It wasn't that Yue Fuguang wanted to pour cold water on the monarch and subjects of Great Yan, but she wanted to remind them not to let one unexpectedly high yield go to their heads, lest they become too harsh on the commoners' crop yields.","Great Yan hadn't taken off yet, so they couldn't afford to get carried away!","Master, do not be disappointed. Having a few thousand jin is good enough for mortals. Haven't you seen that a yield of three hundred jin per acre is already considered top-grade farmland for them?","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers nodded secretly. Yes, yes, even if it were halved, it would still be a high yield they wouldn't even dare to dream of before.","But after Yue Fuguang's words, they calmed down somewhat.","Imperial Father, how about we weigh the corn as well?","After calming down, Xie Zhiyan was the first to react. He still hadn't finished the task with the corn, which was an assignment given by the Junior Preceptor!","Yes, yes, yes, the corn, there's also the corn!","Emperor Mingxi looked toward the green crop fields. On the other side of the fields were the potatoes. Since sweet potatoes had a high yield, potatoes wouldn't be far behind. His Great Yan was truly about to take off!","Just as Emperor Mingxi was hopelessly immersed in the sweet dream of Great Yan taking off, the weighing of the corn was also completed.","Your Majesty, the corn yield per acre is one thousand two hundred and eighty-two jin!","One thousand two hundred and eighty-two jin! Emperor Mingxi nodded repeatedly, saying good several times in a row.","Because the ministers had the gem of the eight-thousand-jin sweet potato yield beforehand, they didn't show signs of excessive joy again, but their excitement was still hard to conceal. Yue Fuguang could even see the few rotten teeth in Elder Lord Wang's mouth.","Corn was different from sweet potatoes and potatoes; it was an existence that could serve as a long-term staple food just like rice, wheat, and millet.","Even at a discount, the yield of this one acre still exceeded two or three acres of Great Yan's upper and middle-grade fields.","The yields of the corn and sweet potatoes quickly spread one after another among the spectating commoners.","According to later records, on that day, from outside the capital city to inside the city, the crying of the common people filled every corner.","It was just that this crying was different from the past. Those were tears of happiness, tears of joy. They were tears of a new life, filled with the immense hope of being able to survive and perhaps even have enough to eat in the future.","At the same time, from that day on, Yue Fuguang's public prestige ranked first in Great Yan with an absolute advantage.","A massive amount of incense offerings surged in continuously from all directions.","System, this is already the fifth energy storage bead. Why do I feel like this incense power is increasing instead of decreasing!","In just half a month, Yue Fuguang had filled five energy storage beads. She asked the system while taking out the sixth one.","Host, after upgrading to level five, my detection range has gone much further. The data shows that your reputation as the Divine Maiden, Junior Preceptor Yue, has already crossed Great Yan and spread to neighboring countries.","Once the reputation of the high-yield fine seeds is confirmed by various countries, even ten more of your energy storage beads won't be enough.","Playing with the bead in her hand, which was filled with incense power and showed brilliant multicolored hues, Yue Fuguang said, That works too. With these backup batteries, when the great drought really comes, relying on them, I can sprinkle rain over the entirety of Great Yan.","Saving people, revealing miracles, and not tiring herself out—it really was the best of all worlds.","This could also be considered another form of taking from the people and using it for the people.","Right, what did you just say, System? Divine Maiden? Is our first secret identity exposed?","Not quite. With the system's restrictions, those people wouldn't be able to speak of it even if they wanted to. It's just a spontaneous title given by the common people.","You have consecutively produced three types of grains with yields over a thousand jin. Even if you don't admit it yourself, they will push you onto the altar and revere you as a Divine Maiden.","Yue Fuguang lay down on the couch, accepting this new title with peace of mind. System, do you think such a reputation could subdue the enemy without fighting in the future!","If fewer people died in wars, wouldn't her task rating be higher? This was tied to points rewards, so she couldn't help but fantasize a bit.","Host, the drought that sweeps across the entire region in the eighth year of Yuankang is the best stage prepared for us.","Perform well, and your name as the Divine Maiden will surely resound throughout the borders of the six nations. The system felt that its host was daydreaming again, so it let her fantasize for a while longer.","Dreams, after all—how many of them can actually be realized?","Yue Fuguang didn't know the system's hidden thoughts and nodded in agreement, feeling that what the system said made sense. Although Great Yan was not small, with the incense power of the energy storage beads to back her up, she had nothing to worry about.","What if, when the time came, hundreds responded to her single call, and people really started an uprising, turning their blades inward!","During this half a month, only around Yue Fuguang was the time quiet and good, presenting a peaceful scene.","Meanwhile, in the imperial court and among the people of Great Yan, incidents occurred one after another."]},{"number":347,"title":"Chapter 347: Sima, Dead Horse","paragraphs":["On the second day after the bountiful harvest of sweet potatoes, potatoes, and corn, the news that their yield exceeded a thousand catties reached the ears of Sima Jing, far away in the Jiangnan region.","According to news Yue Fuguang heard later, on that day, every teacup and saucer in Sima Jing's study was smashed to pieces. The commotion was so loud that even the servants standing ten meters away from the study could hear it clearly.","The news of the family head losing his temper and smashing things in anger spread like wildfire, reaching every corner of the massive Sima estate in less than two hours.","Everyone in the Sima family, whether they were supposed to know or not, received the news, yet absolutely no one dared to go and appease Sima Jing's fury.","Because many people simply did not know where his anger came from.","In the Jiangnan region, it could be said that the Sima family were not only high-ranking regional officials but also the local emperors of this territory.","In this domain, even the words of the one sitting on the imperial throne might not be as effective as the words of their family's lord. So what could possibly make him so furious?","Sima Ying, Sima Jing's eldest son, who had just returned to the estate from outside, heard the servants' report and headed toward the study while pondering this very question.","Their Sima family had been operating smoothly and prosperously in Jiangnan for twenty years, favored by fortune and the God of Wealth.","It was only in the past half-year that things began to go increasingly awry. The father and son even sometimes felt an involuntary chill down their spines.","Seeing the servants standing far away, Sima Ying waved them off and entered his father's study alone.","As soon as he pushed the door open, the first thing he saw was the floor covered in shattered teapots and cups, along with an inkstone missing a corner. Tea mixed with ink splashed everywhere, casting an even darker hue over the dark-colored carpet.","Sima Jing half-leaned behind his massive rosewood desk, his hands resting limply on the armrests of his chair. His eyes seemed to be looking at the door, yet also seemed to be gazing at the distant capital city of Shangjing.","Sima Ying stepped over the mess on the floor, bowed respectfully to Sima Jing, carefully peeked at his expression, and asked softly, Father, what matter has provoked you to such anger?","Sima Jing did not speak. He merely picked up a small slip of paper from the messy desk and threw it to him. It just arrived today. See for yourself!","The light piece of paper fell into his arms, yet he felt his heart sink. The unrolled note in his hand felt as heavy as a thousand catties.","He quickly read the contents, and his face instantly turned as pale as paper, then as dark as ink. His face went from white to black, and from black to red. A drop of cold sweat slid down his temples into his eye, startling him awake.","Father, it is your son's incompetence. I failed to gather the information in time, and I failed even more to destroy those things in time!","He immediately knelt down to beg for forgiveness and began to list his faults.","By this time, Sima Jing had regained the demeanor of a high-ranking regional official, but only his own son Sima Ying knew that his old man was currently an enraged tiger.","Sima Jing looked down at his most valued son, upon whom he placed high hopes. In his plans, this son would eventually lead their Sima family onto the path of supreme power.","Everything had been planned perfectly. He had even discerned from various signs that the Great Yan Dynasty would fall into decline, or even outright ruin, in at most fifteen or sixteen years, and at least ten or eight years.","That would be the Sima family's opportunity. Unfortunately, heaven did not grant human wishes. Out of nowhere dropped Yue Fuguang. At first, he hadn't taken this eight or nine-year-old girl seriously at all. As for her descending with a divine oracle, he didn't believe a single word of it.","Though far away in Jiangnan, he knew absolutely everything that happened in the imperial court without missing a detail. Regarding the courteous, even fawning treatment she received from the emperor and the ministers, he had secretly mocked Xie Fei quite a bit.","He once thought that the emperor had grown old and muddle-headed!","He never expected such a huge surprise would be waiting for him here!","With these three miraculous crops in Great Yan, as long as the millions of commoners were fed, even the people of his Jiangnan would not abandon their good lives to follow their family in rebellion.","Without internal chaos, his Sima family would have no chance.","Sima Jing shifted his gaze to the map hanging on the study wall, where the territories of the six nations were vividly displayed. What kind of moves would these harborers of malicious intent make upon receiving this news?","Sweeping past Northern Li, Western Qiang, Southern Yue, and Nanzhao, his eyes finally settled on Eastern Yi.","Ying'er, has Matsuyama still not been found?","Sima Ying shook his head. Father, Matsuyama and his subordinates vanished completely, leaving no trace behind. My men suspect this might be related to the government officials, but we have no evidence whatsoever.","Sima Jing nodded. He did not care much about whether Matsuyama lived or died. It would be better if that fellow were dead, so his son Oshima would have one less competitor.","Are the things all packed up? His gaze shifted from Eastern Yi to a small island in its nearby waters.","To answer Father, the things you ordered have all been packed away properly.","Sima Jing nodded. Stand up and speak.","Thank you, Father! Sima Ying stood up, but did not dare to sit down.","Sima Jing's hand tapped rhythmically on the rosewood desk. His brows remained furrowed. In the massive study, only the thumping sound and the ticking of the water clock in the corner could be heard.","After a while, Sima Jing knocked heavily on the desk, startling Sima Ying, whose thoughts had wandered a bit.","His father's slightly aged voice came to his ears. Tell the subordinates below that we are not waiting anymore. We start the transfer tonight. Use all the ships our family owns.","Sima Ying's face was solemn. He couldn't help but take a step forward and ask in a lowered voice, Father, are things really this bad? Is there truly no room for maneuver?","Although he also felt uneasy in his heart, he still felt it wasn't bad enough to the point of transferring their wealth and having the whole family ready to flee Great Yan at a moment's notice.","No matter how well they built up that small island, how could it compare to even a ten-thousandth of the prosperous Jiangnan?","The Emperor's heart... is there really no room for redemption at all?","Still unwilling to give up, he added, With your friendship with that person, would he really make a move against us? Thinking of the foundation he had built here over many years, if he abandoned it now, it would truly all be gone.","Grandmother is still here, and the Empress Dowager in the palace is doing well too. The two sisters could always put in a good word for each other, right?","Ying'er, you don't understand that person. He could even raise a hand against his own father, let alone us father and son who have long harbored disloyal intentions?","No matter how careful the people sent by Xie Fei were, he had somewhat noticed them. He had only thought it was a routine investigation, but as months passed, the number of people increased instead of decreasing. They were even stepping closer and closer to uncovering their core secrets, with such precision that it was as if he had known all along.","He knew then that some link on his end had made a mistake and leaked their bottom line.","Otherwise, when he had an audience with His Majesty in the spring of last year, he clearly saw that the emperor showed not the slightest bit of guardedness toward him.","With this emperor of theirs, the longer he delayed in issuing an edict of inquiry, the more Sima Jing felt that the matter had blown up!","No matter how well his treasonous heart was hidden, it had ultimately revealed traces during these years of increasingly smooth sailing.","Two months ago, when those people sniffed out that specific location, he knew that unless there was some other stroke of luck, if the Sima family did not run, they would sooner or later be finished!","If it had been in the past, he might have been able to put up some resistance, but as soon as those three miraculous crops appeared, he knew he had no chance left!"]},{"number":348,"title":"Chapter 348: Are you young man in trouble","paragraphs":["He didn't even need to think about it. As the news of the yield per mu of those three types of crops spread, the ignorant commoners of Great Yan, who would obey anyone who gave them a bite to eat, would surely turn their hearts toward the imperial court.","Even within the royal court, whether genuine or acted, there would be an atmosphere of jubilation.","Soon, Emperor Mingxi received the news. On the very night Sima Jing learned about the crop yields, the news that Great Yan possessed high-yield seeds producing thousands of catties per mu was sent out to sea along with several ships of supplies.","One route went to Dongyi, and the other to that nameless small island.","It was exactly at this time that Emperor Mingxi, who had been laying out his plans for over half a year, finally began to close the net. The leader of this operation was none other than his nephew, the son of the Grand Eldest Princess, Shen Jian.","\"System, are you saying the Sima family has already fallen? Then why haven't our points arrived yet?\"","[Host, the Sima family is involved in too much. As of now, from the entire Sima clan to the local officials they bought off, various factions, including sleeper agents like Shen Wanchuan, and some naval generals and ordinary soldiers, the number of implicated people reaches into the tens of thousands.","This doesn't even count those 'pirates' currently drifting on the sea.","Therefore, for the system to calculate and issue the points, it will probably have to wait until the entire Sima clan is escorted back to the capital.","However, you will soon have another large sum of points credited to your account.]","\"Are you saying the Murong family is almost at the capital?\"","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes, thought of a question, and almost laughed out loud. \"Then this capital city is going to get lively again.","Besides Emperor Mingxi, the current reigning emperor, there's also Murong Qian, who will be posthumously honored as Emperor Shizu of Liang.","Once the Sima family is escorted into the capital, there will also be the future Emperor Taizong of Wei and Emperor Taizu of Wei.\"","\"Host, you also forgot the Great Chu established by Shen Wanchuan's grandson. The Tong family is also implicated this time; both Tong Jiye and his son Tong Chengzong are on the escort list.\"","Good heavens, Yue Fuguang exclaimed to herself. Now, five emperors from the present to the future were gathering together. If there really was such a thing as dragon aura, the capital city would probably burst from it.","\"System, does this world have that dragon aura stuff?\" If it did, she wondered if she could use energy beads to collect some.","[Host, this world doesn't even have spiritual energy, so where would dragon aura come from?]","The system understood its host so well. With a spin of its data, it knew exactly what she was thinking. [You won't be able to collect dragon aura. When these families get beheaded, you could try collecting some sinister aura and resentment instead.]","Those things were not rare on execution grounds and battlefields, but they would quickly dissipate after a person died.","Yue Fuguang shook her head in disgust and tossed the crystal-clear grape in her hand into the porcelain dish next to her. \"System, when I have my own body in the future, I plan to walk the grand and righteous path of cultivation.","I won't practice demonic arts or evil paths. What do I need sinister aura and resentment for!\"","There were no outsiders in this courtyard, so the system ruthlessly exposed her without any hesitation. [If that's the case, Host, why did you buy the Ten Thousand Soul Banner?]","Like a cat whose tail had been stepped on, Yue Fuguang quickly sat up from her lounge chair, looked around, and then righteously retorted, \"System, what I bought was clearly the Human Emperor Flag. How did it become the Ten Thousand Soul Banner?\"","The system glanced at the product name in the shop. It was indeed called the Ten Thousand Soul Banner!","It leaned in a bit closer, only to discover that beneath the huge words \"Ten Thousand Soul Banner,\" there was a line of small text: Alias: Human Emperor Flag!","The system couldn't help but roll its eyes. It hadn't expected that their system network, in order to sell products and give those self-proclaimed righteous people a way out, could come up with such an idea.","Yue Fuguang: Just tell me, is it called the Human Emperor Flag or not!","So there was absolutely nothing wrong with what she bought. If it wasn't to prepare for those people in the east, why would she spend one thousand eight hundred points on this thing?","The officials in the royal court were all kept busy by the downfall of these two families, and various secret rivalries continued unabated.","Among the common folk, however, neither the impending arrival of the Murong family in the capital nor the sudden imprisonment of the entire Sima clan held even half the appeal of potatoes, sweet potatoes, and corn.","Sweet potatoes yielded eight thousand two hundred and sixty-six catties per mu, and potatoes yielded seven thousand three hundred and twenty catties per mu.","Corn was lower, but still yielded one thousand two hundred and eighty-two catties. Moreover, these were staple crops that could be stored long-term.","Commoners gathered in groups of tens or hundreds in teahouses, taverns, and fields. Whenever they opened their mouths, they discussed this matter, each speaking as if they had witnessed it with their own eyes.","As they talked, the topic naturally shifted to Yue Fuguang.","\"Old Man Zhang, coming to the market! Did your family burn incense for the Divine Maiden today?\" The one asking was an old man with a white beard wearing a coarse scholar's robe; he was the accountant of a restaurant in the town.","\"Of course we did. Not just me, but the boys and the women in the family didn't miss a single step.\" Old Man Zhang, who frequently delivered vegetables to the restaurant, and Accountant Xu were old acquaintances. When talking about this, his face wrinkled with a wide smile.","In the past, burning incense for the Divine Maiden was solely his job as the head of the household, but now, the whole family turned out for it.","Old Man Zhang sat down on the rock next to Accountant Xu. Watching the bustling, joyful crowds at the market, the happiness soon spread to his own face. \"I heard from the great lords in the city that it was the Divine Maiden who made the decision to distribute the divine grain to us poor commoners to plant first.\"","Otherwise, come next spring, with limited seeds available, it would never be the turn of ordinary commoners like them. Under the old ways, the seeds would have long been snatched up by the rich and powerful.","How different it was now. \"I heard that after the seeds are distributed next year, officials from above will come down to every village to guide us on how to plant the divine grain, and they won't leave until the autumn harvest is over?\"","The old man in the scholar's robe nodded and lowered his voice, \"That is for the best. With those lords keeping watch, families like ours won't have to worry about the seeds in our hands being 'bought' away by those landlords. Even the yield from the fields is guaranteed not to fall into their hands.\"","The arrival of those officials was both a form of surveillance and protection. For commoners like them, who harbored no crooked thoughts and only wanted to tend to their fields, it was a true blessing.","Hearing this news, a man nearby, whose face had originally been clouded with sorrow, flushed red with excitement. His rough, calloused hands unconsciously tugged hard at the old scholar. \"Old sir, is what you just said true? Will the Emperor really send officials to every village?\"","The old scholar winced, struggling to rescue his arm from the man's grasp, and rubbed his bony hand hard over the spot where the reckless fellow had grabbed him.","Nevertheless, he answered the man's question in a good-natured tone. \"Young man, I heard this news directly from a relative working in the magistrate's office. How could it be false?\"","He had already noticed this man sitting there in a daze for quite some time, his complexion looking unwell. Now that the man seemed almost overly thrilled, the old scholar couldn't hold back his curiosity and asked, \"What is it, young man? Have you run into some trouble?\"","Hearing the question, the man mumbled hesitantly. He looked around, and seeing that no one was paying attention to their small group, he lowered his voice. \"You gentlemen look like men of experience. I would like to ask, if someone wants to pre-order the high-yield grain seeds that are supposed to be distributed to my family, and my family doesn't want to sell but can't afford to offend them, what should we do?\""]},{"number":349,"title":"Chapter 349: Poison, Trap","paragraphs":["Old Man Zhang's expression changed. This young man looked just like him, someone who made a living digging in the dirt. Hearing the meaning behind his words, someone living in the countryside could immediately guess the gist of it. \"Young man, which village are you from? Who wants to buy your seeds?\"","The government had explicitly stated that these seeds belonged to whichever family they were given to. Private trading was forbidden; that was a severe crime.","Even exchanging them among themselves was not allowed. The grain seeds had a fixed quota and were all registered in official ledgers. There could be no messing around with them.","The man lowered his head, his hands anxiously rubbing the corner of his clothes. \"I... I don't dare to say.\"","The old man in the scholar's robe rolled his eyes in thought. Thinking of his relative who worked in the government office, he reassuringly patted the man's slightly trembling shoulder and said, \"Don't be afraid, young man. The government has clearly stipulated that the private sale of good seeds is prohibited. No matter who said what to your family before, you don't need to be afraid. The county magistrate will naturally seek justice for you.\"","The man looked up. \"But, but how could a lowly person like me meet a high-ranking official like the county magistrate? Besides...\"","He swallowed hard. \"Besides, the one who wants to buy the seeds is... is a relative of the Master Registrar.\"","Hearing that it involved a relative of the Master Registrar, the old scholar was not afraid; instead, his eyes instantly lit up. His relative was a jail warden who had always wanted to maneuver his way into the Master Registrar's position. However, the current Master Registrar had a strong family background and had been building his influence for years, so his relative had never been able to achieve his wish.","Now, if they could catch the Master Registrar making a mistake, the opportunity would arrive. One must know that in the Great Yan Dynasty, the most important matter right now was these grain seeds.","He looked around vigilantly, his voice even lower than the man's. \"Young man, are you sure that person is a relative of the Master Registrar?\"","The man nodded affirmatively. \"Everyone in our village knows that the Village Head's youngest daughter became a concubine to the Master Registrar's son, and she is highly favored.\"","Therefore, even though they were routinely exploited by the Village Head and bullied by his sons, they didn't dare to say anything.","The old scholar knew what to do. He pulled the man up and said, \"Young man, come with me. Today, I will definitely make sure you see the county magistrate. Buying and selling grain seeds is a major crime!\"","Even if it was just spoken about verbally right now, it was still unacceptable.","At this time, the three people present did not yet know that a casual chat would bring to light a case, sparing families in situations like the man's from a disaster.","In the Great Yan Dynasty, similar conversations, whether joyful or anxious, were constantly playing out everywhere, centered around the capital city of Shangjing.","Half a month later, this kind of news had crossed the national borders and flowed into the territories of various countries along with the merchant caravans.","The high-ranking officials of various countries, who had already received the news through various channels long ago, still chose to play deaf and dumb when the common people constantly asked them when they, too, could plant such divine grain. They even claimed that this news was untrue, making the people mistakenly believe they were just rumors.","Some people believed the royal courts' words, but even more people chose to believe the rumors.","More and more people chose to secretly worship the goddess statue of Yue Fuguang in their homes.","By the time the high-ranking officials of the various countries noticed it later, this trend had already taken shape in the other countries, aside from Dongyi, and was difficult to suppress.","Coupled with the later news that after the common people of Great Yan personally planted them, the yield of potatoes and sweet potatoes was over four to five thousand catties, and corn was also seven to eight hundred catties.","Worshipping the goddess was brought out into the open, reaching a point where even the royal courts could not stop the trend.","These are all stories for later.","Currently, the common people in Shangjing, as the hometown folks of the goddess, offered her more than just three sticks of incense a day.","They would silently and spontaneously deliver vegetables, eggs, and live chickens and ducks to the front gate of the Yu Manor.","The common people's way of expressing gratitude was simple and unadorned. As long as they thought something was delicious or valuable, they would send it to the Yu Manor's gate.","The gatekeeping servants of the Yu Manor couldn't even catch up to them, and they refused to accept any money. Every day, countless scenes of chasing and fleeing played out, which almost became a scenic sight in Shangjing.","On this day, Yue Fuguang was taking a nap under the corridor when she heard He Jin report, \"My Lady, word has come from the kitchen that someone was found mixing poison into the food given by the common people.\"","Poisoning again!","Yue Fuguang was a bit speechless. Could the people of the six countries and those few noble families not come up with something new for an assassination?","How many times was this now?","\"Have you found out who poisoned it?\"","\"We already have clues. My father and Aunt Luo have gone with Lord Dai Yuxing to catch the culprit.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Once you and Shen Dong finish your work these next two days, spend more time with your parents. It's rare for them to visit.\"","\"I will listen to My Lady.\"","She said this, but ever since the matter of the divine grain spread, Shangjing had gathered spies from the six countries, and the outside of the Yu Manor was not peaceful. How could they dare to truly rest?","Even if My Lady had the Divine Artifact Lord by her side, as well as antidote pills, they still did not dare to relax for a moment.","Because protecting My Lady had nothing to do with her own strength or whether she could protect herself. Keeping My Lady safe and sound was their duty as guards.","As the saying goes, to eat the ruler's salary is to be loyal to the ruler's affairs. It was no wonder.","\"He Jin, release this news to the common people again. This way, in order to prevent bad people from taking advantage of loopholes, they will stop sending things to the manor.\"","\"My Lady, this is a good idea. You don't know how much effort the Master and Madam of the manor have wasted trying not to accept these things, yet they still couldn't stop it.\"","What Yue Fuguang didn't say was that this would inevitably arouse the vigilance of the common people. Perhaps, unintentionally, those people would accidentally fall into the vast ocean of the common people's war.","All the people in Great Yan whose hearts turned toward her would become her ears and eyes. When that time really came, it would be fun!","Not long after He Jin left, the two sisters, Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin, arrived.","Fourteen-year-old Yu Ningxuan, who had just entered the courtyard gate, ran toward Yue Fuguang under the corridor in a manner extremely inconsistent with the teachings of a noble lady, shouting, \"Seventh Sister, Second Brother just sent word. Those people took the bait!\"","Yue Fuguang removed the book covering her face to block the light, looked up at the sweating Yu Ningxuan, and pointed to the teacup on the table. \"Have a cup of tea, sit down, and speak slowly.\"","The two sisters sat down as instructed and poured themselves a cup of tea. After taking a small sip, Yu Ningxuan continued excitedly, \"Second Brother said that the cotton will be completely harvested in two days. The first batch of picked cotton balls has already been shipped out today. If all goes smoothly, it will reach Shangjing in half a month.","And those people clearly didn't care about the cotton; they are only fixated on the harvested rice.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. The cotton in the Sancha fields was harvested on the same day as the sweet potatoes, corn, and potatoes.","The rice was a few days later, and after half a month, it should indeed be finished.","As for her special rice, the yield per mu was even higher than the corn that had drunk spiritual spring water.","A rice yield of one thousand eight hundred catties per mu was truly a miracle and an auspicious sign in this world. It was impossible for those people not to be jealous and not to take risks for it.","Taking the bait was something expected all along.","However, it was understandable for Yu Ningxuan to be so excited. After all, it was her first time participating in this kind of thing, and having a sense of accomplishment was beyond reproach. Even the usually gentle Yu Ningxin seemed to be smiling with her eyes.","These siblings of the Yu family were increasingly to her liking. When she set this plan, they fully supported and actively cooperated from the very beginning. No one questioned the cruelty of the plan or spouted nonsense about heaven caring for every living thing.","\"Tell Second Brother and the others to be careful. Don't let them cast the hook only to be eaten as bait themselves.\""]},{"number":350,"title":"Chapter 350: The Seventh Year of Yuan Kang","paragraphs":["Yu Ningxuan nodded. \"Rest assured, with the most cunning Zheng Feng leading the execution and the politically seasoned Lord Bao holding the fort, Second Brother and the others won't suffer any losses.\"","Yu Ningxin chimed in, \"These people are also quite scheming. They would rather pay extra silver to buy the rice along with the stalks.\"","Yue Fuguang laughed upon hearing this. \"They're just afraid we might trick them with ordinary rice.\"","But this was actually for the best. When they discovered next year that the rice only grew tall but didn't produce any grain, they would only suspect their own farming methods and wouldn't doubt them.","After all, they could rack their brains and still never imagine that there existed crops in this world that could only be planted for one season and could not be kept for seeds.","Perhaps those who refused to believe it would fall for the same trick next year, allowing them to sell another batch of premium seeds at an exorbitant price!","Thinking of this, Yue Fuguang asked, \"Since they are willing to pay more, don't hold back. As for the few people who showed their faces, once this job is done, transfer them back.\"","With goods being resold by their own people, as superiors, it was impossible not to notice or punish them, so these operatives had to become dead men.","\"How are things coming along with the textile factory?\" Yue Fuguang recalled that she had merely mentioned wanting to open a textile factory, handed over the money, the proposal, and the blueprints, and then completely washed her hands of it.","Seeing that the raw material, cotton, was already on its way, she finally remembered this matter.","\"With Aunt and Aunt-in-law watching over it, everything has been going very smoothly. We've hired a full roster of female workers, all of whom are skilled weavers. Now we're just waiting for the cotton Second Brother is transporting to arrive, and then we'll start production.\"","As for Fuguang's suggestion to teach the female workers how to read, the sisters had discussed it and decided they would take turns teaching them first.","Once their grandmother helped find a suitable female teacher, they would finally be able to relax a bit.","Yue Fuguang nodded. The Great Yan textile industry would begin from here. If successful, she believed that within a few years, such factories would spring up everywhere.","Then their standards would become the industry standards, so it was crucial to set a good example.","\"Please keep an eye on the female workers' compensation, sisters. Ensure that every copper coin we spend goes directly to the individuals, rather than lining someone else's pockets.\"","\"Don't worry about that, little sister. With Fourth Aunt keeping watch, no one dares to play tricks right under her nose.\"","While the three sisters were discussing the textile factory, they hadn't expected that He Jin's release of the news about poison being maliciously mixed into the vegetables gifted by the commoners would provoke a massive reaction from all sides.","Not to mention the Emperor and the officials, Yue Fuguang was now not only the highly respected Junior Preceptor, but also a Prince with her own fiefdom.","On the second day of the Autumn Festival, Emperor Mingxi had issued an edict conferring the title of Prince upon Yue Fuguang, and her fiefdom conveniently connected to the Three Forks region.","Whether she was a Prince or not didn't matter to her, but Emperor Mingxi had allocated her a massive piece of land, and Yue Fuguang felt that she could expand her planting operations again next year!","Therefore, the poisoning of a Prince and Junior Preceptor sent shockwaves through both the court and the public.","Cai Xian, Wei Ping, and Feng Tang quickly sprang into action. The mastermind behind this had to be found. Whether it would result in the execution of nine generations or the extermination of three clans would depend entirely on the mood of those at the top.","The Great Yan court was shaken, and the reaction among the common folk was no less intense.","Rumors that wicked villains intended to use their hands to assassinate the Divine Maiden spread from the capital city of Shangjing to the surrounding villages and towns.","Even the most simple-minded commoners sensed that something was terribly wrong.","\"Is there someone who doesn't want us poor folks to have enough to eat and live a good life?\"","This question rapidly ignited the fury of the masses. Anyone who messed with their rations was asking for their lives.","A seed called vigilance quietly took root in the hearts of the people at this moment.","They suddenly developed far more wariness and defensiveness toward strangers.","Hadn't they heard the court officials say it? The ones who poisoned the Divine Maiden were those foreigners and the noble lords from the prominent families.","Because the Divine Maiden had brought forth good crops, it angered those people. So, for the sake of the Divine Maiden and even more for themselves, they could not let those who tried to use them succeed.","After the poisoning incident, Wei Ping and his team conducted extensive investigations. Thanks to tips from enthusiastic citizens, they finally tracked down two brothers who had disguised themselves as commoners.","These two had mingled with the crowd that day and delivered fish they had caught from the river to the Yu Manor.","Later, other commoners identified that these two brothers had also made inappropriate remarks on the day of the Autumn Festival, overtly and covertly expressing malice toward the Divine Maiden.","\"So it was the work of the prominent families?\"","\"Yes, the prominent families have been backed into a corner by the Emperor with no way out. All their actions now are just deathbed struggles.\"","\"The prominent families are deeply entangled with the royal court, and their relationships with various factions are complex and deeply rooted. Uprooting them won't be any easier than dealing with Sima Jing, a powerful regional official.\"","Yue Fuguang was not so optimistic. She didn't believe this incident would be enough to ensnare all the prominent families; there would still be plenty of back-and-forth struggles.","\"That is why, even now, the Emperor has only made a move against the Cui and Bai families. The charges were already laid out for them.","\"It's a pity that the Great Yan court's situation is currently stable. With your high-yield premium seeds sustaining everything, the populace is experiencing an unprecedented level of peace these past few years.\"","Otherwise, why not just start a peasant uprising or something, take the genealogies of the noble families, call roll one by one, and wipe them all out in one fell swoop? How easy would that be!","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes upon hearing the system's words. How could she not know that this method was effective? After all, there were successful precedents.","Unfortunately, the current conditions in Great Yan did not allow for it, so she could only use the slow, grinding approach.","However, Yue Fuguang's eyes darted around. Hearing this guy's words, she knew the system must have secretly repaired the data of the drama-watching system behind her back.","Things went exactly as Yue Fuguang expected. Although Emperor Mingxi and his ministers all knew that the noble families were rotten to the core, completely eradicating them was indeed a long-term task that required careful planning and defeating them one by one.","Therefore, by the autumn of the seventh year of Yuankang, not to mention the minor noble families whose grave grass had already grown tall, only the three most influential major noble families of Great Yan—Zheng, Wang, and Kong—were left lingering on their last breath.","What? Those people bought seeds again this year?","Yue Fuguang was still lying on her exclusive lounge chair in the corridor of the Bright Moon Pavilion, just like that autumn day in the fifth year of Yuankang, watching the pears on the tree in the courtyard swaying in the autumn wind, not knowing when they would fall.","Yu Ningxuan, who was almost seventeen, had grown increasingly graceful and elegant over the past two years, and even the nearly sixteen-year-old Yu Ningxuan beside her had shed her frailty, gaining a refreshing and brisk vigor.","Only twelve-year-old Yue Fuguang seemed to have been left behind by time. Apart from growing a bit taller, she still retained a bit of childishness.","Fortunately, this was not her own body. As a mere tenant, she did not care much about how it developed.","Seeing Yue Fuguang's face practically screaming \"Are they stupid?\", Yu Ningxuan also laughed. She explained cheerfully, The rice they planted last spring grew very well, much taller and stronger than the seedlings from their own country. Unfortunately, it only grew tall and did not bear any rice ears.","So last autumn, they bought another large batch of rice seeds from us."]},{"number":351,"title":"Chapter 351: Is He Getting Cocky Again","paragraphs":["Yu Ningxin picked up an autumn pear from the table and took a bite. \"That time, they even sent people to secretly watch the farmers harvest the rice from the fields from start to finish. Then, following the old rules, they paid a high price to buy the rice ears along with the stalks.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. She had tacitly approved of this matter. If they wanted to watch, let them watch. What they were selling was exactly that batch of rice from the fields. If they wanted anything else, they wouldn't get it anyway.","\"As a result, the rice seedlings grew beautifully this year. After improving the planting methods, the rice ears also formed. It was said that they grew quite well, but it's a pity they only grew ears without yielding any actual rice grains. And so, the three kingdoms still haven't given up, thinking that planting for another year will surely yield plenty of rice.\"","Yue Fuguang curled her lips into a smile. She wanted to trick them a few more times, so in the second year, she switched to a rice variety that was equally high-yielding and equally incapable of being kept for seed. The only difference between the two types of rice was that one produced ears but no grains, while the other hardly produced any ears at all.","This was called proceeding step by step, giving them hope little by little, and making them have the illusion that as long as they tried harder, they would definitely succeed.","She hadn't expected them to actually fall into the trap again this year. As for this year's rice seeds, they surely wouldn't disappoint them. They would produce rice grains, only to be eaten by unknown pests. Come to think of it, their hearts would bleed, wouldn't they?","Yue Fuguang rubbed her increasingly slender and smooth chin, which now showed a distinct jawline. This could be considered collecting early interest for their continuous harassment of her over the past two years.","\"Tell Second Brother to handle the finishing touches well and try not to leave them with any leverage.\" It was not yet time to tear all face with them.","Over the past two years, the Sancha region had been continuously reinforced, and the stationed army had reached over fifteen thousand men. But if they really found out they had been played, they would probably go crazy, and their counterattack would definitely be frantic. So it was better to keep them in the dark for now.","By the autumn of the seventh year of Yuankang, the Great Yan's new army had also grown to two hundred thousand strong. These men were all part of a brand-new army trained and ideologically educated using the new methods she had provided.","She just didn't know if this best-equipped army in all of Great Yan could withstand the impending chaos of the world, where internal and external pressures would multiply due to natural disasters.","Since autumn began, there had only been one autumn rain, and it had actually stopped before it could even wet the ground.","Her prophecy seemed to be coming true. Watching the fine weather day after day, Emperor Mingxi, who had become increasingly smug over the past two years, was now so anxious these days that he had lost all anticipation for the upcoming Wanshou Festival.","Just as the Great Yan courtiers couldn't stop the drought no matter how much secret preparation they made, the un-anticipated Wanshou Festival arrived on schedule.","Among the diplomatic missions from various countries, the ones who came this time were all old acquaintances, and it was also the largest delegation in terms of numbers and scale from each country.","Yue Fuguang still sat upright just below the emperor. From her position, she could see the courtiers and the people of the diplomatic missions below very clearly.","Yue Fuguang's gaze first fell on the few people from the Nanzhao Kingdom sitting at the very front of the diplomatic missions.","The person leading the team this time was an old acquaintance she hadn't seen in over a year, Lan Xuan'er. Although Yue Fuguang hadn't spoken more than a few words to her, she had eaten all the gossip about her and Prince Ming from beginning to end.","It was a pity that Prince Ming died of illness in the deep winter of the fifth year of Yuankang. A heartbroken Lan Xuan'er had never come to Great Yan again since then.","She hadn't expected her to return this year to Shangjing, which could be considered a place of heartbreak for her.","\"Little Zhu, does Lan Xuan'er know that Prince Ming's death was the doing of the Nanzhao Emperor?\"","[Master, if Lan Xuan'er didn't know that the one who made the move was her Empress Mother, you wouldn't be seeing her at this year's Wanshou Festival!]","\"How did she know? The Nanzhao Emperor did it so secretly back then, and the grass on the graves of the perpetrators is already quite tall.\"","[Naturally, it was our kind-hearted Emperor who sent an insider to deliver the news to her.]","Hearing the Divine Artifact mention him, Emperor Mingxi, sitting in the main seat, awkwardly picked up his wine cup and drank with Xie Zhiyan and his son.","At that time, the people he had left by Prince Ming's side had long noticed that someone was secretly administering a slow-acting poison to Prince Ming.","After he found out, he just watched and didn't step in to stop it. Ultimately, Prince Ming's death had nothing to do with him. Even if this Nanzhao princess, Lan Xuan'er, wanted to hold a grudge, she shouldn't hold it against him, the Emperor of Great Yan.","So he kindly pointed out to her who her true enemy was.","With a severe drought approaching, apart from their Great Yan, the political situations of the other countries shouldn't be peaceful and stable either.","The throne was so tempting; how could the little brats below not fight and snatch for it!","\"Oh, so the Emperor also knows how to throw sand into other people's homes? I thought only Great Yan had been infiltrated like a sieve from top to bottom, and that we, as ruler and ministers, just wouldn't fight back when hit or talk back when scolded!\"","Mocked by Yue Fuguang's endlessly sarcastic remark, Emperor Mingxi felt the hairs on his body stand on end, and his toes couldn't help but curl against the soles of his shoes.","Given some time, he could definitely carve out a small palace with his toes.","As for the ministers, they heard absolutely nothing. Today's wine was truly delicious; why did it feel a bit intoxicating!","[Master, although the Emperor has been a bit full of himself these past two years, he hasn't slacked off on his work either. His hands are now almost reaching into the beds of the emperors of various countries.","[With your book as a guide, the Secret Spy Bureau has done a good job these past few years. The emperor will never again be deaf and blind like he was two years ago.]","\"So to speak, as long as Great Yan safely passes the hurdle of this drought, there really is a possibility that it won't perish?\"","[The way Little Zhu sees it, ever since Master appeared, the declining fate of Great Yan has slowly turned around. If the sovereign and ministers of Great Yan can maintain the current situation, there is an eighty percent chance they won't face national subjugation in the fourteenth year of Yuankang like in the original timeline.]","Hearing this, a sharp glint flashed in Emperor Mingxi's eyes before quickly fading away.","A long-held speculation was finally confirmed. Hearing with his own ears today that the divine artifact had certified that Great Yan most likely wouldn't fall meant there could absolutely be no mistake.","At this moment, monstrous waves of joy surged in the hearts of the Great Yan sovereign and his ministers.","Emperor Mingxi, with an excited heart and trembling hands, forcefully suppressed his turbulent emotions. Under the guise of accepting toasts from his courtiers, he quickly exchanged glances with a few of his most trusted ministers, then acted as if nothing had happened.","Over the years, as she grew older, the Junior Preceptor, aside from her unchanging laziness, had become increasingly difficult to fool.","Therefore, they acted with ever-increasing caution in their daily affairs.","Over the past two years, as her divine nature began to manifest, her temperament had become even more elusive. They dared not provoke her ire in the slightest.","\"Who knows if Emperor Mingxi and his ministers can maintain the current situation? I heard the emperor just confiscated some silver from the noble families and already wants to build some garden? Is he getting carried away again?\"","Is he getting carried away again? These words struck coldly against Emperor Mingxi's heart, awakening the civil and military officials who had been immersed in immense joy.","Over the past two years, not to mention the massive amounts of gold, silver, valuables, and vast tracts of land confiscated from the noble clans, which had heavily enriched both the state treasury and the emperor's private coffers.","Just speaking of the time since the downfall of the Sima family, they had vigorously developed maritime trade. Every time a fleet went out to sea, it was escorted by a naval force of several thousand men.","Both the imperial court and individuals had made a fortune, so much so that when the emperor proposed building a summer garden to escape the heat, aside from Feng Tang who raised doubts, everyone else tacitly agreed."]},{"number":352,"title":"Chapter 352: Overcooked, Overcooked","paragraphs":["Everyone carefully peeked at the Emperor, whose face was flushed red and whose smile was still frozen on his face, secretly praying, \"The Little Immortal Lord has already scolded His Majesty, please do not scold us too!\"","\"We only renovated our mansions, we didn't build gardens!\"","[If Master hadn't mentioned it, Little Zhu wouldn't have noticed. It's not just the Emperor who has gotten carried away; every single one of these courtiers below has gotten a bit carried away too.","Once they have money, they buy houses and land, and they take in concubines one after another. This leads to discord between husbands and wives, and infighting among children.","They aren't even afraid of dying in the inner chambers at their old age.","When that time really comes, Master, you absolutely must not save their dog lives.]","A few officials who had recently taken in beautiful concubines suddenly had faces redder than the Emperor's. Faced with the intentional or unintentional gazes of their colleagues, they covered their faces with their sleeves, feeling mortified to death.","\"You already said they are dog lives, so what use is there in saving them? Can they govern the country or manage their households? Trash who only know how to indulge in pleasure are not fit to be officials.","Useless people might as well resign early and go home to sell sweet potatoes!\"","The faces of those people had now turned from red to white. When the autumn wind blew against the cold sweat on their backs, they instantly shuddered.","Whatever romantic and lustful thoughts they once had in their minds were mostly scared away by now.","\"Who else bought land? Where did the land come from? Didn't Emperor Mingxi order that all confiscated farmland be prioritized for distribution or sale to the landless commoners?","Who is competing with the people for profit?\"","Yue Fuguang's bright eyes swept coldly over the people below. Everyone whose gaze she passed over involuntarily shuddered.","They cried out in their hearts that the Little Immortal Lord's gaze was getting more and more terrifying. They... they couldn't bear it!","Feng Tang, Wu Yong, and others looked at their colleagues who instantly chickened out, curling their lips in their hearts and cursing them as cowards. To think they wanted to play tricks right under the Immortal Lord's nose; they truly didn't know how the word 'death' was written!","[I have a list here. I'll put it on the Emperor's imperial desk later to see how he deals with these people, and then Master can decide whether to move to another place.]","Upon hearing this, Emperor Mingxi almost jumped out of his chair.","They were scolding just fine, why did the topic suddenly change!","What did she mean by whether to move to another place? Move where? From the Yu Manor to a villa or a Prince's mansion?","It couldn't be any further!","If it was any further, he really would cry!","Emperor Mingxi used his strong willpower to suppress the urge to stand up.","He glanced down at the courtiers below, who seemed to be exchanging cups and acting perfectly normal.","His eyes swept across everyone like knives.","\"Lord Zhang, have you drunk too much already? Look, your wine is about to spill!\"","A colleague held down Lord Zhang's trembling hand and kindly helped him put the wine cup back on the table. \"The banquet has just begun. Let's drink some tea for a while to dissipate the alcohol.\"","\"Eh, Lord Qian, why is there so much sweat on your face? It's already late autumn, and it's not hot tonight!\"","Asked by his colleague, Lord Qian hurriedly wiped the cold sweat off his face with his sleeve and squeezed out a smile uglier than crying. \"I just get red in the face when I drink. It's all from the alcohol. I'll be fine in a moment, just a moment!\"","In his heart, however, he was screaming: We're done for, we're done for, we're completely done for!","If the Little Immortal Lord wanted them dead, not even God could save them!","Yue Fuguang relaxed and leaned back against her chair. \"That's fine too. I'm getting quite tired of staying in this capital city anyway. Changing places wouldn't be bad.\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang agree, Emperor Mingxi really wanted to reach out and stop her, but he didn't dare. He could only rack his brains for a solution.","Suddenly, his eyes lit up, and he showed a fawning smile to Yue Fuguang. \"Fuguang, in a few days when we are free, I plan to lead the courtiers on an autumn hunt. What do you think?\"","\"An autumn hunt?\"","\"Yes, an autumn hunt, right at the royal hunting grounds, which is less than a hundred miles from the capital.\"","Emperor Mingxi felt this was the furthest distance they could leave the capital.","The reason they hadn't held an autumn hunt in previous years was because of the assassination attempt against him in the third year of Yuankang. The royal hunting grounds had also suffered heavy losses, and it was only in the past few years that the hunting grounds had recovered.","\"Alright.\" Being able to go out for a walk, even if it wasn't far, was good.","[Master, can't you already control the flying hoverboard? Going out to play should be simple.]","\"Going out at night, even if I can travel a thousand miles in the dark, what's the point? It's pitch black, what is there to see!\"","While Emperor Mingxi and his ministers were enduring Yue Fuguang's warnings, the Great Yan officials who had been exchanging cups of wine all switched to drinking clear tea.","Sitting among the diplomatic mission, Bei Ye rolled his eyes, filled a cup of wine, stood up, and bowed to Emperor Mingxi from afar. \"Bei Ye toasts to His Majesty the Emperor of Great Yan, wishing you eternal prosperity and long-lasting national destiny.\"","\"Good, I thank the Fifth Prince for your auspicious words.\"","Emperor Mingxi raised his wine cup and took a small sip. At this time, he didn't dare to drink too much.","\"Little Zhu, why did Beiyue and Bei Ye, two princes from Northern Li, both come this time?\"","[Because Bei Ji has been in poor health these past two years, and his sons are fighting fiercely for the throne. Over the past two years, Great Yan has strictly controlled sweet potatoes, corn, and potatoes.","Although the surrounding countries have managed to get some seeds through various means, if they want to plant them on a large scale, relying solely on the seeds they have, they won't be able to promote them without several years of accumulation.","Therefore, every year, several countries send diplomatic notes to Emperor Mingxi to discuss the purchase of good seeds, but he rejects them all with various excuses.","So for this Emperor's Birthday Festival, the diplomatic missions from all countries came with tasks.","These two brothers should be aiming for this great merit.]","\"Bei Ye is one thing, at least he likes women to some extent, but this Beiyue is very 'single-minded'. Hasn't he already lost his chance? What is he getting involved for?\"","[Master, even if he doesn't become Emperor himself, he can support or ally with one of his brothers!]","\"From what you're saying, do you know who Beiyue has teamed up with?\"","[Master, do you remember I said that even though Bei Ji clearly knew about Beiyue's homosexual tendencies, he still elevated him highly, giving outsiders the illusion that he was the next successor, and even Prince Ming believed it.]","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment. The system did seem to have told her something similar. \"Does this have to do with him picking a side?\"","[Beiyue discovered that his father was using him as a target and actually already had a preferred candidate for the throne in mind.","He and his brothers were all just targets and stepping stones for that person.","With Beiyue's temper, how could he tolerate that? Since he couldn't sit at the table to eat, he was ready to flip the table.]","\"Flip the table? Go against his father? He isn't even the Crown Prince, what makes him think he can go against the Emperor? Because he has a bunch of boyfriends?\"","[How does Master know that he is relying on his boyfriends?]","Yue Fuguang was stunned. She had just said that casually, and she actually guessed right?","What kind of magical country was Northern Li? Why were there so many cut-sleeves everywhere?","She had heard that ancient men, especially noblemen, liked male lovers, but no one told her they liked it this much!","Yue Fuguang glanced at the group of Great Yan civil officials, wondering how many of them were fond of this trend.","Although she had interacted with these people for three years, apart from a few she valued and those related to system tasks, Yue Fuguang actually rarely paid attention to their private lives.","After all, nobody is perfect. She was afraid that once she learned about their private morals, she wouldn't be able to look them in the eye. After all, later generations had heard of how wild the ancients could be."]},{"number":353,"title":"Chapter 353: On the day of your wedding, I shall surely attend to offer my congratulations.","paragraphs":["Thinking of having to rely on these people to help her complete her tasks, forget it, forget it, it was better for her not to know!","As long as they were useful to the country and harbored no ill will toward her, she was willing to choose to turn a blind eye.","How did that saying go again? 'When you succeed, you are surrounded by good people; when you are strong, the world will treat you with gentleness and kindness.'","Was that really true? It could only be said that your strength changed the attitudes of the people around you. As for what kind of people they truly were, that wouldn't change much.","The ruler and ministers of Dayan were exactly like this. If she didn't have the status of an Immortal Lord, would she still be sitting in her current position?","Even if she brought out the exact same things and provided them with the exact same information, she would still end up being manipulated by others.","Therefore, Yue Fuguang was very clearly aware that not everyone surrounding her was a good person. It was merely her status that made them act like good people.","Thus, she had no intention of delving deeply into their true natures.","\"Is his new boyfriend very powerful?\"","[His new favorite has Panshan standing behind him, what do you think? Therefore, Bei Yue feels he now has the confidence to flip the table on his father. Getting his hands on Dayan's high-yield seeds is just part of his plan.","Bei Ye's thoughts are pretty much the same. The old tiger is aging, so naturally, the young tigers are anxious to take their seats at the table.]","Emperor Mingxi always felt that the Divine Artifact's words carried a hidden meaning, but he had no proof.","\"Who is this new favorite of Bei Yue? Panshan...\"","Before Yue Fuguang could finish her sentence, she was interrupted by Bei Yue.","He raised his wine cup toward her and said, \"I have admired Prince Yue for a long time. It is a true regret that we only had a brief meeting two years ago and couldn't get to know each other better.","I sincerely invite Your Highness to visit Beili when you have the time. The scenery in Beili is quite different from that of Dayan, and there are many sights worth seeing.\"","Saying this, he drained the wine in his cup. Yue Fuguang nodded, \"Prince Qi is very thoughtful. If there is an opportunity, I will certainly go.\"","Once they conquered Beili and incorporated it into Dayan's territory, her visit wouldn't even count as going abroad.","Yue Fuguang thought that was the end of it, but unexpectedly, as soon as Bei Yue sat down, Bei Ye stood up.","He also raised his wine cup and said, \"My admiration for Your Excellency is just like my third brother's. However, I have a question, and I wonder if it is appropriate to ask?\"","Would Yue Fuguang indulge him?","She replied directly, \"If the esteemed envoy feels it is inappropriate to ask, then simply do not ask.\"","If he thought she would be polite to him, then this Bei Ye was overthinking it.","She hadn't forgotten the grudge of this guy sending assassins after her. If keeping him alive didn't cause more internal turmoil in Beili, this fellow would have been dead two years ago!","Bei Ye was visibly stunned for a moment. He never expected Yue Fuguang to not play by the rules. Was this person completely disregarding diplomatic etiquette, or did she simply not understand it because she was too young?","Bei Ye only froze for a second. Catching from the corner of his eye that Emperor Mingxi showed no intention of reprimanding her, he quickly recovered.","His smile remained warm and gentle. Yue Fuguang shook her head. This guy was relying on his good looks, smiling with such captivating charm. Unfortunately, she was still young, and honey-traps were completely useless on her.","Bei Ye bowed politely to Yue Fuguang before saying, \"Your Excellency jests.\"","Having found a way to save face, he didn't wait for Yue Fuguang to speak and continued, \"My question just now was, is Your Excellency truly a goddess descended to the mortal realm? Can you summon the wind and rain and live forever, just as the legends say? If so, wouldn't His Majesty the Emperor of Dayan truly enjoy eternal prosperity, just as I wished him earlier?\"","Hearing his obviously provocative question, most people in the grand hall couldn't help but look toward Yue Fuguang, while some from Dayan couldn't stop themselves from glaring angrily at Bei Ye.","What did this guy mean? Asking the Little Immortal Lord about immortality was one thing, but why drag their Emperor into it?","Looking across the six nations, which emperor or person holding great power didn't fantasize about immortality?","If it weren't for the Little Immortal Lord's warning, their Emperor would have already started popping pills in pursuit of immortality by now!","The Fifth Prince of Beili asked this question to sow discord between the Little Immortal Lord and His Majesty, and also to shatter her invincible image as a goddess, thereby diminishing her popularity among the nations.","Wasn't Beili doing this just to take advantage of the situation and snatch the Little Immortal Lord for themselves?","What sinister intentions!","Could Emperor Mingxi fail to see this?","Emperor Mingxi, who was old enough to be Bei Ye's father, naturally saw through Bei Ye's sinister intentions. He slammed his wine cup heavily onto the table.","Before he could speak, Yue Fuguang's lips curled up into a playful smile as she said, \"If the Fifth Prince can answer one question for me first, it's not impossible for me to answer yours.\"","Bei Ye smiled gently and cupped his hands in a salute, \"Please go ahead, Your Excellency. I will certainly tell you everything I know without reservation!\"","A cold light flashed in Yue Fuguang's eyes. \"I didn't see Lord Wei Qingyi just now.\"","She looked straight into Bei Ye's eyes and asked, \"Is Lord Wei sick like last time, or did he simply not come along on this trip?","I heard that the Fifth Prince and Lord Wei have always had a very deep affection for each other. Could it be that you two had a lovers' quarrel? I wonder when we will be able to drink to your wedding?\"","Her eyes were filled with undisguised mocking amusement. \"On the day of your great joyous union, I will definitely go to offer my congratulations.\"","As Yue Fuguang's words fell, the grand hall instantly plunged into an eerie silence.","Buzz, buzz, buzz. The humming of the mosquitoes that hadn't been completely driven out of the hall sounded particularly piercing at this moment.","Pfft!","Hahaha!","Hahaha!...","After just a few breaths of time, the loud laughter of Feng Tang and Wu Yong suddenly echoed through the grand hall.","They were closely followed by Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and the others. Although they were not as bold and unbridled as those two, the looks they directed at Bei Ye all conveyed the same meaning.","They were also very curious as to why Wei Qingyi hadn't accompanied him this time, and whether the two of them were still a couple.","If they remembered correctly, Wei Qingyi had divorced his wife back in the fifth year of Yuankang.","As for Bei Ye, although his princess consort was still the same princess consort, it was no longer a secret that the two lived completely separate lives.","The ruler and ministers of Dayan, from top to bottom, all had faces full of smiles. In contrast, Bei Ye's face had turned from red to black. His tightly clenched fists had white knuckles from exerting too much force. When he looked at Yue Fuguang, a flash of murderous intent crossed his eyes.","Yue Fuguang didn't care much about his murderous intent; after all, it would be as easy as flipping her hand for her to kill him. Instead, she was quite indifferent to his hatred.","She had originally thought that after being humiliated by her and the Dayan courtiers, Bei Ye would storm out in anger. Unexpectedly, he merely flicked his sleeve, his expression shifting a few times before he sat back down in his seat as if nothing had happened.","Yue Fuguang narrowed her eyes, speculating in her heart that Beili must have a massive scheme this time. Otherwise, facing such obvious humiliation, he shouldn't have been able to sit back down so calmly. To be able to do so, this Bei Ye truly had an incredible tolerance, and he was a man of deep calculation.","A minor verbal skirmish quickly dissolved into nothingness as the people in the hall resumed toasting and drinking.","Xi Ling and Xi Yuanshan of the Xiqiang delegation also raised their cups to toast Emperor Mingxi.","Then they toasted the Crown Prince. The Crown Prince had just had a chubby baby boy, making his position even more secure. He was currently riding the crest of success.","Hearing the two Xiqiang brothers congratulate him on the birth of his precious son, he was naturally overjoyed.","\"Little Zhu, look at the Crown Prince. Ever since his chubby son was born, he's been smiling so hard his face is about to crack.\""]},{"number":354,"title":"Chapter 354: Those Who Play Politics Are All Good Actors","paragraphs":["[How could he not be happy? If it weren't for Master's pregnancy-protecting medicine, the Crown Prince wouldn't have had a child so quickly, let alone such a healthy one.","In the original timeline, he didn't have his first son until the eighth year of Yuankang. Because the Crown Princess was frightened during her pregnancy, the child was born prematurely and was sickly.","In the following years, the Crown Prince had no more children. Coupled with the favor shown to Old Nine Xie and his mother, and the manipulation of various factions, the Emperor, tormented by illness and growing increasingly muddled, lost trust in him, which shook his position as the Crown Prince.]","Emperor Mingxi and his son exchanged a glance; the doubts hidden in their hearts were finally somewhat unravelled.","Emperor Mingxi thought to himself that since he cared most about the distinction between legitimate and illegitimate children, how could he have ever entertained the thought of changing the Crown Prince.","It turned out that behind his own muddle-headedness and the favor shown to that mother and son, there was also the reason that the older Crown Prince had been unable to produce a suitable heir.","Thinking of his healthy, adorable son and the Crown Princess's completely unharmed body, the Crown Prince raised his cup to Yue Fuguang and said, \"Zhiyan toasts to you, Royal Aunt. If it weren't for the medicine you gifted, your nephew's wife would not have had such a smooth delivery.\"","Yue Fuguang had been conferred the title of a Prince of the First Rank. She was not of the Crown Prince's generation, but of the same generation as Emperor Mingxi.","Therefore, since then, the royal descendants, from Xie Zhiyan downwards, all addressed her as Royal Aunt or Little Aunt.","Yue Fuguang, who had been elevated by a generation out of nowhere, showed nothing on her face, but she was overjoyed in her heart.","\"You flatter me, Crown Prince. It is all the Crown Princess's own good fortune.\"","As for saying it was what she ought to do as an elder, she would never say such things that would dig a hole for herself.","From the moment Xie Zhiyan called Yue Fuguang Royal Aunt, Fifth Prince Xie frowned imperceptibly, seemingly very resistant to this title.","Anyway, over the past two years, Yue Fuguang rarely saw him address her this way. Every time he saw her, he tried to hide, like a mouse meeting a cat.","After noticing his unusual behavior, Yue Fuguang once suspected that this guy was hiding some treacherous scheme, and even had the system investigate him thoroughly.","Finding that, aside from a few minor issues, he hadn't done anything to harm her, she tossed the matter aside.","Speaking of which, Fifth Prince Xie was already eighteen; why hadn't he taken a wife yet?","The Emperor might have forgotten, but could the Empress and his own biological mother have forgotten too?","Before she could figure out a reason, the system's voice rang in her ears, [Master, Xi Ling and Xi Yuanshan seem to be at odds!]","Yue Fuguang glanced at the two men drinking together. 'They look like they get along quite well. Where do you see them being at odds?'","[Because before they came to attend the banquet, they had a huge argument at the post house.]","'An argument?' Yue Fuguang looked at their harmonious appearance and simply couldn't see any signs that they had just fought not long ago.","She shook her head, 'I really can't tell. As expected, everyone who plays politics is a good actor.'","Yue Fuguang's words made Emperor Mingxi and his officials present blush unconsciously. They all took to drinking tea and eating food to alleviate the awkwardness in their hearts.","Even though they knew perfectly well that the Junior Preceptor wasn't talking about them, they couldn't help but feel guilty!","'Little Zhu, why did these two argue? They are biological brothers with one father as well as cousins. Logically, their relationship should be better than others.'","[Master, biological brothers in the royal family are competitors fighting for the family property. Just look at the princes and princesses of various countries who fight to the death, both openly and in secret, for the throne.","Cousins are people who covet your family property and want to take it for themselves. Just look at Emperor Mingxi and Sima Jing.","What's more, they might not even be aware of this layer of relationship.]","Emperor Mingxi, having just taken a sip of wine, nearly choked when he heard the name of Sima Jing, whose grave grass was already growing tall.","Eunuch Qian, standing two steps behind him, was ready to pound his master's back at any moment, but he didn't expect Emperor Mingxi to forcefully hold it in.","It was just that holding it back made his face a little red, and his throat and nose hurt a bit!","[As for the issue of having the same father, they actually both have their suspicions. It's just that their mothers are very tight-lipped and haven't changed a single word of their story from back then.","As for why they had a huge argument, it has to do with Princess Consort Yi.]","'Xie Zhiyao? What kind of trouble has she stirred up now?'","Over the past two years, the people assigned to watch her had frequently sent back news. For the first year or so after she got married, she was quite well-behaved.","Her marriage was plotted by the Western Qiang royal family. Knowing she had no one behind her to rely on, she went along with it, pretending not to know, and married Xi Yuanshan according to the Western Qiang royal family's arrangements.","During this process, she relied on her beautiful appearance to fully play the role of a timid and fragile victim.","If Yue Fuguang could have seen her makeup at that time, she would definitely have found it familiar, because every day she painted a look full of vulnerability, which certainly drew a lot of sympathetic gazes.","The only thing she didn't win over was the true heart of her husband, Xi Yuanshan.","[Does Master remember that Xie Zhiyao's original marriage alliance target was the Fourth Prince of Western Qiang, Xi Xiang?]","'I remember. Didn't you say that Xi Yuanshan and Xie Zhiyao were set up by someone, which was why they had to change the marriage alliance target?","Does this have anything to do with their argument?'","[Xi Yuanshan suspects that Xi Ling was involved in that conspiracy. Xi Ling naturally cried foul, but Xi Yuanshan seems to have found evidence. Xi Ling firmly denied it, so as they kept talking, they started arguing.]","'So did Xi Ling actually meddle in Xi Yuanshan's marriage or not? They've been married for three or four years now, and according to the intelligence reports, Xi Yuanshan's feelings for Xie Zhiyao aren't even as deep as Xi Ling's feelings for her. What's going on?'","[There is something Master doesn't know. Before Xi Yuanshan acknowledged his royal ancestry, he had a childhood sweetheart with whom he was about to discuss marriage.","Originally, Xi Yuanshan had agreed with that girl that he would return to marry her after acknowledging his family.","As a result of the power struggles within Western Qiang, Xi Yuanshan was recognized as an adopted son. To compensate him, the old Emperor conferred upon him the title of Prince.","This move naturally attracted the jealousy of Emperor Xi Yan's other sons, which led to that conspiracy.","And before the convoy even reached Western Qiang, Xie Zhiyao had used money to bribe a few people in the border welcoming party.","She learned that Xi Xiang, the man she was supposed to marry, was the least favored among Emperor Xi Yan's many sons. Xi Xiang himself was rather cowardly and had no ambitions.","Although his biological mother held the rank of one of the four principal consorts, she was in poor health year-round, rarely left her quarters, and the Emperor's favor towards her was only average.","Therefore, when Xie Zhiyao accidentally found out that someone was plotting against her and Xi Yuanshan, she decisively went along with the flow, and afterwards pretended to be a victim.]","'Since she knew someone was plotting, why didn't she avoid it? Didn't she know that although Xi Yuanshan holds the title of a Prince, his status as an adopted son makes it even harder for him to inherit the throne than Xi Xiang, an unfavored prince?'","Lacking a proper title and legitimate status perfectly describes Xi Yuanshan's current awkward position. Everyone knows he is Emperor Xi Yan's biological son, but he just lacks a legitimate identity.","Given Xie Zhiyao's intelligence and her years of royal education, she shouldn't be unaware of the stakes involved.","[When she first entered Western Qiang, her movements were restricted. The information she received was all what people with ulterior motives wanted her to know, mostly about how much Xi Yuanshan was favored by the Western Emperor.]"]},{"number":355,"title":"Chapter 355: Classic, truly classic","paragraphs":["[Among all the brothers, apart from the eldest prince who had military merits, he was the second to be granted the title of King.","Therefore, Xie Zhiyao naturally assumed that this Prince Yi was favored and had hope of inheriting the throne in the future.","So when she heard that someone was scheming against Xi Yuanshan's marriage, she thought it was because his favor had attracted competitors who didn't want him to have a powerful wife's family as support.","But she didn't know that Xi Yuanshan was just an add-on; the real mastermind behind the scenes had always wanted to scheme against her marriage.]","\"With Xie Zhiyao's temper, knowing she married someone with no hope for the throne, wouldn't she raise hell?\"","[At first, she endured it. After giving birth to her eldest son with Xi Yuanshan in Western Qiang and establishing her foothold, she naturally wasn't content to stop there.","Upon learning that Xi Yuanshan was actually Xi Yan's biological son, she felt her husband still had a fighting chance for the throne.","Thus, the first person she wanted to ally with was Xi Yuanshan's biological brother and cousin, Xi Ling.","The two communicated frequently in private. When this was exploited by those with ulterior motives, it reached Xi Yuanshan's ears that not only did Xi Ling have an affair with his princess consort, but the conspiracy back then was also orchestrated by the two of them.]","\"That logic doesn't quite hold up. Did Xi Yuanshan actually believe it? Xie Zhiyao really makes me look at her in a new light; the strong never complain about their circumstances.","In this battle for the throne, she fights when she has the conditions, and when she doesn't, she creates them to fight anyway. Her dedication to her goals is truly admirable!\"","The sovereign and ministers of Great Yan exchanged glances. The Junior Preceptor was at it again; her focus was always different from theirs. After so many times, this group of shrewd veterans who had played politics for years couldn't help but wonder: was this the difference between mortals and gods?","[Exactly. In just over a year, even without knowing the deeper relationship between Xi Ling and Xi Yuanshan, relying on her intuition and sharpness, she could see that while Xi Ling appeared favored, Xi Yan actually seemed guarded against him. His chances of being named the heir in the future were actually quite slim, which was why she sought him out for an alliance.","She wasn't the only one who noticed; Xi Ling himself had sensed it long ago.","So when Xie Zhiyao approached Xi Ling to collaborate, the two hit it off immediately.","Master, are you going to ask why it wasn't Xi Ling and Xi Yuanshan collaborating, but rather Xie Zhiyao, the Princess Consort, working with him?]","Yue Fuguang nodded. She did indeed have that question, along with another: \"Does Xie Zhiyao really have that much power? Can a mere princess consort represent the entire Prince Yi's estate?\"","[Master, there is only one reason. In the eyes of outsiders, Xi Yuanshan is hopelessly love-struck! Exactly the kind of hopelessly romantic fool you're thinking of.","After being schemed against by various parties into marrying Xie Zhiyao, he turned around wanting to marry his childhood sweetheart as a secondary consort, only to find that she had already married someone else in Nanzhao.","Heartbroken, Xi Yuanshan always had a strained relationship with Xie Zhiyao, the official princess consort who was also a victim of the 'scheming'.","Later, he consecutively took in many concubines who resembled his childhood sweetheart.]","Good heavens! Yue Fuguang practically shouted \"good heavens.\" Classic, this was just too classic!","Having time-traveled for so many years, she never expected to be lucky enough to see the protagonist of a switched-marriage and substitute-lover trope in real life.","She glanced down at Xi Yuanshan. His appearance was indeed not bad. Although he didn't have the classic male lead look, in one's own story, who isn't a protagonist?","Seeing his measured speech and polite demeanor, she hadn't expected him to be a love-struck fool straight out of a substitute-lover novel. She just didn't know if he was genuinely love-struck or if it was just a persona!","According to the usual plot development, wouldn't this Xi Yuanshan eventually stage a sudden realization of regret, where the pure white moonlight becomes a smeared mosquito blood stain?","After a long period of companionship and entanglement, he would finally realize he had already fallen in love with his Princess Consort, Xie Zhiyao, right?","So Yue Fuguang couldn't help but ask her question: \"Little Zhu, could it be that Xi Yuanshan later realized he had fallen in love with Xie Zhiyao, and then upon hearing she was close to his brother, got jealous and deliberately caused trouble for Xi Ling?\"","[Uh... Master, according to the information Little Zhu has obtained so far, the one Xi Ling currently favors the most is his Concubine Pang.","And Xi Yuanshan still doesn't know that this beloved concubine of his, who looks seventy to eighty percent like his childhood sweetheart, is actually Xie Zhiyao's person.]","Yue Fuguang's jaw almost dropped. This plot twist was too unexpected. \"Xie Zhiyao's person? Isn't she afraid that this woman who resembles her husband's white moonlight will rely on his favor to establish a foothold and seize her power?","Rearing a tiger to invite calamity is not an uncommon occurrence.\"","Just how strong Xie Zhiyao's desire for power and control was, the sovereign and ministers of Great Yan knew all too well.","When many noble ladies were still studying food, clothing, and jewelry, she had already participated in her father's grand rebellion.","When other young ladies were planning their marriages, she had already become the core strength of the rebel army, even wanting to use her own marriage to serve the grand cause of the rebellion.","Would such a woman allow someone to challenge her position as the mistress of the prince's estate?","After all, in this society, a husband's favor could still affect the vital interests of herself and her children.","[Does Master think that someone as smart as Xie Zhiyao wouldn't have a backup plan?","Long before Xie Zhiyao personally sent this Concubine Pang to her husband's bed, she had already secretly given her a sterilizing potion.","[Although this drug isn't the exact same kind used by the Xue brothers and Ling Yuanhang, it's enough to ensure Concubine Pang will never bear a child.]","\"Does Concubine Pang know she's been given a sterility drug?\"","It could only be said that Xie Zhiyao still couldn't grasp the main point. If you have a sterility drug, you should just give it to Xi Yuanshan!","As long as Xi Yuanshan, the source, was around, even if Concubine Pang couldn't give birth, weren't there other secondary consorts and concubines?","She really ought to learn from the Xue brothers and Gan Tang.","Thinking of Gan Tang, Yue Fuguang happened to see her raising a cup to offer a toast. Yue Fuguang smiled in response.","[Naturally, she doesn't know. Otherwise, why would she willingly act as Xie Zhiyao's pawn?","Because in her heart, she still hopes to give birth to a child and rely on the child and the Prince's favor to rise in status!","So the current situation in Prince Yi's estate is that Xi Yuanshan enjoys life while Princess Consort Xie Zhiyao is responsible for 'conquering the world.'","Xie Zhiyao did indeed use a little honey trap during her cooperation with Xi Ling, but the two of them are completely innocent.","However, the mastermind behind the scenes deliberately misled Xi Yuanshan, allowing his people to find 'evidence' intentionally left behind to trick him into believing the two had a long-standing illicit affair. They made him think that for the sake of the throne, they didn't hesitate to scheme against his marriage. After all, Xi Ling had visited Great Yan long ago, so it wasn't surprising that they knew each other. All of this was done to sabotage the cooperation between the two parties.]","The ruler and ministers of Great Yan nodded secretly. In the struggle for power, there had always been open plots and hidden schemes. Although doing this was a bit underhanded, they would have chosen to do the same if it were them.","After all, spreading rumors was the lowest-cost and easiest-to-operate tactic in a game of strategy. Sometimes, you didn't even need evidence.","Yue Fuguang was obviously well-prepared for this kind of thing. She asked, \"Little Zhu, is the mastermind you mentioned the same person who schemed against their marriage?\"","[Master, you should ask if it's the same group of people.]","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow. \"You mean this is a group crime?\"","Seeing Yue Fuguang take the bait, the system chuckled and said, [Master, it's not one group, it's two groups! There's an outer layer and an inner layer.]"]},{"number":356,"title":"Chapter 356: Poisoned Tangyuan with Black Sesame Filling","paragraphs":["The system deliberately teased, and as Yue Fuguang crushed the walnut in her hand, it quickly continued: \"In this arranged marriage, strictly speaking, there were actually three victims. Besides Xie Zhiyao and Xiyuan Mountain, there was also Xixiang, whose engagement was stolen.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"True. Xiyuan Mountain was completely kept in the dark, while Xie Zhiyao played along with the situation. So what’s the story with that unprivileged prince Xixiang?\"","\"Master, on the surface, several princes of Xiqiang joined forces out of discontent with Xiyuan Mountain’s claim to the throne, scheming together to suppress him, leading to that setup. But behind it all stood a hidden puppeteer—one of the victims, Xixiang, whose bride was snatched away, leaving him with no recourse to voice his grievance.\"","Yue Fuguang set down her teacup, recalling the partial intelligence she had seen on him, gathered by Dayan. This man was extremely low-key, hardly making his presence known among the princes. \"Xixiang? Why would he deliberately frame his own prospective princess and brother?\"","Given his precarious position in Xiqiang, it seemed unlikely he could snatch a woman of higher status than Xie Zhiyao. Could Prince Qi’s death have made Xixiang abruptly change his mind?","Yue Fuguang couldn’t figure it out, but those seasoned political veterans like Wei Ping and Cai Xuan glanced at each other, wheels turning in their minds, as if they had already guessed the answer.","Xie Zhiyao, a princess seemingly unable to offer any political advantage to her husband—why was she ultimately betrothed to Xixiang? Because he was the weakest, the least favored by the aging emperor.","Would Xixiang willingly marry such an unhelpful foreign commandery princess?","If he had no ambition for the throne, he would naturally obey the arrangement and bring her into his household, which would greatly benefit his stable future once the new emperor took power.","But if he harbored designs on the throne, he would never waste his position as primary consort.","Xixiang and his brothers, including the one on the throne, must have realized this. Xixiang knew they knew too.","So how to evade the marriage required 'wisdom'!","\"Because he had already chosen the best candidate for his consort long ago.\"","\"So from the very beginning, Xixiang only pretended to agree to the marriage alliance. He never actually intended to marry Xie Zhiyao?\"","\"Master, it should be said that he never intended to take Xie Zhiyao as his principal consort. If not for Xiyuan Mountain recognizing his lineage and being granted the title of Relic Prince ahead of the other brothers, sparking jealousy and scheming, his original plan was to trap Xie Zhiyao into losing her chastity before marriage, then magnanimously step forward to sacrifice his own reputation for the sake of diplomatic ties between the two nations, reluctantly taking her as a secondary consort.\"","Yue Fuguang’s face turned cold. While she did not particularly care for Xie Zhiyao—and might even order the system to end her life if she interfered with her own plans—she felt deeply disgusted upon hearing how Xixiang would stoop so low as to ruin a woman’s reputation for his own benefit.","\"This Xixiang is nothing but a black-seed dumpling laced with poison!\"","\"Later, when he saw that the princes were scheming against Xiyuan Mountain, he steered them toward pairing him with Xie Zhiyao.","Thus, the news Xie Zhiyao received about him and Xiyuan Mountain was deliberately leaked by Xixiang’s men. Even what she 'accidentally' heard or saw, and the way the eunuchs and maids fawned over the powerful while belittling the weak, was orchestrated by Xixiang. He knew exactly how a power-hungry woman like Xie Zhiyao would react.","From the moment he learned he would marry Xie Zhiyao, he had already sent people to Dayan’s capital to investigate her character and conduct.","He even learned ahead of the Xiqiu father-daughter pair that Emperor Mingxi planned to take action against Prince Qi’s line.","So he was well aware that once Xie Zhiyao knew about his situation, she would never willingly marry him.","And things turned out exactly as he expected—Xie Zhiyao jumped into the trap even with her eyes open.\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. In truth, she felt that in their ruthless ambition, willingness to use any means, and obsessive drive for the throne, Xixiang and Xie Zhiyao were quite suited to each other—a match of like-minded power players.","But if such a pairing actually succeeded, the first thing they’d do is fight each other!","After all, even two tigers, one male and one female, will vie for dominance in matters of power.","\"Little Zhu, a man like Xixiang—cunning, scheming, selfish, and cold—if he ever gets to be emperor, it will spell major trouble for Dayan.\" Even for Xiqiang itself, it wouldn’t necessarily be good.","If Xiyan could live a few more years, it might not matter. But if he dies within the next couple of years, and the sly, sheep-in-wolf’s-clothing Xixiang seizes power, the consequences would be severe.","Unless she personally executed them, even if Dayan managed to conquer Xiqiang, it would come at a huge cost.","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers exchanged glances. Consciously or not, their eyes fell on Zheng Zicheng, the deputy director of the Secret Intelligence Bureau, seated at the lower end.","As the third-in-command of Dayan’s intelligence department, Zheng Zicheng felt a chill crawl up his spine from the scrutiny of the emperor and his colleagues.","Cold sweat involuntarily beaded on his brow. Clenching his fists, he forced himself not to look at his superior, the Crown Prince, but instead shook his head apologetically at Emperor Mingxi.","Their lack of intelligence on Xixiang was indeed a failure.","Among all the princes, aside from his looks, Xixiang was the most unremarkable. They had been subconsciously deceived by his overly handsome, harmless appearance and his low-key style of operation.","It was only recently, when they heard he was about to marry the daughter of Xiqiang’s Marquis of Changxin, that they began deploying more agents to gather additional information.","Even the latest intelligence would take at least half a month to arrive from Xiqiang.","But regardless of past mistakes, Emperor Mingxi and his ministers now clearly understood that Xixiang could not be allowed to live.","Having someone assassinate him was one option, but if Dayan’s men did the deed... it would leave undeniable evidence for Xiqiang.","But if it looked like a struggle among the brothers, where someone couldn’t help but strike against his own kin...","The ministers couldn’t help but turn their gaze toward Xiyuan Mountain and Xiling. Weren’t two equally sharp swords already conveniently at hand?","Zheng Zicheng received the tacit signal from the emperor and the crown prince and nodded almost imperceptibly. How to skillfully and covertly leak Xixiang’s machinations to those two, making them believe without exposing themselves? That required careful planning.","Zheng Zicheng’s fingers tapped lightly on his desk. Some of his spies in Xiqiang had already wormed their way into the noble circles, but due to insufficient achievements, they had yet to earn the full trust of those princes.","This time, he could choose a suitable target to deliver the message, further boosting his own men’s position.","Yue Fuguang glanced around, noticing the furrowed brow on Zheng Zicheng’s face as he began plotting countermeasures. She knew the matter was settled.","Truly, 'killing with a borrowed knife' was the most cost-effective method!","By now, everyone in the hall was half-drunk, many lounging lazily in their chairs, watching the graceful dance of the performers with hazy, inebriated eyes.","Just now, Gantang had raised a toast to her, which reminded her of something. So she asked, \"Little Zhu, are you sure that after Gantang attended the Crown Prince’s wedding last time, she didn’t rescue Ling Yuanhang on the way back?\""]},{"number":357,"title":"Chapter 357: Poetic Talent 'Unrivaled Among Six Kingdoms'","paragraphs":["[Master, Little Zhu found out that Ling Yuanhang died of severe injuries in the fifth year of Yuankang. On the day he was supposed to meet Gan Tang, the carriage Gan Tang was riding broke down while the diplomatic mission was traveling, causing her to arrive a day late, which ultimately led to the two of them missing each other.]","Hearing the two ancestors mention the breakdown of Gan Tang's carriage, You Mingmin, the Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial, felt his head buzz, and his heart instantly jumped into his throat.","Cold sweat rolled into his eyes, stinging them and causing him to blink rapidly. He couldn't tell if it was tears or sweat flowing from the corners of his eyes.","He hurriedly raised a trembling hand and used his sleeve to wipe the cold sweat from his forehead and the corners of his eyes.","In his heart, he prayed ceaselessly: please, do not let them trace this back to me!","Emperor Mingxi's eyes flickered, and his hand unconsciously tightened around the white jade wine cup, completely unaware that the cup was already empty.","Eunuch Qian, being very perceptive, hurried forward to pour wine for the Emperor. His body perfectly shielded Emperor Mingxi, giving him a moment of respite and timely covering the expression on his face.","Regardless of how nervous the guilty parties felt, the astonished voice of Yue Fuguang still reached their ears, \"The carriage broke down, so they missed each other? As expected, of the Great Dao's fifty, Heaven derives forty-nine, and humanity escapes with one. The variable in this matter actually stemmed from Gan Tang's broken-down carriage! Destiny truly has no fixed numbers!\"","[Master, do you need Little Zhu to investigate the reason behind this?]","The sovereign and officials of the Great Yan collectively shuddered in their hearts. While accepting this judgment, they also comforted themselves inwardly: It's fine, it's fine. Even if the two ancestors found out they did it, they would only think it was part of a political game between the two countries and definitely wouldn't think otherwise.","Yue Fuguang took in everyone's reactions, especially You Mingmin, who was shaking like a leaf. His psychological endurance was simply too poor.","She forced down the corners of her rising lips, paused for a moment, and said, \"There's no need. Since it has nothing to do with us, master and servant, why bother investigating? Perhaps it was the Heavenly Dao of this realm taking pity on the living beings under its rule, and therefore it took away that menace, Ling Yuanhang.\"","[Master, Ling Yuanhang died, but the Ling family is slowly prospering. Ever since Wei Ping and Cai Xian joined forces two years ago and deciphered the cause of death of Ling Langshan and the Ling family elites through subtle clues, the Emperor, remembering Ling Langshan's sacrifice, granted compensation to the Ling clan. Two members of the Ling family passed the metropolitan examination last year, and the entire Ling family relocated back to the capital city of Shangjing this year.]","Yue Fuguang looked toward Wei Ping and Cai Xian. Sensing Yue Fuguang's gaze, the two hurriedly raised their cups from afar. Only after Yue Fuguang drank the tea they offered did she say, \"How did those two suddenly remember to investigate a case from over a decade ago?\"","[Isn't it because, Master, you gifted Wei Ping a copy of the Collected Cases of Injustice Rectified on his birthday? The two of them became obsessed with reading it. After studying it for months, they remembered this case that had puzzled them since their youth and remained unsolved. As a result, one investigation led them straight to the salt merchants and the noble families.]","\"So, the fact that the salt merchants and noble families have been successively purged over the past two years was all triggered by a thread I unintentionally pulled by giving them a book?\"","Yue Fuguang's voice carried a hint of lightness. \"Indeed, the ways of the world are unpredictable. This mortal realm is getting more and more interesting. Little Zhu, we've done quite a few things over these three years. I just wonder what kind of changes it will bring to Great Yan, or even this entire world?\"","That expectant tone brought an unspeakable smile to the faces of everyone who heard it.","The five nations did not yet know that today's Great Yan was no longer what it used to be. When natural disasters struck, it would also be the day they began their harvest.","Before the smile on Yue Fuguang's face could fade, she heard a voice say, \"Respected Junior Preceptor Yue, I am Wenren Xin of South Yue. I have long heard that Your Excellency's poetic talent is unmatched across the six nations. I have come specifically to seek your guidance today.\"","Yue Fuguang was taken aback. Her poetic talent was unmatched across the six nations? Where did that come from?","In the three years she had been here, she had only recited a few poems, and she had clearly stated that they were the works of others; she was merely a courier.","How did it spread and turn into being unmatched across the six nations?","Who was spreading rumors about her? Did they get her permission?","You say unmatched, and it's unmatched?","Wenren Xin? Never heard of him!","She cast her eyes toward the tall and straight figure at the banquet. Wenren Xin was dressed in a moon-white long gown, in his twenties, of average build, and his complexion was paler than most people from South Yue.","Seeing his decent appearance, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but sweep her gaze back and forth between him and Gan Tang.","After shifting into a more comfortable posture, Yue Fuguang finally said, \"How does the esteemed envoy wish to seek guidance? By composing poems?\"","Wenren Xin cupped his hands and said, \"Today is the birthday of His Majesty the Emperor of Great Yan. Why don't we set a topic on the spot and compose poems to celebrate?\"","\"Brother Wenren's proposal is quite good!\" Another person from the Nanzhao diplomatic mission stood up. He looked only a few years older than Wenren Xin, wearing a light cyan robe with wide sleeves, had ordinary features, and sported a short beard.","He cupped his hands toward Yue Fuguang and said, \"I am Kong You of Nanzhao. Greetings, Junior Preceptor Yue.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Mr. Kong also wishes to join this game?\"","She asked very directly. Anyone with eyes could see that they came prepared, so there was no need for her to cover for these people.","Whether they wanted to step on her, a Junior Preceptor and Divine Maiden whose reputation spread wider than her unmatched poetic talent, to climb the ranks, or if they had other plans, she would take them all on!","Isn't it just composing poetry?","Even if she couldn't compose, couldn't she recite?","Yue Fuguang was confident. With five thousand years of cultural heritage backing her up, could she really not defeat two unknown nobodies?","Just as she thought this, she saw a middle-aged man step forward from both the Western Qiang and Northern Li diplomatic missions.","So her opponents weren't two, but four!","\"Song Xian of Northern Li greets Junior Preceptor Yue. I have long heard of Your Excellency's poetic talent, and I hope to have the honor of seeking some guidance from you today.\"","Song Xian was tall and robust. If he hadn't spoken, Yue Fuguang would have grouped him with the martial artists.","\"Lan Fengling of Western Qiang greets Junior Preceptor Yue. My request is the same as Brother Song's. I ask Your Excellency to grant us your instruction.\"","A faint smile curled at the corners of Yue Fuguang's mouth. She didn't answer the two men but instead looked toward the Eastern Yi diplomatic mission.","\"And who does your esteemed mission plan to send out?\"","Her gaze swept over the people of the Eastern Yi mission one by one. Four sheep or five sheep were all the same to her; she might as well call them all up at once.","She could tell that when it came to stepping on her, these nations seemed to have joined forces once again, so it was impossible for Eastern Yi to be left out.","The leader of Eastern Yi this time was Prince Yanji. Facing Yue Fuguang's half-smiling question, he hesitantly stood up, bowed, and said, \"Since the Junior Preceptor has invited us, Eastern Yi naturally will not spoil the fun.\"","He turned to a young man in his twenties seated below him and said, \"Oshima, how about you represent our great Eastern Yi in this challenge?\"","Oshima hurriedly stood up with a humble demeanor and replied, \"Yes, Brother!\"","Hearing Oshima's name, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but take a few extra glances at the man. You had to admit, this young man in his twenties, just from his appearance, looked thirty to forty percent similar to the deceased Sima Jing and his son Sima Ying.","In the autumn of the sixth year of Yuankang, when the entire Sima clan was beheaded, Yue Fuguang had been sitting in a teahouse along the route of the prisoner carts and had seen the Sima father and son from afar. Judging purely by looks, it was certain that this Oshima was indeed the son of Sima Jing.","Hearing this name, the ruler and ministers of Dayan could not help but look over. Their sudden attention caused Oshima Kensei to involuntarily lower his head, as he had grown increasingly cautious over the past year, terrified that the slightest misstep would invite ridicule."]},{"number":358,"title":"Chapter 358: How Hilarious","paragraphs":["\"Now that everyone is here, Wenren Xin, how do you propose we set the topics?\"","Yue Fuguang tossed the melon seeds in her hand back onto the plate and threw the question back at Wenren Xin, lest they blame heaven and earth instead of their own uselessness when they lose later!","Wenren Xin bowed and said, \"I believe it would be best if each of the six of us sets one topic. What do you think?\"","The others nodded in agreement. Yue Fuguang merely smiled and agreed, letting them make whatever foolproof preparations they wanted beforehand.","Faced with the Sage of Poetry and the Immortal of Poetry standing behind her, they were not even worth mentioning.","At this moment, Kong You suddenly said, \"In recent years, it has become popular among us scholars to write lines of irregular lengths, which we call Ci poetry. Why don't we compose both Shi poems and Ci poems for today's match? What do you all think?\"","Although he asked the group, Kong You's eyes were fixed on Yue Fuguang.","Hearing his words, Yue Fuguang suddenly laughed. To think that these few people wanted to forcibly shake the Tang and Song dynasties backing her. How ridiculous!","She made no attempt to hide the smile on her face and said loudly, \"Acceptable!\"","Kong You, who had been full of confidence, suddenly felt a bit unsure because of Yue Fuguang's inexplicable smile.","However, the arrow was already on the bowstring. No matter what thoughts he had, he had to continue. After all, they were the ones who had provoked this matter.","Next came the question of who would set the first topic. Yue Fuguang leaned back in her chair, \"I, the Junior Preceptor, do not mind. Any of you can go first.\"","Seeing her young age, not only did she not take them seriously, but she also seemed to genuinely treat this challenge, which they had planned for nearly a year, as an insignificant game!","Kong You and Wenren Xin exchanged a glance. Kong You spoke first, \"Since it was Brother Wenren who started this, how about you set the first topic, Brother?\"","\"We have no objections.\" The others said, looking up at Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang made a gesture of invitation and said, \"Wenren Xin, please present the topic!\"","Wenren Xin cupped his hands to the crowd and pretentiously thought for a moment, as if he could not find a satisfactory topic.","Turning around, he happened to see the brightly blooming chrysanthemums placed under the vermilion pillars in the hall. He suddenly smiled, pointed at the cluster of chrysanthemums, and said, \"Why don't we use chrysanthemums as the first topic? Everyone is free to choose between Shi or Ci poetry. What do you think?\"","Everyone nodded. At this time, Yue Fuguang also slowly walked down the jade steps and sat in the seats specially set up for the six of them in the center of the hall.","Hearing that the topic was chrysanthemums, Yue Fuguang unconsciously thought of the line that the person is thinner than the yellow flower.","For this round, I must invite my number one talented woman, Sister Zhao, to take the stage.","While Yue Fuguang was grinding ink, the others had already found inspiration and were wielding their brushes on paper. One could only say that their talent came very quickly indeed.","In a moment, Wenren Xin's poem Defying the Frost was completed. A person from Nanyue cupped his hands to everyone in the hall and then loudly recited his verses: \"The west wind cuts to the bone and a hundred flowers wither, alone embracing the cold branch cast like iron. Not all who are aloof must shun the world, where the heart's lamp burns is the spring tide.\"","Bei Ye was the first to clap and praise, \"Good poem! What a wonderful line, Not all who are aloof must shun the world.\"","The others also gave high praise. Wenren Xin appeared modest on the surface, but seeing his slightly raised head, he looked like a rooster that had just begun to fight and was already certain of its victory, eager to spread its wings and show off its gorgeous feathers.","Then came Splashing Gold by Song Xian of Beili.","\"Who splashes golden clouds all over the imperial city? Thousands of arrowheads shoot into the clear autumn. The horse bones of the capital are worth a thousand gold, yet they cannot match a single tender blossom in the frosty sky.\"","As soon as his poem came out, Bei Ye again took the lead in praising, \"Mr. Song has great verses. What a wonderful line, Thousands of arrowheads shoot into the clear autumn. The use of the word shoot is extremely brilliant. What does Third Royal Brother think?\"","Prince Bei Yue smiled and raised his cup, \"I toast to Mr. Song. Sir, you have great talent. However, I am different from my Fifth Brother; I prefer the line yet they cannot match a single tender blossom in the frosty sky.\"","While the two brothers of the Beili royal family exchanged words, the poems of the others were also ready.","Reclusion by Lan Fengling of Xiqiang:","\"Autumn light fills the gaps in the fence, white dew blends with tea to lengthen the flavor. Occasionally, poetry debts from Master Tao arrive, and the moon's marks, deep and shallow, print upon the southern pond.\"","Embracing Fragrance by Da Dao:","\"Golden armor draped in frost stands in the evening courtyard, its faint fragrance refuses to cross the window lattice. Embracing the branch, it defends the Double Ninth promise to the death, leaving a preface for the plum blossoms.\"","Once these two poems were presented, setting aside the others, the members of their own diplomatic missions were the first to highly praise them.","Only Wenren Xin, who initially thought he could outshine everyone, had an increasingly dark expression, especially when Kong You's Ci poem Xing Xiang Zi: Wild Chrysanthemum was presented; his face looked as if it had been splashed with ink.","\"Not claiming spring's glory, instead polishing autumn's gong. Facing the green cliffs, bursting forth like cold stars. The wind carves its jade petals, the dew tempers its golden eyes. Keeping three parts stubbornness, seven parts wildness, and ten parts purity. The deserted path once knew the welcome of fair hands. Who now remembers the bamboo basket and cloud-like hair? Fragrance sinks in the ancient ravine, shadow falls into the empty vase. Leaving only the mountain soul thin, the stone soul silent, the moon soul awake.\"","With the topic of chrysanthemums, Wenren Xin knew that if his own Defying the Frost showed its strength, then Embracing Fragrance displayed its loyalty, Reclusion carried its transcendence, and Splashing Gold depicted its magnificence.","As for Kong You's Ci poem, it revealed an eternal life posture that transcended time and space. The few of them were evenly matched; he had indeed rejoiced a bit too early just now.","He just did not know how Junior Preceptor Yue's work would turn out. As long as any of them surpassed her poem, it would be a victory for them all.","Yue Fuguang, who was on their minds, was slowly copying her poem while discreetly observing their expressions.","It seemed that this provocation was indeed premeditated by their respective countries, but when it came to selecting topics, they might not have truly shared their bottom lines with each other.","After all, given her current reputation among the six nations, the common people might not know who their own emperor was, but they definitely knew the title of Goddess Yue Fuguang.","As for the poetry circles, sorry, that was just a handful of people; she had no interest in knowing about them.","However, it was undeniable that stepping on her reputation to rise to power was a huge temptation and benefit, and several countries wanted to push their own people up.","The result was the current situation where they were all evenly matched.","Among the six people, five poems and Ci had already been presented, and everyone could not help but look at her.","The sovereign and ministers of Dayan, who had not participated in the discussion all along, also could not help but look at their Junior Preceptor. There was no worry on their faces, only faint smiles, showing a relaxed expression of waiting to listen closely to the Junior Preceptor's masterpiece.","Unfortunately, Yue Fuguang did not read her poem. Instead, she said, \"Since this is a competition to determine who is superior, shouldn't we have a wager?\"","Hearing her mention a wager, the expressions of the people from the various countries became unnatural for a moment, as dead memories began to mercilessly attack them.","They had originally thought that by using the pretext of asking for guidance to downplay the competition, they could save on a wager, and if they won, it would be a highly profitable deal requiring no capital.","Who would have thought that just when it seemed they could gloss over it, Yue Fuguang would bring it up at the last moment.","A wager! She was a Junior Preceptor, possessing the title and fief of a prince. Why was she still thinking about the meager winnings of a wager!","Seeing the unpredictable changes on everyone's faces, Yue Fuguang could not help but smile harmlessly, \"Princess Lan Xuan'er and Prince Bei Yue know me. If the wager is too small, it is not worth this Junior Preceptor making a move.\"","She folded up what she had written. In the eyes of some, it seemed she was afraid and was deliberately finding an excuse to cancel the competition.","Wenren Xin, Kong You, and the others, who felt their poems were exceptionally well-written, were certainly unwilling to let it end so hastily.","Whether they could make a name for themselves across the six nations in their twenties and trample the scholars of the world underfoot depended entirely on tonight!"]},{"number":359,"title":"Chapter 359: A Place to Call Home","paragraphs":["\"Your Royal Highness!\" Wenren Xin gazed at Gan Tang with burning eyes, causing a faint blush to rise on her cheeks under his intense stare.","Yue Fuguang thought to herself, the relationship between these two is indeed not simple.","Meanwhile, Kong You also looked toward Lan Xuan'er, but Lan Xuan'er remained silent.","For the past three years, she had never been able to fathom the true depths of this Junior Preceptor.","Even those few poems circulating outside were deliberately spread by the ruler and ministers of Great Yan to build her reputation. As for the rumors growing increasingly outrageous later on, that was the work of people harboring malicious intentions.","Lan Xuan'er had always maintained her doubts about this.","While others thought Junior Preceptor Yue was afraid, only she had a faint feeling that this person was probably setting another trap for their respective countries right here!","However, remembering her mother the Empress's instructions before she came, Lan Xuan'er sighed helplessly in her heart. Even knowing it was a pit, it seemed her only option was to jump right in.","Xi Ling looked at Yue Fuguang. \"What kind of wager does Junior Preceptor Yue think would be worthy enough for us to have the honor of hearing your masterpiece?\"","He smiled at Xi Yuanshan and said, \"Imperial Brother, if I remember correctly, there doesn't seem to be another place like the Three Forks on the border of our two countries, right?\"","Xi Yuanshan nodded. \"A place where three countries intersect? Indeed, there is none.\"","Bei Ye also said to Bei Yue, \"Imperial Brother, there doesn't seem to be one within our Northern Li territory either.\"","Bei Yue nodded and looked toward Yue Fuguang. \"What are your thoughts, Junior Preceptor?\"","Yue Fuguang smiled and said, \"You all know me. I don't have many hobbies usually, I just like to find some bizarre seeds and plant them in the ground.\"","Everyone nodded. Those were no bizarre seeds; those were divine crops!","Not only did they yield high harvests, but their taste was also surprisingly good!","Not to mention the grain, even for the vegetables and fruits, one would have to pay a high price to eat them in their own countries.","Yue Fuguang looked at Emperor Mingxi. \"Thanks to my Emperor's profound favor, I lack no variety of playthings here.","Therefore, I have recently acquired some new high-yield seeds, and I am just missing a piece of land to plant them on.\"","Before the other countries could speak, the moment Emperor Mingxi heard this, he hurriedly interjected, \"Fuguang, if you want to plant things and the space is not enough, I can simply expand your princely fiefdom. Why must you...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, Bei Yue said, \"So the Junior Preceptor is lacking a place to display her talents. That is easy to arrange.\"","He smiled, first cupping his hands in a salute to Emperor Mingxi, and then said to Yue Fuguang, \"I wonder what wager the Junior Preceptor plans to offer?\"","Gan Tang smiled and picked up the conversation. \"We are not interested in land. How about... if the Junior Preceptor loses, you come as a guest to the winner's home?\"","Xi Ling nodded in agreement. \"The Princess's proposal is excellent. Our Western Qiang welcomes the Junior Preceptor at any time.\"","Bei Ye also smiled and said, \"Our Northern Li will also sweep our beds in anticipation, ready to welcome Junior Preceptor Yue at any moment.\"","Lan Xuan'er had no choice but to stand up and say, \"The gates of my Southern Zhao are always open to the Junior Preceptor.\"","Seeing that everyone had expressed their stance, Yan Ji was unwilling to fall behind. \"My Eastern Yi also awaits the Junior Preceptor's visit.\"","Faced with everyone's enthusiastic invitations, Yue Fuguang gave a mysterious smile. \"Since everyone is so hospitable, within my lifetime, this Junior Preceptor will definitely visit all of your homes to take a look around.\"","\"You must not!\" Emperor Mingxi grew a little anxious, and the civil and military officials of Great Yan were even more anxious than their Emperor.","What intentions these people were hiding—they were all thousand-year-old foxes, who couldn't see through it? Weren't they just trying to abduct their family's Junior Preceptor!","This was out of jealousy for Great Yan's development over the past two years, especially its granaries, which could be said to be the most abundant among the six nations.","These people must have found out to some extent that the changes up and down Great Yan today were all related to their Junior Preceptor, which was why they extended such invitations.","Yue Fuguang waved her hand and said to Emperor Mingxi, \"Your Majesty, please calm down and do not be impatient.\"","Seeing that he still had words to say, she directly blocked him by saying, \"Your Majesty, is it that you have no confidence in my poetic talent, which is unparalleled across the six nations?\"","Her behavior at this moment perfectly resembled a spoiled, slightly rebellious, and overly confident brat.","Only then did everyone remember that this Junior Preceptor Yue was not even twelve years old yet. Wasn't it normal for her to be a bit of a brat?","Seeing Emperor Mingxi rendered speechless, his face and neck red, Yue Fuguang shot a glance at Xie Zhiyan, then turned back to Gan Tang, Bei Yue, and the others. \"Are you all certain you want to wager your borderlands with me?\"","The five nations, led by Southern Yue, Western Qiang, and Northern Li, exchanged glances. Gan Tang smiled and said, \"We are willing to offer a small piece of land where our countries intersect for the Junior Preceptor to plant new crops.","We only have one request. If the Junior Preceptor unfortunately loses, please accept our invitation.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"I love going out to be a guest the most!\"","Hearing her words, the corners of the mouths of Great Yan's ruler and ministers couldn't help but twitch.","Who was it that spent all year round just circling between the Prince's estate, the Yu residence, and the Imperial Palace? At first, they could still invite her to the various banquets at their homes, but later on, trying to get this person to attend was incredibly difficult.","She wouldn't come to flower-viewing banquets, nor would she attend wedding feasts. However, the Junior Preceptor's gifts were truly given, and they were all good things!","Yue Fuguang: Why would I go? Someone always falls into the water at flower-viewing banquets. Sigh! If she hadn't brought female guards with her every time, she would probably have ended up matching several couples by now!","And as for wedding banquets, going meant losing at least one blessing talisman. She had quite a few points now and didn't lack that one talisman.","But well, once or twice was fine. Too many times, and attending these feasts lost its novelty, making her too lazy to go out.","Especially the gossip from certain families that had nothing to do with advancing her own missions—she just secretly ate those melons with her system.","She really didn't want to share it; otherwise, this capital city of Shangjing would be turned upside down!","Yue Fuguang didn't care what they thought. She simply turned sideways to Cai Xian and asked, \"Minister Cai, did you bring the map?\"","Cai Xian had been silently preparing ever since he heard Yue Fuguang mention the wager. Now, seeing her turn to ask him, Cai Xian, who had already quietly moved to Yue Fuguang's side, instantly had his eyes light up.","Without another word, he reached into his robes. \"Please take a look, Junior Preceptor.\"","Yue Fuguang took it and unrolled it. It was still the same map from three years ago. How did she know it was the same one? Because the circle she had drawn at the Three Forks last time was still there.","Yue Fuguang cast a meaningful glance at Cai Xian. Three years had passed, yet the geographical layout of the several countries on the map before her hadn't changed a bit; it still looked like a rough sketch.","She hadn't forgotten that she had once presented the clearest map of the six nations in the royal court, and these people had memorized it by heart without even blinking an eye.","Pointing at the borders of the countries, Yue Fuguang said to them, \"I understand your difficulties. You cannot make the decision for too much land.","How about we use a tract of thirty miles of borderland as the wager?\"","Upon hearing this, they revealed troubled expressions. Their initial thought was that a few thousand to ten thousand acres of land would already be a lot.","They hadn't expected this Junior Preceptor to have such a huge appetite, asking for an entire thirty-mile tract of land right off the bat.","Yue Fuguang's smile faded a bit. She swept her gaze over them and said, \"This Junior Preceptor was being considerate of the fact that you are not in supreme power, so I didn't ask for a ninety-mile tract.","What, are you not even as capable as me, a prince of a different surname? You can't even make the call for a thirty-mile stretch of land?","You are all the people most likely to inherit the great thrones in the future. If you don't even have this little bit of courage and decisiveness, how will you govern an entire country in the future?\"","As she spoke, she completely put away her smile. \"Or do you all think that a mere few acres of land are enough to exchange for this Junior Preceptor?\""]},{"number":360,"title":"Chapter 360: Play Something Different","paragraphs":["She waved her sleeve. \"Since you all show so little sincerity, please suit yourselves. I am tired and will no longer entertain you!\"","Seeing her walking toward the jade steps, Bei Ye was the first to lose his composure. \"Junior Preceptor Yue, please wait!\"","Before coming here, his imperial father had granted the two of them the authority to act as they saw fit. As long as there was even a sliver of hope, they had to bring Yue Fuguang back to Northern Li intact.","The other nations were both allies and competitors. After all, there was only one Yue Fuguang, but four allies.","Yue Fuguang did not stop. Instead, she continued walking and said, \"Think carefully before you speak. I do not have that much free time to play games with you all.\"","Bei Yue and Bei Ye exchanged a glance and said, \"Northern Li is willing to wager a thirty-li stretch of land with Junior Preceptor Yue!\"","Seeing that Northern Li had agreed, the others realized that if they chickened out now, wouldn't it just benefit those two brothers?","In truth, everyone still held absolute confidence in their victory. They had made thorough preparations, and the poems they presented today were the absolute best selected over the past year.","Those few had always believed their true opponents were not the dealer, Yue Fuguang, but their own allies.","Yue Fuguang paused, then turned around and asked, \"What about the two princesses and three princes? Will you still participate?\"","Xi Ling said loudly, \"Western Qiang also agrees. A thirty-li stretch of land in exchange for Junior Preceptor Yue visiting Western Qiang as a guest—it is worth it!\"","As soon as his words fell, Gan Tang also smiled and said, \"Southern Yue agrees as well. All of Nanzhao will welcome the Junior Preceptor's visit at any time.\"","Next was Yan Ji. However, since their land did not border Great Yan, Yue Fuguang casually pointed out a small island. Yan Ji took a look and saw that the island was only thirty or forty li across, with barren soil that couldn't grow crops at all.","He assumed Yue Fuguang was unaware of this and had no intention of pointing it out, readily agreeing to the terms.","He also failed to notice the eyes of Cai Xian, who stood beside Yue Fuguang, light up as he secretly thought: What a great location this island has!","Only one party remained. Yue Fuguang looked toward the much more composed Lan Xuan'er. \"Is Princess Xuanping not going to follow?\"","Seeing everyone look at her, Lan Xuan'er felt a deep panic. It wasn't the panic of being stared at, but the dread of falling into a pit and being unable to climb out.","She looked at Yue Fuguang's beautiful, harmless face. When her gaze landed on the lotus mark on her forehead, all her resistance melted into a single sentence: \"Nanzhao also agrees!\"","Realizing what she had just said, Lan Xuan'er helplessly averted her eyes. Her palms were covered in sweat, but she could not change this gamble that the several nations had plotted for so long.","Yue Fuguang nodded and walked back to her desk. \"Lord Wei, are the contracts ready?\"","Wei Ping bowed and said, \"They are all prepared. Please review them, Junior Preceptor.\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"Crown Prince, once you confirm there are no errors, remember to sign them and dispatch them to the respective nations. Everyone, remember to accept your losses gracefully.\"","She smiled as her gaze swept over them. \"Let us continue!\"","Saying this, she unrolled the poem she had copied, Sister Zhao's \"Zui Hua Yin\": \"Thin mist and thick clouds, a sorrowful endless day; Auspicious incense burns in the golden beast. It is the Double Ninth Festival again; On the jade pillow inside the gauze canopy, the midnight chill first seeps through. Drinking wine by the eastern fence after dusk, A dark fragrance fills my sleeves. Do not say one's soul is not consumed; When the west wind rolls up the curtain, I am thinner than the yellow chrysanthemums.\"","When everyone read the final lines, \"When the west wind rolls up the curtain, I am thinner than the yellow chrysanthemums,\" the expressions on their faces were quite a spectacle.","The civil officials of Great Yan showed undisguised joy. \"Great poem, excellent verses!\" They began showering Yue Fuguang with free-flowing praise.","Meanwhile, the people from the other nations saw their faces turn from green to pale, and from pale to red. Even the most active Bei Ye shut his mouth and remained silent.","The originally smug faces of Kong You, Wenren Xin, and the others went blank for a moment.","Had this piece of paper ever left their sight, they would have accused her of not writing the poem herself!","How could it be that after studying for over a decade, the poems they composed couldn't compare to a little girl who had only been schooling for three years?","As for her being some descended goddess, they didn't believe a single word of it.","Finally, Wenren Xin was the first to speak up. \"Junior Preceptor Yue, this poem is beautiful, yes, but it is simply too petty and narrow in scope!\"","Yue Fuguang had long anticipated that since they came specifically for her, they wouldn't concede defeat so quickly. Besides, in literature, there is no absolute first; in martial arts, there is no second.","However...","Since that was the case, they would just go again!","The crowd didn't expect Yue Fuguang to be so agreeable. Her writing was clearly superior, yet she compromised so easily. Not to mention the outsiders,","even the ruler and ministers of Great Yan couldn't help but exchange glances, seeing both confusion and the realization in each other's eyes that the Junior Preceptor was about to stir up some serious trouble.","Figuring this out, they silently took a few steps back, afraid of hindering Yue Fuguang's performance.","Seeing the subtle movements of the Great Yan courtiers, Lan Xuan'er felt even more certain that she was falling into a trap. Unfortunately, a loosed arrow cannot be returned.","Her name was already stamped on the contract, and the ink had dried!","Next came Kong You's poem on homesickness, Song Yu's on longing for someone, and Western Qiang and Eastern Yi's poems on autumn and snow.","After a round among the six of them, the result was still a draw!","Finally, everyone looked toward Yue Fuguang. She said calmly, \"Since we have tied in the first five rounds, and this final round will determine the victor, let us play something different.\"","Kong You asked, \"How does Junior Preceptor Yue wish to play?\"","He silently wiped the cold sweat from his palms with his sleeve. Over these five rounds, they had practically brought out the very best poems in their arsenal.","Yet, they were still slightly inferior to her compositions.","The few of them had brazenly called it a draw, but everyone present knew they were bullying the young and using their numbers to their advantage. And this was on her home turf! Just looking at the expressions of the Great Yan ruler and ministers, they knew that if they tried to pass off shoddy work as good in this final round, they probably wouldn't walk out of the grand hall in one piece.","If Yue Fuguang knew what he was thinking, she would definitely say: Bullying with numbers? This is nothing!","In a moment, she was going to show this group what true bullying with numbers looked like!","\"Why don't we set our own topics? You can write about whatever you want. In the end, we will determine the winner by who writes the most and the best poems. What do you say?\"","Song Yu, Wenren Xin, and the others exchanged glances, all catching a fleeting flash of excitement in each other's eyes.","The allied nations, though they had communicated beforehand and set the topics,","knew that allies couldn't be trusted in the face of profit. Therefore, the several nations had unanimously guessed the topics like candidates preparing for the imperial examinations.","They then sought out great contemporary scholars to ghostwrite poems, while Wenren Xin and the others were responsible for memorizing them.","As a result, they actually had quite a few backup poems stored in their heads. They never expected that these would unexpectedly come in handy at the very end!","Lan Fengling was the first to speak. \"I believe Junior Preceptor Yue's proposal is excellent! What do you think, Brother Song?\"","Suppressing the excitement in his heart, Song Yu nodded in agreement. \"I think so as well. What do you two worthy brothers think?\"","Oshima was left hanging on the side, as Song Yu directly asked for the opinions of Kong You and Wenren Xin.","The flames of guaranteed victory flickered in both of their eyes as they said in unison, \"That is perfectly fine!\"","Seeing that they agreed, Yue Fuguang waved her large sleeve and said boldly, \"Then let us begin!\"","She waved to Wu Yong. \"Prepare the brush, ink, paper, and inkstone!\"","She then sat back in her chair, resting her head on her hand, and said in a relaxed manner, \"Wu Yong, I will recite and you will write. If you get tired, remember to switch with someone else.\"","Sitting opposite her, Wu Yong nodded. At this moment, he still didn't understand what she meant by switching with someone else if he got tired.","He was just responsible for taking notes; he didn't even have to use his brain. How tired could he possibly get?"]},{"number":361,"title":"Chapter 361: Dao Heart Shattered","paragraphs":["But soon, Yue Fuguang would teach him a lesson and use facts to tell him that yes, it really gets tiring!","Yue Fuguang took a final glance at the few people who had already started scribbling furiously. At this moment, the six of them no longer represented just themselves, but the literary foundations of their respective nations.","Yue Fuguang closed her eyes and began to randomly pull from the Tang and Song dynasty poems to recite.","After seeing through their intentions in the first round, she had held back when writing her poems and didn't play her trump cards, the eternal masterpieces.","She had saved them all for this moment to show off all at once. Thus, the moment she spoke, she stunned everyone.","The first to enter the fray was the great Su Dongpo. She recited, When will the bright moon appear? With a cup of wine in my hand, I ask the blue sky. I do not know what year it is tonight in the celestial palaces on high. I wish to ride the wind and return there...","Others were astounded by the profound longing and heartfelt emotion in the poem. To write something so exquisitely unparalleled was truly a harmony of heaven and humanity!","Meanwhile, as Emperor Mingxi and his officials marveled at the poem's brilliance, a trace of worry flashed through their hearts. When the Immortal Lord said, I do not know what year it is tonight in the celestial palaces on high, was she feeling homesick?","She even said she wished to ride the wind and return!","The crowd was reaching out desperately like Erkang in their hearts, with only one thought in mind: Junior Preceptor, please don't abandon us!","Unconcerned with what the emperor and his ministers were thinking, Yue Fuguang just kept her eyes closed and focused on reciting her poems, bringing out another of Mr. Dongpo's masterpieces, The Great River flows east, its waves washing away all the gallant heroes of a thousand ages...","A poem of majestic momentum unfolded before everyone's eyes. Wenren Xin and the others, who had been furiously writing poetry, already felt their Dao hearts wavering when the Prelude to Water Melody came out.","However, they could still barely hold on and continue writing.","But once Nian Nu Jiao was recited, Kong You, the most poetically talented among them, was ironically the first to have his Dao heart shattered.","He had written poetry for three years and listened to so many grandmasters write poems, yet not a single one could compare to the Prelude to Water Melody, let alone Nian Nu Jiao.","He knew that even if he wrote for the rest of his life, he could never catch up to these two poems.","And it wasn't over yet. Yue Fuguang continued to bring out, Bamboo staff and straw sandals are lighter and better than horses, who is afraid? A palm-leaf cape and a misty rain, I will spend my life as I please...","Clack!","The pen in Kong You's hand fell powerlessly onto the table, the ink instantly blooming and ruining a poem he had just finished writing.","Sob, sob, sob!","Before the members of the Nanzhao diplomatic mission even had time to feel heartache over the ruined poem, they heard suppressed, despairing sobs coming from Kong You.","He was crying not only because he was struck hard by Yue Fuguang's three eternal masterpieces, but also because he clearly knew his Dao heart was broken. He, Kong You, would never be able to write poetry again in this lifetime!","The desperate sobbing echoing in her ears did not make Yue Fuguang stop in the slightest. She then brought out a Jiang Cheng Zi, Ten years of life and death, vast and boundless. Though I try not to think of it, I can hardly forget...","The moment this poem came out, Kong You was no longer the only one crying. Suppressed sobs rose one after another, and a grief-stricken feeling of longing spread and infected the entire great hall.","Who didn't have one or two people they longed to see but could never see again, worthy of their yearning?","If they hadn't considered that today was Emperor Mingxi's birthday, a joyous occasion.","Given the time, place, and atmosphere, this place would probably have turned into a mourning hall!","Hearing even more crying, Yue Fuguang merely grumbled inwardly about how sentimental the ancients were, and then switched to someone else. This time, she enlisted the great Li Bai to liven up the overly sorrowful atmosphere.","Do you not see the waters of the Yang River coming from the sky, rushing to the sea and never returning... The Great Yan Dynasty didn't have the Yellow River; its largest and longest river was called the Yang River, so she cleverly swapped the name.","When it came to Master Cen and Dan Qiusheng, Yue Fuguang decisively swapped them for the courtesy names of Wu Yong and Feng Tang: Wu Xingzhi, Feng Jianyue, bring in the wine, let your cups never rest...","Wu Yong, who was still scribbling away to record the poems, instinctively let his hand tremble upon hearing his own courtesy name featured in the Junior Preceptor's poem. As a result, his and Feng Tang's courtesy names under his pen were so messy they were almost unrecognizable.","Behind him, Feng Tang was taken aback for a moment. After his pleasant surprise, he looked at Wu Yong's handwriting and couldn't help but frown. With a grab of his large hand, he lifted Wu Yong by the collar, tossed him to the side, and quickly sat down himself to begin furiously recording.","Wu Yong cried out in his heart, I'm not tired yet!","But he didn't dare to shout it out loud, afraid that making a sound would interrupt the Junior Preceptor's gushing stream of poetic inspiration.","He looked left and right, only to find that the closest empty desk belonged to Kong You. As for Kong You, the man had already slumped to the side, silently shedding tears.","Wu Yong glanced at him and, without a second word, sat right down.","Looking at Kong You, who clearly had nothing left to live for, he shook his head. Of all the people to provoke, you just had to provoke our Junior Preceptor!","Haven't you seen that no matter who you are, the grass on the graves of those who provoked her is already growing tall?","With Kong You's Dao heart broken, Wenren Xin, Song Yu, and the others were now also faintly seeping blood from the corners of their mouths.","The few who had been barely holding on heard a crack the moment Bring in the Wine was recited!","It seemed something had snapped!","Seeking and searching, cold and desolate...","The east wind at night blows open thousands of flowering trees... I search for him hundreds and thousands of times in the crowd. Suddenly, I turn my head, and there that person is, right where the lanterns are waning.","Inside the great hall, whether it was the monarch and officials of the Great Yan or the members of the diplomatic missions, everyone was captivated by these exquisite poems and wine. There was no longer anyone drinking or chatting. Some gathered around, while others leaned back in their chairs with their eyes closed, quietly experiencing the profound atmosphere within the verses.","When will the spring flowers and autumn moon come to an end? How much of the past do we know? I ask you...","Stop writing, I surrender! I... surrender! The moment Li Yu's The Beautiful Lady Yu came out, Kong You, who had been curled up at Wu Yong's feet, could no longer bear it. Word by word, he shouted his surrender.","He was the most anguished one at this moment. His Dao heart was already shattered. If Yue Fuguang didn't stop, he feared that not only would he be unable to write poetry in the future, but he might not even dare to pick up a pen to write essays.","Couldn't they see that the entire hall was silent, completely won over by her poetry? Surrendering wasn't shameful for him!","Hearing the surrender, Yue Fuguang didn't even lift her eyes, continuing, Sing while drinking wine, for how long does life last? It is like the morning dew, and the days passed are full of sorrow...","The wind is urgent, the sky is high, and the apes cry mournfully...","I, I also surrender! Wenren Xin, with a deathly pale face, stared at Yue Fuguang with terrified eyes, as if looking at some terrifying beast.","With red eyes, he looked at Gan Tang and said sorrowfully, Princess! We have lost! A year of preparation, ruined in an instant.","This was not just a matter of losing a bit of ground. He could imagine what a massive uproar the name Yue Fuguang would cause among scholars starting tomorrow!","Some people in his Southern Yue might even enshrine Yue Fuguang on an altar like the common folk do!","In the future, if His Majesty and the officials wanted to touch her, those stubborn scholars... Wenren Xin shook his head in agony. This time, they had truly tried to steal a chicken only to lose the rice!","Hearing Wenren Xin surrender, Yue Fuguang still showed no intention of stopping.","Since she had already started, wouldn't it be a pity to waste this great opportunity and not let these eternal masterpieces continue to be sung in this world!","Not to mention, there were still three people stubbornly holding out!","Song Yu, Lan Fengling, and Oshima thought to themselves: How are we stubbornly holding out? We are simply crushed by these poems to the point of being speechless.","Even Wenren Xin and Kong You had surrendered; how could they possibly have the ability to hold out!","Withered vines, old trees, and dusk crows. A small bridge, flowing water, and households...","A jug of wine among the flowers, drinking alone with no companions...","Last night the rain was sparse and the wind was fierce, deep sleep...","...Yue Fuguang continued reciting her poems."]},{"number":362,"title":"Chapter 362: He Is Actually the Client 'Daddy'","paragraphs":["Smack, smack, smack!","Song Yu and the others, who were still in a daze, were suddenly slapped on the back.","Thump, thump, thump!","Unsurprisingly, the heads of the three men slammed into the desks in front of them. Just as they were about to curse in pain, a faint voice drifted from behind, \"What are you still spacing out for? Hurry up and admit defeat... ah!\"","Their scalps tingled. If they hadn't been surrounded by a crowd, they would have jumped up in fright!","Just what kind of people were around them?","Some were gazing up at the sky, hopelessly captivated by Yue Fuguang's endless stream of masterpieces!","Others were deeply moved by the verses, crying one moment and laughing the next, acting completely unhinged!","Kong You, the first to concede, now had terrifyingly bright eyes. When Song Yu met his gaze, he couldn't help but shudder.","Kong You knew very well that if they didn't stop Yue Fuguang now, no scholar from their nations would be able to suppress her in poetry for decades to come.","All those learned scholars would be utterly conquered by her poems!","Kong You considered himself, much like Wenren Xin, to not be a pure scholar. Otherwise, with so many superior poets in the lands of Nanzhao, why would he be the only one standing here?","\"The affairs of the world are but a great dream, how many cool autumns does one experience in life...\"","\"As if a sudden night of spring breeze has come, blooming pear blossoms on thousands of trees...\"","\"Ascending high to view the magnificent heaven and earth, the vast river flows away never to return...\"","...Yue Fuguang was still reciting poetry!","\"We admit defeat!\"","\"We admit defeat!\"","Before Song Yu and the others could fully grasp the situation, Bei Ye, Xi Ling, and Yan Ji had already shouted out the words of surrender for them!","As the three breathed a sigh of relief, their hearts also sank to the bottom. It was as if all their energy and spirit had been instantly drained, and unable to support themselves, they slumped completely to the ground.","\"The land is so rich in beauty, making countless heroes bow in homage...\"","Yue Fuguang used this poem as her conclusion. She slowly opened her eyes, her gaze sweeping over the shocked and disbelieving faces of the crowd.","Finally, her eyes landed on the ugly expressions of the people from the five nations. \"Gentlemen, yield when you lose a bet. Don't go back on your word now!\"","After saying this, Yue Fuguang hurriedly drank a few mouthfuls of tea. She was dying of thirst!","The people of Dayan knew in their hearts that she was a deity descended to earth, so they could still maintain their composure in the face of these masterpieces.","But the people from the other five nations didn't know that!","So, every single one of them looked at her as if she were some kind of monster!","Naturally, they had met many masters of poetry, and there was no shortage of outstanding talents among them, but...","No one wrote like Yue Fuguang, where every single piece was a classic that would inevitably be sung by the masses!","You might write one, two, or three good poems at a time, but you couldn't make every single one a masterpiece. In the eyes of different people, it was truly hard to rank the poems she presented tonight.","Yue Fuguang didn't care what everyone thought. She just looked down at the table and the floor. Good heavens, was this thick stack of poetry manuscripts all recited by her just now?","She uncertainly asked Wei Ping, who was rubbing his arm, \"How many poems are there?\"","Wei Ping replied, \"To answer Your Excellency, this humble official has thirty-two poems here.\"","\"This humble official has fifty-nine poems,\" Feng Tang said, his hands still trembling slightly.","Wu Yong raised his hand. \"Your Excellency, this humble official has twenty-one poems here.\"","Yue Fuguang smacked her lips. As a literary copycat, putting everything else aside, her memory was quite decent. She had just recited over a hundred poems she had learned from childhood through college in one go!","No wonder her enhanced body felt tired, and her throat was a bit scratchy.","Thanks to Yue Fuguang's performance, Emperor Mingxi's birthday banquet this time was destined to go down in history, leaving plenty of material for future scholars and students to draw inspiration from.","The next day, the capital city saw a literal reenactment of paper becoming expensive due to high demand. And Yue Fuguang's poetic fame spreading throughout the capital was just the beginning.","Her name and poems were drifting toward the borders of the six nations along with Dayan's snowflake paper, stirring up the literary circles and scholars' hearts everywhere.","Despite her massive fame, Yue Fuguang continued to attend court and classes as usual. After all, she was already used to being famous.","Faced with these hundred or so poems that had appeared out of nowhere, regardless of what the top elites thought, the literary circles of the various nations truly exploded.","Although poetry was often dismissed by some scholars as a minor skill, they would say that while gathering to write poems and compose lyrics every single time. Without them, one would be embarrassed to even call it a literary gathering.","Therefore, when the literary circles of the six nations read Yue Fuguang's poems, there was both admiration and skepticism.","Whispers of plagiarism even began to faintly surface on the second day after the poems were revealed.","Regarding these doubts, Yue Fuguang wasn't as furious as the monarch and officials of Dayan, nor did she have the thought of silencing them.","She was indeed a literary copycat, but it was also true that these were original creations in this world.","So, they could doubt all they wanted. Yue Fuguang only asked two questions in response to the outside skepticism, which immediately shut them up.","\"Who did I copy from? Has anyone before me ever written these verses and lines? If so, step forward!\"","Since you say I copied, then find that person, or even find someone of an equal level!","Did the six nations have one?","Yue Fuguang really wanted to put her hands on her hips and laugh out loud. Sorry, but her ancestors were just too incredible; this world truly hadn't produced a figure like that.","Let alone a whole group of stunningly brilliant individuals with entirely different styles—bold and unrestrained, graceful and restrained, romantic or realistic. There was always one to suit your tastes!","[Host, what are you so smug about? It's not like you actually wrote them yourself!]","'These are the treasures left to us descendants by the ancestors of my hometown, can't I be a little proud! System, have you noticed? I flipped through the history books of the six nations and haven't found a single person like this.","Did something go wrong with the evolution of this world, which is why it couldn't birth...'","Before Yue Fuguang could finish her thought, she felt herself locked onto by some kind of aura, a heavy pressure bearing down on her head! It was the Heavenly Dao!!","Suppressing the palpitations in her heart, Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes and quickly glanced up at the sky. A gentle breeze, bright sun, blue sky, and white clouds—it was a beautiful day!","If the clouds in the sky hadn't arranged themselves neatly into a line of text, it would have been even better!","Yue Fuguang really wanted to curse a few times. Only at times like this did she profoundly realize the fact that she was merely a 'false god.'","This was different from people questioning her for plagiarism. She had never intended to claim the title of a talented female scholar in the first place, so she didn't care about that.","But she had clearly mastered supernatural powers with a mortal body, yet she still had to be subjected to the seemingly awakening Heavenly Dao consciousness of this world. It was super annoying!","In the Dayan Dynasty, Emperor Mingxi was above her, but if she wanted to, she could overthrow him at any time!","But this one currently 'above her head' was completely out of her reach!","With a thought, a ball of purple lightning appeared in Yue Fuguang's hand. The color of the lightning ball was now much deeper than it had been two years ago.","The system seemed to sense its host's thoughts and quickly spoke up to stop her, [Host, calm down! The consciousness of this world's Heavenly Dao is awakening.","Moreover, our arrival here has something to do with It!]","'So, It's actually the ultimate client boss!!'","[The system... doesn't know, but it definitely has something to do with It!]","'Did the three hundred years of internal strife cause It damage? Is that why we have our transmigration mission?'","Yue Fuguang rubbed her chin. In that case, they were a help to It rather than a hindrance, which meant the safety of their lives could be guaranteed."]},{"number":363,"title":"Chapter 363: News","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang cast another sidelong glance at the sky. The consciousness of the Heavenly Dao in this world must be incredibly weak, unable to even naturally birth a person of great talent and bold vision to set things right.","It actually needed an outsider like her to step in. As long as she didn't go overboard, It shouldn't have any objections, right?","[The System, being newly born, doesn't know either. Host, let's talk about the poetry for now.] The System changed the subject rather stiffly.","It couldn't exactly tell its host that there had been other taskers before her, but unfortunately, none of them had cleared the game.","Opening the channel time and time again had consumed the Heavenly Dao's energy...","Yue Fuguang figured it out without the System having to explain. Hearing it change the subject, she played along and asked, \"What's there to say about the poetry? Isn't it all resolved? The two thousand points for cultural development have already been credited to my account.\"","Shouldn't this matter be concluded by now?","Speaking of which, she really had to thank the five nations for their scheming. Otherwise, her efforts over the past two years—merely bringing out some books for printing and promotion—would have advanced the mission progress at a truly literal snail's pace.","If she hadn't later supported the establishment of numerous local schools, given the speed of cultural dissemination in this world, who knows how long it would have taken to break down the barriers and bring tangible benefits to the children of commoners.","But she never expected that her unintentional act of fighting for face this time would yield such exceptionally good results. Out of the twenty thousand points required for cultural promotion and dissemination, she had gained a tenth in just one go.","[Host, the poems you presented have caused too great of a stir across the various countries. According to what I've heard from the foreign relay stations...]","[...scholars from those nations have formed groups and are heading to Shangjing.] As for within the Great Yan Empire, those poems had been set to music by interested parties. Even illiterate commoners and young children could sing a few lines, showing just how widely and deeply they had spread.","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow. Forming groups to come to Shangjing? They couldn't be coming to challenge her, could they?","\"System, do they want to compete with me?\"","No wonder the delegations from the other countries hadn't started their return journeys even though more than half a month had passed since the Longevity Festival.","So they were waiting for their own countries' civilian cultural exchange groups to arrive, hoping to win back a round?","Do they even have any land left to gamble with?","[It seems they don't quite understand some of the poems and want to discuss them with you, the poet. Host, you used allusions in some of those poems that don't exist in this world, so, you know!]","Yue Fuguang massaged her temples. She still had plenty of material stored in her head, and even if she ran out, she had the System. However, wouldn't it be a bit beneath her, a divine maiden, to participate in poetry gatherings with mortals?","\"Among those scholars, are there any talents we can use?\"","[What, is the host planning to poach from the five nations?]","\"They'll all become people of Great Yan eventually anyway. It's just a matter of time.\"","[Those with integrity won't betray their countries, and as for those without integrity, would you even dare to use them if they offered their allegiance?]","Yue Fuguang paused. That was actually true!","While Yue Fuguang and the System were discussing the people of the five nations, those very people were also discussing her.","Bei Ye casually flipped through a stack of books on the table. \"Are you sure these were all brought out by Yue Fuguang?\"","A subordinate bowed and replied, \"To answer Your Highness, according to information secretly gathered by our people, these books are called science books.","\"They have only appeared in Great Yan over the past two years. The person who resold them to me said they are about something called 'basic science.'\"","\"In other words, there is more advanced science beyond this?\"","\"I do not know. These books are all printed under the supervision of the royal family. Our people have tried to sneak in several times but were discovered every time.\"","He lowered his head. Shangjing of Great Yan hid many secrets, and over the past two years, they had lost quite a few men trying to infiltrate these places.","Bei Ye tossed the book onto the table and picked up another stack. To be honest, he didn't quite understand these so-called basic science books, but his intuition told him that they contained profound knowledge.","Unfortunately, Great Yan controlled these books too strictly. His men had to spend a large sum of silver just to get their hands on them.","Of the few books on the table, most were enlightenment primers for children; only two were known as science books.","Seeing the Third Prince pick up a children's primer, the subordinate continued his introduction, \"Your Highness, these are the books used for the enlightenment of young children in schools.","\"Over the past two years, more than a thousand new schools have been established within Great Yan, and the books they use are the ones in Your Highness's hands.","\"It is said that they were all provided by that Junior Preceptor Yue.\"","Bei Ye had heard his spies mention this matter back in Northern Li. It was only now that he noticed the paper and printing of the books. Compared to Northern Li, the paper was smooth and even, the text was clear without any ink smudges, and even the binding was much better.","So this was the printing and papermaking technology of Great Yan!","From this, Beiyue became even more convinced that this technology must be inextricably linked to Yue Fuguang. Xie Si and Xie Jiu were likely smoke screens released by the Emperor.","Throughout all of Great Yan, only she was worthy of having princes take the blame for her.","While the Northern Li side was discussing the books, Southern Zhao and Southern Yue were talking about sugar production.","Gan Tang picked up a plate of snowflake sugar and asked in disbelief, \"Ye Jin, are you sure this snowflake sugar is made from this red vegetable?\"","Lan Xuan'er, sitting opposite her, also couldn't help but stare at the two items on the table.","One was snow-white, the other bright red. They would never have thought there was a connection between the two.","The woman in black martial attire named Ye Jin, standing below them, replied respectfully, \"To answer Your Highness the Princess, according to the information I've received, snowflake sugar is indeed made from sugar beets.","\"Sugar beets are only planted in the private fields of Junior Preceptor Yue and the Crown Prince of Great Yan. As for the production process, only the people of Junior Preceptor Yue and the Crown Prince know it.\"","Gan Tang nodded. Over the past two years, the sudden appearance of this snowflake sugar had dealt a massive blow to the cane sugar industries of their two nations.","Fortunately, the quantity was small and it only flowed to the nobles of various countries. Otherwise, their nations' revenues from sugar production would have been squeezed even further.","\"Have you found out why Yue Fuguang isn't expanding the cultivation?\"","Lan Xuan'er felt something was amiss. Logically, this plant should be as easy to grow as radishes.","Snowflake sugar was currently the finest sugar sought after by the nobles of the six nations, so they should be making a fortune.","Why only plant such a limited amount each year? According to normal reasoning, shouldn't they expand cultivation to earn more profit?","It couldn't be that Yue Fuguang and the Crown Prince simply disliked silver, could it?","\"I am incompetent. I have yet to find out the specific reason. Please forgive me, Princess,\" another attractive woman standing next to Ye Jin immediately knelt down to beg for forgiveness.","Lan Xuan'er glanced at Luyi, who was kneeling respectfully on the ground. She was originally someone Lan Xuan'er had planted by Prince Ming's side.","Who knew that Prince Ming would ultimately die at the hands of her own Empress Mother!","After Prince Ming's death, most of the people in his estate were dismissed. Luyi was getting older and had no opportunity to enter the imperial palace of Great Yan.","So, under Lan Xuan'er's instructions, she opened a wine shop. When it came to gathering information, aside from teahouses and restaurants, these small wine shops were the best places.","\"Rise!\" Lan Xuan'er understood that her current status was not what it used to be. The people she interacted with were all from the lower rungs of society. It wasn't hard to gather some gossip, but getting information on someone at Yue Fuguang's level was no easy task."]},{"number":364,"title":"Chapter 364: Suspicion","paragraphs":["\"Xuan'er, do you suspect there is some underlying reason we don't know about?\"","Lan Xuan'er nodded. \"Sister Tang, I can't help but feel that some of Dayan's decrees over the past two years have been rather strange. Especially regarding land, the Dayan court seems to be far too benevolent toward the commoners under its rule!\"","Benevolent toward the commoners? Gan Tang recalled the decrees regarding Dayan that her subordinates had gathered over the past two years.","Her royal brother had also summoned the court ministers to discuss this matter multiple times, but they had never been able to find the reason behind it.","If there was one distinct difference, it was that the Dayan emperor's prestige among the people was the highest among the monarchs of the six nations.","Even her royal brother, the most diligent ruler in the history of South Yue, whose goal was to be a wise and capable sovereign, could not compare.","\"You're right. Dayan has vigorously developed its agriculture over the past two years. Because of those three high-yield crop varieties, this is understandable. But the land taken from officials and the gentry is being sold to the commoners instead of the nobility, and the lords in the court actually agreed to it! That is simply too strange!\"","To travel a thousand miles to become an official is only for wealth. Refusing a fat piece of meat right at their lips inevitably makes one suspicious.","After all, because of Prince Ming, Lan Xuan'er had some understanding of Dayan's officialdom. Since when did those people possess such noble and unyielding character!","The officials of Dayan: Not only is His Majesty above us, but there is also the Junior Preceptor. Who would dare to object? What use is having money if you lose your life and can't spend it!","Didn't everyone see that those who objected were either dismissed from office or demoted?","Moreover, with natural disasters before them and man-made calamities behind them, facing the crisis of national subjugation, they knew all too well how to weigh their options!","\"Sister Tang, look. The effort and money Dayan has spent on water conservancy over the past two years are also vastly different from previous years.\"","Lan Xuan'er pointed to one of the pieces of information on the paper for Gan Tang to see.","Luyi chimed in at the right moment. \"Master, well-digging craftsmen often come to my wine shop to buy wine. According to them, there has indeed been a lot more work over the past two years.\"","Lan Xuan'er and Gan Tang exchanged a glance. They could understand managing the riverways, but this increase in the number of wells being dug...","\"Luyi, did those people mention where these wells are being dug?\"","\"In the cities, villages, and farmlands alike.\" Luyi thought for a moment and added, \"I heard that some villages started digging water cellars to store water since it began snowing last winter. Your subordinate doesn't know if it's true.\"","Digging water cellars to store water, and starting last year?","At this moment, the two women were truly bewildered by the abnormal actions of the Dayan people. Last year brought favorable weather, and it was said that Dayan had a great harvest, especially with those three crops, all yielding bountifully. This was also the reason why Yue Fuguang's popularity among the people surpassed even that of the emperor, and why her title as the Divine Maiden spread wider and wider.","The first half of this year had also been completely normal. Just before they set out as envoys to Dayan, the people of Dayan were anticipating another bumper harvest this autumn due to ample rainfall in the first half of the year.","Lan Xuan'er looked out the window at the completely darkened sky. The moon hung high, its radiance spilling in through the lattice window.","With an inexplicable expression, she said, \"Sister Tang, do you remember when it last rained?\"","Gan Tang was taken aback by her question. From the time the envoy mission entered Dayan until now, nearly two months had passed, and it seemed there had only been a single drizzle that stopped before the ground was even fully wet.","Gan Tang seemed to realize something. Her beautiful eyes widened, and she looked at Lan Xuan'er in disbelief. \"Xuan'er, are you saying... No, it can't be! It can't be!\"","She shook her head repeatedly. \"We know the skill level of Yun Tianxing from Dayan's Imperial Astronomy Bureau. With his abilities, it's impossible for him to predict the weather conditions more than a year in advance!\"","Lan Xuan'er's complexion was also poor, but for the sake of the two nations working together to accomplish their upcoming tasks, she ruthlessly shattered Gan Tang's illusions.","She pointed in the direction of the Yu Manor and said, \"Sister Tang, just because Yun Tianxing can't do it doesn't mean that person can't.\"","Gan Tang still found it somewhat hard to accept. \"Isn't Yue Fuguang just a facade deliberately set up by Emperor Mingxi to fool the world?\" To consolidate power, emperors would use whatever tactics worked best.","Therefore, everyone in South Yue unanimously believed that Yue Fuguang was merely Emperor Mingxi's front, and that the Dayan emperor was fabricating a deity for the sake of imperial power.","She stubbornly insisted, \"Xuan'er, you don't actually think that the so-called descent by divine decree and the title of Divine Maiden spread by the common folk are true, do you?\"","Like Bei Ye and the others, she had never believed it from beginning to end, even though that woman had summoned heavenly lightning to defeat people from their country three years ago.","She merely assumed it was some sort of martial arts world trickery. After all, this person came from a folk Taoist temple, so it wouldn't be surprising if she knew some exclusive illusions.","Back then, the allied assassination attempt on her by various nations was also done out of pride, attempting to crush Dayan's prestige.","If Yue Fuguang truly possessed real abilities as they were now suspecting, then their five nations were in grave danger!","At this moment, besides Gan Tang and Lan Xuan'er, someone else who felt this grave danger was Xi Yuanshan, who was located in a black market somewhere in the capital city of Shangjing.","He was currently radiating a terrifying aura, staring dangerously at the man before him who had his entire body hidden beneath a black cloak.","\"Are you certain this is the information you are selling me?\"","His voice was icy, as if laced with poison.","Two days ago, this person had approached him, claiming to have important information regarding him for sale.","The asking price right off the bat was a thousand taels of gold. Initially, Xi Yuanshan did not believe him, but today, this person had sent him another message.","He said he knew who had sabotaged his marriage, which was why Xi Yuanshan was here.","\"Guaranteed genuine. Besides, Your Highness only needs to send someone to investigate upon returning to know if it is true or false.\" The man, with most of his face concealed beneath a cloak, suddenly let out a sneer. \"After all, not everyone involved in this matter is dead!\"","Actually, upon hearing the first half of the man's words, he already believed him by thirty percent.","After that incident, Xi Yuanshan had mobilized his own forces to investigate thoroughly. The clues vaguely pointed toward a few of his brothers, so he had refrained from ordering a deeper probe.","It was not that he did not want to investigate, but for certain reasons, he could not.","However, whenever he recalled the events of that time, he always had a lingering feeling that even if his Princess Consort was not a direct participant, she definitely knew about it.","Because he could not be certain, he simply lavished his favor upon his concubines and minor wives, propping them up to rival the Princess Consort, thereby establishing a persona for himself as a man who could not forget his old love.","To think that Bei Xiang also had a hand in this! Previously, that man had always presented himself as a victim.","The two of them had even shared drinks and 'heart-to-heart' conversations, holding no resentment toward one another.","Looking at it now, he had truly underestimated this brother of his. Not only had Bei Xiang played him for a fool, but he had also played all the princes of Western Qiang.","He just wondered what kind of expressions those pretentious 'good brothers' of his would make once they learned the truth. He really wanted to see it right now!","A cruel smile curled upon Xi Yuanshan's face, hidden beneath his hood, before it vanished in a flash. In a mere instant, he reverted back to the gentle, 'love-struck' His Highness Prince Yi.","Yet, the name Bei Xiang was repeatedly chewed over on his lips.","In the end, Xi Yuanshan still paid a hefty sum to purchase this piece of information, and the very first person he shared it with was his 'good brother', Xi Ling.","Meanwhile, after shaking off the tail that Xi Yuanshan had sent to follow him, the cloaked man headed straight for East Street.","Yue Fuguang sat in the carriage bound for the royal hunting grounds. Peering out through the window lattice, she happened to see Xi Yuanshan and Xi Ling riding side by side just ahead. It was unknown what the two were discussing, but the atmosphere between them appeared quite pleasant."]},{"number":365,"title":"Chapter 365: Probing","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang felt her heart stir. It seemed Xi Yuanshan had further closed the distance with his cousin by sharing secrets.","Seeing Yue Fuguang looking at them, the two brothers immediately put on gentle smiles and said, The sky is clear and the air is fresh. It is too stuffy to sit in a carriage in such fine weather. Would the Junior Preceptor like to come out and ride a horse?","Xi Ling was not wrong. The day Yun Tianxing chose for this trip was indeed excellent. Except for the lack of rain in late autumn this year, everything else was quite good.","The wind and sunlight today were just like that, cool but not cold, bright but not harsh. Everything was perfectly balanced, so Yue Fuguang only hesitated for a moment before being tempted by his proposal.","She glanced at her attire. She had to admit that Cuizhu was far too foresighted.","Although this was not a riding habit, it did not hinder her from riding slowly.","Shen Chunying and the others saw Yue Fuguang's expression and waved backward without waiting for her orders.","By the time Yue Fuguang stood up and exited the carriage, she saw that Yu Huaixian was already waiting by the carriage, leading her pony.","To avoid causing a traffic jam, Yue Fuguang did not waste words. With a light tap of her foot, she leaped onto the horse.","Host, what a handsome move!","Being praised by the system like this, Yue Fuguang's face first turned red, then black.","For no other reason than Yue Fuguang could not bear the hardship of practicing martial arts, yet she wanted to fulfill her childhood dream of flying over eaves and walking on walls, killing a person every ten steps and leaving no trace behind for a thousand miles.","So, as she grew wealthier over the past two years, she still could not resist the system's temptation. Under its recommendation, she bought the peerless lightness skill that shared her name, Moon Shadow Floating Light.","In the system's words, how could Yue Fuguang not know the peerless divine skill Moon Shadow Floating Light!","System, tell me honestly, how much commission did you take from this movement technique? A lightness skill for mortals cost her eighteen thousand points. These points were almost enough to buy an entry-level mental cultivation method in the cultivation world.","The system remained silent, playing dead!","Seeing Yue Fuguang effortlessly mount the horse, the brothers Xi Ling and Xi Yuanshan exchanged a glance, both seeing shock and confusion in each other's eyes.","Over the past two years, they had constantly investigated Yue Fuguang, but they had never heard the slightest rumor about the Junior Preceptor of Great Yan practicing martial arts.","Looking at her skill, it was not something that could be mastered in two or three years. Their people had not even managed to find out this information. How many more secrets did she have that they did not know?","No wonder the assassinations and kidnappings targeted at her by various countries had never succeeded once; nobody could even touch the hem of her clothes.","Xi Ling put away the confusion on his face and praised, The Junior Preceptor has such excellent lightness skills. Even we, who are a few years older, cannot match it.","Yue Fuguang temporarily let the system off and replied modestly to Xi Ling, Your Highness flatters me!","Xi Yuanshan chimed in, My younger brother is not wrong. Let alone others, the two of us brothers are inferior to the Junior Preceptor in this skill!","Saying that, he laughed out loud. Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow, not knowing what the punchline of this sentence was.","Did she also need to force a couple of laughs to fit in?","What is Brother laughing at? Why not tell me and the others?","The Xi brothers still had smiles on their faces when Gan Tang and Lan Xuan'er, who were originally riding in carriages, also rode over on horseback.","Behind them followed the two brothers, Bei Ye and Bei Yue.","Seeing so many people gathering around, Yue Fuguang felt that it would be better for her to sit back in the carriage. After all, nothing good ever came from these people with ulterior motives gathering around her.","Before she could dismount, she heard Lan Xuan'er say, Prince Yue, Xuan'er wants to discuss a business deal with you. I wonder if that is possible?","Discuss business?","Their family's businesses were all managed by her older sisters, her mother, and her aunts, or else they were in cooperation with the Crown Prince.","She was only responsible for collecting the money and did not have to worry about a thing.","So if Lan Xuan'er wanted to discuss business, she should not have come to her!","Thinking this, Yue Fuguang said aloud, What business does the Princess want to discuss with me?","Glass, white liquor, soap, essential oils, white sugar, tea, and the cotton products from the factories... Counting them all, their family really had a lot of businesses.","A bright smile appeared on Lan Xuan'er's beautiful face. She said, Xuan'er, or rather the nobles of Nanzhao, all love your fine tea.","Unfortunately, the tea production from your tea garden is low, and we can never manage to grab the good stuff.","So, you want to buy some directly from me? This was an attempt to bypass the middlemen and go straight to her, the supplier.","Lan Xuan'er cast an admiring glance. Exactly.","She instantly changed into the demeanor of a young maiden. I wonder if you still have any more here.","She also knew that with Great Yan's climate, the current tea leaves had reached the season of withering. However, the tea trees on this Prince's tea mountain were an exception. Although it was just one hilltop tea garden, it produced tea year-round. Unfortunately, limited by the small amount of land, the production was rather low.","It was said that this was possible because there were hot springs on the mountain. Her people could not get close, so she did not know if the news was true or false. Thus, Lan Xuan'er's move was not only to actually buy tea but also to probe.","Yue Fuguang remained noncommittal to her remarks.","She looked up at the fluffy, cotton-like clouds in the sky, drifting leisurely across the blue porcelain plate of the heavens.","Looking again at the land and mountains connecting to the horizon, she, whose spiritual senses were becoming increasingly acute, could clearly feel the water molecules in the air decreasing day by day.","After this winter, her identity would not be able to be hidden even if she wanted to. Moreover, with her current growth, she no longer needed to deliberately hide anything.","So she turned her face to Lan Xuan'er and chuckled softly, Naturally, there is still some tea left.","Lan Xuan'er immediately put on a huge smile and said, Then Xuan'er is in for a treat!","Gan Tang smiled and teased, Then do not forget to share a portion with me, your older sister, once you get the good tea.","The others also gathered around immediately. Bei Yue said, Junior Preceptor, I heard that the scenery at your estate is considered the best in the capital. I wonder if I might have the honor of experiencing it.","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow. This Bei Yue was even more direct than Lan Xuan'er, who was only probing indirectly.","This guy was directly preparing to visit her home!","Yue Fuguang could have refused directly, but her eyes darted around, and she smiled modestly, Your Highness overpraises it. However, the flavor of the food at my estate is indeed slightly different from elsewhere. If Your Highness has time, you can come and have a taste.","Bei Yue was overjoyed and said, Then I will respectfully obey. When we return from the hunt, I will definitely bring generous gifts and pay a visit.","The Xi brothers exchanged a glance and joined in the fun, saying, Brother Bei Yue, you must call upon us brothers when the time comes.","Then they said to Yue Fuguang, Junior Preceptor, you would not mind two extra mouths from us brothers, would you?","Come, all of you come! She then said to Gan Tang and Lan Xuan'er, The two princesses as well. If you are not in a hurry to return to your countries, come gather at my estate.","Host, if you become familiar with them now, will you not feel unbearable sympathy when the time comes to attack their countries?","Unbearable sympathy? Do you think your host possesses such a thing?","Someone once said that the flower of civilization needs to be irrigated with blood; there is no progress without bloodshed. In her eyes, great unification was a kind of progress of the times."]},{"number":366,"title":"Chapter 366: The Bait","paragraphs":["Whose blood is shed makes no difference.","If the blood of the common people can be shed, why can't the blood of these privileged nobles and aristocrats be shed?","The system really wanted to say, \"You do!\"","Otherwise, why would she have pushed past all opposition to give high-yield seeds to the common people? However, thinking of the fate of those who obstructed and opposed this matter...","The system silently shut its mouth again.","The host, who at first verbally claimed that killing too many people from noble families would harm the harmony of heaven, had spent the last two years releasing exposes aimed at uprooting these noble families entirely, without showing the slightest bit of mercy.","In the end, Yue Fuguang still felt that dealing with these people was too exhausting. After getting some fresh air for a while, she returned to her luxurious carriage to sleep.","In her sleep, Yue Fuguang was awakened by voices growing louder and louder. Listening closely, she realized they were almost there.","She leaned against the carriage window and looked out through the lattice, seeing a giant stone three meters high standing by the road not far ahead.","Carved on the stone were several large golden characters: Western Mountain Royal Hunting Ground.","The convoy did not stop, crossing the boundary stone and continuing forward.","According to Xie Zhiyan, the royal hunting ground was divided into three tiers based on the mountain's terrain.","They should now be at the outermost ten-mile mark. Sure enough, the trees in sight slowly began to change. Past the stone monument, both sides of the road were natural barriers formed by tall red pines. Every set distance, a gilded tiger-head plaque was nailed to a tree, engraved with the words: Imperial Restricted Area, Trespassers Will Be Executed.","Walking forward for no more than five miles, they saw the artificially raised deer park and pheasant garden. Streams were channeled into winding waterways made of white jade. Beside the water stood twelve pairs of white marble auspicious beasts. Copper bells hung on the horns of the Xiezhi, ringing sparsely when the wind blew, startling the brightly feathered golden pheasants in the grass.","The core hunting ground was shaped like the Yin-Yang fish of Taiji. The east was Yang, where bright yellow tents were pitched on the flat and broad meadow, the golden dragons on the tent roofs shining brilliantly in the sunlight.","The west was Yin, preserving the primitive dense forest. Among the twisted branches of century-old cypresses hung thirty-six glazed storm lanterns, which would turn into stars in the forest at night.","At the boundary between Yin and Yang stood a nine-zhang high watchtower. The pillars were made of whole ironwood logs painted deep black, while the glazed tiles of the hunting observation pavilion at the top were as green as kingfisher feathers.","Yue Fuguang heard Xie Zhiyan say that it was the Peacock Blue ordered to be fired by the founding emperor when he was alive, and there was not much of it in the entire Great Yan Dynasty.","Because the founding emperor was a ruler on horseback who loved hunting during his lifetime, this royal hunting ground was built with exceptional care.","At the northern end of the hunting ground was a hunting presentation platform made of white stone. When everyone returned from hunting tomorrow, they would bring their prey here to display.","A three-arch stone bridge spanned the stream at the southern end, with the middle arch exclusively for the emperor's carriage.","Beneath it, a crisscrossing network of hidden channels led fresh water to every tent, with the channel openings covered by bluestone slabs carved with openwork cloud patterns.","Yue Fuguang thought to herself, this is the water source for all these people. If someone were to poison the water, wouldn't it be a disaster?","\"System, keep an eye out. Don't let anyone tamper with the water.\"","Although she had antidote pills, with so many people, she was a bit reluctant to save them all.","Then she could only take precautions at the source, in case someone really targeted it.","She had read plenty of novels in her past life. These kinds of events were always high-risk areas for accidents, with assassinations and poisonings being standard tropes, not to mention that the emperor's original purpose for this trip was impure.","Yue Fuguang followed the crowd out of the carriage and walked slowly into her tent, which was located to the left of the emperor's main tent.","Inside the large tent, a beautiful carpet was laid three feet from the entrance, and the faint, crisp scent of mountain morning dew greeted the nose.","The fragrance came from the incense burning in the lotus-patterned bronze censer on the eastern desk.","Yue Fuguang walked straight to the table, sat down, and asked He Jin, who had followed her in, \"Are all the people we brought settled in?\"","\"Rest assured, my lord. Half of our people are in the tent next to yours, and the other half are on guard at the perimeter.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded but couldn't help instructing, \"Send someone to keep a close eye on the water source to prevent poisoning.\"","The emperor definitely had arrangements, but that didn't stop her from adding another layer of insurance for her own points.","[Host, the emperor is risking so many people as bait this time. Do you think he can catch them all in one fell swoop?]","\"Can't you check whether they can be caught in one fell swoop?\"","The melon-eating system's data recovery seemed to have hit a bottleneck. Over the past year, the system had spent a lot of merit points, but unfortunately, it still couldn't see the whole picture or know the future. It was a bit useless compared to a real melon-eating system.","If she really forced the system to deduce, she wouldn't even dare to mention the direction of the events it calculated several times because it was too uncertain.","However, Yue Fuguang was also content. After all, the task completion rate was currently going according to plan. If the system was lacking, then so be it. It wasn't like they could unbind anyway.","[I can only see those people deploying their forces right now. Some little mice have already sneaked into the hunting ground. As for the later development of the situation, would you believe me if I told you?]","The system was also helpless. Its melon-eating system was clearly suppressed by an unknown energy and hadn't made any progress for over a year.","It couldn't help but suspect whether its secret restoration of the melon-eating system's data had been discovered by the main system.","\"It doesn't matter. For the final strike, I believe the emperor and Huo Ying will be fully prepared.\"","Emperor Mingxi and Huo Ying, who were mentioned by Yue Fuguang, were currently gathered inside the emperor's dragon tent, discussing this very matter.","\"My beloved subject Huo, are you certain those people have come out in full force?\"","Emperor Mingxi sat upright behind the yellow rosewood imperial desk, upon which the map of the hunting ground was spread.","Huo Ying bowed and said, \"To reply to Your Majesty, according to the scouts' reports, a force of a thousand men has scattered in all directions and is heading toward the hunting ground. I expect they should reach the perimeter of the hunting ground tonight.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded. \"Make sure to capture them all, and remember to leave them alive.\"","Otherwise, how could they force them to implicate their mastermind?","\"Rest assured, Your Majesty. We will certainly not let them disturb the elegant mood of Your Majesty and the Junior Preceptor.\"","At the beginning of the hour of Chen the next day, the morning mist in the mountains and forests gradually dispersed, and the hunting ground revealed its most vibrant scene.","Birds flew out from the woods, lowering their heads to sip the flowing spring water, while golden pheasants paced among the Xiezhi statues hung with copper bells.","The flash of a spear tip from an Imperial Guard on duty at the watchtower startled the jackdaws resting in the cypress forest.","The flock of crows swept past the rusted arrowheads on the hunting presentation platform, circled over the stone bridge, and just as they were about to disappear into the depths of the dense forest, two figures suddenly flew out from an angle.","Like two streaks of light and dark gray ink across the sky, they accurately grabbed two lagging jackdaws before they could vanish.","Yue Fuguang, who had come out for a walk, frowned. She decisively stretched out a hand toward the two figures rushing at her, making a stopping gesture.","\"Stop! Dirty!\"","Taxue and Wuhen, who were still clutching the jackdaws under their sharp claws, saw their master's disgusted expression. They tilted their heads, their eyes darting around wildly.","They were clearly thinking!","They looked at each other and then at their own feet. First, Taxue tentatively used its wing to push the jackdaw at its feet a little further away.","While pushing, it didn't forget to observe Yue Fuguang's expression.","Seeing that Yue Fuguang was still frowning, it turned its head and chirped twice at Wuhen, and Wuhen copied it, pushing its prey further away.","Chirp chirp!"]},{"number":367,"title":"Chapter 367: Song Tu, Buddha Tu","paragraphs":["Taxue hopped over to Yue Fuguang's side. Yue Fuguang shook her head, \"Where have you two been running wild these past two days? Your perfectly white feathers have changed color. Go find a place to wash up quickly, otherwise you are not allowed in my tent.\"","The two large birds tilted their heads. After thinking for a moment, they seemingly understood and flew off one after the other toward the water source to the south.","Yue Fuguang shouted after them, \"Taxue, don't pollute the water source!\"","Just as she finished shouting, she turned sideways and saw Xi Ling, who was staring wide-eyed at the departing Taxue and Wuhen, unable to hide his expression in time.","He pointed in Taxue's direction and asked uncertainly, \"Junior Preceptor Yue, was that... was that Lingxiao?\"","Three years ago, when he first came to Great Yan as an envoy, he had gifted Emperor Mingxi a falcon named Lingxiao.","That creature was wild and untamable; even the best falconer in Western Qiang had spent a year without fully taming it.","But the little creature just now, which looked exactly like Lingxiao, seemed a bit too smart and obedient.","When had the overlord of the skies ever been so docile?","Yue Fuguang had spoken such a long sentence, and they actually seemed to understand it.","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"It is indeed the one you presented back then, but it is now called Taxue. If you call it Lingxiao, it won't pay any attention to you.\"","Taxue was a smart and arrogant bird. Aside from acting like a sycophant in front of its meal ticket, Yue Fuguang, it completely ignored everyone else.","Bei Ye and the others standing in the distance also witnessed this scene. Gan Tang and the rest might not understand, but the people of Northern Li, who also loved raising such birds of prey, knew exactly why Xi Ling was so astonished.","Bei Ye couldn't help but narrow his eyes, silently observing Yue Fuguang. The more he looked, the more he felt there were many incongruities about her.","Xi Ling slowly recovered from his shock and couldn't help but offer genuine praise, \"Junior Preceptor Yue, what impressive methods!\"","[Master, guess who I saw?]","'I can't guess, tell me yourself.'","Chirp, chirp!","Having finished their baths, Taxue and Wuhen flew back.","With one bird on each side, they rubbed their heads against Yue Fuguang's legs. Yue Fuguang glanced down and gently scolded, \"Taxue, Wuhen, you're using my legs as a towel!\"","Screech!","Screech!","Seeing people gathering around, and realizing they were strangers, Taxue loudly screeched at the newcomers!","It spread its wings with a flutter, looking like it was ready for a fight.","\"Taxue, quiet!\"","Taxue, who had wanted to screech again, instantly sounded like it had been choked, letting out a soft chirp!","Feeling wronged, it went back to rubbing its head against Yue Fuguang's leg.","The crowd gathered in a circle, their faces full of disillusionment as they watched the two overlords of the sky shamelessly acting cute and throwing tantrums at Yue Fuguang.","[Master, look at the dark-faced guard behind Bei Ye, the one with a black mole just below his eyebrow. His name is Song Tu, the younger brother of Song Yu.]","Using the pretext of greeting the others, Yue Fuguang quickly scanned the guards behind Bei Ye. One of them indeed had a darker complexion and a mung-bean-sized black mole near his eyebrow. His eyes carried a wild glint. In his twenties, he didn't look much like the Song Yu she had seen.","'Why, is this person special?'","[Master, you might not know the name Song Tu, but in the future, he will have another name: Fotu!]","Fotu!","Hearing this name, the Yu father and son, who were walking toward Yue Fuguang with smiles on their faces, suddenly stopped in their tracks.","Behind them, Yu Chongshan's sharp eyes swept over Bei Ye and his three guards. Even though the group had their backs to them, preventing him from seeing the guards' faces.","Yu Chongshan quickly locked onto which one was Fotu, based on the skin color mentioned by the Divine Artifact.","Yu Zhongchun's face darkened, his knuckles cracking as he clenched his fists. The anger in his heart was like a runaway wild horse, clamoring and roaring, threatening to burst out. His three sons had been... had been destroyed by this very thief.","Yu Zhongchun's vision blurred slightly from the surge of anger, but his eyes never left the not-so-tall figure ahead.","No wonder their merchant caravans had traveled back and forth to Northern Li multiple times over the years, expending immense manpower and wealth to investigate, yet never finding the man known as Fotu.","It turned out he was still called Song Tu right now!","And he was a guard by Bei Ye's side!","The Yu father and son narrowed their eyes, concealing the fierce murderous intent in their hearts.","Song Tu seemed to sense something. He couldn't help but turn to look behind him, but he failed to discover the source of the gaze that had made his hairs stand on end.","Not far away were the Yu family members, and further out were the various officials of Great Yan and the envoy delegations.","'So it's him. Since he's here, there's no need for him to leave. The green mountains and clear waters here make it a fine place to bury some bones!'","Yue Fuguang had no intention of sparing someone's life just because they hadn't committed a crime yet and supposedly didn't deserve death.","The minor interlude caused by Taxue and Wuhen in the morning quickly passed. After breakfast, the main event began.","In front of the northern hunting tribute platform, a high stage had been temporarily constructed from massive logs. The Nine-Dragon Golden Tent gleamed dazzlingly under the autumn sun.","Like a lighthouse in the sea, no matter how far away one was, they could see that the Emperor of Great Yan was right there.","Yue Fuguang's eyes flickered. In order to catch all those people in one fell swoop and clear the obstacles for future actions, Emperor Mingxi was being quite ruthless to himself this time.","She looked at the Crown Prince beside her. He was currently wearing a dark blue martial outfit. She couldn't help but curl her lips; this guy wasn't completely stupid, choosing not to wear a flashy yellow.","Otherwise, in the forest, he would be a walking target.","Below them, on both sides of the crimson steps, civil and military officials were lined up like a flock of geese. The civil officials stood with heads bowed in solemnity, while the military officers were clad in imposing armor.","A group of princes, princesses, and members of the envoy delegations stood in the center of the field, all full of vigor.","Yue Fuguang saw that the Seventh Prince and Eighth Princess in the ranks had flushed faces from excitement, their bright, sparkling eyes looking toward her.","Suddenly, nine chimes of a bell echoed from the high platform. Drum music began, and seventy-two Imperial Guards holding dragon flags high filed in through the camp gates. The sound of their iron boots striking the ground made the yellow earth tremble slightly.","The flag-bearing officer galloped past the viewing platform, his scarlet cape pulling into a straight line in the sprint, his voice ringing like a great bell, \"The Emperor arrives!\"","The beaded curtains of the Nine-Dragon Golden Tent were gently rolled up. The light golden dragon motifs on Emperor Mingxi's dark hunting suit radiated brilliantly the moment the curtain was lifted.","The civil and military officials, along with the foreign envoys, bowed in greeting simultaneously.","The Emperor steadily ascended the high platform. As he raised his hand, the flag-bearing officer waved the command flag. Sixteen cowhide drums surrounding the hunting ground thundered, startling a flock of birds in the distant forest.","\"Let the hunt begin!\"","Just as Qian Gui's slightly shrill voice fell, the fences leading to the hunting ground were opened by several guards, and over a hundred imperial guards rushed into the hunting ground first.","Yue Fuguang gazed at the vast hunting ground. Sprinkling this small number of people into it was like a drop of water in the ocean; it wouldn't make any waves at all.","In the ranks of civil officials, some stroked their long beards while looking toward where the dust was rising, while the military officers subconsciously adjusted their quivers and waist sabers.","Emperor Mingxi stood up and slowly walked to the edge of the high platform. He took the exquisite, dragon-carved large bow handed to him by Eunuch Qian.","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow, not having expected the Emperor to still be able to draw such a massive bow.","Her expression was coincidentally seen by Xie Zhiyan standing beside her. He tried hard to hold back his laughter, doing his best to brainwash himself into not thinking too deeply about what the Junior Preceptor's raised eyebrow implied.","His imperial father might be old, but because he hadn't consumed those elixir pills or played with the 'luminous pearls' yet, he wasn't completely useless just yet!"]},{"number":368,"title":"Chapter 368: Why Kill the Father","paragraphs":["Thinking of the luminous pearl, Xie Zhiyan's eyes flickered, and he looked toward Bei Yue in the crowd.","Emperor Mingxi still did not know about the inward criticism his good eldest son and Yue Fuguang had towards him. He was only heard speaking in a loud, clear voice, \"Today, the hunting ground before you lords borders Qixia Ridge to the east, Yinma River to the west, has the pines and cypresses planted by the late emperor to the south, and buries the bones of heroes who died in battle during the founding of the nation to the north.\"","He paused, and the wind carried the trailing notes of his voice into everyone's ears. \"Every cry of a deer here once accompanied the hooves of the founding emperor's steed, and every piece of land was once covered by the bloodstains of our soldiers. It is...\"","\"Therefore, today's hunt,\" Emperor Mingxi suddenly raised his hand, splashing his wine into the vast sky, blossoming into a fleeting rainbow under the sunlight, \"is not for amusement, but to comfort the spirits! It is not for killing, but for martial exercise!\"","Yue Fuguang thought to herself: If the boss wants to make a speech, fine, but there is no need to be so melodramatic.","She lowered her eyes and swept her gaze over the Hanlin Academy scholars among the civil officials below the stage. Who wrote this speech for the boss? Drag them out!","Emperor Mingxi lightly pulled the bowstring, the beef tendon string trembling slightly at his fingertips. \"Civil officials drawing the bow, and military generals chasing the deer, all must remember the common people of the court.\"","He shot an arrow at a distant target, hitting it dead center in the bullseye.","Yue Fuguang fought the urge to clap wildly. She secretly thought that even after being in Dayan for so many years, this habit from her past life still could not be changed.","\"Long live His Majesty's might!\"","\"Long live His Majesty's might!\"","The officials shouted in unison. The drums sounded again, heavier than before, each beat striking against everyone's pulse.","Emperor Mingxi nocked another arrow and drew his bow, but he did not aim at any target. Drawing the bowstring full like a round moon, he shot high into the sky, \"This arrow, to honor the rivers and mountains!\"","All the officials and envoys raised their heads, watching the white-fletched arrow disappear into the firmament, startling the birds in the sky into flight.","Yue Fuguang raised her eyes. Among the startled birds, it seemed her own two birds were there as well!","Why were those two idiots everywhere?!","Just as Yue Fuguang was wondering if she should call those two back so they would not be accidentally killed later, she heard Emperor Mingxi finally conclude his speech, announcing, \"The hunt begins, gentlemen, you may go!\"","As his voice fell, the people in the field cupped their hands in salute to Emperor Mingxi on the high platform, then rushed toward their mounts that were already waiting at the entrance of the hunting ground.","The neighing of horses suddenly rose. Yue Fuguang thought to herself, today's performance has finally begun.","At this time, more than half of the civil officials and military generals in the field had successively followed behind the Crown Prince. Although the civil officials were relatively weaker compared to the military generals, many of them knew some martial arts and were also capable of archery and horseback riding.","For example, her second uncle, Wei Ping, and Feng Tang were all skilled hands.","Emperor Mingxi noticed at a glance that although Yue Fuguang was dressed in casual attire today, she was still sitting on a low chair with no intention of getting up. He could not help but ask, \"Is Fuguang not going down to play with the Crown Prince?\"","Yue Fuguang waved her hand. \"No rush, I will go play in a little while.\"","Following right behind those people now, all the small animals would be scared away by them, and she would not catch anything good if she went over.","[Master, look at the table below where the prizes are placed. Is not one of them a luminous pearl?]","Following the system's prompt, Yue Fuguang looked over. On the table were bows, arrows, swords, and spears, as well as a jade ruyi and a glass goblet. The luminous pearl the system mentioned was held in a red sandalwood box next to the glass goblet, sparkling brilliantly. Its radiance matched the colorful gleam of the glazed goblet.","\"It really is a luminous pearl. Did we not have the Crown Prince tell the Emperor that the luminous pearl is poisonous? Why is it being used as a prize today?\"","Is this aimed at the people in the diplomatic mission?","I just do not know if the Emperor wants to return the item to its original owner or give it to someone else.","Emperor Mingxi's eyes flickered, and the hand holding his wine cup unconsciously tightened. The anger and lingering fear in his heart were once again stirred up by memories.","A year and a half ago, he had seen with his own eyes how miserably Qian Bao, who held the luminous pearl day and night, died.","Crying out in pain endlessly every day, looking emaciated, even the imperial physician Sun Huajing was completely helpless against his symptoms.","It was a disease they had never heard of, until the spies he sent to Beili finally managed to infiltrate the Beili Imperial Medical Bureau.","Among the partial medical records of the Beili royal family and various high officials secretly sent back, there were several people who died of illness with symptoms fifty percent identical to Qian Bao's.","When he learned of this news, Emperor Mingxi nearly crushed the wine cup in his hand. To this day, he still could not be certain whether that old geezer Bei Ji knew this thing was poisonous!","\"Little Zhu, do the people of Beili know this thing is poisonous?\"","Hearing these words, Emperor Mingxi almost shed tears. At this moment, Yue Fuguang was truly his greatest mouthpiece!","[Master, within the Beili royal family, currently only Bei Yue has noticed that there is something wrong with the luminous pearl, that it is not a precious gem but a poisonous one.","Therefore, as early as three years ago, he began secretly investigating all the Beili royals and high officials who possessed luminous pearls.","Unfortunately, he did not know that there are two types of luminous pearls: one toxic and one non-toxic.","The luminous pearl he personally and carefully selected to give to Bei Ji happened to be non-toxic, while the two that Bei Ji casually gave to Emperor Mingxi were both toxic.]","Emperor Mingxi thought: Just say I am unlucky then, I almost died at the hands of that old bastard Bei Ji!","No, in the original historical timeline, he got sick because of this, which allowed Madame Zhou to take advantage of the situation!","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow, \"Little Zhu, are you saying that Bei Yue actually wanted to give his own father a poisonous pearl?\"","It was not strange for royal offspring to want to commit patricide; what was strange was Bei Yue committing patricide.","Ever since the news spread further and wider that he was exclusively devoted to male lovers, he seemed to have become the most hopeless among his brothers to inherit the throne.","According to the information collected by the Secret Spy Bureau from Beili, Bei Yue's power had drastically shrunk over the past two years, and the courtiers who had originally defected to his camp successively switched their allegiances.","His current status in Beili was not even as good as Bei Ye, who also favored male lovers. After all, that guy swung both ways and could still produce offspring.","[Yes, it is the royal family, after all. Patricide is nothing new.]","Emperor Mingxi, who had almost committed patricide: He knew it, he was not the only one who wanted to do such a thing!","\"I am just curious why he is the one committing patricide. If the emperor dies and a brother takes the throne, it seems like the disadvantages would outweigh the advantages for him.\"","In traditional concepts, one's own father holding power and one's own brother holding power were still different.","[Why patricide? It is simply because Bei Ji discovered early on that this son was ruined, so he deliberately used his favoritism to set him up as a target for all the brothers.","Master, guess why Beili has not established a Crown Prince yet?]","Why have they not established a Crown Prince? Is it not because he does not have a favored successor in mind yet?","Among the six nations, only Nanzhao and Beili have yet to establish a Crown Prince. Of course, even for those that have, aside from Dayan which is relatively stable, the struggles for the throne in the other nations are no less fierce.","In the eyes of the emperor's other sons, as long as the emperor was not dead and the Crown Prince had not inherited the great throne, they all still had a chance!","Nanzhao had not established one because the Empress had not yet decided whether to pass the throne to a son or a daughter. As for Beili not establishing one, \"Is it not because the Empress of the central palace has no children?\"","Establishing a Crown Prince is nothing more than appointing the legitimate son if there is one, and appointing the eldest if there is not. Who was the eldest prince of Beili again... Oh, it seems his name is Bei Feng. His mother is just an ordinary concubine who is not favored by Bei Ji; she was only able to rise to the rank of concubine because she gave birth to the eldest prince."]},{"number":369,"title":"Chapter 369: The Melon of Northern Season","paragraphs":["\"Do you know why the central palace has no heirs? In fact, Empress Du Zijun of North Li once carried a child—a fully formed male fetus.","Unfortunately, she suffered a miscarriage when she was eight months pregnant. The child was lost, and her body was so damaged that she could never bear another child.\"","\"Was the miscarriage her own fault, or was she harmed by someone?\"","\"Back then, North Ji used avenging the empress as an excuse to punish the favored concubine, Concubine Li, who was also the empress’s cousin.","In truth, that naive and sweet-natured Concubine Li was deceived by the emperor. The real mastermind behind the empress’s miscarriage was North Ji himself.\"","\"Are you saying North Ji personally killed his own son? Was it because he had so many sons that one more or less didn’t matter?","Or was it because the empress’s family was too powerful, and he feared the Du clan might pull a 'remove the father, keep the son'?\"","Yue Fuguang, having come to this world, truly understood the immense power of great noble families. For someone like Emperor Mingxi, eradicating the scourge of such families required even placing himself on the chopping block.","\"The child in the empress’s womb was North Ji’s second son. So although North Yue was the third prince, he only had one elder brother—the eldest prince, North Feng.","Even though that son died in the womb, the emperor and empress still assigned him a place in the birth order.\"","\"So, because the Du family was too powerful, it aroused North Ji’s wariness.\"","\"North Ji’s smooth succession to the throne relied heavily on the empress’s maternal family. He couldn’t openly move against the overbearing Du clan.","He could only personally sever the extension of their influence—his own son.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded. The power of the Du family was something even he, as the emperor of Da Yan, understood clearly. If he were North Ji, for his own safety, he would have made the same choice.","As long as he lived, he could have more sons, but he only had one life.","Emperor Mingxi glanced at Yue Fuguang, who was sipping tea and enjoying the gossip below. Fortunately, for Da Yan, with this ancestor around, his life was no longer limited to just one.","\"Does the empress know it was the emperor who did it?\"","Yue Fuguang’s eyes sparkled. The Du family being powerful was a good thing—strength would allow them to clash with the emperor, creating internal strife.","Breaching the fortress from within was the most convenient approach!","Emperor Mingxi clearly had the same thought. Using the cover of drinking tea, he shot a glance at Shen Kang, who stood on guard behind him.","Shen Kang silently cupped his hands and quickly left to find Zheng Zicheng, the deputy director of the Secret Intelligence Bureau, who was on perimeter duty.","\"Of course she doesn’t know. If the empress found out, both the court and the harem in Da Yan would be thrown into chaos. That Empress Du is nothing like our Empress Xu.","She’s a formidable woman who holds real power.","To avenge her child, back then, even though Concubine Li was her cousin, she showed no mercy to her or her family.","Even now, without a son of her own, relying on her maternal family’s influence, she has completely controlled North Li’s harem. There are also officials in the court who are her people.","Even when North Li’s Dowager Empress was alive, the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law were evenly matched in their struggles.","So, North Li has yet to appoint a crown prince—not only because there’s no legitimate son from the empress, but also because the emperor and empress disagree on the successor.\"","\"What does this have to do with North Yue committing patricide?\"","\"Because North Ji initially hinted that he wanted to make North Yue the crown prince. The empress and those behind North Feng strongly opposed it, so the emperor gave up the idea.\"","\"So, North Yue harbored resentment because the emperor’s stance wasn’t firm?\"","Anyone with half a brain would find it absolutely impossible. A living emperor versus a dead former emperor—who would be more advantageous to Northern Yue? He wouldn’t be unaware of that.","[Master, because Northern Yue gradually discovered that the emperor not only wasn’t genuinely intent on making him crown prince, but was deliberately propping him up as a target.","Though Northern Yue’s mother’s family wasn’t as powerful as the Du clan, they held military power and could still contend with the Du family, who controlled the civil official faction.]","“So the emperor has a preferred candidate, pushing Northern Yue forward to draw fire for his favored son? That son must either lack personal ability or have weak backing!” He can’t defeat the Du family, nor can he outfight the other sons.","Yue Fuguang clicked her tongue. Truly, an emperor who could personally orchestrate the death of his own crown prince—all his sons were merely chess pieces in his hands.","[Thus, Northern Yue wants to commit patricide. While Northern Ji still shows him some “favor,” he aims to turn false into reality.","Currently, the emperor has explicitly named only Northern Yue as his intended heir. So if Northern Ji dies, the forces behind Northern Yue will definitely push him onto the throne.]","As for his preference for male companions and lack of offspring, those are trivial matters. The imperial family has plenty of brothers; if he can’t have children, he can just adopt one.","“Then why don’t we help him out? Later, let’s find a way to send the Night Orb into Northern Ye’s hands.”","Emperor Mingxi gave a glance to Zhang Zhongping, the Vice Minister of Rites, who immediately understood.","Yue Fuguang and the system naturally caught their interaction, concealing their achievements and reputation.","“Little Zhu, you still haven’t told me which son Northern Ji truly intends to inherit the throne.”","The Northern Li empire has even more princes than the Great Yan—thirteen alive, seven of them adults, making them the main contenders for the throne.","[Master, this story is quite a big scoop. Sit tight, and I’ll tell you slowly.]","Hearing there was gossip to be had, those who had planned to go relieve themselves silently withdrew their extended legs. Gossip cures all ailments; their urgent bladders could wait a little longer.","“Hurry up and tell me!”","Yue Fuguang sounded delighted. This joy wasn’t just about the gossip—it was because the system could unlock secrets about Northern Ji, proving it had grown a bit stronger.","[Master, to talk about Northern Ji, we have to start from his youth. Back then, Northern Ji and Chancellor Wei were known as the Two Pearls of the Liang Capital.","This reputation wasn’t earned through talent or strategy, but simply because they were both handsome and came from noble families.","Young at the time, Northern Ji sought Chancellor Wei’s friendship due to the Wei family’s influence, and they eventually became close friends.","It was with the help of the Wei and Du families, among other powerful clans, that Northern Ji smoothly ascended the throne.","But what the world didn’t know was that, through Chancellor Wei’s repeated assistance and long-term support from the Wei family, Northern Ji developed improper feelings for him, his heart entirely captured.","He often concocted excuses to discuss state affairs with Chancellor Wei, inviting him to stay overnight at the palace, and they even shared a bed, which was once celebrated as a tale of camaraderie in Northern Li.","Later, Northern Ji found that occasional shared slumber couldn’t ease his longing, so he grew bolder.","He repeatedly invited Chancellor Wei to bathe together. Gradually, in private, the emperor’s gaze turned increasingly predatory—nothing like the look of a monarch toward a trusted minister.","Even Chancellor Wei, however dense, could tell the emperor had improper designs on him.]","It's a pity that Chancellor Wei has always been ambitious and naturally wouldn't be willing to give up his bright future just to be reduced to the emperor's male favorite.","Clatter, the melon in Emperor Mingxi's hand fell to the ground without him even realizing it. His sharp eyes stared blankly at the melon stains on his hands as he secretly savored the thought—one must say, gossiping about one's own peers hits differently.","This kind of gossip was truly sweet and flavorful!","The last time gossip this juicy came from Xi Yan's untold story between two women back in the day."]},{"number":370,"title":"Chapter 370: Encountering Body Doubles Literature Again","paragraphs":["Since we have already eaten the gossip of Western Yan and Bei Ji, is there hope of also eating the gossip of Gan Chengjiang of Southern Yue and Lan Qiying of Nanzhao?","They are all emperors, everyone's turn will come eventually... Clatter!","Thinking of this, the melon Emperor Mingxi had just picked up fell to the ground again. They were all emperors... Since they could eat their gossip, could they also eat his?!","He would not naively think these two ancestors would let him off the hook just because of the affection from spending a lot of time together!","Although quite a few of his own affairs had been exposed one after another, if those things from his youth were exposed... Emperor Mingxi wanted to cover his face. He... he still needed his dignity! Begging to be spared JPG.","The crowd silently ate their melons, not forgetting to secretly observe the emperor's expression. The officials saw that His Majesty, who originally looked like he had just eaten a huge piece of gossip and was secretly excited, now had a constantly changing expression. Not knowing what he had thought of, his face turned red and then white. Wang Shouchen and a few others exchanged a knowing look.","Amidst their exchanging of glances, there was only one meaning: why did His Majesty's face, which had just been enjoying sweet gossip, collapse so quickly? Could this story also involve their Majesty?","It could not be!","They were all veteran officials who had followed His Majesty for over a decade; they were quite clear on whether their Majesty liked men or not.","Qian Gui, standing behind Emperor Mingxi, had followed him since his youth. Having served Xie Fei for over twenty years, he could be said to be the person present who understood Emperor Mingxi the best.","Taking one look at the emperor's face, and accidentally recalling the past, what else was there to not understand?","He carefully brought a basin of clean water for Emperor Mingxi to wash his hands.","Yue Fuguang watched Emperor Mingxi and his servant muttering to each other, but she did not care and continued to eat melons with the system. Little Zhu, I remember you mentioned before that when Chancellor Wei was young, he had an intimate encounter with a dancer during a palace banquet.","Afterwards, he repeatedly asked Bei Ji for her, but the emperor refused. It turns out it was not because he was reluctant to part with a dancer, he was jealous!","She knew it! How could an emperor be so stingy? It was not as if he was asking for one of his concubines. It was just a dancer, and his favored minister wanted her. How could he not give her, and even refuse multiple times? So this was where the gossip was.","Hehehe, Master, you might not know this, but that time Chancellor Wei acted uncharacteristically lustful and ended up with that dancer in the palace. If you really get down to it, it was not a huge mistake, but Bei Ji was incredibly angry because of it.","Actually, Chancellor Wei was not truly so lustful that he could not wait to leave the palace. Acting so shamelessly inside the palace was entirely because Chancellor Wei had been drugged at the time!","This time, not only Emperor Mingxi, but even Yue Fuguang and the officials below all gasped in unison.","They were all shrewd people and instantly thought of the crucial point.","Soon their guess was confirmed. Yue Fuguang once again became everyone's mouthpiece. Her voice carried the amusement of eating a huge melon. Did Bei Ji send someone to do it! Does Chancellor Wei know about this? One affirmative sentence, one interrogative sentence.","Master guessed right. It was exactly because Bei Ji saw that Chancellor Wei kept rejecting him, so he wanted to use the palace banquet to resort to this underhanded tactic, intending to force himself on him and make it a done deal.","Unfortunately, he was afraid Chancellor Wei would make a fool of himself on the spot and did not dare to use too large a dose, so Chancellor Wei managed to hold on until the drug took effect on his way to change clothes. The person the emperor waited for but could not find was accidentally encountered by that dancer.","Afterwards, the emperor was naturally furious at the dancer who picked up his leftovers. Seeing Chancellor Wei repeatedly ask for the person, he naturally became even more jealous and resolutely refused to let her go.","At that time, Chancellor Wei also faintly realized that the drug he was given was probably administered by the emperor, but he did not dare send anyone to investigate. No matter the result, it was not something he wanted to see.","Moreover, at that time, the emperor was like a sexually frustrated, raging lion. Besides official duties, Chancellor Wei hid from the emperor everywhere. Sleeping foot-to-foot or whatever, he pushed away whenever he could. Sometimes he even lingered among the flowers to make Bei Ji understand that he truly only liked women.","These actions made Bei Ji extremely dissatisfied and jealous. It was also at this time that a minor official's daughter who looked four or five parts like Chancellor Wei appeared among Bei Ji's harem concubines. She was named Concubine Qing after her first time serving in bed.","For a very long time, Concubine Qing received Bei Ji's exclusive favor, and after she gave birth to the Eighth Prince, she was promoted to Consort Qing.","Oh right, Master, Chancellor Wei's name is Wei Yuqing, and Bei Ji privately calls him Ah Qing.","Good heavens, he was playing the substitute trope here!","You have said so much, are you trying to say that the son Bei Ji most wants to pass the throne to is Consort Qing's son, the Eighth Prince?","Master is so smart, you guessed it right away! The system flatteringly put a high hat on Yue Fuguang before continuing to gossip.","This Consort Qing is a smart one. She is very good at figuring out the emperor's intentions and was willing to be a substitute.","Relying on her superb makeup skills, she managed to turn her four or five parts resemblance to Chancellor Wei into a seven or eight parts resemblance through deliberate imitation.","If it were not for the fact that she was plotted against during her second pregnancy, resulting in a miscarriage that damaged her body so she could no longer give birth, Bei Ji would have more children under his knee than he does now.","It was also that incident that made Bei Ji alert, intentionally slowly giving her the cold shoulder. Consort Qing fell out of favor, and as the years passed, the mother and son gradually became marginalized figures in the Northern Li imperial palace.","It made everyone forget how favored Consort Qing and her son were over a decade ago. At that time, since the Empress had no children, the Eighth Prince was a strong candidate for Crown Prince.","So Bei Ji set up Beiyue as a target to draw fire away from his eighth son, while he secretly did as he pleased.","Bei Ji truly has good methods! This Consort Qing is also quite capable, knowing how to imitate the emperor's white moonlight to gain favor.","Someone who has been a favored consort must have many enemies. To still be able to live peacefully in the harem, the emperor's little schemes to plan for their mother and son actually have not been discovered by anyone.","As a fellow emperor, Emperor Mingxi felt he had the most right to speak on this matter. Back when he favored Lady Zhou and her son, he also planned for them in every way, wishing he could present the best things right in front of them.","Although he had not thought about changing the crown prince at that time, he also thought about making Old Ninth a Prince of the First Rank in the future, carving out a good fiefdom for him so he could be wealthy and honored for a lifetime.","However, his favor was open; he could not learn the Northern Emperor's style of openly demoting while secretly praising.","Master, do you know what this Consort Qing's background is?","Could it be she has another identity and is not a minor official's daughter? Speaking of which, does not the emperor hide his feelings for Chancellor Wei at all?","The emperor's favored consort looked like his most trusted minister, and the two were not related by blood. She did not believe the shrewd people in the Northern Li officialdom had not noticed something fishy.","This identity is naturally fake. Her true identity is the illegitimate daughter of Chancellor Wei's father kept outside the household. Because Old Man Wei did not want his most promising eldest son to be entangled with the emperor and ruin his future.","He came up with this idea. He registered the illegitimate daughter who looked like Chancellor Wei under the name of a minor official in his faction. Consort Qing's real name is Wei Yufu, and Song Furong is her fake name.","So, Consort Qing knew from the very beginning that she was a substitute? And her own biological brother's substitute at that? Good heavens, it turns out they looked alike because they both took after their father.","Before entering the palace, her father naturally told her the whole truth. Although Bei Ji's wicked intentions towards Chancellor Wei were hidden, how could they deceive the powerful and high-ranking Old Man Wei.","Dear friends, please move your prosperous little hands to click on the urge for updates button, thank you! Clasps hands in salute!"]},{"number":371,"title":"Chapter 371: Which One to Support","paragraphs":["[Not to mention that the one he likes is their most promising son. If the emperor keeps him overnight in the palace too many times, wouldn't the little old man notice?","If he didn't know that his son already had someone in his heart, he would really be afraid that Wei Qingyi and the Emperor would develop feelings over time, turning a perfectly straight incense stick into a mosquito coil.","Just in case, the old man decisively sent a daughter in to act as a substitute.]","Yue Fuguang secretly admired them; this whole family was full of talents. They managed to turn a substitute trope into something massive. If everything went smoothly, this hidden Eighth Prince might actually get what he wanted.","She just wondered who Wei Qingyi was helping. Thinking this, she asked out loud, \"Little Zhu, aren't Wei Qingyi and Bei Ye a couple?","Does he know that the Eighth Prince is actually his aunt's son? Between his cousin and his lover, who do you think he will help?\"","Without a doubt, Chancellor Wei would definitely help his nephew, both publicly and privately, but Wei Qingyi's stance was not so certain.","Don't forget, he and Bei Ye also had a 'son'!","The Wei family and the royal family had entanglements across three generations, which was absolutely incredible!","[Wei Qingyi still doesn't know that the Eighth Prince is his cousin. His father still cares about his face and can't bring himself to speak about his past affair with the Emperor, especially when his own son is now involved with the other party's son!]","The officials nodded secretly. If it were them, they wouldn't be able to say it either. How damaging would that be to the majestic fatherly image they had built in front of their sons?","\"Does Bei Yue know the inside story? If he wants to commit patricide, he would need to pull in a few more allies to increase his success rate, right?\"","Bei Feng, who was the most likely to become the Crown Prince, counted as one. If Bei Ye knew about the Wei family's affairs, he would probably latch onto Wei Qingyi and never let go.","Yue Fuguang glanced at Emperor Mingxi from the corner of her eye, only to see him relishing the sweet melon from a jade plate.","She just didn't know which was sweeter: the melon, or the gossip she and the system were spilling!","If she remembered correctly, she seemed to have heard the Crown Prince, the head of the Secret Spy Bureau, mention that there was a double agent sent by Beili in Shangjing.","This guy was sent to Beili by Emperor Mingxi in his early years and eventually became Bei Feng's man. Unexpectedly, over a decade later, he was sent back to Shangjing by Bei Feng to spy on intelligence.","Wasn't this a ready-made great achievement?","Obviously, the melon-eating Emperor Mingxi and Zheng Zicheng, the deputy envoy of the Secret Spy Bureau who had been here for a while, both thought of this.","[These are all old matters from over a decade ago. He definitely doesn't know the detailed inside story, otherwise he wouldn't be constantly guarding against his brothers, but would focus on winning them over instead.]","Just as the system finished speaking, a rumbling sound of horse hooves could be heard coming from the hunting ground in the distance.","Yue Fuguang secretly checked her electronic watch; it was already twelve o'clock. Were they coming back for lunch?","She just didn't know how everyone's harvest was. They wouldn't be able to catch the wild game for lunch today, and she wondered if the afternoon would be as peaceful as the morning.","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but tap the system, \"Tongtong, when and where will those people make their move?\"","[Host, according to the information I've detected, they will first strike at the princes and princesses in the dense forest this afternoon to create panic and internal chaos.","Tonight's banquet and the night itself are one of their main events.]","One of? So there's a second or even a third?","\"Keep an eye out and constantly monitor their movements.\"","[Are we not going to expose this to Emperor Mingxi and his ministers?]","\"Let's not say anything for now. This is also a test of their abilities. If they can't even bury people in the pits they dug themselves, they might not be up to the task of expanding the territory next year or the year after.\"","By then, she would either wait for them to grow or bring out a massive weapon herself.","This was something Yue Fuguang absolutely did not want to see. Gunpowder had already appeared prematurely. As for other firearms, she still hoped they would follow the laws of development.","She would never admit that ever since she learned there were 'ghosts' in the underworld and a heavenly consciousness above, the concept of karma in her heart constantly reminded her not to go to extremes in everything. Even when killing, unless absolutely necessary, it was best to leave the opponent with half a breath!","If she were just a tasker traveling through small worlds, it would be fine, but since she still wanted to walk the path of cultivation in the future, she had to leave a way out for herself.","Soon, everyone arrived at the hunting presentation platform fully loaded with prey. Yue Fuguang took a look; wow, in less than four hours, these people had really caught a lot.","The Eighth Princess quickly ran towards her and said excitedly, \"Little Aunt, Seventh Brother and I saved a white fox pelt for you.","We'll go out and look for more this afternoon to hunt a few more, so we can make a fox fur cloak for you in the winter.\"","Seeing her sweating profusely, Yue Fuguang poured her a cup of water and handed it over, \"That sounds great. Whether I can wear a new cloak this winter depends on you two.\"","She hadn't thought about instilling concepts of animal protection into the people here, mainly because such ideas were inappropriate for the times.","Before cotton, people relied on reed catkins and straw to stuff their clothes for warmth.","Nobles relied on various animal furs and silk wadding to keep out the cold.","Telling them to protect animals? Are you kidding! When their lives were at stake, who cared about the life or death of animals?","And for winter heating, if they couldn't cut down trees in the mountains, the common people would freeze to death before coal became widespread.","It was only in the past two years that coal briquettes and coal stoves slowly became popular. Without needing promotion, these things were easy to obtain and inexpensive. Since they burned longer than firewood, the logging of trees naturally decreased, and many bald mountains regained their greenery.","Hearing her words, the Seventh Prince, who had walked over, happily replied, \"Don't worry, Little Aunt. My sister and I will definitely gather enough for a fox fur cloak for you.\"","\"So confident? Little Seventh, have your archery and riding skills improved again?\"","Before the Seventh Prince could brag, the Eighth Princess had already started to undermine her brother, \"Little Aunt, it's not that Seventh Brother's skills have improved, it's because there hasn't been any hunting for years.","Over these years, the animals in the hunting ground have reproduced well. We saw a lot of prey not long after we went in.\"","Seeing his sister undermine him, the Seventh Prince wasn't annoyed and added with a naive smile, \"Exactly. We spent the morning wandering around the outer edges and still got a good harvest.","We'll go further in this afternoon.\"","\"Little Aunt, do you want to come in and play with us this afternoon?\"","Yue Fuguang originally wanted to refuse, but thinking about the system saying those people would make a move in the afternoon, and seeing the expectant looks in these two pairs of eyes, the words of refusal changed into an agreement.","The Eighth Princess originally just invited Yue Fuguang out of habit, not expecting that she, who usually didn't like to move much, would agree.","She and the Seventh Prince were so happy that if they weren't mindful of their status and the fact that they were outside with their imperial father and foreign ministers watching, they would have jumped up.","Hearing the commotion here, Xie Zhiyan's heart stirred. Since the Junior Preceptor was by the side of his seventh brother and eighth sister, he felt much more at ease.","As for his other younger siblings, he would have to deploy more personnel to protect them in the afternoon.","He looked towards the diplomatic mission again, his gaze lingering on Bei Yue for a moment longer. The revelations Yue Fuguang made in the morning had been reported to him in detail by Zheng Zicheng.","Xie Zhiyan expressed that Great Yan was hospitable. Before this person returned to Beili, the hospitable Great Yan would definitely make sure he 'returned fully loaded!'"]},{"number":372,"title":"Chapter 372: Prepare to Meet the Enemy","paragraphs":["After a hearty lunch, Yue Fuguang mounted her white horse. Followed by dozens of guards and with two wingmen flying overhead, she entered the hunting ground in grand style.","Among the crowd behind them, one person silently slipped away and ran in another direction.","Yue Fuguang, sensing something, glanced back sideways but didn't pay it much mind as she galloped into a small forest trail.","Among the hundred or so horses, only the white horse she was riding seemed to run in a completely chaotic manner!","It was also the Seventh Prince and the Eighth Princess's first time seeing this mount of hers. Previously, during equestrian classes in the palace, she never had to bring her own horse.","Because Emperor Mingxi had long picked out a good horse for her, the offspring of his favorite horse in the Imperial Stables.","The Seventh Prince couldn't help but ask, Little Aunt, why does your horse run so... so differently?","He wanted to say chaotically, but he didn't dare. Even if Yue Fuguang didn't blame him, his father, the Emperor, would scold him if he found out.","Yue Fuguang laughed, This isn't different. It's an ambling horse. It might look chaotic when it runs, but I'm much more comfortable than you are right now.","An ambling horse experiences relatively less bumping. If He Qisha didn't have a knack for taming horses, he wouldn't have been able to train an ambling horse!","However, the Eighth Princess's attention was on the horse's hooves. The Great Yan Dynasty already had saddles and stirrups, but horseshoes hadn't appeared yet.","She was very curious about the sound the white horse Yue Fuguang rode made when walking.","She couldn't help but ask, Little Aunt, why is your horse wearing shoes on its feet? The sound it makes when walking is different from ours.","Ah Rui, these aren't shoes. They are called horseshoes. With them, the horse's hooves can be well protected from harm.","As for extending the working life of the horses, she didn't need to say it. Not only could the Seventh Prince and Eighth Princess think of it, but even the commander of the guards behind them had his eyes light up upon hearing this.","Ever since they entered the hunting grounds, because they were protecting the princes, princesses, and the true golden treasure of Great Yan, they had been nervously guarding their surroundings and hadn't paid much attention to the horses everyone was riding.","Now, after Yue Fuguang mentioned it, they looked again at the private guards following the Junior Preceptor. Led by He Jin and Dai Yuxing, the dozens of people all seemed to have this thing called horseshoes equipped to protect their horses' hooves.","The guard commander immediately called someone over and whispered a few words in his ear. The man nodded solemnly and quickly whipped his horse to head back.","The guards sent to protect Yue Fuguang were all from the batch of smart and highly skilled individuals.","The guard commander naturally thought a bit further. This thing might look simple, but it was a great asset for Great Yan.","The same was true for the other countries.","He not only had to tell His Majesty this news as soon as possible, but he also had to keep it hidden and prevent the diplomatic mission from noticing anything unusual.","The guard commander's idea was simple: if a good thing could be kept from spreading outwards a little longer, then keep it that way.","The group galloped wildly for over a dozen miles in one breath. By now, they had left the outer perimeter of the hunting ground, and the mountains slowly changed color from their original deep green.","The dense forest on both sides of the road now looked like an overturned paintbox. Yellows, reds, and dark greens mixed together, with shifting shades of color. The overlapping blocks of color spread across the mountain forest, blending with the jagged, strange rocks to form the most beautiful scenery commonly seen deep in the mountains.","Golden leaves shone like gold under the sunlight, while a gust of wind sent a layer of dry, dull yellow leaves fluttering down.","As the horses' hooves stepped over them, a rustling sound echoed.","Faced with such beautiful scenery, Yue Fuguang's face was originally full of appreciation, but that was only until her gaze fell upon the rocks and dead leaves deep in the forest.","She immediately pulled back the reins tightly. The two front hooves of the white horse she was riding reared up high, and after neighing twice, it came to a halt.","At the same time, Yue Fuguang raised her hand to signal everyone to stop.","My Lord!","He Jin and the guard commander rode forward to ask about the situation, while Dai Yuxing had already ordered the guards to be on high alert.","Although everything seemed normal at the moment, Dai Yuxing felt that something was wrong.","Yue Fuguang stared at a certain spot in the forest and said, Something is wrong. Everyone, prepare for battle.","Because half the leaves on the trees in the forest had fallen, everyone's field of vision was a bit better here than on the outskirts.","The mountain forest before them was not deathly silent; rather, it was full of vitality everywhere.","There was the rustling of the wind sweeping through the treetops, the occasional friction of birds flying through the woods, and the snapping of twigs and dead leaves as cunning rabbits darted through the dry grass, but there were no human footprints.","This was the scene in everyone's eyes, but at this moment, what Yue Fuguang saw was vastly different from them.","Her eyes seemed to pierce through the surface layer of dead leaves and broken branches on the ground, seeing the deep, shallow, and messy footprints underneath.","These footprints led to the place they were heading to, a hundred meters away, where besides tall trees, there were also huge grayish-white rocks that appeared from time to time.","Unfortunately, Yue Fuguang did not yet have the ability to see through thick rocks to see what was hiding behind them.","But she could barely see through the thin layer of soil to spot the human silhouettes hiding beneath.","Her eyes didn't have thermal imaging capabilities. If she hadn't vaguely seen the hearts in those people's chests beating faster and faster, she would have thought this was a large-scale murder and burial site!","Hearing Yue Fuguang's orders, everyone didn't ask further questions and immediately trusted her judgment unconditionally.","Tongtong, how many enemies are there?","Host, two hundred and eighty-nine people. Over a dozen are scattered behind the trees, more than thirty are hiding underground, and the rest are hiding behind the rocks.","Yue Fuguang glanced back at her own people. Besides herself, the Seventh Prince, and the Eighth Princess, there were eighty-one guards, not even a fraction of the enemy's numbers.","This eighty-one-person guard detail showed how much the Emperor valued them; it was even larger than the Crown Prince's entourage.","But no one could have ever imagined that those people placed such heavy importance on Yue Fuguang. With this kind of lineup, it was enough to assassinate the Emperor.","The people hiding behind the rocks felt their hearts sink when they saw Yue Fuguang's group suddenly stop. They were just a few steps away from entering the ambush circle they had set up.","But the group had suddenly stopped. They had been discovered!","Boss! A man in gray martial attire next to him lowered his voice, looking warily in the direction of Yue Fuguang's group. Did that person discover us? Should we make our move? The only problem was that the distance was a bit far, and the effect of a preemptive strike would be greatly weakened to a minimum.","The man he called Boss wore a black face mask, obscuring his expression. Only a pair of exposed, falcon-like eyes narrowed dangerously, then suddenly widened, shooting out a terrifying murderous intent.","He said in a deep voice, Prepare to strike. Except for Yue Fuguang, leave no one else alive.","Just as he gave the order, Yue Fuguang, sitting upright on her horse, suddenly felt the stagnant murderous intent ahead burst forth like floodwaters breaking a dam, surging violently toward her face.","He Jin, Dai Yuxing, protect the Prince and Princess well! Commander Xue, prepare to meet the enemy!","Dear readers:","As the new year dawns, hoofbeats echo across the snow. May you, upon turning this page, also unfold a year of boundless horizons. May the road ahead be smooth and the path behind leave no regrets. Ride the spring breeze, spur your steed, and gallop onward. May you take your dreams as your horse, live fully in your glorious youth, and journey toward the next magnificent mountains and seas.","Most importantly, may you all be blessed with wealth and leisure, free from illness and sorrow!"]},{"number":373,"title":"Chapter 373: There Are Bad People in the Team","paragraphs":["Her words were still hanging in the air when everyone saw the sky ahead suddenly darken, followed by a soul-shaking humming sound.","\"Protect the Lord!\" The two sisters, Shen Chunying and Luo Shendong, immediately stepped in front of Yue Fuguang.","The arrows from ahead did not come one by one, but swarmed out densely like locusts. Hundreds of arrows were fired at once, tearing through the wind in the forest, bringing up swirling leaves as they ruthlessly bore down on them.","Yue Fuguang acutely smelled a sudden foul stench mixed into the fresh air, thinking to herself that these rats not only liked to set up ambushes.","But they were also despicable and shameless enough to smear poison on their arrowheads. Smearing poison was one thing, but what was the meaning of using dung and corpse fluid?","Were the noble families already so poor that they couldn't even afford poison?","Looking at the dense, dark cloud of arrowheads, Yue Fuguang silently raised her hand. If she really let this strongest long-range attack method of the cold weapon era rain down on them just like that...","Even if the martial arts of the people around her were excellent, they would inevitably be scratched by the sharp arrows and stray shafts.","It all happened in a flash. Just as the rain of arrows was two or three meters away from the group, and the people at the very front had already raised their swords to block, the cold, emotionless voice of Yue Fuguang, who had been sitting calmly on her horse the entire time, rang out: \"Halt!\"","With her single word \"Halt,\" the falling rain of arrows seemed to freeze in the sky. The tips of over two hundred arrows emitted a soul-shaking cold light under the sun, but unfortunately, this lethal cold light was now frozen in the air.","Seeing the scene before them, Yue Fuguang's guards were fine—after all, they had seen even more outrageous things—but the guards sent by the imperial court were visibly stunned. Their eyes were wide open, looking up at the rain of arrows in the sky, and they swallowed hard.","The hands gripping their swords loosened and tightened, tightened and loosened. The cold sweat in their palms silently burned their hearts at this moment, blazing hot.","When they looked at Yue Fuguang again, their gazes had changed. There was only one thought in their minds: the folk tales saying that the Junior Preceptor was a goddess descended to earth were actually true!","Meanwhile, the enemies watched the arrows they had shot suddenly stop in mid-air as if they had seen a ghost. They stared blankly at the suspended arrows, then at the bows in their hands, their hands trembling so much they almost dropped them.","Except for the leader and a few others, the rest couldn't help but take two steps back. Just as the leader gritted his teeth, refusing to believe in the supernatural, and prepared to launch another wave...","The word \"Return!\" was carried over by the wind.","As Yue Fuguang's word fell, the arrows that had been static in the air suddenly flew backwards at an even faster speed than when they came.","Then, the sounds of clashing weapons and muffled groans came one after another from behind the rocks.","It wasn't screaming, but a suppressed gasp squeezed out from between gritted teeth.","With her superior hearing, Yue Fuguang even heard the sounds of people stumbling to the ground and increasingly heavy breathing.","The black-clad leader gritted his teeth and shouted, \"Kill!\" He swept his bloodshot eyes over his now lifeless subordinates and led the charge out himself.","Since the sneak attack failed and the rain of arrows achieved nothing, they would fight a real battle with real swords and spears.","Even if their side had suffered some small casualties, it was still over a hundred men against eighty. The advantage was theirs!","As he rushed out from behind the rocks with over a hundred men, Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow. The ones behind the trees and hiding underground hadn't moved an inch even now.","What great composure!","Engaging in close combat, blades met sword glints, churning up this mountain forest. Leaves rustled down like natural soil, burying the figures that fell with miserable howls one by one.","Yue Fuguang frowned. They were outnumbered. Her guards were fine, all carefully selected experts, but the guards brought by Commander Xue clearly couldn't match the enemy's reckless, life-risking fighting style.","She silently took out an energy storage bead, held it in her hand, and said, \"Disarm!\"","As her words fell, the swords and sabers in the enemies' hands flew out of their grasps with a whoosh in a bizarre, utterly unreasonable manner.","They flew into mid-air, forming a formation of blades and swords, turned around, and pointed at their original owners.","With just one command from Yue Fuguang, the weapons that were theirs a moment ago would ruthlessly stab them the next.","\"Go.\" Unexpectedly, the weapons did not stab the people in the field. Instead, over thirty of them separated and flew out with a swish, plunging toward the areas behind the trees and into the ground.","Along with the occasional screams and the increasingly heavy stench of blood, He Jin and the others exchanged glances. Without needing Yue Fuguang's orders, they dashed straight toward those people.","\"Take them down!\" Commander Xue ordered, and he also led the charge over.","The saying that no matter how high your martial arts are, you still fear a kitchen knife was proven once again. Despite being outnumbered, relying on the swords and blades in their hands, it didn't take long for all two hundred or so enemies to be captured.","Seeing the good harvest, Yue Fuguang's group immediately turned back with their prey.","When their group appeared at the exit of the hunting ground with a long string of captives, Emperor Mingxi and the others were instantly stunned.","\"Fuguang, are you hurt?\" Yu Chongshan didn't even care that Emperor Mingxi was still there. The little old man rushed to the front of her horse with flying steps.","\"Grandfather, I'm fine. Look, not a single scratch!\" If Yue Fuguang didn't have to maintain her public image, she would have spun around beautifully for him.","\"It's good that you're fine, it's good that you're fine.\" Yu Chongshan's suspended heart settled a bit before he continued, \"Tomorrow we will just wait in the main camp. We absolutely cannot go into the woods again!\"","Yue Fuguang thought about tomorrow's situation. It was indeed unsuitable for her to enter the woods again, so she readily nodded in agreement.","She wasn't afraid herself, but she was currently a hot commodity. Going out would easily implicate others. Anyway, she had seen what she wanted to see, so it was better to stay put obediently.","To be honest, even just riding a horse back and forth for over two hours had really tired her out.","After receiving the solicitous inquiries from Emperor Mingxi and his ministers, Yue Fuguang returned to her own tent to rest. The Crown Prince and the others had gone out and hadn't returned yet. She was anxious to find the system for first-hand news.","\"What? Tongtong, are you saying that the diplomatic mission was also assassinated?\"","These people didn't just want a life-and-death struggle; they also wanted to provoke a war between Great Yan and the surrounding countries.","If these princes and princesses were injured or died in Great Yan, even if the two countries didn't go to war, they would still demand an exorbitant price.","The first to bear the brunt would be those three high-yield superior crop seeds. They definitely wouldn't be able to keep them hidden anymore.","\"There's a traitor in the ranks!\"","[The host guessed correctly. The Li family of Xinzhou colluded with Nanyue. Today, they deliberately set an ambush to attack the Nanyue diplomatic mission.","Unfortunately, the Xi brothers were with Gan Tang today. Later, Bei Ye and the others, who were nearby, heard the sounds of fighting and went to rescue them. Those people left a few alive, and the rest were killed by the Nanyue people.]","\"Those princes and princesses weren't injured by the assassins or hurt themselves, right?\"","At this moment, Yue Fuguang was a little worried that those few wouldn't stab themselves a few times just for the sweet potatoes, potatoes, and corn.","Facts proved that her worries were not unfounded. When Bei Ye came to the rescue, he took one look at the situation on the field and the weak fighting style of the Xi brothers, and knew there was something fishy going on.","He had just wanted to go easy on them, but unfortunately, his attendants were too capable. Despite being outnumbered, aside from those who were silenced by the Nanyue people when they saw things going wrong, the rest were quickly taken down."]},{"number":374,"title":"Chapter 374: Where Did It Hurt","paragraphs":["The few of them glanced at the remaining assassins still standing in the arena, exchanged a look, and, with tacit understanding, gripped their swords and took a few steps forward.","Reaching a secluded spot, Bei Ye spoke first, Princess Ronghua, and you two, should I not have come?","He looked at the three of them probing, not missing a single subtle expression on their faces.","Xi Ling chuckled and said, Brother Bei Ye, you worry too much. I merely bumped into the Princess by chance. If anyone shouldn't have come, it is us brothers.","Facing three pairs of eyes all by herself, Gan Tang didn't flinch in the slightest. She curled her lips into a smile and said pointedly, You three brothers don't need to test me. Let me just ask you, are you really willing to miss out on such a golden opportunity?","Seeing the three lower their eyes in thought, she continued, Who knows how many assassins are hiding in this forest. It wouldn't be surprising if we were accidentally injured, or if those people were deliberately coming for us. Afterwards, as long as none of us speaks a word, with the assassins' corpses right here, could the Emperor of Great Yan possibly deny it?","What about those people? Bei Ye didn't turn around, but the others all understood what he meant. As guests, the host would certainly dispatch guards to accompany and protect them.","Therefore, within their group, each person had a ten-man squad of Great Yan's Imperial Feather Guards assigned to protect them. This was also the reason why Bei Ye didn't immediately call for a halt upon noticing something was amiss.","The guards of Great Yan were devoted to their duties and all died in battle to protect our safety. What do you think of this excuse?","Just as Xi Ling was about to speak, Xi Yuanshan said, The sovereign and subjects of Great Yan are no fools. If all their men died while our people suffered no casualties, who would believe it?","Gan Tang shook her head and said, I think Xi Ling is right. As for whether the sovereign and subjects of Great Yan believe it, that's not important. It only matters that it is a fact that we were injured by assassins.","As long as they were injured, their parents could justifiably demand compensation from the Emperor of Great Yan.","A cruel smile appeared on Bei Ye's face. At the right time, it wouldn't be impossible for a few of our own men to suffer casualties. Everything is for our nation; their deaths would be well deserved!","Although his proposal was cold-blooded, the other three agreed with little hesitation. Just as they were preparing for the next step—whether to cut themselves or let the assassins go—they heard rustling in the forest, and a group of people walked out.","The Second, Third, and Fifth Princes rushed over with a group of subordinates, looking disheveled. The moment the two sides met and saw each other's sorry states, they knew the other party had also encountered assassins.","When the Fifth Prince saw the four people standing in a circle, obviously whispering to each other, he had a bad feeling. Before his brothers could speak, he took the lead and said, It's a coincidence that you are all here. It saves us the trouble of looking for you.","With a joyful expression, he said, Please come out with us brothers. Word has come from the Crown Prince that there are too many assassins in the forest right now. It is no longer safe for us to stay here; we need to evacuate immediately.","Hearing their fifth brother say this, Xie Zhimin and Xie Zhixin were stunned at first, then immediately echoed, Yes, it is indeed dangerous here. If it weren't for finding you, we brothers would have left long ago.","Xie Zhixin, for once showing some intelligence, said with a look of relief, It is truly fortunate that none of you were hurt!","Xie Zhimin even waved his hand grandly and praised loudly, Our Great Yan's Imperial Feather Guards have been devoted to their duties. Protecting the delegation today without a single person getting injured is a great merit. You will all be heavily rewarded upon our return.","Thank you, Second Royal Highness! the guards cheered in unison, not just because of the pending rewards, but also because the looming threat to their lives had vanished with the arrival of the three princes.","The three brothers spoke one after another. Bei Ye and the other three showed polite but distant smiles, mounted their horses, and followed the three out of the forest.","The three brothers walking at the very front didn't see the smiles vanish from the faces of the people who had turned their backs, their expressions turning so gloomy that water could practically drip from them.","Meanwhile, the conversation between the system and Yue Fuguang was still ongoing. [Host, rest assured. Before these people could harm themselves, they were coincidentally interrupted by Second Brother Xie and the others. If the three of them had arrived a moment later, the dozens of guards following them would have probably met with disaster.]","The system briefly explained what it saw to Yue Fuguang. Yue Fuguang's hand, holding her teacup, paused in mid-air. Fifth Brother Xie is quite smart.","Her feelings toward him were complicated, especially after discovering that he seemed to have developed feelings for her older sister. It gave her the immediate sensation of a parent watching a wild pig trying to root up their family's fresh, tender cabbage.","She nitpicked his every flaw, able to find a bone in an egg, let alone the fact that he was a member of the royal family, whom she was dissatisfied with in every possible way.","Forget it, let nature take its course. She would neither play matchmaker nor stand in their way; it would all depend on whether they were fated for each other.","She stopped dwelling on this and instead asked about the Crown Prince's situation. Today, aside from the Emperor, the assassins' primary targets were herself and the Crown Prince.","She had willingly gone in as bait to check the situation, while the Crown Prince had been one of the biggest, most tempting baits of this trip from the very beginning.","Her own assassination attempt involved nearly three hundred people; the number attacking the Crown Prince would only be more, not less.","[Host, don't worry. The Crown Prince is not dead, and the number of people assassinating him wasn't even as high as yours.]","What did it mean that he wasn't dead? Did that mean he was injured, and heavily at that?","Is he badly injured? Yue Fuguang was a bit worried. Will it affect the upcoming plans?","The only substantial baits here, aside from the royal father and son, were her. If the Crown Prince really can't do it, then the Emperor will just have to step up!","Hearing her words, the system rolled its eyes so hard they practically reached the sky.","[Host, I thought you were worried about the Crown Prince, but it turns out you're just worried his injury will affect the upcoming plans. Also, does the Emperor know you want to push him out as bait?]","Seeing no one around, Yue Fuguang coughed lightly in embarrassment, forcibly saving face as she said, I'm just worried our plans will fall short at the final hurdle. We are only one step away from completing the mission to eliminate the noble families; we can't give up halfway. Look, the Liu family of Xinzhou has already colluded with Southern Yue. If we strike any later, the fish in our net will slip away.","As for whether the Emperor knew she wanted to push him out as bait... his thoughts weren't important!","Besides, the world belonged to his Xie family. Naturally, they should be the ones doing the dangerous work.","My Lord, His Majesty requests your presence! Before Yue Fuguang could ask for more details, she heard He Jin reporting from outside the tent that the Emperor had summoned her.","Understood! Standing up and ensuring there was nothing inappropriate about her appearance, she slowly walked outside.","Eunuch Qian? Why did you come over personally? As soon as Yue Fuguang exited the main tent, she looked up and saw Qian Gui waiting to the side. There was faint sweat on his face, and his complexion was not very good. Could it be that something had happened to the Emperor?","Unfortunately, she had forgotten to ask the system just now, so she asked directly without any taboo, Did something happen to His Majesty?","Qian Gui also knew his expression had caused Yue Fuguang to overthink, so he quickly stepped forward and whispered, My Lord, His Majesty is perfectly fine. It is the Crown Prince... the Crown Prince has been injured!","Yue Fuguang nodded. Then let us go take a look.","As long as he still had a breath left, she had nothing to worry about. The fact that she possessed miraculous medicine was known to quite a few high-ranking officials over the past two years.","For the Emperor to summon her at this time, there was probably only one purpose: to ask for medicine for the Crown Prince."]},{"number":375,"title":"Chapter 375: Celestial Note","paragraphs":["Qian Gui led her into the Crown Prince's main tent. She instantly sensed the oppressive atmosphere inside. Aside from the Emperor, several Ministers were also present.","Emperor Mingxi's face was livid, and Cai Xian and the others were pale. There were tea stains and uncleared broken porcelain on the floor.","The crowd, who had been standing on both sides with their heads bowed, looked at her as if they had seen their great savior. Their eyes lit up astonishingly as they bowed and greeted her one after another.","After returning the greeting, Yue Fuguang sat below Emperor Mingxi. She glanced toward the inner compartment before asking, \"Your Majesty, how are the Crown Prince's injuries?\"","Emperor Mingxi pursed his lips, hesitating for a few breaths as if it were hard to speak of, before saying, \"The injuries are not too severe, but the location of the wound...\"","Seeing his hesitant demeanor, Yue Fuguang wondered, Could he have been injured in an unmentionable place?","If it was really as she thought, it wouldn't be appropriate for her to ask for details, so she said, \"I wonder if my medicine will be of any use.\"","There was truly no precedent for this; even in the cultivation world, there were no pills specifically for that area. They could only treat a dead horse as a living one and hope for the best!","Yue Fuguang thought about how the Crown Prince already had an eldest son. As long as he was raised well, there was no fear of lacking an heir. As for having only one child, Yue Fuguang felt it was enough; there wouldn't even be anyone to fight over the inheritance. How wonderful!","Seeing Yue Fuguang bring up the medicine on her own initiative, the worried expression on Emperor Mingxi's face eased considerably. \"With Fuguang's medicine, regardless of whether it works or not, both I and the Crown Prince will remember your kindness.\"","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment, then took out a Rejuvenation Pill and a Lesser Restoration Pill, saying to Emperor Mingxi, \"Why not show these pills to Imperial Physician Sun to see if they suit the symptoms?\"","Emperor Mingxi gave Qian Gui a look. He immediately stepped forward, picked up the two jade bottles on the table, and entered the inner room.","\"Little Zhu, can the Rejuvenation Pill and Lesser Restoration Pill be given to the current Crown Prince?\"","\"Master, the Crown Prince can use the pills. He was also poisoned with corpse toxin. If the Crown Prince hadn't taken your antidote pill in time, he wouldn't have even survived the journey back to the camp.\"","Sure enough, what she encountered was not an isolated case.","\"Wasn't the Crown Prince just going fishing? How did he almost get himself killed?\"","\"Who told him not to have Master's abilities? The number of guards he brought was similar to yours, and the number of assassins they encountered was also comparable, yet their casualties were over half.\"","\"Have all the assassins been caught?\"","\"Half of them escaped, but Wei Shouyi has already led men to pursue them. Those people are also injured and won't be able to run far.\"","The Emperor and his subjects didn't wait long outside. Just as Yue Fuguang was eating her third pastry, she saw the curtain of the inner room twitch, and then the pale and haggard Crown Prince walked out, supported by Qian Gui.","Upon seeing Yue Fuguang, tears faintly shimmered in his eyes. He bowed and said, \"Zhiyan thanks Little Aunt for bestowing the medicine!\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"As long as you are fine. Quickly, sit down and speak.\"","Xie Zhiyan's face stiffened for a moment. He subconsciously waved his hand and smiled, saying, \"I've been lying down for too long, and my body is stiff. I'll just stand.\"","Yue Fuguang cast a subtle glance over his body.","\"Little Zhu, what's going on with the Crown Prince? After taking two pills, why does he still look so weak?\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang call him weak, a faint blush immediately appeared on the Crown Prince's previously pale face, and his upright posture grew even stiffer.","\"Perhaps the time has been too short, and the pills haven't fully exerted their medicinal effects yet.\"","The Crown Prince nodded frantically in his heart. The divine artifact was right; it was just that the medicine hadn't kicked in yet. He really wasn't weak!","\"Your Majesty, will the evening banquet still be held as usual?\"","Seeing the Crown Prince recovering, the Minister of Rites, Zhang Zhongping, finally found an opportunity to ask his question.","Emperor Mingxi gently rubbed the auspicious patterns on the side of his cup. After pondering for a moment, he said, \"The banquet will proceed as usual.\"","He looked at the Crown Prince and asked, \"Crown Prince, can your body still handle attending the banquet normally?\"","\"Replying to Imperial Father, Little Aunt's medicine has miraculous effects. I am fine.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded slightly and then addressed Huo Ying, who was standing below, \"Have the personnel been arranged?\"","\"Rest assured, Your Majesty. I have arranged sufficient manpower at every key location throughout the hunting grounds, maintaining a relaxed exterior but strict interior security, just as Your Majesty instructed.\"","Soon, Yue Fuguang saw exactly what Huo Ying meant by a relaxed exterior and strict interior.","\"Little Zhu, are those Shen Kang and Song Xiang? Why are they dressed like that? Are they role playing?\"","\"Master, it is indeed them. They thought we wouldn't recognize them just because they changed their clothes. What kind of eunuchs are as masculine and straightforward as they are? Are they afraid people won't notice them?\"","Shen Kang and Song Xiang, who were currently bowing to pour wine and serve dishes for the Emperor and the Crown Prince, paused their movements upon hearing the two of them complaining.","Then, they quickly glanced at Eunuch Qian, who was standing by the side. Their bodies slowly softened, their heads lowered even more, and humble smiles appeared on their faces.","Song Xiang even considered whether he should pinch his throat and say, \"Please enjoy your meal, Your Highness.\" But after thinking about it, he decided against it. With his gruff voice, even if he pinched his throat, he wouldn't sound like a eunuch.","\"Little Zhu, look at the dejected faces of those people from the diplomatic mission. Is it because they failed to successfully self-mutilate and are unwilling to give up on extorting the Emperor?\"","\"Master, it's a good thing they didn't actually stab themselves. Otherwise, even if they were injured, one dose of your medicine would cure them, and their suffering would have been for nothing!\"","Clang! Clatter! Crash!","A series of clattering sounds came from the diplomatic mission. They had either knocked over their wine cups or dropped their chopsticks onto the floor.","Hearing the commotion next door, several of them suddenly looked up. They looked at each other, all seeing shock and... confusion in each other's eyes.","What had they just heard? It was a heavenly voice!!","If it wasn't a heavenly voice, who could make it so they felt surrounded by the sound? It seemed sometimes far, sometimes near, sometimes strong, sometimes weak, as far away as the horizon, yet as close as right in front of their eyes.","This voice... this voice clearly came from the mouth of a young child.","But looking around, the entire banquet hall was brightly lit, and there were no young children to be seen!","Bei Ye's hands trembled slightly. The palace servants replaced his chopsticks with new ones, but he tried several times and couldn't pick them up.","For the first time, he felt that ivory chopsticks weren't absolutely necessary for him to use!","The panic in his heart was not only because he heard the heavenly voice but also because their hidden little schemes had been seen through!","They had acted covertly. Even if the Great Yan guards were present at the time, they hadn't made a move yet, so the guards shouldn't have known their intentions.","But now, with the heavenly voice ringing in their ears, their actions had clearly been exposed!","He caught Gan Tang's eye in his peripheral vision. Both of them simultaneously looked toward the Great Yan Emperor and his subjects, seeing that the crowd was exchanging cups and chatting very naturally.","Could it be that the voice just now was only heard by the few of them involved?","Bei Ye and Gan Tang quickly dismissed this guess. Although the two of them hadn't reacted as dramatically by knocking over cups and dishes, they clearly saw Lan Xuan'er and Bei Yue lose their composure for a moment.","Gan Tang understood Lan Xuan'er well; she must have heard it too.","Bei Ye was even more direct. Taking advantage of a toast, he lowered his voice and said, \"Imperial Brother, was that just now...\"","Suddenly realizing something, Bei Ye's eyes widened instantly. He had been too panicked just now, only thinking that there were no children in the venue, but how could he forget that there was another voice just now?","Although the voice was somewhat ethereal, thinking about it carefully, it was clearly... the voice of Yue Fuguang, the Junior Preceptor of Great Yan who descended by divine decree!","He abruptly raised his head, the fake, polite smile he had just directed at Bei Yue still frozen on his face.","He watched as the Eighth Princess of Dayan said something to Yue Fuguang. Though he didn't know what was said, she nodded repeatedly, a bright smile lighting up her face."]},{"number":376,"title":"Chapter 376: The Emperor's Melon Is Big and Sweet","paragraphs":["Turning his head slightly, he caught sight of the Xi brothers sitting opposite them from the corner of his eye. They were also covertly observing Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang ignored the various burning and probing hidden gazes. Her peripheral vision lightly swept over their pale faces. With a slight purse of her lips, she thought: The surround sound produced by the system is truly worth having!","Caring little for whether they lived or died, she continued her performance. \"Little Zhu, these people are quite pitiful too. The two brothers from Beili are being schemed against by their own biological father, used as targets to protect his most beloved son and attract all the open and hidden attacks from the court and beyond.","\"As for the two from Xiqiang, one has an unknown father, and the other is being plotted against by his own brother while pretending to be a love-struck fool.","\"Gan Tang is even more pitiful. Her father favored a concubine, and the causes of her mother's and brother's deaths remain unknown. Gan Sheng picked up the throne for cheap, yet he constantly guards against her, the legitimate princess.","\"And Lan Xuan'er seems the most likely to inherit the throne as the Empress of Nanzhao, but unfortunately, she doesn't know that her second sister and third brother are currently more valued by their Empress mother. It is only a matter of time before she is replaced.\"","The individuals mentioned naturally matched themselves to her words. Their faces changed colors as vividly as the autumn scenery in the forest she had seen today.","Especially Bei Yue and Gan Tang; they knew their own situations very well, and Yue Fuguang was absolutely right.","Particularly Gan Tang, who had never given up investigating the truth behind the deaths of her mother, the Empress, and her brother.","However, years had passed, and she had yet to find much useful information. Since Yue Fuguang said this, did she know something?","[Master, that Gan Chengjiang is just like Emperor Mingxi's father. They both wanted to depose the Crown Prince and support the son of their favored concubine to take the throne.","However, the late emperor did not have Gan Chengjiang's luck. He failed, whereas Gan Chengjiang not only succeeded but also did so without arousing the suspicion of his court officials.","Just look at Gan Tang. She definitely never suspected that her own royal father was one of the true culprits who murdered her mother and brother!]","Having these old matters brought up multiple times, Emperor Mingxi was already able to treat them with indifference, especially since he was the victor. A secret sense of pride even rose in his heart.","He calmly ignored the covert, evaluating glance Gan Tang shot his way.","It was also this glance that made the monarch and his subjects even more certain that the members of the diplomatic mission could indeed hear the inner thoughts of the Junior Preceptor.","Emperor Mingxi concealed the dark gleam that flashed through his eyes. When he looked up again, his expression was entirely warm and genial.","\"One of them? Were there others involved?\"","Hidden beneath the table, Gan Tang's distinctively knuckled hand turned faintly white from clenching her fist too tightly.","She forcefully suppressed the surging emotions in her heart and the tears threatening to spill from the corners of her eyes. With trembling hands, she gripped her wine cup and downed it in one gulp.","Cough, cough, cough!","She seemed to have choked on the wine, coughing incessantly, her eyes turning red from the exertion.","\"Sister Tang, drink slowly.\" Lan Xuan'er used the pretext of patting her back to block most of the probing gazes with her own body.","[Does Master remember Little Zhu telling you that Gan Chengjiang's death was related to the Changsheng Sect?]","\"What, does this have something to do with the deaths of Gan Tang's mother and brother?\"","[In his early years, Gan Chengjiang firmly believed in the Changsheng Sect. Nanyue is rich in herbs, and some within the Changsheng Sect were highly skilled in medicine. They achieved great fame for a time by healing the sick and saving lives.","Because of this, they gained Gan Chengjiang's trust and were appointed to search for immortal herbs and refine immortal elixirs.","The pills refined by the Changsheng Sect of Nanyue mostly used medicinal herbs, which was different from the heavy metal-laden pills Emperor Mingxi took later on.","The medicine he took was too nourishing. Eating it year after year, as his body grew old and weak, unable to handle such strong tonics, he ended up being nourished to death!]","\"Didn't you say the Changsheng Sect was highly skilled in medicine? Could they not know about Gan Chengjiang's condition? Were they doing it on purpose?\"","[Because the Changsheng Sect, or rather Panshan, had already used Gan Chengjiang to achieve their goal of replacing the Crown Prince, it naturally didn't matter to them whether he lived or died.]","\"Panshan planned early on to let Gan Sheng take the throne, and then ally with Beili and Xiqiang to annex Dayan? So the upcoming three hundred years of chaos are also part of Panshan's plan?\"","[Great chaos in the world and frequent dynastic changes make it easier for Panshan to support the people they favor to take power.","Master, I only told you that after Dayan was divided by the three nations, due to their weak control over Dayan's territory and resistance from local forces, their power contracted within a few years due to internal political instability. This led to the emergence of temporary regimes like Great Liang, Great Wei, and Great Zhou.","In fact, apart from the rise of Dongyi, the other nations—Beili, Xiqiang, Nanyue, and Nanzhao—were also plagued by constant internal strife. Xiqiang and Beili didn't last many years before they followed Dayan into ruin.","Over the course of three hundred years, Nanzhao was annexed several times by the Nanyue dynasty, which saw frequent changes in rulers.","Although that Gan Tang later became the Emperor, she was also the last Emperor of Nanyue, assassinated in her sleep.","Her son fled and managed to establish a resistance force, but two years later, he was betrayed, defeated in battle, captured, and tortured to death.]","\"Hiss! Sounds like hardly anyone in this room has a good end!\"","[Exactly! Mortals only have a short lifespan of a few decades, yet they exhaust themselves scheming and deceiving for fame and fortune, only to meet terrible ends. I don't know what they're after!]","\"After who dies the most miserably?\"","[Speaking of miserable, Bei Yue might still be able to enjoy a brief period of glory under Bei Ji's deceptive flattery. That fool Bei Ye actually thinks Chancellor Wei will support him.","In reality, it's all an illusion used to confuse him and the court officials. They have joined forces with Bei Ji, openly repairing the gallery roads while secretly marching to Chencang.","Once Bei Yue falls, it will soon be Bei Ye's turn. The old emperor is letting him replace Bei Yue as the new target, all so his eighth son can smoothly inherit the throne.]","\"Tsk tsk tsk, how absurd! They are all his father's sons, but the difference between who he loves and who he doesn't is way too obvious!\"","[Just as absurd as Bei Ji is Xi Yan. Xi Yan isn't like Bei Ji, who is entirely focused on supporting the son of his favored concubine to take the throne.","He treats all his sons like Gu bugs, raising them to fight each other. He actually got this inspiration from Nanzhao.]","\"Raising Gu? Then Xi Yuanshan and Xi Ling must have it really rough!\"","Swept by Yue Fuguang's faint gaze, Xi Ling and Xi Yuanshan felt an icy chill in their hearts. A bone-piercing coldness engulfed their bodies, nearly freezing their very minds.","Unlike Xi Yuanshan, who was struck by the revelation that he was being schemed against and raised like a Gu bug by his own father, Xi Ling was more concerned about the phrase \"unknown father\"!","Wasn't his father Xi Yan? How could his father be unknown!","Thinking of the endless rumors surrounding the mystery of his birth mother since he could remember, Xi Ling lowered his head, concealing the cold gleam in his eyes.","Not only was his mother unknown, but his supposed biological father might also be fake. Could Xi Yuanshan truly be his cousin?","It wasn't that Xi Ling was completely oblivious in his heart, but he dared not dwell on it. He constantly warned himself that the matter of the heavenly voice had yet to be verified, so what it said could not be entirely trusted.","Therefore, when Xi Yuanshan looked over, he deliberately raised his wine cup and offered a distant toast to Xie Zhiyan.","Seeing Xi Ling's obvious evasion, Xi Yuanshan said no more. In truth, like Xi Ling and the others, he still did not fully believe in the heavenly voice.","Hearing the massive gossip regarding the royal families of various countries, the diplomatic mission was shrouded in gloom, while the monarch and officials of Dayan were filled with just as much joy.","They put into practice Emperor Mingxi's words before the banquet began: \"Today's gathering is all about enjoyment. Everyone, please make yourselves comfortable and do not be bound by formalities.\""]},{"number":377,"title":"Chapter 377: Who is Wei Xiang’s first love","paragraphs":["They toasted each other, exchanging cups back and forth in a lively atmosphere.","The military officials played drinking games, their voices rising higher and higher, while the civil officials were much more refined, composing poetry and matching couplets... It would have been even better if the poems these people were quoting weren't the ones Yue Fuguang had \"created\" during the Emperor's Birthday Banquet.","When she heard You Mingmin, the Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial, raise his wine cup to toast the Western Qiang delegation while reciting the line, \"I urge you to drink one more cup of wine,\" Yue Fuguang subconsciously picked up the fruit juice in front of her and took several gulps.","Awkward, it was truly too awkward!","[Master, there is something even more shocking. You see, Chancellor Wei rejected Bei Ji's courtship multiple times because he actually loved someone else in his heart. However, due to their statuses, the two could not be together.]","\"Oh, a woman who could catch the eye of the previous generation's Number One Young Master of Northern Li must be extraordinary. Little Zhu, quickly tell me, who exactly is Chancellor Wei's first love?\"","Not just Yue Fuguang, even Emperor Mingxi and his officials noticeably lowered their voices from their poetry and drinking games. Even those pretending to be drunk subconsciously rolled over, perking up their ears so as not to miss a single word.","The famous Chancellor Wei was of their generation, and they also wanted to know what the woman he loved looked like!","Only the two brothers, Bei Ye and Bei Yue, reacted differently. One snorted the wine he had just drunk out of his nose; Bei Ye quickly covered his mouth with a handkerchief, using the act of wiping to hide his flushed cheeks.","His imperial father and Chancellor Wei?","Then did he and Qingyi count as a continuation of their affection? It was a pity that Chancellor Wei did not know what was good for him. Not only did he reject his imperial father's courtship, but he also secretly fell in love with another woman!","Bei Ye thought about what would happen if Wei Qingyi treated him like this... He instantly felt the sweet fruit wine in his mouth turn bitter.","When Bei Yue heard his imperial father's romantic history, the corners of his mouth subconsciously curled into a mocking smile. His hand unknowingly rubbed the jade pendant he had worn at his waist for over three years, tracing the carved silk tree flowers on it over and over again.","He seemed unable to hear the heavenly voice anymore; his ears were filled with the sounds of his imperial father doting on him in public, only to repeatedly scold him in private for straying from the right path and being unrepentant!","Only today did he realize that the wrong path his imperial father kept calling a heresy was one he had walked himself!","Not only had he walked it, but he had also been rejected by his beloved!","Bei Yue took a large gulp of wine. Unfortunately, his father had feelings, but Chancellor Wei had no interest. How... pathetic!","Bei Yue even maliciously wondered if his imperial father was jealous that he could attain his lover!","[It is the Empress of Nanzhao, Lan Qiying. When Chancellor Wei was young and followed his father on a diplomatic mission to Nanzhao, he met Lan Qiying, who was still the Crown Princess at the time. Wei Yuqing fell in love with the beautiful Lan Qiying at first sight and was completely captivated upon their second meeting. He even considered marrying into Nanzhao. This describes how deeply infatuated Chancellor Wei was back then.]","When Lan Xuan'er heard the heavenly voice suddenly mention her imperial mother, and alongside the Prime Minister of Northern Li no less, she felt her blood rush to her head, her face turning completely red.","She was so shocked that she felt nailed to the spot, unable to move an inch. She had a secret in her heart that she had never spoken of to anyone.","She had known for a long time that she was not her father's child; she was simply given to her father to raise after her imperial mother gave birth to her.","Lan Xuan'er did not dare to look around. She always felt that the mystery of her birth, just like Xi Ling, was a scar that none of them wanted to uncover.","\"Did Bei Ji know about this?\" She did not need to elaborate on how strong the desire for control and possessiveness was in a man, especially an emperor.","[Of course he knew. That was why he was going crazy with jealousy at the time. It was also him who secretly allied with Old Man Wei to stop it, which was why Wei Yuqing failed to go to Nanzhao.","However, Chancellor Wei did not know any of this, because Bei Ji had not yet ascended the throne at that time. Although the Wei family secretly supported him, his grand cause had not yet been achieved, so the Wei family was still a target he needed to win over.","Therefore, even though he discovered his feelings for Chancellor Wei, he had to hide them for various reasons.","It could not be discovered by outsiders, especially Chancellor Wei's father, Old Man Wei, so everything was done in secret.","The funniest part is that Chancellor Wei at the time, known as the Number One Young Master of Northern Li, considered himself a confidant of Bei Ji. Having nowhere to express his deep love for Lan Qiying, Bei Ji became his sole listener!]","\"Hahaha, hahaha!\" Yue Fuguang's laughter echoed throughout the banquet hall, steadily overpowering the light melodies being played by the musicians.","Emperor Mingxi and his officials forced themselves not to rub their slightly aching ears. It could be said that when it came to acting, through years of accumulation, they were all professionals.","Unlike the few in the delegation, who were just short of covering their ears!","\"I finally know why, when looking through the chronicles and unofficial histories of various countries, I saw multiple records and speculations about the discord between the Emperor of Northern Li and the Emperor of Nanzhao.","The official history analyzes it based on politics, interests, and other factors, but the folk unofficial histories are much more exciting, entirely filled with the love-hate entanglements between the two.","It turns out this entanglement is real, just that the target was wrong. It wasn't that the two loved each other but couldn't have each other, but rather that they both loved the same person and couldn't have him!\"","Lan Xuan'er's hand holding the teacup trembled, and the warm tea spilled onto her hand, leaving a faint stain.","From the corner of her eye, she caught Bei Yue looking at her. Their eyes met, and then they quickly looked away.","Just as she was wondering if today's banquet was dragging on for too long, she heard the heavenly voice suddenly change the subject. [Master, look at the third dancer on the left in the center.]","Yue Fuguang looked over as told. It was a rather tall dancer wearing a thin beaded tassel veil, with a pair of fox-like eyes that naturally exuded charm when looking at people.","Although her face could not be seen clearly, just by looking at those eyes, one could tell she was a beauty.","\"What's wrong with this dancer?\" She didn't think the system would specifically bring her up just because she looked good.","[Master, he is a man. Not a ladyboy, but a man cross-dressing as a woman. The hairpins on his head are all concealed weapons.]","Without the system needing to say more, those who heard it had already guessed his identity.","The Great Yan monarch and officials all breathed a sigh of relief. The stage had been set for so long, and they had finally waited for the main character to perform.","Hearing this, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but take a few more glances at the person.","Just looking at that figure, graceful and lithe, like a tender willow sprouting in early March, soft yet possessing a nascent resilience.","And the way he looked at the guests... Yue Fuguang clicked her tongue in her heart. It was like the lingering threads of a broken lotus root, clinging and seductive!","With this charm that completely crushed the other dancers, if the system hadn't spoken up, who would have thought he was a genuine man!","Hearing that there was an assassin, the people in the delegation visibly relaxed. They finally didn't have to be forced to listen to their parents' love stories anymore!","Although they had heard a lot of seemingly useful information from it, without verification, they would not completely believe the words of the heavenly voice.","Gan Tang and Lan Xuan'er huddled together, eating pastries and whispering to each other, while the delegations from Northern Li and Western Qiang began to toast each other.","Only Yan Ji and Oshima, who had been out of the loop and couldn't hear anything, were still oblivious. Unaccustomed to the alcohol of Great Yan, the two had been thoroughly intoxicated during the first half of the banquet and had not yet sobered up.","[Master, look at the lead dancer again.]","\"Is she also a man cross-dressing?\""]},{"number":378,"title":"Chapter 378: The Killing Game Isn't Over Yet","paragraphs":["I have to say, this dancer had a tall and slender figure. As she danced, her fluttering dress occasionally revealed a flat abdomen with faintly visible, lean muscles. Looking closer, her exposed brow and eyes exuded a somewhat heroic, masculine spirit.","She looked more like a man than the other person.","[Not quite, Master. Her name is Du Shuirong, and she goes by the resounding nickname 'Poison Young Master'.]","\"Isn't Poison Young Master a man?\"","She had always been under the misconception, based on the title, that Poison Young Master was a man.","But she had forgotten that Black Widow wasn't a woman either!","Yue Fuguang was a bit speechless. The three weirdos of the martial arts world truly lived up to their reputation: a Drunken Rakshasa who was both yin and yang, and a Black Widow who was a man dressed as a woman.","And now here was Poison Young Master, who turned out to be a woman.","Yue Fuguang glanced at Wei Ping, whose excitement was practically written all over his face, and Cai Xian, who was staring at the dancer without even blinking.","If she didn't know that he just wanted to send her to the heavenly prison to reunite with Drunken Rakshasa and the others, she would have thought the elderly Cai Xian was lusting after the dancer.","[She just likes to dress up as a young master to hunt for romance; she's not a real man.]","Hunt for romance—was it the kind of romance she was thinking of?","Good heavens, the ancients in this world were not traditional in their thinking at all. First there were cut sleeves, and then mirror rubbers. Everyone had their own preferences!","\"Isn't Poison Young Master from Panshan? How did she get mixed up with the noble families?\"","[Master, Du Shuirong's original name was Bai Shuirong. She is the illegitimate daughter of the deceased Second Master of the Bai family, and she is also the cousin of the Third Crown Princess, Bai Nianzhu.","She later took her mother's surname. Her biological mother was originally from Nanzhao and was the Holy Maiden of the Immortality Sect.]","What a complicated background!","Yue Fuguang watched the dancers in the center of the hall begin to spin to the increasingly cheerful rhythm of the music. Poison Young Master was like an elegant and beautiful bird, drawing everyone's attention.","\"So, the Bai family and Panshan have been in cahoots for a long time? Then their family's demise was not unjust!\"","Just as Yue Fuguang's words fell, a sudden change occurred in the hall. The dancer who was a man dressed as a woman approached the Second Prince and suddenly pulled a gold hairpin from his head, stabbing it toward the prince's chest.","He even shouted, \"I'll kill you, you scumbag!\"","If one didn't know the truth, just this single sentence would be enough for everyone present to imagine a grand drama of love and hate.","Following his sudden attack, the Second Prince was forced into an awkward dodge. Before the guards could arrive, the other six dancers acted as if they were frightened, holding their heads and screaming in panic as they dodged.","While the Second Prince awkwardly dodged the most fatal strike and everyone's attention turned to them, Poison Young Master quickly slipped to the side of the Crown Prince, who was five or six meters away.","\"Watch out!\"","\"Protect His Highness!\"","With a clang, the sound of metal striking and falling to the ground came from beside the Crown Prince.","Song Xiang, disguised as a eunuch, appeared out of nowhere beside the Crown Prince. A short sword hidden at his waist blocked Poison Young Master's fatal strike just in time.","Xie Zhiyan neatly spun and retreated a few steps, while Song Xiang led the guards forward to fight with Poison Young Master.","The dancers hiding all over the place exchanged glances and suddenly rose up, attempting to attack the ministers closest to them.","\"Ah!\" Yue Fuguang heard a scream and looked toward the sound in the distance.","She saw five dancers. Out of four of them, two attacked Gan Tang and Bei Ye, while the other two headed toward the civil officials of Great Yan. Unfortunately, they lost the initiative and were kicked down by those who were already prepared.","Only the last person held a bloody gold hairpin, which flashed with a golden-red light under the lamps.","In front of her was a civil official from Great Yan. Yue Fuguang recognized him; his name was Song Bo. She wondered if he had been blinded by beauty.","During the chaos in the hall, he actually tried to use his fat body and greasy appearance to shield the beauty from the storm, protecting her behind him, only to be ruthlessly backstabbed.","\"You...\" He turned around slowly in disbelief, blood gushing from the corner of his mouth, his fat face filled with unwillingness and ferocity.","[Master, that person seems to have been hit in a vital spot. I'm afraid he will die from his severe injuries in a moment. Right now, no one can save his life except for your pills.]","\"Then should I wish him a safe journey?\"","[Master, you aren't going to save him?]","\"Why should I save him? To die under a peony flower, he should die with no regrets!\"","Out of the seven dancers, two assassins rushed at the prince and the Crown Prince. Everyone was exceptionally alert. Only this Song Bo was blinded by beauty. Even at a time like this, he didn't forget to pull a beauty into his arms. Yue Fuguang had seen him taking advantage of her just now; the dancer had only ended up behind him to dodge his groping hands. So if he didn't die, who would?","Emperor Mingxi couldn't quite maintain his composure. His minister acting so disgracefully made him, the sovereign father, lose a great deal of face in front of the diplomatic mission.","In a matter of moments, all six were taken down. As they were being pressed down, Du Shuirong deliberately cast a glance at the Third Prince. That glance contained too many indescribable 'feelings'?","Xie the Third was stunned by the look. As if suddenly realizing something, he said to the Crown Prince, \"Royal Brother, you must believe me. I don't know this woman!\"","Poison Young Master, who was about to step out of the main hall, suddenly turned around with a sorrowful face and said, \"Dear Xin~, Nianzhu is my cousin, and you actually say you don't know me!\"","Yue Fuguang was so provoked by her calling him Dear Xin that she almost threw up the pastries and tea she had just eaten.","Xie the Third was even worse off. He was so frightened that he took a few steps back, only stopping when he crashed into the pillar behind him.","His eyes widened as he stared in horror at the tall, thin back of Poison Young Master, who was already being dragged out of the hall by the guards.","Yue Fuguang saw his legs trembling non-stop, like an old man in his twilight years struggling to stand.","His terror was probably not just because he was publicly framed, but also because of Poison Young Master's identity as a member of the Bai family and Bai Nianzhu's cousin.","The assassins only targeted the Crown Prince and the Second Prince, completely ignoring Xie Zhixin, who was right nearby. This easily led people to think the worst.","He looked hopefully at Yue Fuguang, who had sat back down, hoping this immortal lord could say a word for him.","As long as her inner thoughts mentioned this matter, the truth would surely come to light, and his innocence would be restored.","At this moment, Xie Zhixin wanted to hear the inner thoughts of these two ancestors more than ever before.","Once everyone was seated, the knocked-over cups and plates had been swiftly cleaned up by the palace servants and replaced with new ones. Emperor Mingxi waved his large sleeve and ordered those below, \"Continue the music, continue the dance!\"","After Eunuch Qian refilled his wine, Emperor Mingxi stood up, raised his cup, and said loudly, \"Today was fraught with danger, but as long as our sovereign and ministers are of one heart, disasters will naturally dissipate. My lords, drink up this cup!\"","\"Thank you, Your Majesty! May Your Majesty live a long and boundless life, and may our Great Yan's national destiny be prosperous!\"","\"May Your Majesty live a long and boundless life, and may our Great Yan's national destiny be prosperous!\"","[Master, in this hall, besides the two of us, master and servant, who else has the ability to live a boundless life!]","\"Little Zhu, you can't blame mortals for having a wish for immortality.\"","The sovereign and ministers of Great Yan: Exactly, we are just thinking about it. Thinking about it doesn't cost any money.","The members of the diplomatic mission: What does this mean? What did we just hear? Junior Preceptor Yue and that mysterious figure actually said they could live a boundless life!","Could it be that they had truly met living immortals?","Hearing the talk of longevity, the people in the hall harbored their own hidden thoughts. Amidst the deafening roar of the crowd chanting their toasts, only Yue Fuguang frowned slightly as she caught sight of a few people's wine cups from the corner of her eye. Was this never going to end?"]},{"number":379,"title":"Chapter 379: Killing Game 2: Guessing","paragraphs":["Seeing the wine about to enter his throat, she quickly picked up a peanut from the desk and flicked it out with a whoosh.","The red, crispy peanut precisely struck the hand of the Crown Prince, who had already raised the cup to his lips.","Smack!","The white jade wine cup fell to the ground, but surprisingly, it didn't break!","Yue Fuguang: Her hand slipped, she didn't control her strength well, it was definitely not because her martial arts skills were lacking!","The Crown Prince looked at the cup that rolled twice on the ground, raised his head in surprise, and looked at Yue Fuguang with confusion. The Emperor and the various officials who were constantly paying attention to the situation at the high seats also looked at Yue Fuguang in bewilderment.","They didn't think she had any malicious intent towards the Crown Prince, but they just didn't understand the purpose of her action.","Some clever ones had already reacted—that wine...","\"Little Aunt, is there a problem with Zhiyan's wine?\" Xie Zhiyan suddenly realized what was going on while his imperial father was staring at the spilled liquor from his cup.","Yue Fuguang nodded with appreciation on her face and said, \"There is poison in the wine. Someone must have added it just now during the chaos.\"","It should be known that during the banquet, the wine and food presented were inspected by no less than three people together. It was not easy to poison them at that time.","But it was different once they were brought to the tables. Very few people would suspect that the wine they had been drinking safely would suddenly become poisoned.","So the assassination just now was the first move. After Poison Young Master and the others failed, the poison in this wine was the second move laid out by those people.","'Little Zhu, check and see what else has been poisoned besides the Crown Prince's wine.'","[Master, besides the Crown Prince's wine, there is also His Majesty's bird's nest porridge. Except for the Third Prince, the soup bowls of all the other princes and princesses also contain poison.]","Slam!","Emperor Mingxi heavily slammed his wine cup back onto the desk. \"Investigate! Investigate this thoroughly for me! I want to know who is so bold as to poison the Crown Prince right under my nose!\"","His tiger-like eyes shot towards Zheng Zicheng and Zhang Zhongping, who had already stood up to plead guilty. \"Minister Zhang, clear away all the food and drinks, and check if there are any others that have been poisoned!\"","\"Deputy Envoy Zheng, you will thoroughly investigate all the maids and eunuchs in the hall today. I want to know everyone's background!\"","After the two received their orders and left, Emperor Mingxi showed fatigue on his face. He waved his hand and said, \"It is getting late today. The banquet ends here. Everyone, disperse!\"","Hearing the words \"getting late,\" Yue Fuguang couldn't help but yawn. As she walked outside, she didn't forget to complain to the system, 'Little Zhu, these assassins are such a buzzkill, never-ending from morning till night!'","[Don't be angry, Master. They are not done yet. There is still a huge show tonight.]","'Are these assassinations serious? One act after another, the emperor definitely prepared in advance. What advantage can they possibly get?'","[Because some of them have already sneaked into the hunting grounds. The poison for the Crown Prince, princes, and princesses was administered by those people during the chaos.","Master, there is a secret skill in the martial arts world called human skin masks. Those people used human skin masks to swap identities with the palace servants and blend into the banquet.]","The Crown Prince, Wei Ping, and the others following behind her exchanged glances. Human skin masks, they had long heard of them. Even in the Imperial Prison, Wei Ping had once searched one out from Luo Feng.","As thin as cicada wings, shaped like human skin, with a soft and delicate touch. Unfortunately, Luo Feng also obtained it by accident and didn't know the production process.","'On the royal family's side, even the emperor couldn't escape it. Why is it that only the Third Prince wasn't poisoned? And the words of that Poison Young Master, was he trying to divert the disaster and stir up strife among the royal brothers?'","Hearing that the topic had finally come to him, Xie Zhixin, who had fallen a few steps behind everyone and was intentionally or unintentionally isolated by his brothers, became so emotional that tears streamed down his face!","Bei Ye, who was walking beside him, inexplicably glanced at this Third Prince of Dayan from the corner of his eye. He couldn't help but feel that this Third Prince, who was silently weeping as he walked yet smiling so joyfully at the same time, must be seriously ill in the head!","Could it be that the war of succession in Dayan is even more cruel than in their Beili? Look, it has driven a man completely mad!","[Xie the Third is just a huge scapegoat. Keeping him alive serves two purposes: first, to make him take the blame; second, if he luckily avoids suspicion, after the royal heirs and the emperor are all dead, they will push him to the throne. After all, this man is also a son-in-law of an aristocratic family and can be considered half an ally.","Once Bai Nianzhu gives birth to a son, they can eliminate the father and keep the son. Even if the Third Princess Consort is unwilling, what can she do? As an orphan and widow, they can then easily control the emperor to command the nobles. Ultimately, Dayan will still be in the hands of the aristocratic families.]","Xie Zhixin: I really thank you for considering me an ally! Eliminate the father and keep the son? To hell with that! Thank your whole family JPG.","Xie Zhixin silently gritted his teeth, his delayed rebellious phase suddenly striking him.","He would not take the blame, and he definitely wouldn't sit on the throne! Do not cue JPG.","He looked through the crowd at Yue Fuguang walking at the very front. With this ancestor around, it was most suitable for him to safely be a carefree prince!","[As for the words of Poison Young Master, they were openly meant to provoke the relationship between the royal brothers. As long as a tiny seed of doubt is planted.","The current balance and stability among the princes could be broken.","The internal stability of the royal family is the last thing the aristocratic families and Panshan want to see.]","Emperor Mingxi nodded, while the group of princes and princesses trailing behind him looked thoughtful.","...","Inside Beiyue's large tent, except for the two dead-drunk brothers from Dongyi, all the other parties were gathered together.","Although their countries had often joined forces in the past, each person had their own hidden agendas. This was the first time they sat so intimately around a single table.","Seeing the others remain silent, as the host, Beiyue was the first to speak. \"My fifth brother and I have already asked several officials of our Beili diplomatic mission. None of them heard those two voices.\" To prevent eavesdropping, Beiyue kept his mouth shut about Yue Fuguang's name.","The others nodded. \"It is the same for us!\"","A sharp gleam flashed across Xi Ling's eyes as he said, \"Could it be that only the few of us are favored by the heavens and can hear the voices from heaven?\"","\"Do you think the ruler and officials of Dayan also heard the heavenly voices?\" Lan Xuan'er frowned. Based on her understanding of the Dayan court, she couldn't help but feel that their reactions from the Crown Prince's attack until the end of the banquet were somewhat strange.","But she couldn't pinpoint exactly what the problem was.","Gan Tang said, \"Sister Xuan'er is the most familiar with the Dayan court. If even you can't tell, the rest of us definitely can't be sure.\"","After all, she had been serving as an envoy to Dayan since she was fourteen. When it came to familiarity with Dayan, only Beiyue among those seated could match her.","Bei Ye rubbed the teacup in his hand and said quietly, \"Let's set aside whether the Dayan court can hear it or not. We need to figure out why it's the few of us who can hear it.\"","His gaze seemed to pierce through the large tent towards where the Dongyi diplomatic mission was staying. \"Those two brothers from Dongyi don't seem to be able to hear it either. Also, we are still not sure if the heavenly voices are trustworthy. Furthermore...\"","He looked around at the group. \"One of the voices is definitely Junior Preceptor Yue, but who is the other one? Do you really believe her identity as a goddess descended from heaven?\"","Could this be a trap set by the Dayan court, using some secret information they knew to set them up here?","They didn't see Yue Fuguang's mouth moving, so who's to say she wasn't using ventriloquism? Don't forget, she seemed to know martial arts."]},{"number":380,"title":"Chapter 380: How Much of Heavenly Voices Can Be Trusted","paragraphs":["Prince Xiyuan Shan continued, \"Only we can hear it. Is it a conspiracy or a blessing from heaven? It's really hard to say, isn't it, second brother?\" He looked at Xi Ling, who had been silent.","Xi Ling forced a bitter smile and didn't want to respond.","Gan Tang pursed her lips and stared fixedly at the teacup in front of her, saying softly, \"Then how much truth do you think there is in the words of the Heavenly Voice?\"","She held the cup with both hands, as if trying to draw a moment of warmth from it to soothe her icy and shivering body and mind at this moment.","\"As far as I know, my father's sudden death is indeed related to the Cult of Immortality. Although this is a secret of the royal family of Nanyue, there are still a few people in the royal family who know the inside story.","I accidentally found out about it when I was secretly investigating the mystery of my mother's and elder brother's deaths.\" These pieces of information were obtained at a high price, so their credibility was quite high.","She looked around at the others and said, \"In my Nanzhao, at least 70% of what the Heavenly Voice said is true.\"","Since it involved the deaths of her mother and elder brother, regardless of why that voice let her hear it and what conspiracy was behind it, now that she knew the truth, she would verify it one by one and avenge them at all costs.","Regarding this matter, she wondered how much the Jiang family and that imperial concubine, now the empress dowager, were involved! Since the Heavenly Voice said that her father was one of the manipulators, then there might be a second or even a third.","Gan Sheng! Her dear elder brother, how much did he know and how much did he participate in?","Seeing that Gan Tang had already exposed the family scandal, Prince Xiyuan Shan looked at Xi Ling sitting on his right again with a half - smile and said, \"Second brother, do you know what Xi Yi and Xi Qiao did regarding my marriage?\"","In response to Prince Xiyuan Shan's question, Xi Ling didn't answer immediately. Instead, he lowered his eyes and thought for a moment before saying, \"Since Prince Yi asks, I won't hide it.\"","His tone was sincere. \"At the palace banquet that day, the drugs in your and Princess Yi's wine were indeed done by several brothers working together.","Although I didn't participate in it, I was also guilty of not reporting it.\"","He raised the teacup in his hand and said seriously, \"I'll use tea instead of wine to apologize to you, brother.\" Then he drank the tea in the cup in one gulp.","Prince Xiyuan Shan didn't drink the tea that Xi Ling offered immediately. He casually swirled the slightly cool tea in his hand. In the pale - yellow tea soup, several green tea leaves were rising and falling.","He said coldly, \"I recently accidentally learned a piece of news. Whether it's Xi Yi or Xi Qiao, they were all being used as guns!","There is another person behind the scenes manipulating this matter!\"","Seeing that Prince Xiyuan Shan didn't drink the tea he offered, Xi Ling wasn't angry. There was still a sign on him indicating that his father was unknown. If everyone confirmed that what the Heavenly Voice said was true, then... He looked at the people who knew the situation, especially Prince Xiyuan Shan, this brother who had an interest conflict with him.","How could he keep his secret and identity...","Hearing Prince Xiyuan Shan's words, he couldn't help frowning and said, \"Brother, do you mean... Father?\"","The Heavenly Voice had said that their father was raising them brothers like poisonous insects, sitting back and watching them fight to the death to determine the winner.","Prince Xiyuan Shan shook his head. \"It's Xi Xiang. He had already joined hands with the powerful officials in the court, and he also had a candidate in mind for the princess.","Xi Yi and the others were all led by him to do this. He seemed to be a victim, but in fact, he was the one holding the knife.","As for our dear father... He should have taken in all the actions of everyone!\"","As he spoke, Xi Ling recalled carefully. Suddenly, he opened his eyes in horror and stammered, \"So, so since then, Father has shown a lot of favor to the fourth brother and arranged for him to gain experience in the Ministry of Personnel...\"","It turned out that it wasn't compensation for his princess being'snatched', not a sudden outburst of fatherly love, not appeasement, but a reward! A reward for this son's means of playing everyone in the palm of his hand!","The stronger one was, the more Father would support him. But he was also outstanding among the brothers back then, the most favored son by Father both in the court and the public, and his power was constantly expanding. Now, wasn't he being suppressed everywhere?","Was it because Father began to suspect that he wasn't his own son, or because his power was about to threaten the imperial power?","Xi Xiang today was very much like himself yesterday. What means did he have to prevent himself from becoming today's Xi Ling?","Father was old, but his might as a tiger remained. Could this young tiger, Xi Xiang, fight against his father...","Prince Xiyuan Shan drank the completely cooled tea in the cup in one gulp. The bitter taste made him frown slightly. He told himself that the tea had been brewed for too long and was too strong.","Bei Ye and the others understood what the two brothers meant. In Xiqiang, what the Heavenly Voice said was at least as credible as in Nanyue, about 70%.","Bei Yue tapped his finger on the table rhythmically, and finally he gave a heavy tap, making a loud \"thud\" sound, which was particularly harsh in the quiet tent.","He gritted his teeth and said in a deep voice, \"To be honest with you all, more than three years ago, I noticed that my father's so - called favor towards me had other intentions.\"","He looked at Bei Ye with pity in his eyes. \"I was set up as a target for my brothers to attack, and you, fifth brother, are my successor.","I think you've also noticed that my favor from Father has declined in the past two years because I ordered my subordinates to shrink my power, and Father also noticed that I was secretly investigating...\"","\"So Father found out that you, this chess piece, had other thoughts and didn't want to continue fighting according to his plan, so he supported me!!\"","Indeed, Father's favor towards him had been increasing in the past two years, and it had started since his first mission to Dayan.","He had thought at that time that it was because Wei Qingyi had spoken well of him in front of Prime Minister Wei. Now, thinking about it, it's not certain which side Prime Minister Wei was on!","Then, which side would Qingyi support? The eighth brother or him?","Seeing that the others were exposing their family scandals without reservation, Lan Xuan'er also said softly, \"As for the matter between my mother - emperor and Prime Minister Wei, I'll secretly investigate it when I go back. You two elder brothers, please also take the trouble to investigate Prime Minister Wei.\"","As for the possibility that Prime Minister Wei might be her father, she would never say it. There was no evidence, and it wasn't something to be proud of.","Bei Ye said, \"Don't worry, younger sister. Even if you didn't say it, for our own future and destiny, we'll do our best to investigate!\"","The several people looked at each other. Although only Gan Tang said that what the Heavenly Voice said was at least 70% credible, in their hearts, they believed it about 80% to 90%.","They just didn't know why only they could hear it! If it was a matter of status, what was lacking in the two brothers from Dongyi?","Could it be that they were disliked by the Heavenly Voice because they drank too much?","And what about the monarchs and ministers of Dayan? Did they also hear it? Did they only hear it today, or had they started hearing it several years ago? This was actually really important!","Why? This was also the question of the system at this moment.","Yue Fuguang thought for a while and said, \"A great disaster is approaching. When several countries are affected, Dayan, this granary, will definitely be targeted by several parties.","With Dayan's current national strength, it can't fight on all fronts without defeat for the time being. So, the internal affairs of each country can't be too stable.\"","She smiled and said, \"When it comes to causing trouble, who is more suitable than these princes and princesses? They have the status, means, and position.","They have both hatred and grievances in their hearts. They are all chess pieces. As long as the emperor doesn't fall, none of them can ascend to a higher position.","Moreover, after knowing that even if they destroy Dayan, their own countries won't last long, these people will become the biggest advocates of peace in their countries!\""]},{"number":381,"title":"Chapter 381: Hundred Birds Paying Homage to the Phoenix","paragraphs":["She only needed them to stall for a little time for Great Yan.","As for their suspicions about her identity, it didn't matter!","As long as it was proven that she wasn't lying, even if they knew it was a conspiracy, they would still follow the script she had written for them in order to save themselves.","[Host, aren't you afraid that once they find out, those few will join forces?]","\"So what if they join forces? You placed the strictest restrictions on them. They cannot speak of it to outsiders, only to each other. They will naturally harbor a bit more awe and deliberation in their hearts.\"","Yue Fuguang looked at the large stacks of beautifully engraved plastic cards in the system space, bearing inciting slogans like \"The Five Kings perish, the Four Seas unite\" and \"The Divine Maiden descends, the Mandate of Heaven lies with Yan.\"","There would come a day to use them!","Yue Fuguang let out a big yawn as she spoke, climbing into bed while telling the system, \"I'm going to sleep first. Remember to keep an eye on things outside. Unless the Emperor or the Crown Prince is about to kick the bucket, even if the sky falls, it can wait until tomorrow!\"","Yue Fuguang thought drowsily that sleeping too little would stunt her growth, though she hadn't slept any less and didn't seem to have grown much taller either. Fortunately, she might be able to leave in a few years, otherwise, being stuck with this height until she grew old...","Chirp chirp chirp!","Chatter chatter!","Chirp chirp chirp chirp!","Chatter chatter chatter!","Yue Fuguang woke up to this annoying chirping and chattering argument. Although she didn't know what they were cursing about, judging by the commotion, both sides were swearing quite dirtily.","The moment she sat up, Cuizhu heard the noise, called out a greeting, and immediately brought two little maids in with water to serve Yue Fuguang as she washed up.","While helping Yue Fuguang wash and dress, Cuizhu casually asked, \"Miss, will you have breakfast first, or go out to take a look?\"","Yue Fuguang toyed with a box of exquisite jewelry on her dressing table and asked, \"What's going on outside? What's all this chirping and arguing about?\"","She had just recognized the calls of her own Taxue among the noise. With such a loud voice, it was probably taking on a whole flock of little birds single-handedly without losing the upper hand.","Speaking of this, the dimples on Cuizhu's cheeks deepened. Her hands moved nimbly to style Yue Fuguang's hair as she said in a crisp voice, \"You don't know yet, Miss! Our Taxue saw the tits in the woods being bullied by jackdaws, so it went up and chased all the jackdaws away.","But then a flock of magpies came and landed on that big tree behind our tent. When Taxue saw them, it tried to chase them away too. However, not only did the magpies refuse to leave, but they also flew over to the persimmon tree next to it. Once Taxue saw these uninvited guests occupying its fruit tree, it immediately lost its temper.\"","Cuizhu inserted the last small gold hairpin into Yue Fuguang's hair, pouting her lips toward the outside. \"So they started arguing. Before you woke up, Miss, they almost got into a real fight.\"","Yue Fuguang also found it amusing. \"Aren't tits the food of Taxue and Wuhen?\" Standing up for its own food—that was exactly the kind of bird-brained thing the shrewd Taxue would do!","\"The magpies here are quite arrogant, daring to squabble with the lords of the sky?\" Weren't they afraid of becoming their next meal?","Cuizhu laughed, \"These birds have been flying back and forth outside your tent since early this morning, Miss. Many of them landed on the trees around our tent. If it weren't for Taxue and Wuhen, there would be even more. This servant feels they are here for you, Miss.\"","Cuiyu, who walked in lifting the tent flap, heard this and chimed in with a smile, \"Sister Cuizhu is right. Could it be that the birds have also heard of our Miss's name as the Divine Maiden and come to pay their respects!\"","Cuizhu nodded seriously, agreeing wholeheartedly. \"They say all things have spirits. These little creatures are very spiritual; they must know the Divine Maiden is staying here.\"","Yue Fuguang smiled and shook her head at their words. She didn't believe the theory that the birds were coming for her.","She knew her own truth. The Divine Maiden was just a disguise, not her core. There was no leaking divine aura for the creatures here to sense.","She licked her lips. She certainly hadn't eaten a small amount of the wild game at the banquet last night.","As soon as Yue Fuguang and the others stepped out of the tent, they turned and saw several large trees behind them densely packed with numerous birds. The key was that there were many different species, big and small, all of which were the most common varieties in this mountain forest.","Seeing her appear, Taxue, who had been squawking the loudest, immediately fell silent. It and Wuhen quickly flew toward Yue Fuguang.","They landed on her left and right at her feet.","Flap, flap!","Before Yue Fuguang could bend down to smooth the somewhat messy feathers of the two large birds, the birds perched on the surrounding trees suddenly flapped their wings and took flight.","Cheep!","Chirp!","Tweet!","Chatter!","Amidst various birdcalls, even more birds flew out from the forest. They chirped and circled above Yue Fuguang's head, refusing to leave, and their ranks grew increasingly massive.","Yue Fuguang looked up, only to see that the sunlight above was almost entirely blocked by the dense flock of birds. With a great rustling of wings, there were at least a thousand of them.","What was going on? Were the birds holding a general assembly over her head?","\"System, keep an eye out for me. Don't let some bird with no civic virtue poop on my head!\"","Seeing the situation before her, for some reason, Yue Fuguang didn't think about earthquakes or natural disasters. Her first reaction was worry—worrying that in this moment, one of them might not be able to hold it in and drop something on her!","The image was too beautiful; she didn't dare to imagine it!","[Host, it's not just the birds flying here. Look closely; there are many animals hidden in the surrounding forest. There are three tigers alone! There's also a wolf pack, dozens of wild boars, and a big clumsy bear behind the rocks next door.]","Yue Fuguang frowned and looked toward the distant mountains and forests. There really seemed to be things moving in the shadowy thickets.","At this time, the flock of birds above her head was still growing, and the commotion here quickly attracted Emperor Mingxi and the others.","The Yu father and son looked at the flock of birds in the sky with worried faces and said, \"Fuguang, are you alright? Is there some kind of warning with the birds acting like this?\"","They hadn't forgotten the various books Yue Fuguang had brought out over the past two years, which included information on animal warnings before an earth dragon turned over.","They couldn't help but feel this was very similar to the current situation. Could it be that the drought was going to be accompanied by an earthquake?","Yue Fuguang shook her head. She understood her grandfather's meaning, but the system had shown absolutely no reaction regarding whether an earthquake would happen in Great Yan at this time and place, which proved it probably wasn't an earthquake.","However, just to be safe, she still told the system, \"System, try to sense if there's any possibility of an earthquake.\"","Seeing Yue Fuguang shake her head meant there was no danger of an earthquake. \"If it's not a warning, then what's going on with these birds?\" Yu Zhongchun frowned as he looked at the flock of birds circling in the sky. Suddenly thinking of something, he said to Yu Chongshan, \"Father, I once read about the legend of A Hundred Birds Worshipping the Phoenix in a miscellaneous record.\"","His furrowed brows slowly relaxed, and his eyes grew brighter as he looked at Yue Fuguang. \"A Hundred Birds Worshipping the Phoenix is an auspicious omen.\"","As for whether this auspicious omen manifesting on a subject rather than the royal family would cause the Emperor to be wary, the Yu father and son weren't worried.","Couldn't they see the joyful expression on Emperor Mingxi's face as he strode over?","Gan Tang and the others following behind Emperor Mingxi silently exchanged glances. The complexity in that look was something only the few who had heard the heavenly voice would understand.","The suspicions in their hearts were melting away bit by bit. Going from struggling with Yue Fuguang's identity to believing in it had only taken a single night."]},{"number":382,"title":"Chapter 382: Good Omen or Warning","paragraphs":["Gu-ah— Gu-ah—","Just as everyone looked up at the sky, they saw over a dozen large birds flying gracefully out of the distant pine forest.","As they flew closer and their appearances became clear, someone shouted loudly, Your Majesty, they are immortal cranes! Immortal cranes!","Immortal cranes were praised by the world as auspicious birds symbolizing longevity. Seeing over a dozen at once, each with an elegant and immortal posture, everyone cried out that this was a sign of great fortune.","The crowd instantly boiled over with discussion. It seemed as if these auspicious birds could take away the impending drought.","People's eyes shone. The gloom of last night's fierce battle was diluted by this morning's chorus of a hundred birds, especially when they saw the cranes circling above their heads, prompting continuous congratulations to Emperor Mingxi.","Even the members of the diplomatic mission had to admit that this was indeed a sign of good fortune.","Only Yue Fuguang, who had received a scientific compulsory education and experienced the most unscientific of things, harbored doubts about this scene in her heart.","As the saying goes, she knew her own worth very well. The appearance of these birds was a bit unusual.","System, are you sure there is no earthquake?","Rest assured, Host. I spent a massive amount of energy probing underground, and found no anomalies within a hundred miles.","The system then glanced at the Great Yan monarch and his officials, who were so caught up in the so-called auspicious signs that they only knew how to say auspicious words and lacked any sense of crisis. It could not help but complain, Master, what are these people getting so excited about? These birds are not coming for the emperor.","The officials who had just been endlessly showering the emperor with flattery suddenly did not know whether to spit out the words on the tip of their tongues. Their faces turned bright red, unsure if it was from embarrassment or shame at their own previous words.","Emperor Mingxi coughed lightly. Just as he was about to speak, the dozen or so immortal cranes traced a beautiful arc in the air and landed one after another in front of Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang: They really are coming for me!","Their long wings slowly folded. With a highly human-like Gu-ah— cry toward her, their slender necks bent into an elegant arc, their red crowns lowered, and their beaks lightly touched the ground.","Standing on one leg in a golden rooster posture, they silently demonstrated their submission to Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang looked down at the cranes, which were barely shorter than her. The touch of vermilion on the top of their heads was especially striking between the pure white and ink black.","Just as the cranes submitted, the hundred birds fell silent. They fluttered down onto the surrounding ground without fear of humans. Only then did Yue Fuguang see clearly.","Some held the brightest and most beautiful feathers in their beaks, while others carried fruits still bearing crystal dewdrops.","There were even a few vermilion birds and monal pheasants carrying ginseng with broken roots and dark red lingzhi mushrooms in their beaks.","Sun Huajing looked over and over again, his eyes full of heartache. This ginseng looked to be over a hundred years old, right?","And this lingzhi mushroom grew so well!","These birds did not know how to dig properly. They took good ginseng and broke all the roots off the main stem. How much medicinal efficacy must have been lost!","And that large lingzhi mushroom had damaged edges.","Do you need something? Yue Fuguang did not know if they could understand her words.","She was not narcissistic enough to think these birds were really paying homage to her like a hundred birds to a phoenix. Bringing gifts and acting so submissive meant they definitely had a favor to ask.","Little Zhu, help translate and see what these little guys want from me.","Gu-ah—","Gu-ah—","The cranes cried out a few times, turned their long necks toward the depths of the mountain forest, and cried out a few more times in that direction.","Cluck!","Cluck!","The forest responded with a chorus of clucking sounds, followed by several large, snow-white swans flying out from within.","They landed in front of Yue Fuguang with equal elegance, their long swan necks also bending into elegant arcs like the cranes.","Their forms could not help but remind Yue Fuguang of a birthday in her childhood when she received a music box with a spinning swan carved into it from her father.","That was one of the few times in her memory when her father's gift was not a black card, but a carefully chosen present. Therefore, she had treasured that music box for many years.","Master, the cranes say there are humans hiding in the mountain forest. They smell danger. The swans came from the direction of the great lake; those people, some have hidden in the water.","The system took the cranes' intermittent expressions, processed them, and relayed them to Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang lowered her eyes and thought about the meaning of these disjointed words. It was certain that people were hiding in the forest. If they were not the imperial court's people, they were assassins sent by the noble families.","She had woken up a bit late today and had not had time to ask about the emperor's harvest during the night. Could it be they had not cleaned up properly, allowing fish that slipped through the net to hide in the woods and disturb the birds inside?","No, if it was as she guessed, then what was going on with those fierce beasts hiding in the forest?","They could not possibly be dissatisfied with the food delivered to their door!","The Great Yan monarch and officials simultaneously thought of this possibility. Although the large net they cast last night had not caught all the fish.","But those who slipped through the net could not make any waves. Therefore, Emperor Mingxi had sent a large number of personnel into the forest in pursuit. Victory was in his grasp, so he was not anxious at all.","Your Majesty, are there still guards in the forest?","Yes, you did not know last night, but a group of assassins entered the hunting ground camp. Although most were caught, a few slipped away and hid in the mountains.","Shen Jian and Wei Shouyi took men into the forest, and I expect it will not be long before they capture everyone.","Yue Fuguang glanced at the ground, which had been cleaned but still bore obvious traces. A thick layer of dirt had been shoveled away; did this mean a lot of blood had flowed?","How many people did Your Majesty send in? Where are they all right now?","Yue Fuguang looked at the birds in front of her, then glanced at the faint silhouettes in the distant mountain forest, feeling a rather bad premonition.","Emperor Mingxi gestured to Huo Ying behind him. Huo Ying immediately stepped forward and said, Reporting to the Junior Preceptor, from last night to this morning, three thousand one hundred men have gone in successively. The latest news is that they have spread a net and searched up to thirty miles away, found traces of the assassins, and are currently pursuing them all the way forward.","Minister Huo, how many assassins came last night, and how many hunting ground guards do we have left now?","After a brief thought, Huo Ying replied, Last night, there were about a hundred and seventy to eighty assassins. We captured a total of one hundred and thirty-two assassins, of which seventy-eight were taken alive.","Our camp's Royal Guards still have one thousand eight hundred men, and there are over five hundred other guards.","At this time, Huo Ying also had a bad premonition and could not help but ask, Has the Junior Preceptor thought of something?","Yue Fuguang was a bit speechless. A few dozen people ran away, and they transferred over three thousand guards away. This strategy of luring the tiger from the mountain was so obvious; she did not believe the emperor and the others could not see it.","The main camp here only had a little over two thousand combatants left to protect such a large group of people at the very top of the Great Yan Dynasty's pyramid. How could that be enough!","Yue Fuguang cast a suspicious glance at the emperor. Could it be that the emperor had a backup plan and was deliberately beating them at their own game?","Regardless of whether the emperor had a backup plan or not, Yue Fuguang decided to first resolve the danger in the mountain forest. She did not believe the emperor's backup plan could solve the crisis in the woods."]},{"number":383,"title":"Chapter 383: Thunder and Rain","paragraphs":["For flocks of birds to be startled into flight and fierce beasts to flee in panic, this was no small matter. But how did these birds think to come to her for help?","Could it be that there were some among them as intelligent and spiritual as Taxue!","\"Little Zhu, scan the mountains and see where there might be major risks.\"","After issuing the command to the system, Yue Fuguang looked at Emperor Mingxi, Huo Ying, and the other officials, saying, \"Your Majesty, my lords, according to the information you have gathered, how many people have the noble families mobilized this time?\"","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers exchanged glances, then raised their eyes to sweep over the members of the diplomatic mission, who had been standing to the side watching the show without uttering a single word.","Meeting the emperor's gaze, the group merely smiled politely, showing absolutely no intention of taking the hint and leaving.","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but follow Emperor Mingxi's gaze and glance at them. Tsk tsk, as expected of people cultivated by the royal family, their skin was unusually thick.","Regarding Yue Fuguang's question, Emperor Mingxi did not hide anything and directly said, \"The noble families have mobilized about two thousand seven hundred people this time. They are all death-sworn assassins and private troops raised by the families, as well as some domestic servants and guards.\"","To even use domestic servants and guards, it seemed the noble families were truly betting their entire fortunes this time, planning a fight to the bitter end with the emperor.","Since that was the case... \"Your Majesty, since the noble families have even sent their domestic servants and guards, have you ever considered that they might have hired assassins?\"","Yue Fuguang pointed to the distant mountain forest and said, \"Over the course of yesterday, they lost no more than seven or eight hundred people. So where are the rest of them?\"","[Master, I found them. There are assassins hiding in multiple locations in the forest, numbering over a hundred. They... the woods around them have been drenched in oil!]","The situation was urgent. Ignoring the energy consumption, the system immediately broadcasted a live feed for Yue Fuguang. When the live broadcast appeared, the monarch and ministers of Great Yan remained relatively calm, as it wasn't their first time seeing it.","The members of the diplomatic mission, however, were so shocked that they staggered back several steps. If it weren't for their years of royal education and martial arts training, which gave them steady temperaments and firm stances, their weak legs would have caused them to collapse to the ground.","Fortunately, although they wanted to watch the show, they also knew not to be too annoying, so they stood a bit further away.","Therefore, regarding their abnormal behavior and pale, ghost-like faces, Yue Fuguang and the Great Yan monarch and ministers unanimously pretended not to see anything.","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers had already discussed in private last night that the members of the diplomatic mission could hear the Junior Preceptor's inner voice, although it was still unknown whether this was a blessing or a curse.","But even if the emperor and his ministers had any thoughts, they had to wait until these people left the territory of Great Yan to act on them.","Fortunately, this matter could not be communicated to those who couldn't hear it, so they were temporarily forced to keep the secret.","Lan Xuan'er and Gan Tang, the two women, supported each other tightly, leaning against one another with expressions of sheer disbelief, yet they couldn't help but look at the scene in mid-air with amazement.","The people from Northern Yue either clenched their fists or tremblingly rested their hands on the exquisite sabers at their waists. Only Yanji and Oshima looked on in bewilderment at the group's sudden change in complexion and slightly trembling bodies.","It was as if they had suddenly suffered some sort of fright. But the two brothers looked up at the sky and all around; the things that were flying in the sky were now obediently squatting on the ground. There was nothing special!","Could it be that there was some hidden meaning in the conversation between the Great Yan emperor and his ministers that they had missed?","Yanji couldn't help but scratch his head, standing on his tiptoes and craning his neck to look inside. Hateful that he was too short; he could only hear the conversation but couldn't see the specific situation inside.","The people from Western Ling turned a blind eye to the comical expressions of these two oddballs from Eastern Yi.","Right now, they were not only frightened by the clear situation of the mountain forest projected in the air, but they also imagined what would happen if this move was used when two armies faced off...","Then the enemy's military formations would have absolutely no secrets left. What would be the point of fighting? Just offering up their heads?","As the scene rotated, the entire image was divided into more than ten smaller screens. Each screen showed varying numbers of people, ranging from ten to twenty. Without exception, there were large, obvious oil stains nearby them.","Everyone's hearts trembled. Was this going to be a fire attack? It hadn't rained for months, and this mountain forest couldn't withstand even a single spark, let alone with oil added!","The system kindly marked the specific location of each point on the map within a hundred miles around the hunting ground.","The monarch and ministers of Great Yan watched with pounding hearts. These dozen or so fire points enclosed everyone within a potential inferno. This was meant to bury the entire mountain forest along with them!","Emperor Mingxi gritted his teeth. The noble families truly had good calculations, and they were ruthless enough!","The complexions of the diplomatic mission members were even uglier than those of the Great Yan monarch and ministers. It wasn't that they were worried about their own safety.","Rather, a sense of powerless despair lingered in their hearts, enveloping them like heavy, sunless dark clouds, pressing down so hard they couldn't catch their breath.","If they still had a trace of guardedness and suspicion towards the Heavenly Voice yesterday, seeing such a scene now made their hearts quail.","Looking again at the smiling Yue Fuguang, an unprovoked sense of dread welled up within them. Great Yan had a Divine Maiden. Let alone talk of swallowing Great Yan, all their previous plots against Great Yan would vanish like bubbles before Yue Fuguang!","The first thing they should be considering now wasn't who to annex, but what they could use to save their own dynasties.","Seeing this encirclement, Yue Fuguang was also filled with lingering fear. Fortunately, these people probably wanted to use their numbers to lure more of the Royal Guards into the woods, thereby burying them all in one fell swoop, which was why they had delayed making their move.","Normally, a fire caused by oil cannot be put out with water. But luckily, the fire hadn't started yet. Yue Fuguang, with her hands behind her back, prepared to solve the problem immediately.","[Master, what do you plan to do? Do you want Little Zhu to strike them with lightning and just hack them all to death?]","Hearing the chilling murderous intent in the Divine Artifact's words, everyone couldn't help but shrink their necks.","\"Little Zhu, you can't strike them with lightning. If the sparks ignite the mountains, it'll be troublesome.\"","[It seems oil can't be put out with water either.]","Yue Fuguang said, \"We can use a combo attack.\"","As her words fell, everyone saw the image in the air suddenly darken. The sunlight in the sky was blocked by dark clouds, and in mere moments, a fierce storm of wind and rain broke out.","The rain had only fallen for a brief moment before turning into heavy, swirling snow. The rainwater on the ground rapidly froze into ice. Especially in the areas with large oil stains, the ice and snow congealed into a yellowish-brown color.","Just as everyone was shocked by Yue Fuguang's methods, rumble—","Rumble—","Crackle!","Crackle!","Lightning flashed and thunder rolled. In the broadcast, those people first held their heads and looked for a place to shelter from the rain, then they were so shocked by the October snowfall that they forgot to hide. Shivering, they stood there blankly, not knowing if it was out of fear or the freezing cold.","Before they could sober up from the successive weather changes, the rumbling sound of thunder came from above their heads.","They instinctively looked up and saw the last glimmer of light in their lives, the lightning that accompanied the thunder.","The lightning illuminated their eyes, and it also took away all the light within them.","By the time the hundred-plus people fell after being struck by lightning, their bodies had already turned into charred corpses, occasionally emitting gray smoke and residual sparks of electricity.","Seeing this, Gan Tang and Lan Xuan'er were so terrified that they stumbled back several steps.","Their originally pale faces were now flushed with an abnormal redness. Large beads of sweat rolled down their temples, hanging precariously from their delicate jaws, on the verge of dropping."]},{"number":384,"title":"Chapter 384: Has the Crisis Been Resolved","paragraphs":["Bei Ye wasn't faring any better. Especially Bei Ye—over the past few years, he had personally commanded or participated in planning several assassination attempts against Yue Fuguang.","If she wanted revenge, there might not even be a speck of his bones left!","The high-ranking officials of various countries had long known that the Junior Preceptor of Great Yan could summon heavenly lightning. They originally thought her abilities were limited to what she displayed during the Longevity Festival in the fourth year of Yuankang, which was at most enough to knock someone unconscious.","Who could have known that not only could she summon the wind and rain, but she could also call down heavenly lightning to strike hundreds of people dead at once? Her methods and ruthless nature made them deeply fear her from the bottom of their hearts.","Especially the fact that she could actually control rain! Given the current time, when a severe drought seemed imminent, if Great Yan had this Junior Preceptor Yue, what drought would they have to fear?","They just didn't know how much area her rainfall could cover with her current level of power.","The sovereign and ministers of Great Yan weren't as pale as the members of the diplomatic mission. Although their hearts also trembled a few times with the sound of the thunder, they had seen the world, so they could still hold steady, right?","The sovereign and ministers of Great Yan: Not steady at all! Mentally hugging themselves tightly.","Although some of them had seen the Junior Preceptor strike the Cao family with lightning with their own eyes, they had never seen her take over a hundred lives in a single move!","Even if it were a hundred pigs, a martial arts master would have to expend some effort to deal with them. Not like their great, omnipotent Junior Preceptor, who annihilated them all in an instant.","The crowd didn't realize that even when they mentioned Yue Fuguang in their minds, they couldn't help but add an honorific prefix.","Yue Fuguang subtly rolled her eyes, ignoring the expressions of the Great Yan sovereign and ministers that constantly shifted between fright and pleasant surprise.","She reached out and unceremoniously stroked the smooth, snow-white feathered backs of the swan and crane closest to her.","With one hand on the left and the other on the right, she ran her hands over them. The sensation was just as she had imagined, cool, smooth, and delicate to the touch, like the finest silk.","Faced with Yue Fuguang's touch, the two large birds flinched slightly before letting her pet them as she pleased.","Just as Yue Fuguang was about to reveal a perverted expression, the system hastily reminded her: Host, pay attention to your expression management. Do not make expressions that do not fit your immortal persona!","If it hadn't reminded her in time, its host would have made a cheap expression and ruined her character!","Chirp!","Chirp!","Seeing that its meal ticket was about to be snatched away, Taxue immediately refused to accept it. With two chirps, it forcefully shoved the white swan aside and placed its large head under Yue Fuguang's hand.","Chirp, Master, pet me!","Looking at Taxue's darting eyes, which seemed to hold eight hundred schemes but still looked adorably clueless, Yue Fuguang chuckled softly.","I accept your gifts. The crisis has been resolved, and it is time for you to return to the forest!","Little Zhu, tell them that the intruders have been dealt with and they can safely go home.","Cluck!","Caw!","Led by the crane and the swan, the birds let out a few clear, pleasant cries toward Yue Fuguang. Then, under their leadership, the flock of birds put down their gifts and took to the sky.","After soaring into the sky, they circled three times above Yue Fuguang's head before flying off in a massive flock into the vast mountain forest.","The crowd looked at the feathers, fruits, ginseng, lingzhi, and other medicinal herbs on the ground, all clicking their tongues in wonder.","Emperor Mingxi even deliberately played dumb, saying, Fuguang, did these birds put on such a grand display just to specifically bring you these things?","He picked up a century-old ginseng from the ground that had lost all its root hairs and said, What a pity for such a good ginseng!","Crunch! Crunch!","A crisp sound reached everyone's ears. They turned around in unison, only to see Wu Yong holding a red apple and munching on it.","Seeing everyone looking at him, Wu Yong's face instantly turned redder than the apple in his hand. He swallowed the apple with difficulty and stammered to Yue Fuguang, I... I just wanted to help the Junior Preceptor test if it was poisonous!","Would you believe that?","His father, Wu Yuanjing, closed his eyes. This gluttonous, disgraceful thing! If he weren't his only biological son, he would have beaten him to death.","While brainwashing himself that this was his own flesh and blood, he rapidly wracked his brain, trying to figure out how to smooth over this embarrassing situation.","Before he could speak, he heard Yue Fuguang ask, Wu Yong, is the wild apple delicious? Is it sour?","Seeing that Yue Fuguang had no intention of blaming him and even asked about the taste, Wu Yong hurriedly replied, It's sour. It's not as delicious as the ones on the Junior Preceptor's mountain!","Yue Fuguang nodded and told him, Then you are in charge of leading people to collect all the fruits and wash them clean.","She looked at the thousands of fruits of various types and sizes on the ground and said, I want to use these fruits to brew monkey wine. Do a good job, and when it's ready, I'll give you a jar.","Hearing the task, Wu Yong was so happy he almost jumped up. He repeatedly agreed, Yes! Don't worry, Junior Preceptor. I will keep an eye on things, and absolutely not a single fruit will go missing. I will make sure they are washed spotlessly clean for you later!","His gaze swept past the Emperor's family and over the various officials, looking at them as if guarding against thieves. Everyone was left speechless.","They really wanted to say that among all their colleagues, besides him, the glutton, who else would pick up fruit from the ground to eat? Not to mention that these fruits belonged to the Junior Preceptor!","Only this fool, relying on the Junior Preceptor's favor, would dare to act like this.","Having settled the matter of her harvest, Yue Fuguang turned around, put away her smile, and said seriously to Emperor Mingxi, Your Majesty, please issue an order to recall Shen Jian and Wei Shouyi's two teams as soon as possible to protect you. As for the assassins in the forest, it won't be too late to catch them later!","Emperor Mingxi also recalled the earlier topic and immediately understood. Does Fuguang mean that the noble families still have a backup plan and will launch a sneak attack on us?","His gaze fell on the distant mountain forest. The forest was completely silent now, and not a single bird could be seen. If it weren't for the fact that the fruits on the ground hadn't been fully gathered yet, one might have thought everything that had just happened was merely a delusion.","He said, Just now, I faintly heard the roar of thunder in the mountains. I wonder if some unforeseen event occurred inside.","He turned to Xie Zhiyan beside him and said, Crown Prince, send out a few more teams. You must bring Shen Jian and the others back as soon as possible. And while you're at it, bring back the oil stains that have been frozen into ice blocks; otherwise, it will be difficult to deal with once they melt.","Fuguang, when do you think they will make their move?","Little Zhu, if I'm not mistaken, those people should make their move when the forest fire starts. But the Emperor doesn't know the sinister intentions of the noble families. How should I answer?","Just say you don't know! With so many officials around, can't they think for themselves? They ask you everything, Master!","Yue Fuguang deeply agreed, so she said without any psychological burden, Your Majesty, I do not know either!","The corners of Emperor Mingxi and his ministers' mouths twitched. He expressed understanding on his face and said gently, It's fine. I will discuss it further with the officials.","Yue Fuguang watched as Emperor Mingxi left with the officials. When she looked up, she met the eyes of the few members of the diplomatic mission who had been watching her from tens of meters away.","Well, the way they looked at her was quite complex; one would need a pie chart of emotions to illustrate their rich inner thoughts and feelings!","Her heart stirred, but she didn't show it on her face. She merely gave them a faint nod and entered her own large tent without looking back.","She still hadn't eaten breakfast yet, and she was starving!","Lan Xuan'er and the others watched Yue Fuguang's figure disappear. They exchanged complex glances; at this moment, no one had any interest in speaking."]},{"number":385,"title":"Chapter 385: They've Broken In","paragraphs":["The group returned to Bei Yue's large tent together in tacit agreement, sitting in the exact same spots as the previous night. However, sitting there now, their moods were vastly different from before.","They sat in relative silence, yet their hearts were filled with thousands of words they yearned to pour out.","Finally, after taking a small sip of water from her cup, Gan Tang spoke softly, \"I wonder if you all have noticed, but it seems we are unable to speak of the Heavenly Voice to anyone other than the few of us here.\"","She had forgotten about it last night, and it was only this morning that she remembered to ask her most loyal maid about the Heavenly Voice.","It was then she realized that as long as she attempted to speak about the Heavenly Voice, even just a single word, it felt as if an invisible giant hand was strangling her neck.","If she hadn't stopped herself in time, she might have actually suffocated to death.","The others nodded silently. They had discovered this last night, and because of it, they hadn't slept well all night. They stayed awake until dawn, looking much more haggard.","Because of this, their doubts about the contents of the Heavenly Voice dropped from fifty percent to twenty percent.","Lan Xuan'er sighed, \"I wonder if having this ability is a blessing or a curse for us?\"","They lowered their eyes, hiding the complex emotions in their hearts and the schemes they could not share with outsiders.","The Heavenly Voice seemed unpredictable in its blessings and curses for the group, but a voice in Bei Yue's heart told him that this was his opportunity.","Since he was certain that his imperial father was using him as a target, he would jump off the chessboard. Whoever wanted to be this pawn could be it; he certainly wouldn't toil for the benefit of others anymore.","Thinking of this, he glanced out of the corner of his eye at the deep-in-thought Bei Ye. If this kid wanted a seat at the table, then he would let him have it.","He just didn't know how Wei Qingyi would choose between him and the Eighth Prince when the time came.","The Xi brothers exchanged a glance and silently turned their heads away. Now that they had a shared secret they couldn't reveal to outsiders, their relationship suddenly became delicate. They couldn't interact without any grudges immediately, but they wouldn't be at each other's throats like before either. After all, they all shared common enemies in their imperial father and siblings.","Hearing the system's report, Yue Fuguang had long anticipated their reactions. She said, \"Ignore them for now. As long as they don't hinder our mission, let them be.\"","It would be even better if they could hurry back to their own countries to cause trouble!","Yue Fuguang felt the air getting increasingly dry. Because the Great Yan had stored water early on, the land had not yet shown obvious signs of drought, but experienced old farmers already felt a looming sense of crisis in their hearts.","It had barely rained for almost two months. In the past few days, she had heard Wei Ping complain more than once that in the subordinate states, counties, and villages, armed conflicts between villages over water for irrigation had increased significantly compared to previous years.","[Host, those people have arrived!]","So fast? The arsonist had been struck to death by her lightning, and seeing no signal to act, they had lost their patience so quickly!","\"How many people came, and where are Wei Shouyi and Shen Jian?\"","[Less than two thousand people, mixed with many from You Tan and the Heavenly Star Pavilion. It will take Wei Shouyi and the others at least thirty to forty minutes to get here at their fastest.]","Those people couldn't wait that long. The number of people on both sides was about the same, which was a disadvantage for their side.","[Master, someone has snuck over to the prison where Poison Young Master and the others are being held!]","The system's sudden warning was loud, and in just an instant, it reached the ears of Emperor Mingxi and the others hundreds of meters away.","Shen Kang immediately stepped forward and said, \"Your Majesty, I will go take a look!\"","Emperor Mingxi waved his hand, \"Take more people. If Poison Young Master tries to run, even if she is dead, she must stay!\"","Now that the person was in his hands, if she escaped, not only would the diplomatic mission laugh at them, but given her status as someone from Panshan, she couldn't be let go!","\"Yes!\"","Emperor Mingxi then looked at Huo Ying, \"Are all the men arranged?\"","Huo Ying said with a solemn face, \"Answering Your Majesty, everything is arranged. I will go over and personally command them now. Even if we have to fight to the death, we will hold out until Lord Shen and the others arrive.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded, and soon all the people from the Ministry of War in the tent left with Huo Ying.","Finally, Emperor Mingxi looked at You Mingmin, the Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial, and Wei Ping, saying, \"You two dispatch more men to protect the people of the diplomatic mission. You absolutely must not let anyone exploit a loophole.\"","Both the sovereign and his ministers knew in their hearts that waiting for scholars and literati from various countries to come to Great Yan for academic exchange was a sham. The diplomatic mission delaying their return had only one purpose: the high-yield grain seeds.","Over the past month or so, the various countries had submitted memorials multiple times, all of which were rejected by Emperor Mingxi on the grounds that their country had no surplus seeds.","You Mingmin bowed and said, \"Please rest assured, Your Majesty. I will gather those people together and personally protect them closely. Even if we subjects are injured, we will not let them suffer a single scratch.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded and finally rested his gaze on the Yu family father and sons, \"Beloved Subject Yu, please pay more attention to Fuguang's side.\"","Given the Junior Preceptor's current martial prowess, they weren't too worried about her safety, but there was always a \"just in case.\"","And that \"just in case\" was something Great Yan could not afford.","Yu Chongshan said, \"Rest assured, Your Majesty. My two sons and I will go over right now.\"","Yu Chongshan led his eldest and second sons toward Yue Fuguang's large tent. They knew very well in their hearts that they weren't going to protect Fuguang.","It was His Majesty sending them to Fuguang's place for their own safety, to hide from the impending danger.","As soon as the trio entered the door, they saw their granddaughter curled up on the chaise lounge looking outside, like a well-fed cat.","Seeing her grandfather and the others enter, Yue Fuguang stood up and asked, \"Grandfather, has His Majesty arranged everything securely?\"","Just as she asked this question, the faint sound of battle cries could be heard in the distance.","After the father and sons found places to sit, Yu Chongshan said, \"Everything is arranged. We just need to hold out for the time it takes to drink three cups of tea, and rescue will arrive.\"","Not only would they be waiting for the over three thousand men that Shen Jian and Wei Shouyi had taken out, but also for the two thousand men of the Left Martial Guard who were rushing here after seeing the signal.","Yu Chongshan was right. At this moment, Song Xiang, who had gone to fetch reinforcements, was leading the two thousand men of the Left Martial Guard, riding whip and spur toward the hunting ground camp.","Along the way, he saw messy footprints of varying depths on the ground. The sweat on his face grew more profuse, whether from anxiety or the exhaustion of riding.","\"Faster, a little faster!\"","He turned back and shouted to the people behind him, \"Everyone, saving His Majesty today is a great merit, and His Highness the Crown Prince will surely reward you heavily!\"","He then said to a young general, \"Cavalry go first, tell the people behind to run faster! Go and keep an eye on them personally!\"","\"Yes, I accept the order!\"","While the reinforcements were rushing to the battlefield, over at the hunting ground, Yue Fuguang heard the increasingly clear battle cries outside and smelled the faint scent of blood drifting in the air.","Had both sides drawn blood right after engaging in close combat?","As the battle cries drew nearer, her sharp hearing could already faintly make out the sound of clashing swords and blades just a few hundred meters away from her tent.","\"System, has someone broken in?\"","[Host, do not worry. More than a dozen assassins took advantage of the chaos to sneak in, but they were discovered by the guards, and the two sides are now fighting.]","Feeling uneasy, Yue Fuguang stood up and walked outside. She was afraid that if the workhorses... ah, no, the lords, who were working for her had the bad luck of being injured by blind swords and spears, she would have to train newcomers all over again. How could novices be as useful as experienced hands?"]},{"number":386,"title":"Chapter 386: Make a Move","paragraphs":["Why couldn't Yue Fuguang be a boss back in her hometown? Well, her way of thinking was the exact opposite of those who ran companies.","To save costs, those people loved to find ways to get rid of veterans and replace them with newcomers, because newcomers were cheap!","Yu Zhongchun and the others naturally heard the sounds of fighting drawing closer outside. Seeing Yue Fuguang walking out, they were just about to voice their objections to stop her.","Turning their heads, they saw his father, Yu Chongshan, also immediately stand up and follow his granddaughter out of the tent.","Hey! Yu Zhongchun gave a bitter smile to his younger brother, Yu Shuchun. Yu Shuchun just threw his hands up in resignation and walked after them.","Smiling and shaking his head, Yu Zhongchun also jogged to catch up.","Both his father and his daughter had minds of their own. As a son and a father, it was better for him not to say much and just obediently follow along.","The four members of the Yu family stepped out of the main tent. Looking up, they saw that about three hundred meters diagonally ahead, near the camp entrance, dozens of armored guards were locked in combat with over a dozen men in black.","System, are these night-stalking suits the mandatory uniform for doing evil deeds? It's broad daylight, and both sides are fighting head-on. What's the point of these people wearing all black?","The system thought for a moment and replied, Could it be that bloodstains aren't obvious on black clothes, so they don't have to scrub them hard after work, and they can wear them again on their next job?","Also, dyeing techniques in ancient times are backward and expensive. Maybe black clothes are relatively cheaper compared to other colors? Assassins aren't exactly wealthy, either!","The system shook its head. It couldn't help but feel that although these assassins lived on the edge of a blade, they were all poor wretches. It had just silently scanned their bodies, and would you believe it, the dozen or so of them combined didn't even have ten taels of silver!","With just these few pieces of broken silver, how were the people looting the corpses later supposed to divide it? One could only say the system was thinking a bit too far ahead.","Yue Fuguang didn't know what the system was thinking. She only felt that its answer made quite a bit of sense. She silently shook her head in her heart; the assassin profession wasn't exactly high-risk, high-reward!","Seeing three more of their guards injured and falling to the ground, she caught sight of Beiyue, Gan Tang, and the others silently sneaking out from behind a large tent out of the corner of her eye.","They all held weapons in their hands, followed by the trotting Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial, You Mingmin, who kept shouting, Your Highnesses, you must not...","Must not what? Yue Fuguang turned her head curiously, only to see the group charging directly at the assassins on their own initiative.","Yue Fuguang frowned. After being bluffed and frightened by her, were they still not giving up on trying to injure themselves? If so, wouldn't all her previous efforts have been in vain!","As soon as the assassins saw their attire, it quickly matched the information they had. The value of assassinating these princes and princesses of the diplomatic mission was much higher than tangling with ordinary guards.","Their boss had told them to charge into the inner perimeter without restricting specific assassination targets. There was only one rule: the higher the status, the richer the reward.","Half of the dozen or so assassins broke off to surround the members of the mission. Seeing the assassins rushing over, Beiyue and the others had excited gleams in their eyes.","They had seen Junior Preceptor Yue standing not far away, watching their side. They had to put on a good performance.","Those who wanted to perform well didn't know that because of their past records, their actions had already been misinterpreted by Yue Fuguang.","Beiyue and the others, including the two princesses Gan Tang and Lan Xuan'er, all possessed real martial arts skills. Facing professional assassins who were clearly experts, the adrenaline in their bodies erupted with unprecedented energy at this moment.","As the oldest, Beiyue took the lead and charged at the assassins. He moved as swiftly as if he were flying, feeling his whole body filled with strength and courage.","However, their increasingly excited expressions caused Yue Fuguang, who had been paying attention to this side all along, to misunderstand even further.","Watching the group brawl, with both sides fighting desperately, she became more and more certain of her earlier guess: these people just wouldn't give up and wanted to use the assassins' hands to self-mutilate.","Seriously, going to such lengths just for some grain seeds was too much! Was this the responsibility of being a member of the royal family?","Seeing the crisis over there, the Yu father and son reacted. As the muscle of the Yu family, Yu Shuchun couldn't help but say, Father, although the people of this mission have decent skills, it seems they won't fare well against these professional assassins! Should your son go over and help?","They knew very well that although the Emperor didn't like these people, for the sake of diplomatic relations between the countries, he still had to treat them with great courtesy.","The personal safety of these people in Great Yan could not be compromised, otherwise, it would be handing the other countries an excuse to start trouble.","Yu Chongshan didn't answer him immediately, but instead turned his head to ask Yue Fuguang, Fuguang, what do you think?","Yue Fuguang pondered for a moment and said, Second Uncle doesn't need to go over.","Going over alone wouldn't be of much help. Her own guards had all been dispatched, and there was no one available at the moment.","Moreover, Yue Fuguang saw another seven or eight assassins charging toward the camp.","As soon as her words fell, a man in black suddenly appeared behind Gan Tang. He dodged a guard's thrust and, using the momentum of retreating, arrived right behind her.","If his face hadn't been covered, one would have been able to see the triumphant smile curling at the corner of his mouth. With lightning speed, he raised his sword and thrust it toward the back of Gan Tang's heart.","If this strike hit, Gan Tang would be dead on the spot.","Watching this scene, Lan Xuan'er's eyes widened in horror as she shouted, Sister Tang, watch out!","Gan Tang was entangled by the person in front of her. Although she had heard the sound of the blade cutting through the air behind her, it was already too late to dodge.","In this moment of crisis, she only barely prepared to avoid a fatal blow to her vitals.","Yue Fuguang sighed softly and couldn't hold back from making a move.","With her hands behind her back, she quickly formed a hand seal. Crackle, rumble! In the clear, cloudless sky, several loud claps of thunder suddenly appeared.","They struck the assassin behind Gan Tang swiftly and with unparalleled precision. Then, the dozen or so men in black who could still fight, along with the several black-clad assassins who had just broken through the defense line and reached the battlefield, were all taken out in one wave.","One moment, these people were slaughtering everything in their path, thinking their sneak attacks would succeed; the next moment, they had been struck unconscious. White smoke slowly rose from their bodies, and fine threads of lightning occasionally flickered across them.","Because they were wearing black clothes, the tattered fabric covered their charred skin. Only by the faint smell of cooking meat drifting in the air could one judge how well-done these people were.","Yue Fuguang had held back this time, only striking them enough to lose their combat ability without intending to take their lives.","Just yesterday, she had single-handedly killed over a hundred people. Although the system had given her rewards at the time, ensuring she didn't feel much psychological burden from killing.","The fact that the system gave rewards proved that those people deserved to die.","She hadn't forgotten that the system later quietly told her there were still a few small mountain villages in the nearby mountains, along with some unregistered mountain dwellers.","If that fire had been allowed to spread, animals would have lost their homes, and some humans would likewise have lost the places they relied on for survival.","The old, the weak, women, and children certainly might not have been able to outrun the blaze.","Host, your Lightning Summoning Art is getting more and more proficient!","It had seen that the host's hands moved so fast they left afterimages!","Hearing the system say this, Yue Fuguang unconsciously puffed out her chest and held her head high. Of course it was getting more proficient. Did it really think she spent all her free time sleeping?"]},{"number":387,"title":"Chapter 387: Is It Possible That You Are the One Who Got Dragged Into It","paragraphs":["In her free time, she had secretly practiced the hand seals for wind, rain, thunder, lightning, and snow for quite a while. Especially the Cloud and Rain Seal she was about to use—that was her trump card for showing off, so she didn't dare be unfamiliar with it.","Looking at the two dozen assassins who were now \"medium-rare,\" Yue Fuguang felt quite proud of her sense of proportion.","She looked up at the distant guards, who had initially been too frightened by the sudden thunderbolts to move. After hearing one of the defending generals say something to them, the crowd excitedly rushed forward with ropes to tie up the captives.","Meanwhile, Gan Tang and the others witnessed all of this with their own eyes. The explosive thunder had rung right in their ears, and one assassin after another was struck down before them, their life or death unknown. The sheer shock of it was far greater than what they had seen on the canvas that morning.","Because they were too smart and had too many thoughts, they actually lacked the blunt resilience of the guards, who quickly accepted the explanation of \"heavenly punishment\" and happily went to clean up the mess.","As for Beiyue, Gan Tang, and the rest, every single one of them still had ringing ears because they were the closest. The deafening thunder had left their brains momentarily stalled.","When a visceral, lingering fear crept into Gan Tang's heart, the assassins who had wanted to kill her had already been carried away by the Dayan soldiers. She could only turn around silently, looking toward Yue Fuguang with a mix of astonishment and gratitude.","Yue Fuguang couldn't care less about what Gan Tang and the others thought. Anyway, she had already saved them. If these people dared to pull any more stunts, her patience was nearly exhausted, and she wouldn't rule out teaching them a harsh lesson.","The group suddenly shivered for no apparent reason. They saw that Yue Fuguang wasn't looking at them, but rather gazing outside the camp.","They followed her gaze. Although they couldn't see anything, the shouts of battle outside could be heard clearly.","Clatter, clatter. The ground trembled. A loud flurry of horse hooves echoed from the distance, and within moments, a squad of armored cavalry came galloping down the road leading to the hunting grounds.","\"Fuguang, look quickly, have the reinforcements arrived?\" Emperor Mingxi had walked up behind her at some point. Lacking Yue Fuguang's abilities, Emperor Mingxi could only guess by the sound and couldn't yet see the cavalry led by Song Xiang rushing to the rescue.","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Judging by the commotion, the vanguard should have arrived.\" By now, she could already see a sweating Song Xiang wielding his long spear as he fought his way in.","Over an hour later, this two-day assassination attempt, meticulously planned and executed with all the might of the noble families, finally came to an end.","The imperial retinue stayed at the hunting grounds for another two days. On the surface, it appeared to be the Emperor's benevolence and consideration for his subjects, waiting until everyone had satisfied their craving for hunting before setting off to return to the capital.","During this time, Yue Fuguang also followed the Crown Prince and the others into the woods for a while. She didn't fire a single arrow but had a bountiful harvest, simply because the moment she stepped into the forest, all sorts of prey offered themselves up to her.","If it wasn't a rabbit rushing out and crashing into a tree, giving her a live performance of the primary school idiom of waiting by a stump for a hare, it was a perfectly flying pheasant suddenly twisting its neck and tumbling out of midair, landing right on the ground in front of her horse's head.","A few beautiful, pure-white fox cubs even dashed in front of her horse. At first, everyone thought they had come out to steal the wild pheasants, but who knew they would just stand still after rushing out. They didn't even glance at the still-warm pheasants on the ground; they just tilted their heads and stared adorably at Yue Fuguang with their foxy eyes.","Yue Fuguang was overwhelmed by the cuteness of these fluffy creatures tilting their heads. She glanced at the prey scattered all over the ground, then turned to look back at the hunting ground entrance, which was less than a kilometer away from their location.","Weren't these little guys a bit too eager to \"sacrifice\" themselves?","This bizarre kind of \"hunting\" suddenly made Yue Fuguang feel bored. A hunt without any chasing or hiding offered absolutely no sense of experience. She swore she would never come again!","Yue Fuguang turned her horse around and headed for the entrance. The Crown Prince signaled for everyone to pack up the game and rode after her. The group had just exited the hunting grounds when they looked back and saw a few little tails following behind them.","Aside from the three foxes that had run out earlier, which Yue Fuguang hadn't taken with her, there were now two iron-eating beast cubs that had appeared out of nowhere!","Their distinct black-and-white coloring reflected in Yue Fuguang's increasingly bright, black-and-white eyes.","As a true native of Xia, who could resist wanting to raise such an adorable creature?","Yue Fuguang didn't even think twice. She quickly dismounted, scooped up the two panda cubs that looked to be only three or four months old, and decided on the spot to adopt all five fluffy babies.","She was someone who understood etiquette; relationships required give and take, and she wouldn't just take their children for nothing.","Thinking of the impending severe drought across the land, she secretly cast a localized heavy rainstorm over the entire mountain forest that night.","She did it in secret, but the upper echelons of the entire camp knew full well that this was the work of their Junior Preceptor.","Hearing the pattering sound of heavy rain outside their windows, many got up in the dark of the night and secretly peeked out from their tent windows.","The camp was dry without a single drop of rain, yet the continuous sound of a downpour battering the leaves echoed from the mountain forest.","The heavy rain lasted for most of the night. When everyone woke up the next morning and looked into the distance, they saw that more than half the leaves on the trees had fallen overnight.","It was worth mentioning that in the starry night sky over the hunting grounds that night, a loud clap of thunder had struck without warning, hitting a tent directly and resulting in one casualty.","The Dayan sovereign and subjects, awakened by the thunder, heard the guards report that a heavenly lightning bolt had struck the tent of the Northern Li diplomatic mission's Fifth Prince.","When they heard that the Fifth Prince was fine, but his attendant Song Tu had unfortunately been struck and killed, the Dayan officials who had been preparing to get up and check the situation silently crawled back into bed, pulled up their covers, and closed their eyes to sleep—all in one smooth motion.","It was just an insignificant attendant who died, no big deal!","Besides, they wouldn't dare interfere in this matter. Sleep, sleep, they knew absolutely nothing!","Meanwhile, Bei Ye stood in the tent destroyed by the thunderbolt, looking up at the head-sized black hole in the roof. He looked out from the black hole and could still see the twinkling stars in the sky.","Could someone tell him what on earth was going on?","Was Yue Fuguang trying to strike him dead?","No, no, no. Bei Ye shook his head so hard it nearly snapped off; he refused to believe this was aimed at him.","If Yue Fuguang truly wanted him dead, with her methods, she couldn't possibly miss.","Since the one who died was Song Tu, then he must have been the one she intended to strike from the very beginning.","Was it a warning?","Otherwise, why didn't she strike earlier or later, but precisely when Song Tu was on night watch? This action must have been meant to warn him. As for why she chose Song Tu...","Bei Ye had his own guesses. Song Tu was currently his top guard and the one he trusted most. During the assassination attempts against Yue Fuguang, it was Song Tu who had passed on messages several times.","Bei Ye had originally planned to send him to the military for training and heavily cultivate his talents once they returned to Northern Li.","Unfortunately, before he could implement his plan, Song Tu was \"implicated\" by him and died!","Bei Ye's head was still a bit dizzy from the thunder, and his ears were ringing. He moved to another tent for the rest of the night and lay awake with his eyes open until dawn.","Yue Fuguang: Is it possible that you were the one being implicated?"]},{"number":388,"title":"Chapter 388: Maybe we should just leave it alone.","paragraphs":["It could only be said that this was a beautiful misunderstanding. Because of Bei Ye's fear and guilty conscience toward Yue Fuguang, he didn't dare utter a single word even though he knew she was the one who did it.","It could be said that Song Tu's departure was both earth-shattering and completely silent.","On the way back to the city, apart from Yue Fuguang who had gained new pets, the Yu family father and son, who had finally avenged their great grievance, smiled the most joyously.","On the day they set off to return to the capital, Emperor Mingxi saw how much Yue Fuguang loved the five fluffy little creatures and smiled, saying they would come again next year.","Although it is said that a ruler never speaks in jest, Emperor Mingxi was clearly going to break his promise this time. No one anticipated that the situation would develop so rapidly. By the time the emperor and his subjects returned to hunt here again, several \"next years\" would have already passed.","And the five fluffy creatures would have already started their own families, becoming a large clan of beasts.","But at this moment, the five cubs were still at the age of playfully competing for favor, completely unaware that the winds of change were approaching!","Ever since Yue Fuguang began feeding the little ones with Spirit Beast Pills, they grew smarter by the day.","Whether it was the little fox or the panda, they were the intelligence representatives of the animal kingdom. With the enhancement of the Spirit Beast Pills, their intelligence had already reached the level of a three- or four-year-old child. Who would have thought that these adorable little things would one day rule over all beasts?","Nearly two months had passed since their return from the hunting grounds. The aftermath of the aristocratic families' affairs had not yet concluded, and the end of the year was fast approaching.","Just as the wealthy households and commoners of the capital were beginning to purchase goods for the New Year, reports of droughts from various regions began to consecutively roll in.","Across the entire Great Yan territory, barely a drop of rain had fallen for over four months. The crops in the fields, especially in areas where winter wheat was planted, were barely holding on because they had stored water early on. However, the situation was not optimistic. In the water-scarce north, some villages and counties were already beginning to suffer to varying degrees.","Fortunately, although the drought in Great Yan was severe, there was still just enough water for the people and livestock to consume.","If it hadn't been for the Ministry of Works starting to build water conservancy projects and river channels two years ago...","...digging wells and opening ponds, and the Emperor secretly decreeing that all prefectures and counties consciously and secretly store water, the drought would have been much worse.","During the grand court assembly before the Emperor officially sealed his jade seal for the holidays, the atmosphere was noticeably heavy.","Emperor Mingxi sat majestically on the dragon throne, his brows furrowed as he listened to the Minister of Revenue, Dong Qianli, report on the recent drought.","After reporting the drought situations in various regions, Dong Qianli continued, Your Majesty, according to the reports from various places, the grain reserves in the Ever-Normal Granaries, Charity Granaries, and Community Granaries are still considered sufficient.","However, if it is truly as the Junior Preceptor's master said and the drought lasts for two or three years, this humble subject worries that chaos will inevitably arise over time.","Should we mobilize some of the local garrisons to protect them?","Over the past two years, due to the promotion of three high-yield superior seed varieties, most regions had planted one or two seasons, and the commoners rarely had abundant surplus food to live on.","But due to seed supply issues, a small portion of people only received the seeds during this year's autumn harvest, meaning the earliest they could plant them would be next year.","Dong Qianli, like the venerable Lord Wang Shouchen of the Court of Agricultural Affairs, worried that if the drought truly became severe, the common people would become so hungry that they would eat the seeds.","After all, the group of people who had just received the seeds were those who were only just starting to plant high-yield grains and didn't have much surplus food at home.","If the drought really lasted for two or three years, no one knew what it would develop into by then. If they were truly on the verge of starving to death, who would care whether what they were eating was seeds or not, just to stay alive?","You might ask, since they were worried the commoners might eat the seeds out of hunger, why did the imperial court go against common sense and distribute them early?","Couldn't they just wait until the beginning of spring next year to distribute them?","This brings us to the personal motives of Wang Shouchen and Dong Qianli. They made this decision after careful consideration from multiple angles.","The tens or hundreds of catties they distributed were both seeds and the final lifesaving grain for those families! It could also be considered a tacit form of compensation.","If the drought continued until next spring without a single drop of rain, even with stored water, planting grains on a large scale would no longer be realistic.","Sweet potatoes and potatoes, which could not be stored for too long, could become a family's lifesaver in addition to the portion used for planting.","After the two proposed this decision, the court debated it for several days. Ultimately, it was Yue Fuguang who had the final say, allowing the seeds to be smoothly distributed.","Because Yue Fuguang knew very well in her heart that the heavens wouldn't rain next year or the year after, but she could make it rain! Therefore, these seeds would definitely be planted on time.","At this moment, hearing Dong Qianli ask about the guards, Emperor Mingxi thought for a moment and then asked Huo Ying, What does my beloved subject Huo think?","Seeing the Emperor address him, Huo Ying stepped forward and bowed in salute while pondering and carefully choosing his words. To reply to Your Majesty, this humble subject personally believes that Minister Dong's words are reasonable.","At present, it seems the commoners have surplus grain on hand, and the granaries across the regions are safe. However, if it is truly as the Junior Preceptor said, and the drought continues without rain for a long time, the people will inevitably panic. As their stored grain is slowly consumed, during this period, if anyone with ulterior motives stirs up trouble, it will very likely bring about disaster. The more he spoke, the more confident he became, his voice growing much firmer as he boldly guessed, Then, their first target will undoubtedly be the granaries.","What he didn't say was that the current small number of guards at the regional warehouses seemed fine for now, but later on, as the drought worsened, even if the imperial court intervened, grain prices would inevitably rise.","He was afraid that someone might embezzle the grain they were guarding or collude with outsiders to target the reserves. Mainly, he had been frightened by the large number of corrupt officials caught in Great Yan over the past two years. Huo Ying admitted that he didn't quite trust the integrity of his colleagues.","[Master, did Dong Qianli just say that the grain reserves in the Ever-Normal Granaries, Community Granaries, and Charity Granaries are sufficient?]","[It seems he said so. What's wrong, is there a problem with what he said?]","Is there a problem with what he said? This sentence replayed over and over in Dong Qianli's mind. Cold sweat instantly beaded on his forehead, and his heart sank halfway.","Anyone who understood the Divine Artifact Lord knew that whenever this happened, it meant something bad was about to occur.","At this moment, Dong Qianli couldn't help but feel suspicious. Could it be that there was a problem with all these granaries?","Just a tiny bit of suspicion surfacing in his heart made Dong Qianli feel as if the remaining half of his heart had also gone completely cold.","If this was truly the case, once the Divine Artifact Lord spoke today, who knew how many people's lives and deaths would become unpredictable.","Trembling, he used the opportunity of wiping his sweat with his sleeve to steal a glance upward at the Emperor.","At this time, Emperor Mingxi appeared calm on the surface, earnestly listening to the admonitions of his courtiers, but his hands had gradually tightened their grip on the armrests of the dragon throne.","A great disaster was approaching, and only food and water could stabilize the hearts of the people and the military. If there was a problem with the Ever-Normal Granaries, who knew how many disasters it would provoke.","He muttered in his heart, only hoping that the problem was isolated to one or two places, and that the embezzlement of a small handful of people would still have harms within a controllable range.","[The problem seems to be a bit big, but that's not important. Even if the sky falls, it won't delay Master's three meals a day, right? How about we just ignore it? It's quite tiring!]","The words just ignore it made Emperor Mingxi's heart not only turn cold but also clench tight. If one looked closely, they could see his chest heaving up and down. His face, which had been fairly calm just a moment ago, was now slightly distorted and flushed red.","The entire grand hall also suddenly fell silent for a moment. As if by prior agreement, everyone silently shrank their bodies and lowered their heads even further, striving not to stand out too much."]},{"number":389,"title":"Chapter 389: Who Moved the Granary","paragraphs":["Even those who could not hear the inner voices had grown shrewd over the past few years. No matter the reason, following the lead of the prominent officials in front was guaranteed to be the right move.","After a brief pause in the center of the grand hall, Huo Ying immediately braced himself and continued to report on the garrison situations across various regions and the available manpower that could be mobilized.","Dong Qianli, his face already deathly pale and his legs trembling, stepped out of the ranks shivering. He silently found an inconspicuous spot to kneel and wait for his punishment.","Yue Fuguang seemed to have suddenly taken an interest in the gossip. With a voice full of deep curiosity, she said, \"Little Zhu, how big is this matter?","Sitting here is boring anyway, hurry up and tell me to relieve your master's boredom!\"","[Since Master wants to hear it, Little Zhu will tell you in detail.]","Emperor Mingxi instantly sat up straight. Hearing rustling sounds behind him, the Crown Prince slightly turned his head, only to see his younger brothers silently edging closer to him.","The Crown Prince felt helpless; his not-so-broad physique could not possibly shield the figures of his several younger brothers.","These few had already developed a stress response. They did not know when it started, but every time those two ancestors started gossiping, they could not help but want to hide.","Xie Zhiyan really wanted to say that if his younger brothers had not gotten involved, there was absolutely no need to be afraid.","[Master, look at the Fifth Prince down there. Although his maternal grandfather is not in the imperial court, he is the current Inspector of Hezhou, which can be considered the equivalent of a high-ranking regional official.","Although his power and the emperor's favor are far less than what Sima Jing had back then, and the emperor has intentionally weakened the power of local chief officials over the past two years.","However, with years of operation and having a prince as a grandson in the court, various local officials outside would also sell him a favor due to his status as the prince's maternal grandfather.]","\"So he is the one with the problem?\"","The Fifth Prince Xie Zhixin's mind buzzed. He could not hear any sounds clearly in his ears at this moment; the continuous buzzing made those voices seem very far away.","His vision darkened in waves. He staggered half a step, and just as he was about to fall, he involuntarily reached out and grabbed the Crown Prince's sleeve, as if clutching at his last straw.","Second Brother Xie and Xie San both cast a sympathetic glance at him. That glance contained only one meaning: see, as long as these two ancestors start gossiping, someone is bound to suffer.","\"I seem to remember that in the original history, Hezhou Inspector Du Mingqi was demoted to a commoner after secretly supporting the Fifth Prince's failed bid for the throne. Later, Fourth Master Xie fabricated multiple charges against him, and his entire family was thrown into prison.","The female family members were sent to the Entertainment Bureau, and all males over the age of ten were executed.\"","[Master remembers correctly, but history has now severely deviated, and the trajectories of many people's fates have also changed.","Look at several people down there who, in the original historical timeline, should have been dead long ago with grass growing tall on their graves, yet they are still alive and kicking.]","Those few who knew they were supposed to be dead long ago silently lowered their heads even further, afraid that the two ancestors would see the corners of their mouths that they could not help but curl up.","They could not help but feel smug; every day they lived now was a bonus!","\"So, is this Du Mingqi because of us?\"","[You cannot count it like that. It is a fact that he participated in the fight for the throne. In the original history, he was not immediately executed after being discovered for various reasons. It was only later that Fourth Master Xie collected evidence to convict him in order to strike at Fifth Prince Xie. You should know that although Fourth Master Xie's motives were impure, he did not wrong Du Mingqi too much.","Look at him now. Even knowing that the Crown Prince's position is secure and the emperor has no intention of changing his heir, he still has not given up and wants to push Fifth Prince Xie to the throne.","To this day, he is still constantly wooing officials of all levels in the local areas.]","\"Does Fifth Prince Xie know what Du Mingqi is doing?\" Yue Fuguang glanced at Xie Zhiquan, whose face was already drained of color.","The system curled its lip, [What does it matter if he knows or not? If Du Mingqi really offered the throne to him, do you think he would sit on it or not?]","Second Brother Xie and Xie San ignored their brotherly bonds and could not help but raise their eyebrows at their half-terrified younger brother. The meaning was all in their eyebrows, which translated to one sentence: 'Would you sit on it?'","[This fight for the throne is like a certain ugly country's presidential election. Winning people over is not just about talking; it requires giving real benefits and spending money.","So the current fight for the throne is just like the ugly country's election Master has seen: building a public persona, drawing big pies, and spending massive amounts of financial and material resources to buy people's hearts.","The fight for the throne lasts even longer than a presidential election. After all, no one knows when the current emperor will die.","As long as the emperor does not die, the wooing cannot stop, and the spending of money cannot stop either.]","Hearing the last two sentences, everyone shrank their necks again. Alas, they were all numb to it!","Emperor Mingxi: I am the one who is the most numb, okay! Melancholy smoking JPG","\"So this Du Mingqi targeted the grain for the sake of money? Did he reach his hands into the Ever Normal Granary?\"","[Correct. Dong Qianli initially said there was no problem with the Ever Normal Granary, which was also the result of the officials in Hezhou tampering with things, concealing the truth, and making false reports.","Across the entire territory of Hezhou, most areas planted those three types of grain this year, resulting in a bumper harvest. Half of the grain stored in the Ever Normal Granary consists of these three types of grain.","Master probably does not know yet, but the seeds of these three types of grain have been hyped to astronomical prices outside the borders of the Great Yan.]","Over the past two years, neighboring countries mobilized all their spies planted throughout the Great Yan dynasty just to get their hands on them.","Their goal was to smuggle the improved seeds out of the country. After more than two years of effort, based on the seeds currently in the hands of various countries, if it weren't for the drought, they could have scaled up production in another two to three years and potentially promoted it nationwide in five years.]","Emperor Mingxi's face was even darker now than when he heard about life-and-death matters. With every word the system said, his face darkened a fraction more. By the time he heard the last sentence, his expression was as black as the bottom of a pot. A freezing, oppressive atmosphere filled the grand hall. Aside from Huo Ying, who was still dutifully giving his report, the other ministers were as quiet as mice, not even daring to breathe too loudly.","Kneeling on the ground, Dong Qianli couldn't help but tremble. At this moment, there was another person kneeling beside him: the Investigating Censor, Feng Tang.","The two brothers in distress exchanged a glance, both inevitably recalling the terrifying scenes of judgment in the underworld.","They were guilty of negligence, but they just didn't know how His Majesty would punish them.","Meanwhile, the elderly Lord Wang Shouchen was deeply heartbroken, clutching his chest and panting softly.","\"No wonder I heard a few days ago that the Secret Spy Bureau's prisons were overflowing, and they had to apply to the Ministry of Revenue for funds to expand the cells and hire new guards.","So it was all caused by these three types of grain. Does that mean all the Ever-Normal Granaries within He Prefecture have been compromised?\"","Standing at the back of the crowd, Zheng Zicheng silently clenched his jaw and also dropped to his knees. Over the past two years, because of the improved seeds, spies who had been hidden in Great Yan for decades, even passing their roles down through generations, had been forced to make a move.","This had also given his bureau an opportunity. Their harvest was indeed substantial, bringing a lot of glory to the Secret Spy Bureau.","But how long had it been before they heard this terrible news? The superior officials were guilty of negligence, and as the Vice Envoy of the Secret Spy Bureau, he shared the exact same guilt!","[It's not quite that bad. Only about half of them have problems. To be precise, the problem with this half lies with those three types of high-yield grains stored inside.","Master, you probably don't know this yet, but the beautiful accounting books completely fail to match the actual inventory. The parasites of Great Yan will never be eradicated no matter the era; you kill one batch, and another simply takes its place!]","The system's words were laced with deep murderous intent. The greed of these people had almost ruined their mission, so it was no wonder it was angry. After all, human lives were points!"]},{"number":390,"title":"Chapter 390: They Believed It","paragraphs":["[Colluding with Du Mingqi and certain officials, they replaced the sweet potatoes, corn, and potatoes inside with stale grain. Some greedy officials, wanting to embezzle even more, didn't follow Du Mingqi's safer method. Thinking themselves clever, they substituted grain with sand and gravel, while the bolder ones simply recorded grain quantities in the ledgers, leaving the warehouses completely empty.]","Hearing this, Xie Zhiquan's legs trembled violently. If not for his two good brothers, Second Brother Xie and Xie San, holding him up, his legs would have given out long ago.","Joking aside, looking at their imperial father's expression, one wrong move could easily lead to a reckoning later. Besides, these two were experienced veterans in such matters. No matter what, they had to listen quietly and absolutely must not disturb those two ancestors.","Otherwise, it would be adding crimes upon crimes! At this thought, the two recalled the beatings on their backsides and the days spent reflecting on their mistakes behind closed doors.","They wanted to say that although attending court occasionally brought heart-stopping terror, being locked in their estates unable to go out was another kind of torture entirely. Compared to being locked up waiting to die or being forced to make babies, they much preferred attending court to enjoy the drama.","\"Did Du Mingqi sell the substituted grain to our neighboring countries? Western Qiang, Northern Li, or Nanzhao and Nanyue?\"","The diplomatic missions from these countries, for whatever reason, still showed no signs of returning home even though the New Year was fast approaching.","Over a month ago, scholars and men of letters from various countries had arrived in the capital city of Shangjing. Yue Fuguang had indeed received quite a few visiting cards from all sides over the past month.","Unfortunately, she had no interest in poetry gatherings, literary salons, or flower-viewing parties, and hadn't accepted a single invitation. For some unknown reason, her seemingly arrogant behavior didn't attract resentment or criticism; instead, her reputation in the literary circles of various countries only grew better and better.","Like the diplomatic missions, these people had no intention of returning home. It seemed they were planning to celebrate the New Year in the Great Yan Dynasty.","[Du Mingqi contacted a major grain merchant and plans to sell the grain in batches soon.]","\"So Du Mingqi's embezzlement stems from the struggle for the throne, not colluding with the enemy and treason?\"","[Master, on the surface, it appears to be embezzlement driven by the greed of certain Hezhou officials led by Du Mingqi. But in reality, it involves treason and colluding with the enemy. However, the traitor isn't Du Mingqi, but a sub-prefect under him in charge of salt and grain named Song Min.","Strictly speaking, Song Min's ancestors were from Northern Li. During the previous dynasty, parts of the border lands of Lianzhou and Hezhou were in the hands of Northern Li. Later, when the Great Yan Dynasty was founded, the founding emperor reclaimed them.","The two countries drew their borders, which is how the Master's lawless tri-border zone came to be.","This Song Min's ancestors moved there from Northern Li. Later, when the founding emperor reclaimed that land, the commoners living there became citizens of Great Yan.]","\"So this Song Min's body is in Great Yan but his heart is in Northern Li, and this grain is also meant to be sent to Northern Li?\"","Reminded by the system, she finally recalled that after she was made a prince, Emperor Mingxi had carved out a massive fiefdom for her right next to her tri-border land.","A portion of this fiefdom was located in Hezhou!","[It's not that noble! Ultimately, Song Min is just greedy too.]","Yue Fuguang suddenly thought of something. \"Little Zhu, are you saying that officials in my fiefdom are also involved?\"","[A few are involved. Master, you might as well report this to the emperor, replace these people, and select your own personnel. The chances of issues arising with people we choose ourselves are much smaller.] At the very least, they would investigate them thoroughly going back five generations.","\"Let me think about it. The new imperial scholars from the sixth year of Yuankang, aside from those still in the Hanlin Academy, have all been assigned posts. If we want to select people, we can only wait for the special imperial examination next spring. We could pick some capable provincial graduates and imperial scholars from the upcoming metropolitan examination to use.\"","Ever since she started doing missions, it indeed took a toll on the officials. Over the past few years, many from top to bottom had died, been demoted, or been exiled. Quite a few positions had opened up at the lower levels, which greatly benefited the senior officials and the newly minted imperial scholars.","\"Little Zhu, do you mean the grain embezzled by Du Mingqi and his gang hasn't been sold yet?\"","[Correct. Because the grain had just been put into storage, the supervising officials sent by the emperor were quite reliable and only returned to the capital after personally watching the grain enter the warehouses.","This is also why Dong Qianli said there were no issues with the Ever-Normal Granary, as the supervising officials included those sent by the Ministry of Revenue.","Because of this, Du Mingqi didn't dare act rashly. He waited until these people returned to the capital before conspiring with the various officials he had roped in to secretly swap out the stored grain.","His original intention was to pass off inferior goods as high quality, wanting the silver but not wanting to cause a real disaster that would attract Emperor Mingxi's attention.","After all, having navigated the turbulent waters of officialdom for years, anyone with half a brain could tell from the imperial court's policies over the past two years that they were preparing for a major disaster.","So, he adopted someone's suggestion and came up with the idea of replacing the high-priced sweet potatoes, potatoes, and corn with stale grain.","Who knew that his subordinates were even more insatiably greedy than he was, risking their lives for silver.","Not only did some replace grain with sand and gravel, but bolder ones directly cooked the books.","This Song Min was one of them, and that so-called major grain merchant was brought in by him—an impostor sent by the Emperor of Northern Li.]","Emperor Mingxi took the tea handed over by Qian Gui. Suppressing the urge to smash the cup, he gulped down three mouthfuls to force down the raging fire in his heart.","However, his bloodshot eyes and overflowing murderous intent could not be extinguished by a mere cup of cold tea!","[There's also the matter of the natural disaster. Because of the court's policies, the lower-ranking officials actually had their suspicions, especially since not a single drop of rain has fallen in these latter months of the year.","Their suspicions deepened, so Song Min, much like with the grain, half-sold and half-gave away his speculations to the Northern Li people.","Aside from Northern Li, Western Qiang, Nanyue, and Nanzhao have also successively received related news from Great Yan over the past two months.]","\"Did they believe it?\"","Yue Fuguang looked at the gloomy sky outside. Counting today, it was already the third day. The sky had been overcast for three days, and the common people of the world had hoped for three days.","Unfortunately, the heavens only remained overcast without raining. The greater the people's hopes now, the greater their disappointment would be later.","For just a bit of rain from the sky, her statues had sold out yet again.","The loud prayers outside the estate begging the Goddess to bring rain could be heard even through the walls of the Yu Manor.","Spontaneous rain-praying rituals organized across various regions had started as early as a month ago.","[They didn't believe it at first, especially when they learned that Great Yan had started preparing over two years in advance. But as more time passed without rain, they had no choice but to believe it.]","\"So the diplomatic missions still haven't returned because they want to stay in Great Yan to get first-hand news of the imperial court's movements in real-time?\"","[That indeed accounts for a large part of the reason.]","Emperor Mingxi swept a dark glance at You Mingmin and Zheng Zicheng. With years of tacit understanding between sovereign and subjects, the two immediately grasped his meaning.","Before the stolen grain could be recovered, the news absolutely must not leak out. They had to keep a close eye on the Northern Li people in particular!","Those few could all hear the Junior Preceptor's inner voice. It was alarming to think about how they had spent the past two months making roundabout inquiries about the Junior Preceptor.","They had expressed their desire to pay a visit more than once.","Fortunately, the Junior Preceptor didn't like joining in the bustle and rarely had the chance to meet with these people."]},{"number":391,"title":"Chapter 391: News from the Dongyi","paragraphs":["Otherwise, with the inner thoughts of these two ancestors broadcasting like loudspeakers that could be heard from far away, this secret might not have been kept.","Yue Fuguang and the System: Are we really a person and a system with so little sense of propriety?!","\"Western Qiang and Northern Li are still alright, in the same situation as Great Yan, suffering from a continuous drought for two or three years. However, Nanzhao and Nanyue are experiencing drought first, and by the second half of next year, they will face severe floods. Didn't Eastern Yi start raining a couple of days ago when it was cloudy?\"","[Yes, this is already the third day. Continuous and unrelenting torrential rain is falling, as if all the rain meant for the other five nations is pouring down on the four islands of Eastern Yi.","The people of Eastern Yi could not even rejoice for three days before some areas began to flood.]","Strictly speaking, among the six nations, the first to suffer the ravages of natural disasters was Eastern Yi.","While Yue Fuguang was still discussing the floods in Eastern Yi with the system, inside the diplomatic hostel of the Honglu Temple, Gan Tang, Bei Yue, and a few others were sitting around in a quiet and elegant tearoom.","However, this time, the gathering included Yanji and Oshima, who had been subtly ostracized by the others ever since the incident with the heavenly voice.","\"Brother Yanji, is what you said true? Is there really a torrential downpour in Eastern Yi?\" Gan Tang could not help but ask for confirmation again upon hearing Yanji mention the rain in Eastern Yi.","\"I also received a message by carrier pigeon today. My royal brother sent the news two days ago, around the same time as Brother Yanji. But Nanyue is still suffering from a severe drought.\"","Logically, since Nanyue and Nanzhao were located in the south, they were the nations least lacking in water among the six. They never expected to encounter a once-in-a-century drought this year.","If one calculated carefully, their drought had actually started even earlier than that of Great Yan.","Yanji nodded solemnly with a serious expression, but anyone with eyes could see the unconcealable smile leaking from his eyes.","\"As you all have heard, the message I just received clearly states that there is heavy rain in Eastern Yi.\"","Saying this, he carefully took out a long slip of paper from his sleeve pocket. The other words had already been crossed out by Yanji, leaving only the words \"heavy rain on the four islands\" and the date.","The crowd calculated the time; it was only three days ago, which was indeed the fastest flying speed of an adult pigeon.","Bei Yue gently tapped his fingers on the table and said slowly, \"First, congratulations to Brother Yanji. Eastern Yi is the first to escape the drought, which is truly worthy of celebration. However, I wonder how long this rain will last and whether it can completely relieve the drought.\"","Hearing his words, the uncontrollable smile on Yanji's face slowly faded. He had the same worry, which was why he didn't laugh wantonly when he received the news, nor did he mock these guys who usually looked down on him for believing Great Yan's rumor that the drought would last for three years.","After all, even the emperor of Great Yan had not explicitly announced that there would be a severe drought, yet these people believed it first!","Don't think he didn't know; these people were definitely hiding something from him!","Hmph, how dare they look down on him, the prince with the greatest chance of inheriting the throne of Eastern Yi? Weren't they now forced to come to him begging for information?","He subtly glanced at the beautiful faces and graceful figures of Lan Xuan'er and Gan Tang.","These two women were indeed prettier than his sisters. His royal father intended to form marriage alliances with several countries, and he could suggest to his father to consider Nanyue and Nanzhao first.","The beauty of these two women each had its own merits, and Yanji momentarily didn't know which one to choose.","Although a bunch of dirty thoughts popped into Yanji's mind at this moment, it did not stop him from dealing with the group.","He nodded seriously and solemnly, saying, \"I have already sent a message back to my country via carrier pigeon. I presume I will get concrete news in a few days. You all just need to wait for the good news.\"","The good news Yanji spoke of did not keep him waiting long. Just four or five days after he said this, he received the latest news from Eastern Yi.","The heavy rain on the four islands of Eastern Yi had poured continuously for four days without stopping. Many low-lying areas on the islands had already been flooded, and the message asked him if any places in Great Yan had experienced rain.","Upon receiving this news, Yanji's good mood from the past few days was completely swept away, replaced by a massive, unfounded panic.","Knock, knock, knock!","Just when he didn't know what to do, there was a knock on the door.","\"Brother Yanji, you aren't asleep yet, are you? Xi Ling and the others invited us to gather in the tearoom. Everyone else has already gone over; it's just the two of us left.\" It was Bei Yue, who had been keeping an eye on his movements.","Yanji was no fool. He could hear from Bei Yue's words that the group was certain he was in his room, not even giving him a chance to play dead—no, play asleep.","\"Brother Bei Yue, wait a moment, I'll be right there.\" Yanji picked up the slip of paper in his hand, stared at the dancing flame in the lamp on the table, thought for a moment, and finally sighed softly, tucking the slip of paper into his sleeve pocket.","Although he intended to hide it, every country had its own intelligence network. Yanji was certain that at this moment, let alone the other countries, even His Majesty in the capital city of Shangjing had probably already received the exact news about the continuous rainfall in Eastern Yi.","Every country was suffering from drought, and only yours was getting rain. Who wouldn't pay extra attention to that!","Yanji was not wrong in his thinking. Although it was a bit late, Emperor Mingxi still urgently summoned several of his most trusted ministers into the palace for a discussion after receiving the news that Eastern Yi had been experiencing heavy rain for five consecutive days.","\"Your Majesty, in my humble opinion, barring any accidents, if we factor in the time it took to deliver the message, Eastern Yi has probably been enduring heavy rain for seven or eight days straight.\"","The Minister of Revenue, Dong Qianli, was still holding the slip of paper delivered by the carrier pigeon. At this moment, he fully believed the Junior Preceptor's words that the heavy rain in Eastern Yi would last for over a month.","Emperor Mingxi nodded; he thought the same.","Emperor Mingxi suppressed the urge to curl up the corners of his lips, coughed lightly, and asked in a seemingly casual tone, \"Then, in the view of my beloved ministers, how should our Great Yan respond?\"","After asking this, Emperor Mingxi casually picked up the lotus teacup painted with exquisite landscape scenery in front of him, gently blew away the floating leaves in the tea, and carefully took a sip. His eyes, hidden behind the cup lid, lifted slightly, sweeping across the faces of his important ministers.","The several Ministers kept their heads slightly lowered, only using their peripheral vision to glance at their colleagues standing beside them. When their peripheral gazes met, they silently lowered their eyes again, pretending to be deep in thought.","Feng Tang, who was standing in the back row, saw that the old foxes in front were all silent. He wanted to step forward several times but pulled his leg back each time.","As if sensing something, he carefully raised his head, meeting the emperor's gaze. The ruler and minister locked eyes, and the emperor's eyes were full of encouragement.","Under Emperor Mingxi's expectant gaze, Feng Tang clenched his fists, took a deep breath, stepped forward, bowed, and said, \"Your Majesty, in my humble opinion, for our Great Yan at this moment, doing nothing is doing something.\"","Emperor Mingxi put down his teacup and smiled, saying, \"Beloved Minister Feng, elaborate.\"","Feng Tang cupped his hands toward Emperor Mingxi and continued, \"Your Majesty, if the lands of Eastern Yi really experience a month of continuous heavy rain as that person said, how many places on the four islands will be left unflooded by then?","And how many commoners will survive? After a great disaster, there is bound to be a great plague. Our Great Yan just needs to watch from the sidelines and blockade the coastline under the pretext of safety, ensuring that they cannot obtain any medicine or food supplies from the mainland...\"","Feng Tang did not know that his advice at this moment perfectly blocked Eastern Yi's path to rise.","In the original timeline, it was also this continuous heavy rain that nearly dragged Eastern Yi into an abyss of eternal doom.","Yanji, who was sent as an envoy to Great Yan, took Sima Jing's illegitimate son, Oshima, with him on his way back to his country. He personally went to ask for help, and the Sima family secretly transported a large amount of medicinal herbs and food to Eastern Yi by sea."]},{"number":392,"title":"Chapter 392: Conspiracy and Open Conspiracy","paragraphs":["It was tantamount to undermining Great Yan to fatten outsiders during Great Yan's own difficult times. As one fell, the other rose; helping Dongyi tide over its crisis caused the prices of medicine and grain within Great Yan to soar significantly.","Without the Sima family's subsidies, how could Dongyi have risen to power later on?","One must know that the supplies Dongyi received were originally meant for the disaster-stricken people in Great Yan's Jiangnan region. Dongyi flourished, while the people of Jiangnan suffered heavy casualties due to a lack of food and medicine.","Now, the grass on the graves of the Sima clan had withered and yellowed twice over. Without a traitor draining their own resources to help them this time, what would Dongyi use to survive this calamity!","Emperor Mingxi tapped his fingers lightly on the imperial desk, raised his eyes, and asked Huo Ying, \"My dear minister Huo, what do you think? And my dear minister Ling, the students of the Imperial College seem quite active these past few days.\"","Hearing the Emperor call his name, Huo Ying stepped forward steadily, bowed, and said, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, this humble subject feels that Lord Feng's words are reasonable.\"","He weighed his words and said slowly, \"Dongyi is currently a place of trouble. As the rain continues to fall, internal strife is bound to arise.","Our Great Yan only needs to guard the coastline well to prevent 'pirates' from robbing the coastal people. Without supplies, they won't last long.","By then, a riddled and devastated Dongyi will be a good Dongyi.\"","Feng Tang's eyes flickered as he added, \"If pirates really do come ashore, our dynasty's new naval forces can just use them for training.\"","Feng Tang cupped his hands toward Emperor Mingxi, his eyes suddenly astonishingly bright. He said, \"Your Majesty, this subject suggests that we keep the captured 'pirates' well-preserved.","After Dongyi's floods and plagues have passed, we can issue a 'state letter' and take these people to Dongyi to demand an explanation. Dongyi's naval forces disturbed the peace of our dynasty's people; shouldn't we properly calculate the compensation with them?\"","Everyone understood the hidden meaning in Feng Tang's words. They could only say that this kid's heart was truly black. Was this the reason why the Junior Preceptor valued him so highly?","Ling Yinghua also stepped forward and said, \"Replying to Your Majesty, there is no shortage of erudite scholars among the students of the Imperial College. This humble subject suggests that we could also send some of them to the south in rotation.","Whether they personally go to Dongyi for disaster relief or stay in Great Yan to help the people in the south, we shall see their own choices.\"","Feng Tang stepped forward again to add, \"If there are students who wish to personally go to Dongyi for disaster relief, Your Majesty is benevolent, and the imperial court can send ships to safely transport them to the island, and pick them up after the disaster.","Dongyi has the responsibility to guarantee the personal safety of our dynasty's students. If they meet with an accident... our Great Yan will definitely seek an explanation from the King of Dongyi.\"","Good heavens, Ling Yinghua, standing next to him, cried out inwardly. He looked at Feng Tang in shock and doubt, as if knowing him for the first time.","These venomous schemes came one after another. Speaking the gentlest words while doing the most ruthless things. With his words out, if any Imperial College student really lost their head and went to Dongyi...","That would truly be like hitting a dog with a meat bun—gone never to return. Even if they were perfectly safe in Dongyi, he could open his eyes wide and claim they died in Dongyi!","Ling Yinghua still had this bit of confidence and discernment!","Just like the members of the diplomatic mission still living in the post house. Minister You had people watching them in three shifts for twelve double-hours a day, not daring to stop for a moment, afraid that they would get injured, fall ill, or play disappearing acts, only to have their people demand them back.","In extraordinary times, every country was suffering from either droughts or floods. No one was having a good time. Great Yan could not afford to be extorted over this, but that didn't stop them from scheming against others.","The few members of the diplomatic mission being muttered about by Ling Jijiu were currently sitting around in the tearoom they had visited three days ago.","On such a cold day, they had the windows open. Outside were a few snow-white plum blossoms, faintly emitting a refreshing fragrance.","If one didn't know that despite the winter being as cold as ever, not a single snowflake had fallen, those trees full of flowers would be mistaken for winter snow.","Because they were guarding against eavesdroppers, they opened the windows. The surveillance personnel sent by You Mingmin didn't dare get too close and could only watch them from afar to ensure no one met with an 'accident'.","In the brazier before them, the burning charcoal made a soft crackling sound, which seemed especially loud in the silent room.","Gan Tang held his teacup with both hands to warm them. Lan Xuan'er stared blankly at the exquisite plum blossom pastries on the table. She remembered that Prince Ming, Xie Ying's favorite winter snacks were these various pastries made from winter plum blossoms.","Xi Ling looked at the snow-like plum blossoms outside the window, drinking tea brewed with freshly picked plum blossoms, feeling a sense of pity in his heart. If only it would snow now, how wonderful it would be.","His leisure formed a sharp contrast with the others who were frowning tightly at the note in the middle of the table.","Xi Yuanshan was the first to break the silence, saying, \"So Brother Yanji, you speculate that even today, the heavy rain in Dongyi has not stopped?\"","Although Yanji really wanted to deny it, rational analysis forced him to nod heavily. \"Yes, I do have this concern.\"","With continuous torrential rain for days on end, let alone other places, even the capital where nobles gathered and the royal residences were located, the drainage capacity of the waterways there was worrying under such heavy rain.","In such a cold winter, after being drenched in rain, if it froze after the rain stopped, Yanji dared not imagine the consequences. And Oshima, who was sitting beside him without saying a word, had a somewhat dull gaze at this moment.","Not knowing what he thought of, he blurted out. Although his voice was soft, everyone present, including Xi Ling who only had half his mind on the matter, heard it clearly.","He murmured softly, \"If only father were still here. Such a great man like him would definitely have a way to save Dongyi.\"","Except for Yanji, whose face showed a moment of awkwardness, the rest of them had faces full of question marks. Who was Oshima's father?","Someone who could save Dongyi single-handedly could not be an unknown nobody, yet they had never heard of this person!","Seeing their inquiring faces, Yanji didn't want to expose his own family's shortcomings and quickly changed the subject, saying, \"How much do you all believe the rumors that Great Yan prepared for the drought two years in advance?\"","Xi Yuanshan glanced at the people opposite him, lowered his eyes, and chuckled lightly. \"I have met Yun Tianxing, the Director of Great Yan's Directorate of Astronomy. This person does have some ability.","But to say that he could predict a major disaster years later through star charts two years in advance, I don't believe it.\"","Bei Ye also chimed in, \"In my opinion, Great Yan was just lucky. Their agriculture has developed quickly in the past two years, so the accompanying water conservancy projects naturally had to keep up. Thus... all these measures just happened to coincide with the severe drought, which was then over-interpreted by those with ulterior motives and spread as something miraculous.\"","For some unknown reason, Bei Ye didn't want Yanji to think too much, especially when it involved Yue Fuguang.","Yanji shook his head and said with a half-smile, \"You haven't forgotten that Great Yan also has a 'Divine Maiden', right?\"","Sure enough, speak of the devil!","He had long felt that they were hiding something from him. Ever since they returned from the hunting grounds, they had paid special attention to that Junior Preceptor. They thought they hid it well and that he didn't know!","Their attitude toward Junior Preceptor Yue was also very intriguing, being both respectful and fearful. As members of foreign royal families, they shouldn't have such feelings toward a minister of another country, even if she had been granted the title of prince and was hailed as a Divine Maiden by the commoners.","He firmly believed that Great Yan was 'creating a god', but their attitudes made him unable to resist testing the waters.","When Bei Yue heard the words 'Divine Maiden', his hand pouring tea paused for a moment. After slowly filling his cup with tea, he chuckled lightly and said, \"Brother Yanji still believes the rumors of those ignorant and foolish commoners?\""]},{"number":393,"title":"Chapter 393: Are those envoys behaving themselves","paragraphs":["Yan Ji's eyes flashed, and he chuckled lightly, \"To be honest with you all, I truly believe that Junior Preceptor Yue possesses some divine abilities.\"","He looked up and swept his gaze over the six people. \"Otherwise, you wouldn't be suppressing the scholars and students of your own countries, forbidding them from criticizing her.\"","The expressions of the others changed simultaneously. Bei Ye even forced a laugh, \"Brother Yan Ji is overthinking it. We are guests on someone else's turf, so naturally, we should have the self-awareness of guests, shouldn't we?\"","Meanwhile, Yue Fuguang, the very person they were discussing, was currently nestled in a warm lounge chair. As she snacked on the plum blossom cakes sent from the palace, she listened to the system broadcasting the latest news to her.","\"Tongtong, are you saying these are all Feng Tang's advices to the Emperor?\"","This man had quite a brilliant mind. She had only murmured a few extra words in his ear, and he had managed to draw inferences, playing both open and hidden schemes to perfection.","Even though I've set my sights on your territory, I definitely need a justifiable cause. If you send your navy into my dynasty to plunder the commoners, we naturally have to lead our troops to your doorstep to demand an explanation.","As for whether these pirates were actually disguised Dongyi navy soldiers, that wasn't important.","Especially the part about the Imperial Academy students—how was that any different from the classic excuse of a missing soldier from back in the day?","[Host, I truly believe it this time. If we weren't pretending to be a deity, the two of us combined wouldn't be able to outsmart him alone.]","The system had been present for every word its host had spoken to Feng Tang. For Feng Tang to infer so much from its host's fragmented words meant he had far more cunning than its host.","As the saying goes, the supreme art of war is to subdue the enemy through strategy. Great Yan's current response was much better than the initial plan of its ruler and ministers. At the very least, it could save the lives of tens of thousands of Great Yan soldiers while leaving the other countries speechless.","Yue Fuguang smiled smugly. The gap in status could make up for their lack of intellect. Even if her actions were somewhat inappropriate, others would automatically come up with justifications for her. This was the convenience that came with status.","Having understood the plans of Great Yan's ruler and ministers, Yue Fuguang felt relieved. Dongyi was merely the first step. As for the other countries, without her special support, given Great Yan's current national strength, they would have to gnaw them down one by one.","She just didn't know if they would give them the chance to defeat them individually.","Thinking of this, she set down the plum blossom cake in her hand and asked the system, \"Are those members of the diplomatic mission behaving themselves?\"","[The self-harm incidents haven't happened again. You Mingmin's people are keeping a very close watch. Bei Ye and his group wanted to go out and contact the spies in Shangjing a few times, but they had to drop the idea because of the tails behind them.]","Recalling what the system had told her a few days ago, Yue Fuguang asked, \"Because Du Mingqi, Song Min, and the others were suddenly imprisoned, Northern Li's avenue for purchasing high-quality seeds was blocked.","The old emperor's spies planted in Shangjing contacted Bei Ye and Bei Yue, asking them to find a way to investigate the cause and purchase the seeds. Did those two do it?","Have the spy dens planted by the old emperor in Shangjing been wiped out yet?\"","The moment this was brought up, the system immediately got energized. It said happily, [Zheng Zicheng truly lives up to being Zheng Feng's father; both father and son are equally full of schemes.","After Zheng Zicheng and the Crown Prince followed that person to their den, they didn't arrest them immediately. Instead, they played the long game to catch a bigger fish.","Sure enough, a couple of days ago, they took down three dens in one swoop and arrested over a dozen people.","Host, one of these three dens was directly controlled by Gan Sheng.]","Hearing that South Yue was involved, Yue Fuguang's interest was immediately piqued. \"Weren't they catching Northern Li's spies? How did South Yue get dragged into this?\"","Are spies in this era all this unprofessional? Having horizontal connections between members is bad enough, but crossing borders? Do they really need to expand their business that widely?","[I went to eavesdrop on the interrogation. It seems it was because a spy from Northern Li fell ill and went to a medical clinic run by a South Yue spy for treatment.","As a result, after a few interactions, they discovered each other's identities. Since they are in the same line of work, certain habits among peers are easily spotted.","So the two of them started contacting each other privately, sometimes even exchanging intelligence. That time, he used the excuse of seeing a doctor to visit the clinic just to gather information on Song Min, which was how the Crown Prince and his people set their sights on the South Yue clinic.]","One could only say the South Yue people were unlucky, happening to run right into Great Yan's line of fire.","\"Didn't Bei Ye and Bei Yue know that You Mingmin sent people to monitor their actions? Why didn't they give a warning?\"","Surely her previous instigation and intimidation couldn't have taken effect this quickly!","[Host's words must have worked. The rift between Bei Yue and the old emperor is growing larger by the day. As for Bei Ye, although he is in Great Yan, he sent a trusted aide back to Northern Li after returning from the hunting grounds. Having verified the Host's words, he is even less likely to cover up anything for the old emperor.]","The system's voice grew even more cheerful as it spoke, [If it weren't for the fear of not being able to explain things when they returned, the two of them would have loved to help the Crown Prince and the others eradicate all the spies Bei Ji planted in Great Yan.","However, even just losing these two dens has infuriated Bei Ji. A letter fiercely cursing his two unfilial sons is currently on its way to Shangjing.","In a few days, the two of them will get to enjoy this fatherly love from thousands of miles away.","As for the matter of the high-quality seeds, their several petitions to Emperor Mingxi were just a show of feigned compliance for the rest of the diplomatic mission. In reality, they haven't done a single piece of actual work, clearly just going through the motions.]","Ever since returning from the hunting grounds, it was obvious that these few people had been slacking off, yet they were unusually active in gathering all sorts of information.","Yue Fuguang and the system had just been talking about them a couple of days ago. Today, Cuizhu walked in holding several invitation cards.","Yue Fuguang casually opened one of the golden cards. Upon seeing the vigorous and beautiful handwriting on it, she could not help but raise an eyebrow and praise, \"Good calligraphy!\"","She picked up another pale blue card, and a faint, cold fragrance wafted over. It was the unique, delicate scent of green calyx plum blossoms.","Her fingers tapped lightly on the remaining three cards on the table. After a brief moment of thought, she instructed Qingzhu, \"Prepare some tea and pastries. We have guests arriving.\"","Watching Qingzhu head toward the small kitchen, Yue Fuguang then told Cuizhu to invite the guests in. \"Bring them to the front tearoom. I will be there in a moment.\"","The New Year was fast approaching. Not a single snowflake had fallen, yet the weather was colder than in previous years, and the Hongwen Pavilion had already closed for the holidays.","She had become increasingly indolent over the past two days. Having asked the Emperor for a leave of absence, she had not attended morning court for three days. Looking at her loose hair bun and casual loungewear, she called for Cuiyu to help her freshen up.","By the time a completely refreshed Yue Fuguang arrived at the tearoom, Gan Tang, Bei Yue, and the others were already there.","Seeing her enter, they all stood up to pay their respects. Yue Fuguang wore a faint smile as she returned their greetings one by one. Neither overly warm nor cold, this slightly formal attitude made the group feel even more uncertain.","After everyone took their respective seats as host and guests, it was the older Bei Yue who initiated the conversation. Smiling, he picked up a carved red sandalwood box from his side and placed it on the table.","He opened the copper clasp and took out a perfectly round, dazzling pearl the size of a peeled lychee. \"Lord Junior Preceptor, this bright pearl is named the Moon Pearl. I came across it by chance.\"","Seeing that Yue Fuguang did not show much expression even when presented with such a beautiful pearl, he sighed inwardly. Sure enough, with Yue Fuguang's high status in Great Yan, what kind of rare treasures had she not seen? However, this was the absolute best thing he could offer at the moment.","His smile grew even more humble. \"The New Year is approaching. As a guest residing in Great Yan, I have few worldly possessions. Only this pearl can be considered a rare novelty. Therefore, I took the liberty of visiting today to present this pearl to Your Excellency as a New Year's gift. I hope you will not decline.\""]},{"number":394,"title":"Chapter 394: I Give You a Grand Stage; Speak Up If You Have a Dream","paragraphs":["When Yan Ji ordered his men to bring up a red coral over a meter tall, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but start complaining to her system.","\"Little Zhu, why do you think these people suddenly came to my door with precious gifts? If we really think about it, our only relationship consists of assassinations and being assassinated.\"","Hearing the word \"assassination,\" the several people sitting below—except for Yan Ji and Oshima, who couldn't hear the voice—all lowered their heads. Their faces turned either flushed or pale, and their hands twisted together beneath their wide sleeves.","[Master, is it possible that the weasel paying respects to the hen harbors no good intentions? Besides, as for these gifts, only they mortals would find them precious. Mortal items without any spiritual energy aren't even worthy of being used as decorations in our immortal cave.]","Mortals? Mortal items?","The few people, already terrified by the word \"assassination,\" astutely caught these words. As they repeated them over and over in their minds and seemed to come to a realization, only they knew the stormy waves crashing in their hearts.","\"You are all too kind. I usually dislike trivial matters and have had little contact with you all. I haven't even asked yet, are you accustomed to living in the post house?\"","Bei Yue was currently so frightened by his own speculations that his legs were shaking like Parkinson's. Hearing Yue Fuguang's question, he still firmly stood up to reply on behalf of everyone, \"Thank you for your concern, Junior Preceptor. The post house is very comprehensive, especially Minister You, who has been taking great care of us.\"","Yue Fuguang held back her laughter, really wanting to ask if his so-called \"taking great care\" meant sending people to watch them in three shifts. That was indeed quite the \"care\"! If Bei Yue hadn't said it through gritted teeth, it might have had a bit more credibility.","\"Minister You is experienced and prudent, and he is familiar with you all. If you need anything, there is no need to hold back. Keeping you all safe and sound in Great Yan is something we can still manage.\"","Yue Fuguang's words sounded like a warning to everyone's ears. Xi Ling and the others thought back to the little schemes they had hatched at the hunting ground that day, and they couldn't help but feel even more afraid to say anything, only murmuring their agreement.","For some reason, facing Junior Preceptor Yue now gave them more pressure than facing their own imperial fathers and mothers. Of course, the two clueless brothers from Eastern Yi were the exception.","Seeing Gan Tang with her head slightly lowered, her gaze constantly falling on the exquisite guest pastries on the table before her, Yue Fuguang smiled and picked up a pastry from her own small table, taking a small bite. \"The pastries made today taste quite good. Would you all like to try some?\"","The group hastily thanked her. Eating meant they didn't have to speak, and they actually breathed a sigh of relief in secret. Even Bei Ye, who disliked sweets, picked up a piece of milk cake with trembling hands and took a tiny bite.","After finishing a piece of pastry, Yan Ji noticed that the group had been acting abnormal since they walked in. Now, each of them looked like frightened quails, timid and submissive. The way they gnawed on the pastries made them look exactly like ignorant country bumpkins. They hadn't mentioned a single piece of the official business they had agreed upon before coming.","Bei Ye and the others: What do you know, you trash! Speechless.","After eating the pastries, the few with decent martial arts skills immediately noticed a very faint warm current slowly flowing through their body's eight extraordinary meridians. Their previously trembling bodies and the somewhat sluggish minds from expending too much energy dealing with Yue Fuguang had now cleared up significantly.","As the group buried their heads in eating, Yan Ji, after desperately winking at Bei Yue and the others for the fifth time to no avail, could only bring up the topic himself. \"The Junior Preceptor's pastries are indeed delicious. I have never eaten such novel varieties even in the Eastern Yi palace.\"","The system couldn't help but complain, [These pastries are all varieties from over a thousand years later, of course you haven't seen them. The ingredients are excellent things that mortals can't even grow, it'd be weird if you had eaten them!]","Cough, cough!","Cough, cough!","Perhaps because they found them delicious, or perhaps out of panic, Gan Tang and the others ate piece after piece. Hearing the system's words now, the few who were nibbling on the pastries almost choked to death on the food in their mouths, but they couldn't bear to put them down.","Lan Xuan'er looked a bit embarrassedly at the snowflake crisp in her hand, wondering if she should continue eating or continue eating!","Before Yan Ji could utter his next words, he was suddenly interrupted by their coughing. He frowned and shot a warning sidelong glance at Bei Ye; his voice was the loudest, truly detestable!","\"Everyone, eat slowly, don't choke.\" After showing concern for them, Yue Fuguang's gaze fell back onto Yan Ji, signaling him to continue.","Yan Ji reorganized his disrupted thoughts and still decided to use the pastries as a talking point.","He glanced at Bei Ye and, seeing quite a lot of white crumbs dropped on the table in front of him, frowned in disapproval. \"Brother Bei Ye, I remember you dislike sweets. If so, you could just explain it to Junior Preceptor Yue. The Junior Preceptor is benevolent and presumably wouldn't blame you for it. Why must you waste food like this?\"","Bei Ye: Is this dog coming at me? Do I look like a soft persimmon?!","He carefully stole a glance at Yue Fuguang. Seeing no extra expression on her face, his heart relaxed just a tiny bit. When it came to grudges, the one he had forged with her was the biggest among them all!","Seeing Yan Ji trying to use him as a scapegoat, if it were in the past, Bei Ye would have given him a huge slap across the face long ago. But right now, in front of Yue Fuguang, he didn't dare to act out of line at all.","The moment a slight wicked thought crossed his mind, he would think of the massive crater at the hunting ground that night, and Song Tu, who had been struck into a bloody pulp.","His death was more tragic and terrifying than anyone else's, further indicating that Junior Preceptor Yue was warning him!","Seeing Bei Ye remain silent despite being spoken to like this, Yan Ji thought he had the moral high ground and had left him speechless. So, he pointed at the crumbs on Bei Ye's table. \"Brother Bei Ye really shouldn't be so wasteful. A single extravagant expenditure of ours is enough for an ordinary commoner's family to live on for many days.\"","Those crumbs in front of Bei Ye were actually the shredded coconut attached to the milk cake. Among the six-colored pastries on the table, this was indeed the least sweet one.","However, Yue Fuguang wasn't going to say much. Watching them bite at each other was much more interesting.","Seeing Yue Fuguang's gaze also fall upon the table in front of Bei Ye, Yan Ji thought his scheme had succeeded. Since the others had no intention of supporting Bei Ye either, he continued to attack him.","\"Nowadays, with constant droughts and floods across the various nations, who knows how many commoners are going hungry because of it. As members of the imperial family supported by the people, we should naturally lead by example and find ways to save the masses from their suffering in this critical moment.\"","He opportunely revealed a sorrowful expression, then looked at Yue Fuguang with a face full of envy. \"My Eastern Yi does not have the blessing of Great Yan to obtain a divine figure like Junior Preceptor Yue, who can foresee natural disasters and make preparations early on!\"","Hearing this, Yue Fuguang knew exactly what kind of nonsense he was going to spout, but she merely smiled and didn't reply.","I'll give you a big stage; if you have a dream, just speak it out!","[Master, what does he mean by this? Isn't it normal for a divine being to know these things? Since this ugly thing knows Master is a divine figure yet still has a face full of schemes, is he complaining that his life is too long? Just watch Little Zhu strike him dead with a lightning bolt, unless his life is too tough!]","\"Little Zhu, look at Bei Ye and the others. They tried to assassinate me several times, and I still kept their little lives. What does Yan Ji's minor antic amount to? Calm down and just watch the show. They're nothing but ants that can be crushed casually. It won't be too late to deal with them when I get tired of watching.\""]},{"number":395,"title":"Chapter 395: Plea","paragraphs":["[Master is just too bored staying in this mortal realm, which is why she kept the dog lives of these few people for amusement. Otherwise, with Little Zhu's temper, the grass on their graves would already be towering high.]","The few people whose grave grass should have been towering high were either shrinking their necks or freezing in place as if hit by an immobilization spell. Only their slightly trembling bodies indicated that this was not a still picture.","Especially Bei Ye, who was specifically singled out. His pupils dilated for a moment, and his trembling hands tightly gripped a corner of his clothes, forcefully resisting the urge to immediately jump up and beg for forgiveness.","Because he had just horrifyingly discovered that when he wanted to say something about the past assassination attempt, his throat felt as if it were being choked by an invisible force, rendering him completely unable to make a single sound.","Sitting next to him, Bei Yue saw his younger brother trembling like a leaf. Beneath the table, he silently stretched out his foot and gave his brother's calf a swift kick.","A sharp pain shot up Bei Ye's calf, instantly sobering him up quite a bit. He swept a glance at Bei Yue from the corner of his eye, temporarily forgiving his opportunistic revenge.","Aside from terror, the feelings in their hearts were incredibly complex. In the past, they had always viewed others as ants. They never expected that one day, a mountain even more immovable than their imperial father and mother would appear before them. Experiencing what it was like to be the ants themselves—only those who endured it could understand the taste of it!","Only Yanji, who was completely oblivious to all this, saw that Yue Fuguang was not taking the bait. He silently gritted his teeth and continued, Junior Preceptor, please forgive my presumptuous visit today. This humble king has an unreasonable request, and I hope Your Excellency can agree to it for the sake of the good neighborly friendship between our two countries.","[Good neighborly friendship between our two countries? What kind of good neighbor sends their navy to masquerade as pirates to plunder their neighbor's merchant ships and pillage their neighbor's citizens? Colluding with Sima Jing in an attempt to subvert the Great Yan's empire, and decades later, when the other countries' national power declined, even trying to swallow an elephant like a snake, invading the Central Plains to sit as the sole overlord of this world.]","With every crime the system listed, the hearts of Bei Yue and the others sank a fraction further. The words 'she knows everything' looped infinitely in their minds.","The matters of Dongyi, whether past or future, she knew them all!","Then, aside from the assassination, Junior Preceptor Yue probably, most likely, knew absolutely everything else each of them had ever done.","The group looked with pity at the still-oblivious Yanji as he continued talking to himself, If the Junior Preceptor can agree, my Dongyi will surely offer a heavy reward in the future.","Yue Fuguang chuckled carelessly, her fingers gently rubbing the outside of her teacup. It seemed the patterns on it were more interesting than Yanji's so-called heavy reward. Her voice was somewhat cold and distant, Your Excellency exaggerates. This Junior Preceptor is highly regarded by the Emperor and supported by the people. Wealth, power, fame, and profit are all in my hands.","She set down the teacup. The crisp sound of the cup's base hitting the tabletop felt like a strike against the hearts of everyone seated.","Although I do not know what your request entails, this Junior Preceptor is young, and the floods are a major issue. I am afraid I cannot help Your Excellency with anything.","Hearing the word 'young', the others suddenly remembered that after the new year, this person would only be twelve years old!","[Although Master is already over three thousand years old, her age as a human is indeed younger than the few people sitting here.]","The two Xi brothers had been so nervous earlier that their mouths were completely dry. Seeing that Yue Fuguang's attention was entirely on Yanji, they exchanged a glance and finally gathered the courage to pick up the completely cold tea on the table to take a sip, only to hear the claim of being three thousand years old.","Cough, cough!","Clatter!","One choked on the cold tea so hard that his throat ached and his nasal cavity burned, his tears flowing out uncontrollably.","The other's hand trembled, nearly dropping the cup in his hand to the floor. Fortunately, Xi Yuanshan was a martial artist, and he managed to catch the cup in time after it slipped from his grasp.","Please forgive us, Junior Preceptor. It was our brotherly duo who lacked manners. The two hurriedly stood up, apologizing with utmost trepidation.","Yue Fuguang waved her hand dismissively and said, No matter, sit down, all of you!","Thank you for your magnanimity, Junior Preceptor! The two carefully perched only half of their bottoms on their chairs, not daring to sit fully, and they certainly did not dare to touch the tea and snacks on the table again.","They were terrified that the entity known as Little Zhu would spout some other shocking revelation.","At this moment, the group had no spare energy to ponder how those three thousand years were calculated. They all looked at Yanji, whose conversation had been interrupted once again and who had been explicitly rejected by Yue Fuguang. His face was now a mix of embarrassment and anger, entirely devoid of his previous supreme confidence.","With a contorted face, he forced down his emotions, stood up again, and took two steps forward. He Jin, who was standing behind Yue Fuguang, immediately reached for the sword at his waist.","By her side, Shen Chunying silently took half a step forward. Yue Fuguang waved her right hand, and Shen Chunying immediately bowed and silently retreated.","Yanji acted as if he hadn't seen their movements. He stopped about four or five meters away from Yue Fuguang, bowed ninety degrees, and replaced his expression with one of sorrow. He spoke with earnest pleading, Junior Preceptor, please hear me out. It has been raining heavily in my Dongyi lands for ten consecutive days. Seeing that the New Year is only three days away, my dynasty's people are still living in deep waters and scorching fire during this festive season.","Yue Fuguang nodded, playing with the jade pendant at her waist, but the words she spoke were exceptionally cold, And what does that have to do with this Junior Preceptor?","[Exactly, beneath the immortals, all are ants. He doesn't actually think we would care about the lives of mortals, does he?]","The six-person ant squad silently lowered their heads, trying their best to minimize their presence. Bei Yue especially regretted suggesting they come to the Yu Manor to test this person.","If they managed to walk out of the Yu Manor intact later, it would be entirely thanks to their ancestors in the underworld fighting tooth and nail to bless them.","Yue Fuguang's cold and ruthless words left Yanji stunned on the spot. People like them usually spoke and acted with as much tact and subtlety as possible. When had they ever seen someone so blunt? Moreover, saying such things showed a complete disregard for her own reputation and the diplomatic relations between the two countries.","Yanji simply couldn't understand where Yue Fuguang, who wasn't even twelve years old yet, got her confidence. Was she not afraid of being punished by Emperor Mingxi?","With the New Year approaching, Emperor Mingxi, whose imperial seal was already stored away for the holidays, was still diligently reviewing the last few memorials in the Imperial Study.","Suddenly, an inexplicable chill ran down his body. He felt a premonition, always suspecting that some unruly subjects were out to harm him again!","With his smile frozen on his face, Yanji felt truly helpless at this moment. He cast a pleading look at Bei Ye and the others.","Bei Ye, who had just been stepped on by him, still held a grudge. He rolled his eyes at Yanji and then lowered his head to play with his own hands. Bei Yue, who had proposed coming here, didn't dare look at him, and the others all kept their heads down, pretending to be quails.","Yanji wore an expression of grief and indignation. Hadn't they agreed to advance and retreat together before coming here? Why was every single one of them playing dead now!","Just when he was at his most helpless, a timid voice came from behind him, Junior Preceptor, my royal brother and I have both heard that you were once guided by an immortal. By observing the celestial phenomena, you know of droughts and floods, and with a pinch of your fingers, you can calculate fortune and misfortune.","With a thud, he fell heavily to his knees, prostrating himself on the ground. Yue Fuguang glanced at the wooden floor of the tearoom. Very good, it wasn't broken. Otherwise, she would definitely make this person pay until he didn't even have his underwear left.","Oshima Tadashi lay prostrate on the ground, his voice even more earnest than Yanji's. Junior Preceptor possesses immortal methods. I, Oshima Tadashi, implore you to look upon the diplomatic relations between our two countries and the millions of citizens in Dongyi, and help us divine just once: when will this heavy rain in our dynasty cease?","Thump, thump, thump!","Three loud kowtows smashed heavily against the wooden floor. Yue Fuguang felt a bit of regret watching this. If she had known earlier, this tearoom should have been paved with blue bricks—that would have kowtowed you to death!"]},{"number":396,"title":"Chapter 396: What did you say, you heard it too","paragraphs":["If one didn't know better, they would think he was here visiting a grave!","Yanji had also recovered from his various emotions at this time. He gritted his teeth, knelt down as well, and prostrated himself on the ground, saying, \"I beg the Goddess to take pity on the people of my dynasty and save them from the flood.\"","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow. They were even calling her Goddess now. They wanted to put her on a pedestal and emotionally blackmail her!","But that would require her to have morals in the first place!","She didn't have such a thing. What was the use of putting her on a pedestal?","Yue Fuguang was impervious to persuasion and repeated, \"What does this have to do with me, the Junior Preceptor?\"","Yanji's mind only went blank for a moment before he regained his fighting spirit. He looked at Yue Fuguang, who had started playing with the purse at her waist again, with a look of disapproval. \"You are a Goddess. Shouldn't a Goddess have compassion for the world?","Many people in my dynasty also worship the statue of the Junior Preceptor at home. They are also your believers. Doesn't Your Excellency want to save your own believers?\"","The corners of Yue Fuguang's mouth curled up slightly, forming a mocking smile. \"Are you referring to the worship where even secretly burning a stick of incense to a statue will get you thrown into prison, or the part where the Dongyi imperial court will burn any statue or portrait of me on the spot if they find it?\"","Her smile grew wider, but it didn't reach her eyes. \"There are no believers of this Junior Preceptor in the four islands of Dongyi, so what does their life or death have to do with me?\"","Faced with Yue Fuguang's questioning, Yanji, who knew more about the inside story, seemed to have all his strength and bones drained from his body. He slumped to the ground, his face ashen.","At this moment, he regretted more than ever that he had supported his father's massacre of the lowly commoners who worshipped Yue Fuguang's statue instead of the Amaterasu Omikami.","If they hadn't done that, would the result have been different?","Yue Fuguang: You're overthinking it. It wouldn't have been any different!","Yanji's reflection at this time was not that he thought he was wrong. He only regretted that he hadn't been secretive enough when he was trying to establish his authority and make an example of others, which led to this matter reaching Yue Fuguang's ears and causing today's humiliation.","Yes, in Yanji's eyes, Yue Fuguang was deliberately humiliating him. As for the reason? It was very simple. Among the six countries, only the Dongyi imperial family had insisted on cracking down on Yue Fuguang's believers in the country in recent years.","The show was over, and Yue Fuguang wanted to send them away. She picked up her teacup and took a small sip. \"The tea is cold. I suppose you don't like cold tea either. It's almost the New Year, and everyone is very busy. I won't keep you for lunch.\"","Beiyue and the others: That's not what you said on the way to the hunting ground!","Beiyue and the others led Oshima, whose face was flushed, and Yanji, who kept his head down and showed no extra expression, all the way out of the Yu Manor.","Yue Fuguang thought that this matter would end here. Except for some people in the imperial court who were still paying attention to when the rain in Dongyi would stop, most people's minds were focused on the drought in their own country and the New Year's family reunion and visiting friends.","Yue Fuguang had become increasingly lazy over the past two years. Except for the first year she arrived, when she followed Old Madam Yu and her husband out to visit relatives and friends for New Year greetings, she had been hiding in her own courtyard for peace and quiet every year since.","\"Golden Bean, call me Auntie!\"","Yue Fuguang held a bright yellow golden lock with red tassels and teased the eldest son of her eldest brother's family, who was just over a year old, like teasing a puppy.","\"Goo... goo!\"","\"Goo... croak!\"","The little milk dumpling, dressed up like a red envelope, sucked in his stomach and pouted, trying hard to call her Auntie clearly. Unfortunately, he was small and weak. After trying a few times, he still let out the sounds of a pigeon and a frog!","\"Okay, okay, Auntie heard you. I'll give you the jade pendant to play with.\"","Seeing that the little guy refused to admit defeat and was about to gather his breath to pout and call her again, Yue Fuguang quickly stopped him and stuffed the heavy golden lock in her hand into his chubby little hands.","It wasn't that she was kind-hearted and didn't want to tease the child. It was really because this boy tried too hard every time he called her Auntie, and his saliva sprayed like a fountain, not distinguishing between friend and foe.","\"This is for our Jade Bead.\" Yue Fuguang said as she stuffed a translucent white jade pendant into the hands of a beautiful baby who was sitting in a pile of pretty dolls, looking at this one, touching that one, and smiling so much that her eyes curved into crescents.","Yu Ningxuan took a soft and glutinous milk cake to tease her soft and glutinous little niece, who was even softer than the milk cake in her hand, given to her by her second sister-in-law. \"Jade Bead, your Seventh Auntie's pastries are the most delicious. Let Auntie hug you, and I'll give you the cake.\"","Upon hearing about the delicious cake, the little friend Jade Bead immediately dropped the doll and crawled towards Yue Fuguang. Auntie said Seventh Auntie's pastries were the most delicious, so of course she had to let Seventh Auntie hug her.","\"Hey, you little traitor, you only know how to be close to your Seventh Auntie!\" Yu Ningxuan pretended to tickle her.","Jade Bead obviously had experience. She immediately crawled faster, twisted her little bottom, and buried her head in Yue Fuguang's arms, not forgetting to peek at her aunt.","Yu Ningxin and the others laughed heartily when they saw this. \"Jade Bead will be one year old soon. She crawls so fast. When it's time for her first birthday catch, we should get her a big venue.\"","Yu Ningxuan also laughed. \"Don't underestimate this little girl just because she's small. She's very smart.\"","It was unknown whether it was because Fuguang usually spoiled the two little ones too much or gave them too much, but these two little guys knew to be close to Fuguang just a few days after they were born.","When they grew a little older and started to recognize people, they even ranked her ahead of their own parents.","What they liked most was to surround her, neither crying nor making a fuss, very well-behaved!","Yue Fuguang picked up a piece of milk cake and gave it to the chubby baby whose teeth hadn't fully grown yet. \"Eat the cake. Our Jade Bead won't pay attention to your Second Auntie. When spring comes...\"","\"Miss, several princes and princesses from the diplomatic mission have come to pay you New Year greetings. They have already arrived at the front hall.\"","Just as Yue Fuguang was about to make empty promises to the little guy, she saw Cuizhu come in with a visiting card.","Yue Fuguang regretfully handed the glutinous rice dumpling in her arms to Yu Ningxuan and straightened the collar on the little girl's chest. \"Be good, Jade Bead. Seventh Auntie will make empty promises to you next time.\"","\"Second Sister, keep an eye on them. Don't let the little guys choke.\"","\"Don't worry, don't worry!\" The sisters had learned a lot of the first aid methods taught by Seventh Sister. They heard that two days ago, the granddaughter of Lord Bao's family had used this method to save her younger brother who choked on a date. This matter spread widely for a while, and many people suddenly wanted to learn this first aid method.","Seeing that Yue Fuguang wouldn't even spare children, the system couldn't help but complain. [Host, you've made a whole basket of empty promises to these two little guys. They can't possibly eat them all!]","'When I was a child, I was also promised a bunch of wishes. How many of them were actually fulfilled in the end?'","[You're planning to pass down the empty promises you've eaten to the next generation, right!] Even if this next generation wasn't born by the host herself.","Yue Fuguang raised her head proudly and strode outward. 'Why can't this be considered a kind of inheritance!' These were her own nephew and niece. One family shouldn't eat two families' empty promises.","Speaking of making wishes, the system remembered something else. [Host, it's been almost five months of drought. The commoners outside burn a stick of incense to you every morning and evening, praying for sweet dew to fall from the sky and for favorable weather this year.]","'I heard it too!'","Yue Fuguang didn't stop her steps, but her words startled the system.","[Host, what did you say? You heard it too? Did you hear the wishes of those commoners outside the Yu Manor?]"]},{"number":397,"title":"Chapter 397: It's a pity he hasn't lived a good life in two years.","paragraphs":["\"It's not from outside the estate, but from those praying devoutly to the statues. I... I seem to have been able to faintly hear their voices in my dreams over the past two days.\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"It's intermittent and not very clear, but I can be sure they are praying for a bountiful harvest and favorable weather.\"","Hearing this, the White Dumpling in the system space instantly expanded a size. [Host, if you can hear these voices, does that mean... your powers have grown stronger again?]","Yue Fuguang looked at the twelve perfectly round energy storage beads in her spatial ring. Of course they had grown stronger. As the drought worsened and the common people saw no hope, the only thing they could place their hopes on was the gods.","As a living 'god', she naturally became their top choice.","She hoped these people would try a little harder, so she would have the power to truly resolve this drought.","\"Greetings, Lord Junior Preceptor.\" As soon as Yue Fuguang entered the guest reception hall, Bei Yue and the others hurriedly stood up to bow to her.","\"There is no need for formalities, please sit.\" Yue Fuguang maintained her usual cold demeanor.","It had only been five days since their last visit. For these royal descendants who were used to being flattered, her place was not exactly a welcoming spot.","After the overt and covert warnings from last time, how did they still have the nerve to come?","Yue Fuguang's gaze swept over them. The smiles on Bei Yue, Gan Tang, and the others were all forced; it seemed they were not very willing to make this trip.","Only the two brothers from Dongyi were different. When Yanji saw her, his face was full of determination to win her over, while Oshima was faintly excited.","Has this guy still not given up? Was she too soft-handed, giving him a good attitude the first two times, causing him to have some delusions?","\"Lord Junior Preceptor.\" Sure enough, they had barely sat down and taken two sips of tea before Yanji impatiently jumped out first.","He stood up and tried his best to straighten his stature, which was less than 1.6 meters. Hmm, has this guy grown a bit taller after not seeing him for a few days?","[Host, he put thick soft insoles in his shoes!]","So he was wearing height-increasing shoes. How scheming!","Not to mention Bei Yue and the others, even Gan Tang and Lan Xuan'er were taller than him. Wanting to increase his height was understandable.","Little did Yue Fuguang know, Dongyi planned to form marriage alliances with several countries, and one of the marriage candidates was Yanji. Of course he had to properly maintain his non-existent image!","\"Disturbing Junior Preceptor Yue this time is still regarding the rain in my Dongyi.\" His face full of excitement restrained itself slightly when speaking of the rain. \"Heavy rain has been falling in Dongyi for fifteen days without stopping. Yanji comes with sincerity, once again begging Lord Junior Preceptor to help divine when this heavy rain will stop.\"","Yue Fuguang watched him speak words of pleading while the arrogance on his face did not diminish in the slightest. She wondered if this guy had never begged anyone before and didn't know the proper attitude for asking for help. As for the sincerity he spoke of, she didn't see any of it.","She didn't respond to Yanji's words, only swept her gaze over the other 'smart people'.","Under Yue Fuguang's gaze, Bei Yue's face grew increasingly awkward. Blushing, he stood up and said, \"Lord Junior Preceptor, please allow me to report. The land of Dongyi has suffered from continuous heavy rain for days, and the entire nation is deeply worried. Many places across the four islands have been flooded, and the number of Dongyi citizens who have died from floods, starvation, and cold has reached tens of thousands.\"","He peeked at Yue Fuguang's expression. Upon hearing that over ten thousand civilians had died, her face remained calm, and she even had the mood to drink tea and eat pastries.","Bei Yue muttered in his heart: It seems this person is truly as the intelligence reported—she doesn't care much about the life and death of ordinary citizens and acts solely on personal preference.","If that was really the case, she would be very difficult to manipulate...","\"Therefore, hearing that Lord Junior Preceptor can divine good and bad fortune, observe the clouds, and calculate the weather, the Emperor of Dongyi has specially prepared generous gifts, hoping Lord Junior Preceptor can lend a helping hand.","The whole of Dongyi will definitely be grateful for Your Lordship's grace. Once the matter in Dongyi is resolved, we will surely build temples to worship Your Lordship for generations.\"","After speaking, he covertly shot a glance at Yanji, but in his heart, he hated him to death.","If it weren't for diplomatic relations between the two countries, and the fact that the delegation wasn't under his sole command—his father's planted spies watched the two brothers day and night—whoever wanted to come to the Yu estate could come, but he certainly didn't want to take the initiative to approach her.","This Junior Preceptor's glass-like eyes seemed to see through everything. He had no secrets at all in front of her. This made the highly secretive Bei Yue extremely uncomfortable. In front of her, he inexplicably felt a bit intimidated and inferior.","[Host, this Bei Yue is much better at speaking than that Yanji. It's a pity he won't live for more than two years.]","Seeing that everything he wanted to say had been said by Bei Yue, Yanji was not only ungrateful but also harbored hidden resentment toward him for stealing his chance to show off.","With a hint of anger on his face, believing this matter was guaranteed to succeed, his words lacked some respect. \"Our Emperor's sincerity is absolute. Please consider it carefully, Lord Junior Preceptor.\"","Hearing the system's words, Bei Yue stood frozen in shock on the spot. How could he have the mind to care about Yanji's attitude or what kind of blow he would suffer?","At this moment, he only felt a chill spreading from the soles of his feet to his entire body, as if he were being held underwater, unable to breathe.","The bone-piercing cold made the expression on his face a bit stiff.","Yue Fuguang's words entered Bei Yue's ears as if through a deep layer of water. He could see her and hear the sound, but he couldn't clearly make out what she was saying. His brain seemed to have lost the ability to process information.","\"Royal Brother, don't just stand there in a daze, Lord Junior Preceptor is speaking to you!\"","Bei Ye and the others naturally heard the contents of the heavenly voice as well, and they could understand Bei Yue's feelings upon hearing such bad news for the first time.","If this person truly predicted things like a god as the rumors said, then the date of Bei Yue's death wouldn't be wrong.","At this time, aside from the person involved, Bei Yue, the one with the most complex feelings was his younger brother, Bei Ye.","Ever since they could remember, the two had fought endlessly for their father's favor and benefits. Suddenly hearing that his royal brother didn't have long to live, he actually wasn't as happy as he had imagined; instead, his heart felt a little empty.","Bei Yue quickly composed his emotions and bowed in apology. \"Please forgive me, Lord Junior Preceptor. Last night, I had too good a time chatting with old friends and drank a few too many cups of wine. I am lacking energy today.\"","His complexion wasn't very good, seeming to truly confirm his words that excessive drinking led to low spirits.","Yue Fuguang nodded with full understanding. \"Then sit down and speak.\"","Her gaze swept over them, giving a seemingly unintentional reminder. \"Although there are many social engagements during the New Year, you gentlemen shouldn't drink too much, lest it affect your health negatively.\"","[Exactly. If this Bei Yue hadn't drank too much and lowered his guard, how could he have been poisoned with a slow-acting toxin without realizing it? It shows that drinking not only ruins affairs but also costs lives.]","\"Little Zhu, who poisoned Bei Yue? Was it Bei Ye or someone among Xi Ling and the others?\"","As her words fell, this time it wasn't just Bei Yue who was nervous; Bei Ye and the others also immediately became alert. While pricking up their ears to hear the answer, they didn't forget to exchange glances with each other.","For some reason, everyone suddenly looked suspicious. The small alliance the group had built based on a shared secret became precarious because of this poison.","Yue Fuguang: Suspecting one's neighbor of stealing an axe perfectly described their mindset at this moment!","They looked at each other as if guarding against thieves, all feeling that someone else had done it. After all, no matter how much they drank, they clearly knew whether they had made a move themselves or not."]},{"number":398,"title":"Chapter 398: Generous Gift","paragraphs":["If it wasn't him, then it had to be someone else!","Oshima seemed to sense that the atmosphere had suddenly taken a wrong turn again, and he unconsciously shrank back into his chair.","He didn't understand why, despite sitting quietly and trying to be invisible, Beiyue and the others had swept their gazes over him several times. For a start, he hadn't provoked anyone.","In the suddenly quiet atmosphere of the parlor, only Yanji, with his peculiar way of thinking, assumed that Beiyue must have offended Yue Fuguang, which led to the recent warning. Seeing Yue Fuguang's attention focused on Beiyue and his group only confirmed this speculation in his mind.","Unable to resist asserting his presence, he spoke up, Junior Preceptor, regarding my earlier request, I wonder what your thoughts are. Our court has shown utmost sincerity this time, I...","Yue Fuguang set down the teacup in her hand. The crisp clinking of the cup against the lid startled the few people secretly trying to solve the mystery and cut off the rest of Yanji's words.","Yanji. It was the first time Yue Fuguang looked at him directly. Yanji broke into a light sweat at being suddenly called by name. Meeting her indifferent eyes, his heart inexplicably trembled. That utterance of his name gave him the illusion of being called out by the grim reaper.","I told you last time, wealth, power, and fame are already in my hands. What do you intend to use to move me?","A mocking smile tugged at the corner of her mouth. What makes you so sure that I will definitely favor your so-called generous gifts?","The smile on Yanji's face froze. He only just remembered that despite talking for so long, he hadn't even presented his list of gifts yet.","Please wait a moment, Junior Preceptor! He hurriedly reached into his sleeve, and soon a bright red, gold-stamped gift list appeared in his hand.","While bowing to present it to Yue Fuguang, Yanji didn't forget to shoot a covert glare at Beiyue.","Beiyue was baffled by the glare and was almost angered to the point of laughing at his bridge-burning behavior.","Beiyue secretly ground his teeth. If he wasn't still preoccupied with figuring out who had poisoned him, he would definitely teach this fool a lesson.","Yue Fuguang carelessly took the gift list from Cuizhu. The first few items were fine; although precious, she already had plenty of them.","But when she saw the last two items, her heart couldn't help but stir. Building a temple to worship her—she actually didn't want the Dongyi people to do this.","After all, Dongyi was destined to be destroyed. She planned to send them all to mine after leveling Dongyi. If people worshipped her, she would feel somewhat guilty.","[Host, if the Dongyi people truly worship you, will you change your attitude toward Dongyi?]","No! Yue Fuguang's answer was resolute, without the slightest hesitation.","Mining was hard labor and far from the Dayan mainland. Transporting people from Dayan would be time-consuming and laborious. With the Dongyi people as ready-made laborers, why waste her own country's people?","What really tempted her was the final item: Dongyi was actually willing to gift her an island reef as a token of gratitude. Counting the one she won last time, wouldn't she have two overseas properties?","Yue Fuguang raised her eyes to appraise the seemingly composed Yanji. In truth, his frequently blinking eyes and unconscious swallowing had already betrayed his nervousness.","Placing the list on the table, Yue Fuguang tapped her finger lightly on the last item. Yanji, you expect to move me to act with a barren island reef where nothing grows? Have you forgotten that I already own an island just like this?","Saying this, she shook her head in boredom. There is nothing on it but sand, rocks, and seabirds. What use do I have for it?","Hearing Yue Fuguang's questioning, Yanji, who originally felt sixty percent confident, panicked slightly. He didn't know why, but in front of this official, he always felt his royal aura was completely crushed, leaving him lacking in confidence.","That was why he couldn't help but be verbally arrogant. Despite his smug appearance, it was all an act; he was actually very insecure inside. He just couldn't understand—compared to this minor, where was he lacking?","However, glancing at Beiyue and the others, who were usually even more boastful than him but were now as obedient as pet cats, Yanji finally felt a bit better.","These myriad thoughts flashed through his mind during just a few breaths of silence. He carefully pulled a nautical chart, or rather a partial map of the area surrounding the four islands of Dongyi, from his sleeve pocket. Please take a look, Junior Preceptor.","He unfolded the map, and he and Oshima each held one side. The map was about a meter long and wide, mostly depicting the ocean. In the center were four large connected islands, which should be the Dongyi mainland.","Scattered around the four islands of Dongyi were various large and small islands. The first one Yue Fuguang noticed was the small island she had won in the poetry competition.","Yanji pointed to an island situated at a moderate distance from the Dongyi mainland to show her. Please look, my lady. Dongyi's sincerity lies in this small island, named Chrysanthemum Island. Although it is true that no crops are currently grown there.","However, I believe that with your reputation as a divine maiden and your profound expertise in agriculture, you can certainly grow food. It shouldn't even be difficult to achieve a bountiful harvest of those three types of crops on Chrysanthemum Island.","He gave Yue Fuguang a fawning smile. I heard that the delicious sweet potato is particularly drought-resistant and can be planted even in sandy soil. You might as well plant plenty of sweet potatoes on the island.","He grew more excited as he spoke. You need not worry about the transportation of the harvested crops. As long as you can grow them, Dongyi is willing to purchase any amount at a high price, and we will cover the maritime shipping.","His blatant calculations were not only obvious to Yue Fuguang, but even Beiyue, Gantang, and the others could hear Dongyi's ulterior motives.","Beiyue's face darkened bit by bit. He knew Dongyi had offered Yue Fuguang heavy gifts this time, and he even knew a little about the gift of an island.","But he never expected that Yanji, who seemed to wear all his scheming on his face, would hide such a trick from him. He had even been used as a pawn.","While secretly cursing Yanji's cunning and hating his own carelessness, Beiyue had to admit that even he thought this was a brilliant idea!","There must be an expert guiding Dongyi from behind the scenes; Yanji's brain alone could never come up with such a scheme.","Dongyi was giving away a practically useless island reef. No matter what Yue Fuguang planted on it in the future, being so far from Dayan and so close to Dongyi, it would ultimately benefit Dongyi.","Whether they bought the crops or stole them, they couldn't lose!","Beiyue carefully stole a glance at the calm-faced Yue Fuguang. If he could see the problem, it was impossible for her not to notice. He just didn't know what she would choose to do.","The Dongyi people had long heard that this Junior Preceptor of Dayan lacked neither gold, silver, nor rare treasures, but only had an interest in land. The fact that she was worshipped by the common people as an agricultural deity proved her reputation was well-deserved.","Therefore, Yanji felt that if he just pushed a little harder, he could persuade this stubbornly impenetrable Junior Preceptor Yue.","Rest assured, Junior Preceptor. Although this island is not large, there is a small hill on it, and the hill has two freshwater springs.","As for whether it was enough to irrigate the land and crops, he stopped himself in time. Although Yanji had never been to Chrysanthemum Island himself, based on his experience and understanding of the folks at court, it probably wasn't enough."]},{"number":399,"title":"Chapter 399: Island, Withered Bones Vanish","paragraphs":["[Master, although divining the weather is nothing to you, it's really not worth it for a useless reef.]","\"Little Zhu, don't you think this is a good excuse to go out? With this small island, I can openly go out to sea and have fun.\"","\"System, are there any mines on this island?\"","It was completely bare without a single plant, so it couldn't possibly be entirely devoid of minerals too!","[Host, stop dreaming. Gold and silver mines aren't like cabbages you can find on just any random island.]","Hearing the system's words, Yue Fuguang wasn't too disappointed. The main reason was that she genuinely wasn't short on money right now.","As a mission-taker, she didn't plan on establishing hegemony here anyway; the wealth she currently had on hand was more than enough for her to squander.","Yue Fuguang stood up, took two steps forward, and stopped about three meters away from the map. Her gaze landed on the map, seemingly looking at the Chrysanthemum Island that Yanji had mentioned.","But only she knew that she was actually looking further outwards, at a much larger reef not too far from Chrysanthemum Island.","\"System, is that the reef where the gold and silver mines are located?\"","[Host, that is the island. It is no more than forty nautical miles from Chrysanthemum Island.]","A look of disdain appeared on Yue Fuguang's face. Pointing her finger at the location of the gold and silver mines, she said, \"There is a larger island right here, yet you choose not to offer it to me, instead specifically picking the smaller Chrysanthemum Island. Is Dongyi looking down on this Junior Preceptor?\"","At this moment, Yue Fuguang's face was so cold it could drop ice shards. She exuded a chilling aura, making it seem like she was furious after sensing she had been slighted.","Before Yanji could even offer a few words of defense, Oshima was so frightened that he fell to his knees with a heavy thud.","He bowed his head to the floor and loudly proclaimed, \"Please forgive me, Lord Junior Preceptor. The island you mentioned is named Yuexi, and it is the sacred land where our Dongyi ancestors first rose to power.","The land on Yuexi Island is barren. Although it has a larger area, it is highly mountainous, and the mountains are mostly covered in weeds and low shrubs. It is completely unsuitable for cultivation, and...\"","Yue Fuguang impatiently waved her hand to cut off his remaining words. She sat back in her seat, coldly observing the two brothers—one standing, one kneeling. \"You just need to tell me whether or not you can swap Chrysanthemum Island for Yuexi Island. This Junior Preceptor does not want to hear anything else, nor do I care.\"","Her domineering and ruthless demeanor made the surrounding people silently lower their heads and play dead, though Gan Tang and Lan Xuan'er couldn't help but steal a few glances at Yue Fuguang.","Oshima looked incredibly troubled, cold sweat breaking out on his forehead out of pure anxiety. Seeing his foolish state, Yanji had no choice but to take over and say, \"Lord Junior Preceptor, it is not that we are unwilling to give it to you. It is truly because that place is the sacred land of our royal family's rise, considered our ancestral grounds, so...\"","He didn't state what \"so\" meant, but the implication was glaringly obvious. In Great Yan, unless there was some deep-seated blood feud, a normal person would never forcefully demand someone else's ancestral land, especially a prosperous place with excellent feng shui. If Yue Fuguang insisted on taking it, it would be a grave breach of etiquette!","\"Are all your ancestors buried there?\" If it was the royal cemetery of Dongyi, she would feel rather disgusted by it too.","Yanji nodded, then shook his head. \"Aside from the first few generations of ancestors, the rest are cenotaphs. Yuexi Island is quite far from the mainland, making it inconvenient for sacrificial rites. Therefore, after every generation of our late kings passes away, a cenotaph is erected on the island.","Yuexi Island holds a vastly different significance for our royal family. If you desire it, My Lord, the news will undoubtedly spark massive controversy once it reaches our clan. This... if it drags on for a long time, we might be able to wait, but the common people of Dongyi cannot!","Please show us mercy, Divine Maiden!\"","Good heavens, this guy clearly didn't believe her claims of being a descended Divine Maiden, yet to achieve his goals at this moment, he was throwing all his pride and dignity out the window.","However, Yanji did make a valid point: time waited for no one. Calculating the days, the torrential rain in Dongyi would stop in just half a month. If the news of her wanting Yuexi Island was sent back and they started endlessly haggling over it, and too much time passed, wouldn't all her efforts end up being for nothing?","\"Forget it, how unlucky!\" Yue Fuguang leaned her body back against her chair, suddenly seeming to lose all interest in Yuexi Island. \"Chrysanthemum Island it is, then.\"","She put away the gift registry. \"This Junior Preceptor is kind-hearted and cannot bear to see the people of Dongyi suffer, so I will take the trouble to perform a divination for you.\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang finally relent, both Yanji and Oshima were overjoyed. Yanji put on a flattering, fawning expression. \"Lord Junior Preceptor, I wonder if we need to prepare anything for this divination?\"","Yue Fuguang waved her hand. \"No need.\" At this moment, she appeared exceptionally generous and easy to talk to. \"This Junior Preceptor will cast the hexagram at the beginning of the Chen hour tomorrow. You can just come wait for the news after the Chen hour.\"","Having said this, her patience was entirely spent. Ignoring all the empty formalities of serving tea and seeing guests out, she waved off the group. \"Alright, if there is nothing else, you may all leave!\"","Checking the time, it was already noon. No wonder she was feeling both hungry and sleepy.","Everyone stood up in unison, bowed respectfully, and then retreated together.","Only Bei Yue was still anxiously dwelling on the unresolved matter of his poisoning. As he left, he looked back three times with every step he took.","He desperately hoped that Yue Fuguang and that invisible 'Little Zhu' would bring the matter up again.","[Master, that Bei Yue is going to die. Bei Ji won't pin the blame for this on Great Yan, will he?]","Constant longing must yield an echo. Sure enough, the group had barely walked a few steps out of the flower hall, just as Bei Yue was on the verge of giving up, when he once again heard the news of his impending death.","He was already much calmer than he had been earlier. Aside from his face being slightly pale and his footsteps being a bit unsteady, he just walked slower and slower, making it look as though the physical discomfort from a hangover was still heavily affecting him.","\"How much longer does Bei Yue have to live? The New Year has passed, and the diplomatic mission has been staying in Great Yan for almost half a year now. It's about time for them to head back.","Little Zhu, calculate the time. Will he die while still in Great Yan?\"","A brief flash of embarrassment crossed Bei Yue's face. These two were discussing his life and death as simply and casually as if they were talking about another sunny day. It made it somewhat hard for him to maintain his composure.","However, with his life hanging in the balance, and fully aware of the capabilities of those two, he didn't dare harbor the slightest bit of resentment.","In order to hear a little more information, Bei Yue didn't even need to fake his awful complexion. He simply kept his hand clutched over his stomach and deliberately slowed his pace.","When the servants escorting them out of the estate saw Bei Yue's actions and pale face, they guessed that this esteemed guest might have eaten something bad. Given the statuses of the group, they didn't dare urge them to hurry up.","They merely continued to grumble endlessly in their hearts, thinking that a wild boar couldn't appreciate fine grains. One had to know that in their estate, the Seventh Miss enjoyed the absolute best treatment.","Especially after the Seventh Miss was granted a royal title, her provisions were entirely unique within the estate. The tea and pastries she used to entertain guests were all top-tier delicacies. To actually get an upset stomach from eating such things truly showed a total lack of fortune.","Feigning illness, Bei Yue had no idea that his actions were drawing the silent mockery of the Yu estate's servants. Right now, he only cared about who the poisoner was, what kind of poison he had been given, and whether he could still be saved.","From the corner of his eye, he glanced at Lan Xuan'er beside him. This woman was a peerless master of both medicine and poison. Now that the few of them shared a common secret, she would surely lend him a hand and save him, right!","[To avoid drawing suspicion, the poisoner gave him a slow-acting poison. This kind of slow-acting poison must be administered a total of five times. Last night was the third time.","I don't know when the diplomatic mission will set off to return home. If they delay by a few days, Bei Yue will probably end up a corpse in Great Yan.]","\"What a hassle. Forget it, considering Emperor Mingxi has been relatively obedient, I'll help him out one more time.\""]},{"number":400,"title":"Chapter 400: To Fight or Not to Fight, Either Way It's Death","paragraphs":["[Master, what do you want to do? The Bone Dissolver poison in Bei Yue's body has an extremely rare antidote. Moreover, those afflicted by this poison will have their bones slowly crumble into dust after death.]","Hearing that it was such a vicious poison as the Bone Dissolver, both Lan Xuan'er and Bei Yue changed their expressions simultaneously. Lan Xuan'er silently shook her head at him, indicating that she was powerless to help, her eyes filled with the 'blessing' of wishing him a good journey to the afterlife.","Bei Yue: Thank you so much for that!","[Is Master going to detoxify Bei Yue? In the world today, it seems Master is truly the only one capable of saving his miserable life.]","Bei Yue's nearly dead eyes suddenly widened. As for whether it was a miserable life, that didn't matter!","His lifeless eyes were instantly lit up with an overwhelming desire to survive. He wished he could turn back right now and beg Yue Fuguang to save his miserable life.","The Bone Dissolver didn't just turn bones to dust after death; after the fifth poisoning, the bones would start crumbling before the person was even fully dead!","He was not only afraid of death, but he was also afraid of pain!","Who knew that his newly kindled hope would be extinguished again by Yue Fuguang's next words.","Yue Fuguang refused heartlessly, \"I won't save him. Not only do we have no friendship, but we also have a personal grudge. The only reason I haven't killed him myself is that I don't want to dirty my hands. Why would I save him? Since when is your master such a magnanimous immortal?","Besides, hasn't he only been poisoned three times? As long as he avoids the poison the next two times, his little life can be temporarily preserved until he returns to his country. Why would he need my rescue?\"","Bei Yue: So you just don't want to see me die in Great Yan!","Thinking of the things he had done in the past, Bei Yue felt a rare sense of worry and fear that didn't just stem from the dread of a stronger person.","At this moment, his heart was mostly filled with a guilty conscience. He wasn't too surprised by Yue Fuguang's answer; if it were him, he would have made the same choice.","Thinking this way, the light in Bei Yue's eyes slowly died out again. The others watching him felt full of sympathy but also really wanted to laugh.","If they hadn't known that those two were unaware of their eavesdropping, they would have thought they were teasing him on purpose.","\"Little Zhu, go and destroy the other two packets of poison. Just make sure he won't be poisoned by this again while in Great Yan.\"","[Rest assured, Master. However, once this Bei Yue returns to Northern Li, he will undoubtedly die. The Bone Dissolver poison in Li Sanming's hands all came from the mastermind poisoner within the Northern Li royal family.]","Bei Yue didn't hear the name of the poisoner at this point, which left him somewhat disappointed. But without needing to overthink it, he could easily list the names of a few suspects. He just had to investigate them one by one. As long as he didn't die, he would definitely avenge this!","\"So this is yet another dark scheme for the throne?\" Yue Fuguang complained as she stood up and walked outside. \"I really don't know what these mortals are thinking. With a short lifespan of only a few decades, they could be doing anything else. What is the point of using it all to fight for power and profit?\" Yue Fuguang began making light of a situation that didn't affect her.","[Master, is there a possibility that it's precisely because their lives are short that they like to fight even more? After all, if they don't fight, they'll die in a few decades anyway! If they do fight, they'll still die in a few decades!] The system was not only fond of talking nonsense but also enjoyed stirring up trouble.","They'll die in a few decades anyway!","These words were not only heard by Bei Yue but also hammered into the hearts of the others. The few who had originally been enjoying the show suddenly felt their footsteps become incredibly heavy. At this moment, they felt as if they were walking through an endless swamp.","They knew that everyone would die eventually, but it seemed like today was the first time they truly faced this issue. We seem to... really be going to die... in a few decades!","Especially since the youngest among them was eighteen and the oldest, Bei Ye, was twenty-five. How many more eighteen or twenty-five years did they have left to live?","Everything they were fighting to the death for right now couldn't be taken with them after they died!","All their enemies and lovers could not accompany them. Death was a very private and lonely affair!","Yan Ji, who was in the best mood and had the lightest footsteps after accomplishing a major task, had been walking excitedly at the front.","\"Oshima, let me tell you...\" He turned around happily, wanting to tell Oshima that they would send the results back to their country without a moment's delay as soon as they got them tomorrow. But when he turned around, he saw that apart from Bei Yue, who had a 'stomachache,' the others seemed to have 'fallen victim' too?","Yan Ji's small eyes darted around. Could Junior Preceptor Yue have spiked their tea and pastries? Otherwise, why did every single one of them look like a corpse?","Fortunately, he had been busy doing great things just now and wasn't as idle as the others. He hadn't even had the time to take a few bites of the tea and pastries. Otherwise, wouldn't he be just like them right now?","Yan Ji figured out the crux of the matter, believing he had seen through everything. He glanced at the servant leading the way. Ultimately, considering that the location was inappropriate and they hadn't truly obtained the information yet, it wasn't wise to offend Yue Fuguang at this time.","So he walked up to them with his hands behind his back and said, \"We are all friends, so I kindly remind you all: no matter where you go, you must remain vigilant. Don't just stuff whatever you see into your mouths.\" He had seen it clearly just now; these guys had eaten quite a bit.","He gave them an arrogant nod. \"I have said all I need to say. Think it over carefully!\"","Xi Ling glanced at this idiot who knew nothing and instantly straightened his back. Bei Ye, Gan Tang, and the others did the same. Their originally heavy and possessed states of mind were suddenly mostly dispelled by this person's interference.","\"Hey! Slow down, wait for me!\"","Yan Ji reached out his hand dramatically, not knowing how his single sentence had turned into good medicine. Their legs were no longer sore, their stomachaches were cured, and they were walking even faster than him.","No sooner had Yan Ji and his group stepped out of the Yu Manor than Emperor Mingxi found out about it.","\"Qian Gui, did these people visit Fuguang for the matter of the Dongyi flood again?\"","Because of Yue Fuguang, no one dared to plant spies in the Yu Manor, but Emperor Mingxi could still make a rough guess.","He picked up the freshly refilled tea Qian Gui had poured for him and took a gentle sip. The rich aroma of the tea instantly dissolved between his lips and teeth. \"The tea Fuguang grows still suits my taste best.\"","Emperor Mingxi set the teacup down and looked outside the hall. \"I wonder if Fuguang agreed to that boy Yan Ji, and what price Dongyi is willing to pay in exchange?\"","Qian Gui tentatively suggested, \"Should we have Ping Yi and the others go to the posthouse to investigate? I heard that Yan Ji looked very happy when he left, while the others didn't look too well.\"","Just as the two were talking, the Crown Prince walked in. After bowing in greeting, he smiled and said, \"Imperial Father, Lord Junior Preceptor has sent word. Today, Dongyi gifted her a reef island named Chrysanthemum.\"","\"Dongyi gifted Fuguang a reef island?\" Emperor Mingxi's face instantly wrinkled into a smile. \"Qian Gui, bring the map.\"","Eunuch Qian quickly found Great Yan's newly drawn map of Dongyi and spread it out on the imperial desk. Emperor Mingxi searched carefully across the vast sea. \"Chrysanthemum Island, here it is, neither too far nor too close to Dongyi.\"","Emperor Mingxi observed the surroundings of Chrysanthemum Island for a while, then heavily dropped his magnifying glass. He sat back on the imperial throne, his voice turning a few degrees colder. \"The King of Dongyi harbors no good intentions!\"","It was bad enough that there were always villains trying to harm him, but in the past two years, there were also constantly villains trying to steal their Junior Preceptor. If the former made Emperor Mingxi both angry and resentful, vowing to take revenge sooner or later, then the latter made him wish he could immediately drag the culprits out and behead them!"]}]);
